VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aHIRSCH, MICHELLE, S., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by HIRSCH,MICHELLE S.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED BIOPSY:\u000aBreast tissue with atypical ductal hyperplasia, apocrine metaplasia,\u000aand microcalcifications associated with benign epithelium (including\u000athe area of atypical hyperplasia).\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: S/p lt breast core bx REMOVED_DATE  ADH on core - two areas of ca++, both\u000awired and was clipped.\u000aOperation: Lt direct needle breast bx.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: ADH, lt breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Lt breast bx with calcifications, ADH on core.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Marking and 2 ca++ clusters in specimen. DS\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SHEN,JIAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "left breast biopsy with calcifications, ADH on core", and consists of a\u000afragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (5.5 x 6 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with two attached\u000awires and received with mammogram. The x-ray is reviewed and clacifications\u000aand a clip are identified. Cross sectioning of the specimen reveals a\u000awhite/tan area (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) adjacent to the first wire which was\u000aindicated as the area including calcifications. This area is located adjacent\u000ato the inferior margin and 1 cm from anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior margin. Adjacent to the second wire, there is a\u000alinear, white/tan area (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is located REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000aanterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from inferior margin, 1 cm from posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from superior margin, more than REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral margin and more than 2\u000acm from medial margin. The suspicious areas are entierly submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  area for abnormal calcification which is indicated by the first\u000awire, 12 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  suspicious area which is indicated by the second wire for core\u000abiopsy site, 10 frags, ESS.\u000ajis\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
