VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kevin Golden, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Vania Nose, MD, PhD\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, EXCISION WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS":\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Cribriform, micropapillary\u000aNuclear grade - Low\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - anterior, posterior, lateral, medial,\u000asuperior\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - inferior (focal REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aComplex sclerosing lesion\u000aPapilloma\u000aSclerosing adenosis\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition): pTis Nx MX.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000aNOTE:\u000aSeveral foci of atypical ductal hyperplasia are within REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral\u000amargin of the original specimens, but final lateral margin (specimen D) does\u000anot show presence of atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aThis case was reviewed with Dr. D. Dillon (Breast Pathology Service), who\u000aconcurs. Dr. Susan Lester, Breast Pathology Service, reviewed selected slides,\u000aand concurs.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "SUPERIOR SHAVED MARGIN":\u000aBreast tissue with atypical ductal hyperplasia (at least REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amargins).\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aC. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "MEDIAL SHAVED MARGIN":\u000aBenign breast tissue with atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aD. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LATERAL SHAVED MARGIN":\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 71 yo s/p REMOVED_DATE  LUOQ core biopsy of calcifications, noted on\u000a10/30/07 MMG pathology revealed DCIS.\u000aOperation: L breast wire localized lumpectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L DCIS.\u000aRADIOLOGY COMMENT:\u000aCalcifications, clip and intact wire within the specimen. Dr. Gombos.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue short/superior, long/lateral, whip stitch chest wall\u000amargin.\u000aB/2. Superior shaved margin whip stitch new margin.\u000aC/3. Medial shaved margin whip stitch new margin.\u000aD/4. Lateral shaved margin whip stitch new margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and medical record number.\u000aPart A, "left breast tissue, short stitch superior, long stitch lateral,\u000awhipstitch chest wall margin", consists of one wire-localized lumpectomy (6.1\u000acm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to\u000aposterior; REMOVED_DATE g). The specimen was received with a localization wire in\u000aplace and a short suture marking the superior margin and long suture marking\u000athe lateral margin. An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates a\u000awell-circumscribed density with a clip located in the bracketed area of the\u000awire. The specimen is inked for evaluation of margins; posterior equals black,\u000aanterior equals blue, superior equals red, inferior equals green, lateral\u000aequals yellow, medial equals orange. Tissue consists of dense fibrous\u000aparenchyma with multiple areas of hemorrhage ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. Within the area of a clip is a tan/brown well-circumscribed lesion\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. This area is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin,\u000a0.3 cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin. The margins consist of unremarkable adipose tissue. The specimen was\u000asectioned superior to inferiorly and submitted in its entirety. Note: The\u000aarea of the clip is in micro cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of specimen, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "superior shaved margin, whipstitch equals new margin", consists of one\u000afragment of yellow/tan soft tissue consistent with adipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, with a stitch located on one side. This side designated new\u000amargin was inked black. The entire specimen is submitted for review.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin fragments, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aPart C, "medial shaved margin, whipstitch new margin", consists of one fragment\u000aof yellow/white soft tissue consistent with adipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen contains a stitch on one side and this side was inked\u000ablack. The entire specimen is submitted for review.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial shaved fragment, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aPart D, "lateral shaved margin, whipstitch equals new margin", consists of one\u000afragment of yellow/white soft tissue consistent with adipose tissue measuring\u000a5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen contains a stitch on one side which was inked\u000ablack. The entire specimen is submitted for review.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aKG/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
