VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Derek K Marsee, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia with associated calcifications.\u000aCalcifications in association with benign epithelium.\u000aSecretory changes, multifocal.\u000aThere is no evidence of in situ or invasive carcinoma, including margins.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000aSelected slides of this case were reviewed by Dr. A. Richardson, Breast\u000aPathology Service, who concurs.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, NEW MEDIAL MARGIN:\u000aBenign breast tissue with associated calcifications.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Wire-localization biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Microcalcifications, R breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1/A. Right breast tissue.\u000a2/B. New medial margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in two parts, each labeled with the patient?s name and\u000aunit number.\u000aPart A, was received fresh and labeled "#1. Right breast tissue", and consists\u000aof a REMOVED_DATE (medial to lateral) x REMOVED_DATE (inferior to superior) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to\u000aposterior) cm breast excision with a localization wire in place. The specimen\u000awas received previously inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.. An accompanying specimen\u000aradiograph demonstrates a tight cluster of calcifications adjacent to the\u000alocalization wire. The specimen was sectioned from medial to lateral and\u000aentirely submitted. The tissue consists of fibrous adipose tissue and the\u000acalcifications were localized to blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 5 frags, ESS (perpendicular)\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags each, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: wire localized sections with probable calcifications, 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lateral margin, 5 frags, ESS (perpendicular)\u000aPart B, was received in formalin and labeled "#2. New medial margin", and\u000aconsists of one piece of tan/pink tissue (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). One surface of\u000athe tissue was inked orange by the surgeon. The new medial margin is re-inked\u000aorange, and the old surgical margin is inked black by the pathologist. The\u000aspecimen consists primarily of adipose tissue with no discreet lesions\u000aidentified. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: New Surgical margin, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: New surgical margin, 3 frags, ESS\u000aDM/cdm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Derek K Marsee M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aPrelim Dx Release by Derek K Marsee M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aNo Action - Prelim Sent by Derek K Marsee M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/13/2005\u000a[report_end]
