VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Rachel E Factor, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, TERMINAL DUCT EXCISION FOR NIPPLE DISCHARGE:\u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA (best seen in block #2).\u000aIntraductal papilloma (0.3 cm).\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aCysts with apocrine metaplasia.\u000aNOTE: No carcinoma is seen after complete histologic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast nipple discharge, failed ductogram, negative mammogram.\u000aOperation: Right breast terminal duct excision.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast nipple discharge.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a(1) (R) breast terminal duct excision; short suture-superior, long-lateral,\u000asingle-anterior.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "Right breast terminal duct excision", and consists of a portion of\u000afibroadipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen has cautery\u000aartifact on the edges. A long double stitch designates the lateral aspect of\u000athe specimen, and a short double stitch designates the superior aspect of the\u000aspecimen. There is a single stitch, which is designated as anterior but sits\u000adeep to the superior suture. The surgeon was called to clarify that the single\u000astitch designates the nipple duct region. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol. Note that the area designated by the single stitch for the nipple\u000aduct is inked black (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). A radiograph does not accompany the specimen.\u000aOn sectioning, the specimen is 80% fibrous with some cystic areas. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multiple frags, ESS.\u000aref/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Rachel E Factor M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/17/2005\u000a[report_end]
