VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DONALD P GOLDSTEIN M.D.\u000aCASE: BG-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Stacey A. Simons, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Marisa R Nucci, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, NEEDLE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aBenign breast tissue with fibrocystic changes including focal epithelial\u000ahyperplasia, apocrine cysts and dense stroma.\u000aFibroadenoma, REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of\u000athe specimen, including margins.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION:\u000aBenign breast tissue with fibrocystic changes including apocrine\u000ametaplasia, dense stroma and sclerosing adenosis.\u000aFocal microcalcifications are associated with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast mass, needle localized in X-ray.\u000aOperation: Excision of same\u000aExcision of right breast mass\u000aOperative Findings: None given\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right needle localized breast mass excision\u000aB/2. Reexcision right breast mass\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aSpecimen #1: Intact wire within the specimen. No calcifications are seen.\u000aNo definite calcifications in 1st specimen. Hook wire present.\u000aSpecimen #2: Approximately 4 punctate calcifications seen in 2nd specimen, no\u000adefinitive cluster seen.\u000aReviewed images with surgeon Dr. Goldstein.\u000aAwait path -> ?re-image approximately 3 months with mammo.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is submitted fresh in two parts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand unit number, and is accompanied by two sets of radiographs labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number with no markings by the radiologist to indicate\u000athe location of the lesion. The first set of radiographs show the localization\u000awire and the second set of radiographs have no localization wire.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right needle localized breast mass", consists of an unoriented\u000askin ellipse (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm). The deepest aspect\u000aof the specimen is comprised of the deep firm white tissue, approximately REMOVED_DATE x\u000a3.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm. Overall dimension of the specimen excluding the localization\u000awire is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The surgical margins are inked blue. The specimen\u000ais sectioned to reveal a homogeneous but variegated yellow to white firm mass\u000aat the dimension previously described. The remainder of the specimen is\u000alobulated yellow adipose tissue. The region of the wire tip is found in\u000acassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and the specimen is sectioned and submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Firm white region of specimen, localization wire region in\u000acassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior portion of specimen with skin ellipse, multi frags,\u000aESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Re-excision RT breast mass REMOVED_DATE ", consists of an unoriented\u000afragment of fibroadipose soft tissue (4.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with no localization\u000awire. The mass is almost entirely comprised of firm, white fibrous tissue,\u000awith only a thin border of adipose tissue on one edge. The outer surface of\u000athe entire specimen is inked blue. Sectioning reveals a solid white mass with\u000aa small yellow punctate region, and focal areas of hemorrhage and fibrosis.\u000aThe specimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White mass with attached adipose tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aNote: Part B container came with two labels, both designated "#2. Re-excision\u000aRT breast mass REMOVED_DATE ", and due to the submission of two form 86 for the same\u000anumber, specimen labels have been attached to the back of the form 86.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BG-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Marisa R Nucci M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
