VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Travis J Hollmann, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE, BIOPSY (including FSA):\u000aOne lymph node with no tumor present.\u000a(3 H&E levels examined.)\u000aLEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY (948g):\u000aNo residual carcinoma identified.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (two foci).\u000aCalcifications in stroma and associate with benign epithelium.\u000aBreast with multifocal fat necrosis, hemosiderin-laden macrophages, fibrosis,\u000aand giant cell reaction consistent with prior surgical changes.\u000aColumnar cell change.\u000aSkin with scar.\u000aOne(1) lymph node (intraparenchymal) with no tumor present.\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. D. Dillon, Breast Pathology Service, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast IDC and DCIS found incidentally at breast reduction.\u000aOperation: Total left mastectomy and SNB.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left axillary sentinel node - FS.\u000aB/2. Left breast, stitch on superior skin.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE" (FSA):\u000aOne lymph node negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: Lucian Chirieac, M.D.\u000aResident: STACEY A. SIMONS, MD, PATRICIA A. R. BRUNKER, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aELEANOR CHEN, MD, PHD\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Left axillary sentinel node - FS", consists of a single fragment\u000aof yellow/pink soft tissue (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with minimal fibroadipose\u000atissue from which a single candidate lymph node (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is\u000adissected. The candidate node is bisected and entirely submitted as FSA.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSA remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of fibroadipose tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left breast, stitch on superior skin", consists of a 948-g simple\u000amastectomy specimen received with a single stitch designating the superior skin\u000aper the surgeon and measuring REMOVED_DATE S-I, REMOVED_DATE M-L, and REMOVED_DATE cm A-P. The specimen\u000ahas a brown/tan portion of skin (3.5 S-I, REMOVED_DATE M-L and excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE \u000acm - circumareolar resection) with nipple (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The deep resection\u000amargin contains no skeletal muscles and is inked black and serially sectioned\u000afrom medial to lateral to reveal numerous areas of yellow/tan, indurated\u000aadipose tissue (? fat necrosis versus tumor). Area A is located at the 12\u000ao'clock aspect and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, area B is located at the 6\u000ao'clock aspect of the specimen and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, area C is\u000alocated anterior and lateral to area B and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and\u000aarea D is located in the tail of the specimen and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aThe closest distance from potential tumor to the deep margin measures REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aand the areas of fat necrosis/mass appear to abut the anterior skin ellipse.\u000aThe specimen is not received with an axillary tail, however, approximately five\u000acandidate lymph nodes in the lateral aspect of the mammary tissue are dissected\u000aand entirely submitted for review. The specimen was reviewed with Dr. Susan\u000aLester of the Breast Pathology Service.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area A, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area B, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area C, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area D, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Single bisected node, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Candidate lymph nodes, multi frags each, RSS.\u000aTH/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/11/2006\u000a[report_end]
