VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Surgical margin\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Matthias D. Hofer, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS (PART B):\u000aSEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, single focus, associated with\u000acalcifications and core biopsy site (see NOTE).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia, focal\u000aCalcifications are present associated with normal breast epithelium.\u000aCore biopsy site changes are present.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aNOTE: A single duct involved by a cribriform proliferation of cells with low\u000agrade nuclei associated with calcifications but without necrosis is present\u000aassociated with the core biopsy site (seen on REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDlevels 2 to 6 only). As in the\u000acore needle biopsy, the lesion is qualitatively sufficient for DCIS, but the\u000afocus measures < REMOVED_DATE cm in total and overall, given the low volume of disease\u000apresent a diagnosis of severe ADH rather than DCIS is favored. This severely\u000aatypical focus is located < REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, midway between the\u000asuperior and inferior margins (0.5 cm from the inferior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe superior margin). Stains for ER, PR and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were attempted but the\u000afocus is not present on deeper levels used for immunohistochemical stains. Dr.\u000aSusan Lester has also reviewed slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID with levels and agrees with the\u000ainterpretation.\u000aRIGHT BREAST ADDITIONAL INFERIOR SHAVE MARGIN (PART A):\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia, focal\u000aNormal breast tissue with rare calcifications.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: ADH - right breast.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy and additional\u000ainferior shave margin.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: ADH - right breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA. Tissue, right breast, short suture = superior, long suture = lateral.\u000aB/2. Right breast tissue inferior shave margin - suture = superior.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass + clip in specimen. OR called 11:45 - KC.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aPart A. The specimen is received in formalin, in one part, labeled with the\u000apatient's name, unit number, and "R breast tissue, inferior shave margin", and\u000aconsists of an irregular portion of fibrofatty tissue (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000awith a suture along one aspect designating superior, which is inked blue. The\u000aopposite, unsutured aspect is inked black and the specimen is serially\u000asectioned to reveal 95% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, and 5% white fibrous\u000atissue, with no discrete masses or lesions identified. The specimen is\u000asequentially submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aPart B. The specimen was received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and\u000aunit number and "#1. Tissue, right breast." The specimen consists of\u000awire-localized lumpectomy measuring REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior\u000ato inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior. The specimen is oriented with two\u000asutures and is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. A wire enters the specimen at the medial aspect and exits the\u000aspecimen at the lateral/inferior aspect. The specimen is accompanied by a\u000aradiograph showing a wire and a clip within a distinct mass. The specimen is\u000asectioned from medial to lateral into eight slices, the medial aspect is\u000adesignated as slice #1. The clip is recovered in slice #4 and slightly within\u000aa hemorrhagic area located within a firm tan/yellow mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.8 cm. This area comes within REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin, less than REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ato the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE to the lateral margin.\u000aCorrelation with the radiograph is established. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted for histologic review.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicular sections, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular sections, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aCP/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/1/2008\u000a[report_end]
