diograph as illustrated on centricity demonstrates a\u000awire entering the lateral aspect of the specimen and does not exit, localizing\u000aa clip. There is also an area of calcifications identified. The specimen is\u000ainked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The specimen was serially sectioned from medial to lateral to\u000areveal a previous biopsy site with a centrally located clip. The majority of\u000athe specimen is fibrous tissue (80%) with the remainder yellow lobulated breast\u000atissue (20%). The specimen is entirely submitted for histology.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial end, perpendicular sections, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial cross sections from medial to lateral, clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags\u000aper cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral end, perpendicular sections, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left breast biopsy the more medial side (short stitch anterior,\u000along inferior) x3 pieces", consists of a REMOVED_DATE g portion of fibrofatty breast\u000atissue that was oriented per the surgeon such that a short stitch designates\u000aanterior and a long stitch designates inferior. The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aanterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm superior to\u000ainferior. The specimen radiograph as illustrated on centricity demonstrates a\u000awire entering the lateral aspect of the specimen and exiting the medial aspect\u000aof the specimen. The wire is localizing in area of calcifications, but no clip\u000ais present in the specimen. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal predominantly fibrous\u000abreast tissue (85%) with the remainder a yellow lobulated breast tissue (15%).\u000aAlso received in the container are three detached fragments of fatty soft\u000atissue (up to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension). The external surface of the three\u000afragments is inked black. The specimen is entirely submitted for histology.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Separately received fragments, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial end of main specimen, perpendicular sections, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial cross sections from medial to lateral, 2 frags per\u000acassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral aspect of main specimen, perpendicular sections, 5 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BG-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aPAV/am\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 02, 2009 at 05:04:11PM\u000a[report_end]
