VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: David C. Park, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION AND EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, levels examined).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread, focal calcifications and\u000ainvolvement of adenosis.\u000aExtensive calcifications mainly in benign epithelium including lobules,\u000aadenosis, columnar cell changes and cysts.\u000aFibroadenoma (0.5 cm).\u000aNOTE: An immunostain for E-cadherin (on block 18) is negative in the focus of\u000ainterest, supporting the diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 63 year-old female with mammo REMOVED_DATE  revealing L breast\u000acalcifications UOQ - not amenable to core bx.\u000aOperation: L B breast WL bx.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue, short stitch superior, long stitch lateral, whip\u000astitch on chest wall margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aCalcs in specimen with 2 wires. OR called. SS.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. Left breast tissue with double wire localization", and\u000aconsists of a left breast lumpectomy specimen (7.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a short\u000astitch designating superior, long stitch lateral and a whip stitch on the chest\u000awall margin. The specimen is received with an accompanying radiograph that\u000ashows calcifications on the anterior/inferior side and the posterior medial\u000aside. On the accompanying radiograph, there are two localization wires\u000aentering the lateral aspect of the specimen with the tip of one wire\u000a(arbitrarily designated #1) exiting the posterior aspect of the specimen at the\u000asite of the chest wall margin. The tip of the second wire (arbitrarily\u000adesignated #2) exits to the medial side of the specimen. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from lateral to medial. On cut section, there is a diffuse\u000aarea of firm fibrous tissue that involves the entirety of the lumpectomy\u000aspecimen with areas of fibrosis abutting the inferior, posterior, superior,\u000amedial, lateral and anterior margins. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen serially sectioned from lateral to medial, multi frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicular, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aDCP/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/1/2007\u000a[report_end]
