VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aMUELLER, JAMES, D, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by MUELLER,JAMES D,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aIntraductal papillomatosis.\u000aFlorid ductal hyperplasia.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aBiopsy site.\u000aCysts.\u000aMicrocalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of ADH.\u000aOperation: Wire loc breast bx.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammo.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Wire loc breast biopsy.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass in specimen. DN Smith, MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by OH,KIRSTINE YUNG-TING,M.D.\u000aReceived fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name, medical unit\u000anumber and "#1 right breast wire localized lesion", are two fragments of\u000ayellow/pink/tan soft tissue (6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with\u000awire localized in place on the larger fragment. In addition a mammogram is\u000apresent with a breast tissue specimen and a wire localizing needle within it.\u000aA central mass is seen adjacent to the needle with sparse microcalcifications.\u000aThe two unoriented fragments are inked blue, serial sectioning reveals a\u000apredominantly fatty breast (approximately 50% by volume fibrous tissue), with\u000aan area of hemorrhage (0.2 cm in diameter) and multiple cysts. In addition,\u000aareas of bright yellow discoloration in the fibrous tissue are present,\u000aconsistent with fat necrosis. An area of slight nodularity or increased tissue\u000adensity is identified within the specimen (0.5 cm in diameter). Serial\u000asections (excluding fatty tissue) are entirely submitted. Sectioning of the\u000adetached breast fragment reveals similarly white fibrous breast tissue (60% by\u000avolume) and no dominant lesion.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slices of larger breast fragment, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro 6&7: bisected slice of larger breast tissue, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro 8&9: bisected slice of breast larger tissue, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro 10&11: bisected slice of breast larger tissue, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro 12&13: bisected slice of larger breast tissue, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro 14: slice of larger breast tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 15&16: bisected slice of the smaller breast tissue, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000ako\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
