VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aODZE, ROBERT, DANIEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by ODZE,ROBERT DANIEL,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION":\u000aRESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - solid, cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aSize (max area in one block) - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aNumber of blocks/total - 2:12 blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - superior, inferior, anterior, posterior,\u000amedial, and lateral\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia\u000aCysts\u000aBiopsy cavity\u000aSkin with scar\u000aSkeletal muscle\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - performed previously\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of left breast cancer. See previous BWH pathology report.\u000aOperation: Re-excision, left breast bx site (left partial mastectomy).\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast tissue, short superior, long lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by JEDLICKA,PAVEL J.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1 left breast tissue". It is an oriented breast lumpectomy specimen (5.5\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an attached skin ellipse (4.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm) containing a REMOVED_DATE \u000acm healed linear scar. A short superior and a long lateral orienting sutures\u000aare present. The specimen is inked by the pathologist per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior =\u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Sectioning reveals a\u000acentral area of old hemorrhage, fibrosis and fat necrosis, grossly consistent\u000awith prior biopsy/excision site, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The distances\u000aof this area to the nearest margins are as follows: REMOVED_DATE cm to medial, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ato lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm to superior, less than REMOVED_DATE cm to\u000aanterior and REMOVED_DATE cm to posterior. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is\u000acomposed of almost exclusively lobulated adipose tissue without any additional\u000alesions.\u000aMicro 1&2: biopsy site and nearest medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 3: biopsy site and nearest lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: biopsy site and nearest inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: biopsy site and nearest superior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 6&7: biopsy site and nearest anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 8&9: biopsy site and nearest posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 10&11: additional representative biopsy site, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: representative uninvolved breast, 1 frag, RSS.\u000apj\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
