ateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000asuperior to inferior margin. There is a short suture designating as superior\u000aand a long suture designating as lateral, per surgeon. The specimen is inked\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThere is a wire that enters the lateral margin and exits the posterior margin.\u000aThere is an attached mammogram showing a lesion that is close to the superior,\u000aposterior and inferior margins. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal\u000athe clip measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm abutting the posterior and inferior\u000amargin and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin\u000aand greater than REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial and lateral margin. No other gross\u000alesions are identified. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral, posterior, superior and inferior margins, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Clip, anterior, posterior, superior and inferior margins, 2 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior, posterior, superior and inferior margins, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior, posterior, superior and inferior margins, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior, posterior, superior, inferior and medial margins, 2 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin perpendicular, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. R breast tissue medial to specimen #1, suture on aspect close to\u000aspecimen #1", consists of one fragment of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a stitch designated as aspect closest to specimen #1,\u000aper surgeon. Half of the specimen closest to stitch is inked blue, and the\u000aother half is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal one\u000afocal discoloration measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm that abuts the blue-inked\u000amargin. The specimen is entirely submitted. There is an accompanying\u000aradiograph showing no lesion pacification.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Stitch half perpendicular section, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lesional tissue, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Right breast tissue medial to specimen #1, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Black-inked margin, perpendicular, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. R breast tissue inferior to specimen #1", consists of one fragment\u000aof yellow fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is\u000aunoriented and entirely inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to\u000areveal a white cystic nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm abutting the margins.\u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Right breast tissue inferior to specimen #1, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cyst, right breast tissue inferior to specimen #1, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart D, "#4. Tissue from directly underneath nipple", consists of one fragment\u000aof skin punch biopsy measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in depth. The specimen is\u000abisected and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tissue from directly underneath nipple, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BG-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aER:lc\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday August 12, 2009 at 01:36:11PM\u000a[report_end]
