VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Comedo, solid, cribriform, papillary,\u000aclinging\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate to high\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total: - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm): - deep (multifocal), medial (focal),\u000aanterior (focal), inferior (multifocal)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS Atypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia\u000aPapilloma\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - Tis pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Pending\u000aNOTE: The superior and lateral margins are not well seen and cannot be\u000aseparately evaluated.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block 2):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) POSITIVE (2+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Lt needle loc breast bx.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Unspecified.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcs & hookwire in specimen. DIR\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HONG,XUEFEI,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "left needle localized breast biopsy", and consists of a\u000afragment of breast tissue (3.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is inked by the\u000asurgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. An accompanying radiograph shows calcifications and wire in\u000athe specimen as documented by the radiologist.\u000aMicro 1&2: possible calcifications, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 3&4: remainder of specimen, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 5: lateral margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 6: medial margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000axh\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
