(no signature on form)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SMOUSE,JASON H.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the\u000apatient's name, unit number and "#1 tissue from left breast DCIS site, stitch:\u000along - lateral, short = superior", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion\u000aof fibrofatty breast tissue and overlying tan skin ellipse (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm), a\u000alocalization wire, and accompanying radiograph and two sutures designated by\u000athe surgeon (long - lateral and short - superior). The specimen is received\u000apreviously inked according to pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green;\u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. There is a REMOVED_DATE cm in length, well-healed,\u000alinear scar on the skin ellipse which is at the nearest radial margin. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral revealing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.5 cm, tan/white, indurated, ill-defined mass which is REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, 2 cm from the medial margin and\u000agreater than REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. Just lateral and anterior to the\u000amass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, ill-defined, focally hemorrhagic focus with fat\u000anecrosis (? previous excision/biopsy site) which is subjacent to the\u000aaforementioned skin scar. This area comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin and is at\u000aleast REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial and lateral margins. The remaining breast tissue\u000aconsists of approximately equal amounts of yellow/tan, lobulated fat and\u000atan/white, focally cystic, dense fibrous stroma. The entire mass (probable\u000aprevious biopsy site and area of calcifications [corresponding with\u000aradiograph]) is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast mass in relationship to margin, sequentially from medial to\u000alateral, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  probable previous biopsy/excision site to include relationship\u000awith all margins (submitted from medial to lateral), multi frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro 24: representative lateral margin nearest biopsy site, 2 frags, RSS.\u000adfi\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
