VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000a1) SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT SENTINEL NODE" (including REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aTwo (2) lymph nodes with no tumor present.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000a2) SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST":\u000aBreast tissue with no residual invasive ductal carcinoma or DCIS present.\u000aBiopsy cavity.\u000aSkin with cicatrix.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Extensive DCIS and small invasive carcinoma.\u000aOperation: Left sentinel lymph node biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Left sentinel node - FS\u000a2) Left breast - short superior, long lateral\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "1) LEFT SENTINEL NODES" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,2):\u000aTwo (2) sentinel nodes with no tumor seen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by RUCKER-SCHMIDT,RACHEL L.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart 1, "Left sentinel node", consists of two fragments of pink/tan soft tissue\u000a(2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Two lymph nodes (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000agreatest dimension) are identified within the soft tissue. The lymph nodes are\u000aentirely submitted for frozen section evaluation as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro 1: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 2: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag, ESS\u000aPart 2, "Left breast - short superior, long lateral", consists of a 202 gm left\u000abreast mastectomy specimen (16.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with attached triangular\u000apiece of skin (8.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm), including nipple (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE cm). Included with\u000athe specimen are two sutures placed by the surgeon to designate the superior\u000aand lateral orientation. A REMOVED_DATE cm, thin, well-healed scar is present on the\u000askin superior and lateral to the nipple. The deep margin of the specimen is a\u000asmooth fascial plane without grossly identified skeletal muscle. The deep\u000amargin is inked in black and the specimen is serially sectioned. A centrally\u000alocated, white fibrous area (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), grossly consistent with a\u000aprevious biopsy cavity is identified. This cavity is grossly within REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe deep inked margin. The specimen is grossly 40% tan/white fibrous tissue\u000aand 60% golden yellow adipose tissue. The lateral portion of the specimen is\u000athinly sectioned and examined. No lymph nodes are identified. Representative\u000asections are submitted for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Sections of biopsy cavity, medial to lateral, 5 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 8: Skin with scar, 1 frag, rSS\u000aMicro 9: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 10: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 11: Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 12: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 13: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000arlr\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
