VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNUCCI, MARISA, ROSE, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NUCCI,MARISA ROSE,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "SENTINEL NODE, RIGHT AXILLARY" (including REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aTwo (2) lymph nodes with no tumor present.\u000a(Levels examined).\u000aRIGHT BREAST, MASTECTOMY:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia, focal.\u000aPrior biopsy site with repair reaction.\u000aFocal epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aOne (1) lymph node with no tumor present.\u000aSkeletal muscle.\u000aSkin with scar.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "SUPERIOR PIECE OF BREAST", EXCISION:\u000aBenign breast tissue and skeletal muscle.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Cancer of right breast.\u000aOperation: Right breast mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Cancer of right breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Sentinel nodes, right axillary.\u000a2. Right breast.\u000a3. Superior piece of breast.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1 SENTINEL NODES RIGHT AXILLARY" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aTwo (2) lymph nodes, negative for tumor.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by YOU,MINGJIAN JAMES,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000asname and unit number.\u000aPart 1, "Sentinel nodes, right axillary", consists of two fragments of pink/tan\u000alymph nodes (1.2 cm in greatest dimension and REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension).\u000aThe larger lymph node was frozen as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and the smaller lymph node was frozen\u000aas REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro 1: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart 2, "Right breast skin and tissue", consists of a 193 gm mastectomy\u000aspecimen (15.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a white/tan skin ellipse (7.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThe upper middle portion of the breast has a semi-solid area (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) that was previously tatooed by the surgeon. This area is REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000askin surface and REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin. The remaining breast parenchyma\u000aconsist of approximately 60% of white/tan fibrous tissue and approximately 40%\u000aof yellow/tan adipose tissue. The skin, nipple (1.2 cm in diameter), and areola\u000a(2.2 cm in diamter) are grossly unremarkable. Grossly, no skeletal muscle is\u000aidentified. One pink/tan lymph node (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is identified and\u000asubmitted. No other lesions are identified in the specimen.\u000aMicro 3: One bisected lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Firm area and surrounding tatooed area, 6 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 13: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 14: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart 3, "Superior piece of breast", consists of a fragment of unoriented\u000awhite/yellow/tan soft tissue (6.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Superior breast tissue, 4 frags, ESS.\u000amjy\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
