VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANNE GEORGIAN-SMITH M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Justine A Barletta, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A\u000a1 CM PALPABLE IRREGULAR MASS:\u000aMinute fragments of normal breast tissue.\u000aNote: Specific histologic features of a mass forming lesion are not seen.\u000aRadiologic correlation is suggested to ensure the biopsy is representative of\u000athe targeted lesion.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 55 y o woman with palpable lump Lt breast; strong family history.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: ~ 1 cm, Palpable irregular mass.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: upper outer\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 14G Ultrasound\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 14G Ultrasound - Green cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "Left breast", and consists of multiple red-yellow to white\u000afibrofatty cores (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are received in a\u000agreen cassette. The specimens are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/4/2007\u000a[report_end]
