VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Elizabeth A. Steensma, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A PRIOR BIOPSY SITE MARKED BY A CLIP AND\u000aRESIDUAL CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (block 1; levels examined), associated with\u000acalcification.\u000aPrior core biopsy site with adjacent calcifications associated with normal\u000abreast epithelium.\u000aNOTE: The patient had a prior core needle biopsy for calcifications at Faulkner\u000aHospital that revealed ADH (Faulkner # REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). No carcinoma is seen in this\u000aspecimen after complete microscopic examination, including margins.\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. S. Lester, Breast Pathology Service, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left needle localized breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left breast mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast biopsy after needle loc. (long lateral - short superior).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aClip, calcs, 2 intact hookwires and (old) hematoma in specimen d/w Dr. DI by\u000aDr. M.N. 12:55 pm.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Left breast biopsy, after needle local; long lateral - short\u000asuperior", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm excision of fibroadipose\u000atissue, oriented by sutures designating superior (short suture) and lateral\u000a(long suture) margins. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange (inked by prosector). Two\u000alocalizing wires enter the superolateral aspect of the specimen and at least\u000aone of the wires exits the inferior/anterior medial aspect of the specimen.\u000aThe specimen is received with a radiograph demonstrating the localizing wires\u000ain place adjacent to a clip and a focus of calcifications. Sectioning\u000ademonstrates a central hematoma (at least REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with central\u000acavitation and chalky white fragments of foreign material compatible with\u000aGelfoam beads. The hematoma itself approaches within REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aclosest lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe closest medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest anterior margin. There\u000aare no obvious masses, lesions, or other abnormalities grossly. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted, sequentially from medial to lateral. The remaining\u000aspecimen is predominantly comprised of tan/yellow, focally hemorrhagic adipose\u000atissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sequentially from medial to lateral, with\u000aperpendicular medial margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and perpendicular lateral margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, multi frags, ESS.\u000aThe tissue of interest (tissue containing clip) is located in micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (section\u000awith clip) through approximately REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000adb/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/5/2007\u000a[report_end]
