VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST, TISSUE":\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, with pagetoid spread.\u000aIntraductal papilloma wiht epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia, florid, diffuse.\u000aCysts and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aNOTE: There is no invasive carcinoma or ductal carcinoma in situ present\u000a(including evaluation of margins).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of right nipple discharge and abnormal ductogram. Dr.\u000aDenison is concerned that abnormal ducts may be due to DCIS.\u000aOperation: Right mammographically-directed breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right nipple discharge and abnormal ductogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 - right breast tissue - short = superior, long = lateral.\u000aInked per pathology protocol.\u000aNOTE: Dr. Denison did not feel specimen mammogram would be helpful; therefore,\u000aspecimen mammogram was not done.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by RUCKER-SCHMIDT,RACHEL L.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "right breast tissue, short = superior, long = lateral", and\u000ais a breast needle localized excision specimen (6.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which\u000aincludes two sutures placed by the surgeon to designate the superior and\u000alateral orientation of the specimen. The specimen includes a needle\u000alocaliation wire; however, no radiograph is received with the specimen. The\u000aspecimen is received previously inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for\u000aevaluation of margins: red = superior, green = inferior, blue = anterior,\u000ablack = posterior, yellow = lateral, and orange = medial. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from inferior to superior to reveal no discrete mass.\u000aNumerous serous fluid-filled cysts (varying from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest\u000adimension) are present throughout the specimen. The cyst wall of the largest\u000acyst is smooth, shiny, without projections. The specimen is approximately 90%\u000afibrous tissue and 5% fatty tissue. Representative sections (approximately 40%\u000aof the specimen) are submitted for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro #1-2: Superior margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #3-4: Lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #5-6: Medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #7-8: Posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #9-10: Anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #11-12: Inferior margin, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #13-14: Additional representative sections, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
