VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1) RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A CLIP:\u000aRESIDUAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, present adjacent to a biopsy site.\u000aCalcifications are associated with ADH.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, multiple foci in multiple blocks.\u000aFibroadenoma.\u000aNOTE: No clip was identified in the tissue radiologically or after\u000apathologic examination.\u000aNo invasive carcinoma or DCIS is seen after microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen including margins.\u000a2) ANTERIOR SUPERIOR BREAST TISSUE, RIGHT:\u000aBreast tissue with no atypia or malignancy seen.\u000aNote: A clip was not identified in this specimen after radiologic and\u000apathologic examination.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 56-year-old female with right breast calcifications on mammo. REMOVED_DATE \u000acore biopsy showed ADH, ALH, fibroadenoma. Also status post right breast\u000abiopsy in 1996 showing a cellular fibroadenoma versus low grade phyllodes\u000atumor.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammo.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Mass right breast.\u000a2. Anterior superior breast tissue, right.\u000aRadiology for specimens #1 and #2: No clip.......J. Meyer, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMO,LESLEY C.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, mass right breast", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000apiece of soft tissue, which has been previously inked by the surgeon.\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen has a needle\u000alocalization wire, and two (2) sutures, long denoting lateral and short\u000adenoting superior. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely\u000afor analysis. A specimen radiograph is received which reveals a wire but no\u000alesions.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior perpendicular margins, 4 and 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast parenchyma sectioned serially from superior to inferior,\u000a1 or 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 13: inferior perpendicular margins, 8 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, anterior superior breast tissue, right", and consists of\u000amultiple pieces of yellow fibroadipose tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate,\u000athe largest fragment: REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is inked in black and\u000aentirely submitted for histologic analysis. A specimen radiograph is received\u000aand does not reveal any lesions.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right anterior superior breast tissue, 3 and 1 frags,\u000arespectively, ESS.\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
