VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Skin biopsy (other than cyst/tag/debrid/repair\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kevin B Long, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN LABELED "1. LEFT BREAST LESION":\u000aSkin with ulceration, pustule and abscess formation,\u000aacute and chronic inflammation, foreign body giant\u000acell reaction, and fibrosis.\u000aEpidermal inclusion cyst.\u000aB. SPECIMEN LABELED "2. RIGHT BREAST LESION (STITCH AT 12:00)":\u000aSkin with chronic inflammation, foreign body giant cell\u000areaction, fibrosis, and fresh dermal hemorrhage.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Non-healing lesions - right and left breast scans.\u000aOperation: Excision - 2 lesions.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Bilateral breast lesions.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Left breast lesion (stitch at 12:00).\u000a2. Right breast lesion (stitch at 12:00).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1 Left breast lesion", consists of a white/tan skin ellipse (2.7 x\u000a1.2 cm, excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm), oriented by a single suture (designated\u000a12:00). Located in the center of the ellipse is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, flat area of\u000agranular/hemorrhagic skin. The specimen is inked blue from 9:00 to 3:00, and\u000agreen from 3:00 to 9:00.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3:00 tip, en face, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 9:00 tip, en face, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross-sections, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2 Right breast lesion (stitch at 12:00)", consists of a white/tan\u000askin ellipse (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm, excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm), oriented by a single\u000asuture (designated 12:00). Located in the center of the ellipse is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm, hemorrhagic and focally crusted lesion, which extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe closest (9:00) radial margin. The specimen is inked blue from REMOVED_DATE 00, and\u000ait is inked green from REMOVED_DATE 00.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 12:00 tip, en face, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 6:00 tip, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross-sections, multiple frags, ESS.\u000akel/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Kevin B Long M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/17/2005\u000a[report_end]
