VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDILLON, DEBORAH, A, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by DILLON,DEBORAH A,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, LOWER INNER, 11 G ULTRASOUND-GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A\u000aSPICULATED MASS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA with ductal and lobular features, moderately\u000adifferentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson grade II/III) measuring at least\u000a0.3 cm in size in this limited specimen.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type, (low nuclear grade) is\u000afocally present.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by DILLON,DEBORAH A,M.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 1):\u000aEstrogen receptor - POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor - POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - NEGATIVE (0)\u000aNOTE: External control for Her2/neu shows appropriate membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 53-year-old female with mass, right lower inner quadrant.\u000aOperation: 11g ultrasound.\u000aOperative findings: Cores obtained.\u000aBreast Imaging Findings: Spiculated.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Carcinoma.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Cores in white cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHANG,BRIAN S.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "Right breast, in an unlabeled white cassette, and consists of\u000amultiple, soft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000almb\u000aReports to: FROST, ELISABETH, PEPPERELL M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
