VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a+1) SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY":\u000aBenign breast tissue with dense fibrosis and calcifications, and a\u000afibroadenoma.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000a2) RIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - No\u000aHistologic Type - Lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - I(Well)\u000aNuclear Grade - Low\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - Absent\u000aSkin invasion - Absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - Deep\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia\u000aFibroadenoma\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa pNX MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Pending\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 23):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 55 year old female with R breast cancer.\u000aOperation: Bilateral simple mastectomies, insertion of bilateral tissue\u000aexpanders.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 - left breast, stitch on axilla.\u000a#2 - right breast, stitch is lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SCHMIDT,JASON F.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aThe first, additionally designated "#1 - left breast stitch on axilla",\u000aconsists of a 97 gram simple mastectomy specimen (10.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There\u000ais an attached tan/pink skin ellipse (6.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an eccentrically\u000aplaced everted nipple (0.9 cm in diameter). No scars or lesions are noted on\u000athe skin surface. A single suture is present which is designated by the\u000asurgeon as axilla. The deep margin consists of a smooth glistening fascial\u000aplane which is inked black. The breast parenchyma is composed primarily of\u000atan/white fibrous tissue (approximately 80%). The remainder of the breast\u000aparenchyma consists of yellow lobulated adipose tisuse (approximately 20%). No\u000adiscrete lesions are identified. The tissue designated as axilla is\u000aextensively examined for possible lymph nodes, and no possible lymph nodes are\u000aidentified. Representative sections of the specimen are submitted for\u000amicroscopic examination.\u000aMicro #1-2: Upper/outer quadrant, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro #3-4: Lower/outer quadrant, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro #5-6: Upper/inner quadrant, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro #7-8: Lower/inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #9: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aThe second, additionally designated "#2 - right breast stitch is lateral",\u000aconsists of a 111 gram simple mastectomy specimen (13.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There\u000ais an attached tan/pink skin ellipse (6.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an eccentrically\u000aplaced everted nipple (1.3 cm in diameter). On the skin surface, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000asuperior/lateral to the nipple, there is a single curvilinear scar (0.7 cm in\u000alength). A single orienting suture designated axilla is present. The deep\u000amargin is composed of a smooth glistening fascial plane which is inked black.\u000aThe breast is primarily composed of rubbery tan/white fibrous tissue\u000a(approximately 90%). The remainder of the breast parenchyma is composed of\u000ayellow lobulated adipose tissue (approximately 10%). There is a focal area\u000adeep to the skin scar that may represent the prior excision site. No\u000adefinitive lesions are identified grossly. The tissue in the area designated\u000aaxilla is extensively examined for possible lymph nodes. A firm area (0.4 x\u000a0.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm) is present in the upper outer quadrant, but no definite lymph\u000anodes is identified. Representative sections of the specimen are submitted for\u000amicroscopic examination.\u000aMicro #10-11: Upper/outer quadrant, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro #12-13: Lower/outer quadrant, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro #14-15: Upper/inner quadrant, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro #16-17: Lower/inner quadrant, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro #18: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #19: Skin with possible scar, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #20-22: Possible prior excision site, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro #23: Firm area in upper outer quadant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #24-31: Remainder of the outer quadrants, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000ajfs/\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
