VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCONNOLLY, JAMES, L., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by CONNOLLY,JAMES L.,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1, RIGHT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, (seen on block 9, level 4 and block 6).\u000aCalcifications associated with benign breast tissue.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 53-year-old post menopausal female, not on hormones, with prior\u000aradiation treatment for Hodgkin's disease. REMOVED_DATE  mammogram\u000ademonstrates right superior 2 cm area of calcifications for which\u000abiopsy is recommended (not amenable to core biopsy).\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue, short stitch superior,\u000along stitch lateral and whipstitch deep margin.\u000aCalcifications in specimen. Dr. Smith\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by WU,DAVID,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1, right breast tissue", consists of a breast excision specimen (3.5 x\u000a4.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm), with multiple surgical sutures, long designating lateral and\u000ashort stitch desinating superior, whipstitch designating deep margin. The\u000aspecimen is previously inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green;\u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. In addition, there is a wire localizing\u000aareas of interest as demonstrated on a radiograph accompanying the specimen\u000afor which the radiograph reads calcifications in specimen. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from posterior to anterior to reveal a single continuous\u000apoorly circumscribed area of palpable nodularity (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aAdjacent to this area on the inferior portion is a foci of hemorrhage (0.3 x\u000a0.3 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The area of nodularity is about the lateral superior portion of\u000athe specimen. The areas of interest approach the lateral, inferior, posterior,\u000asuperior margins within less than REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is composed of 90%\u000aadipose tissue, 10% fibrous tissue. The entire (100%) specimen is submitted\u000afor microcscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  anterior margin, perpendicular, may appear green, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posterior margin, perpendicular, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  rest of the specimen submitted from anterior to posterior,\u000aincluding areas of interest, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000adwu\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
