 unit number, and\u000a"Right breast site #2, lateral", is a single, brown/tan cassette, labeled "A.\u000aCa++", which contains multiple, yellow/white fibrofatty soft tissue cores (1.8\u000aX REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "A. Ca++", multiple frags, ESS.\u000aDFI/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/4/2005\u000a[report_end]
