VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Matthias D. Hofer, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A PRIOR CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY SITE:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, adjacent to the core needle biopsy site.\u000aIntraductal papilloma, associated with the prior core needle biopsy site.\u000aNote: The patient underwent an MRI guided core needle biopsy at Faulkner\u000aHospital that showed an intraductal papilloma involved by ADH (reviewed as\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). The findings in the excision are similar to those in the core\u000abiopsy.\u000aNo malignancy is seen after complete microscopic examined of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, who concurs with this\u000ainterpretation.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: ADH, right breast.\u000aOperation: Localized excision.\u000aOperative Findings: See op note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Preop: ADH.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Tissue, right breast - to mammo at 12:33.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aIntact wire, clip and density are within the specimen. Dr. Eva Gombos.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen was received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit\u000anumber, and "#1. Tissue, right breast". Specimen is accompanied by a\u000aradiograph showing a central density with a clip, traversed by the localization\u000awire. The specimen is received pre-inked and consists of a wire localized\u000abreast excision specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE cm (S-I) x REMOVED_DATE cm (A-P) x REMOVED_DATE cm (M-L).\u000aA wire is identified that enters the specimen in the superior/lateral aspect.\u000aThe specimen is sectioned serially from anterior to posterior into seven slices\u000a(slice #1 equals anterior aspect, slice #7 equals posterior aspect). In the\u000acenter of the specimen is an area of hemorrhage visible measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm,\u000alocalized REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin and approximately REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the posterior and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin. This cavity is best\u000aseen in slice #4. Adjacent to this cavity, most prominent in slice #3 and\u000aslice #4 is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm area of tan/yellow slightly firm tissue. This area\u000acomes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin,\u000a0.6 cm of the lateral margin and REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial margin. The clip is\u000arecovered in slice #4. The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic\u000areview.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #1, perpendicular sections, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, perpendicular sections, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: 8899.\u000aMDH/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
