VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: LORRAINE B. SMITH MB,BCH,BAO\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Qinghong Yang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST UPPER OUTER 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aCalcification associated with a dilated duct with associated mucin production,\u000aand calcification present in mucin pools in stroma, see NOTE.\u000aNOTE: One core fragment contains a pool of mucin within the stromal tissue with\u000aassociated large calcifications. Another core fragment shows a benign mucin\u000aproducing dilated duct with associated large calcification. Although the\u000afindings likely represent an area of ruptured mucinous cysts, a more\u000asignificant mucinous lesion cannot be excluded in this limited biopsy given the\u000apresence of mucin pools in stroma. Excision of the area should be considered.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 51 year old with cluster of calcifications in upper/outer left breast.\u000aIn formalin at 10:15.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: 5 mm, non-palpable and calcifications.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: upper/outer.\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 11G Ultrasound.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast core biopsy tissue in two pink cassettes - A/with calcs abd\u000aB/no calcs,\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in one part, labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number, and "left breast", and consists of two pink cassettes. The\u000afirst pink cassette, labeled "A", contains multiple cylindrical focally\u000ahemorrhagic fibrofatty soft tissues (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The\u000asecond pink cassette is labeled "B", contains multiple cylindrical focally\u000ahemorrhagic fibrofatty soft tissues (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is\u000asubmitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of pink cassette labeled "A", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of pink cassette labeled "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000ajc/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aMonday August 10, 2009 at 03:50:20PM\u000a[report_end]
