hagic fibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.3 cm), which are received in five white cassettes with pink top. The\u000aspecimens are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with pink top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with pink top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with pink top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with pink top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with pink top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "blue top/white bottom - left breast", consists of multiple\u000ayellow-white focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.3 cm), which are received in three white cassettes with blue top. The\u000aspecimens are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with blue top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with blue top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with blue top, multi frags, ESS.\u000acp/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aFriday REMOVED_MONTH 26, 2009 at 04:03:33PM\u000a[report_end]
