r", consists of an irregular tan/pink fibrofatty tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm) with a whip stitch marking the new margin. The sutured aspect is\u000ablack inked and the remainder of the specimen is blue inked. Sectioning\u000areveals unremarkable fibrous (50%) and fatty (50%) tissue. Also received in\u000athe same container is an irregular unoriented white skin (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm excised\u000ato a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm), which is inked and submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Right breast medial shave margin whip stitch new margin",\u000aconsists of an irregular tan/pink fibrofatty tissue (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which\u000adisplays a whip stitch marking the new margin. Defect is black inked and the\u000aremainder of the specimen is blue inked. Sectioning reveals unremarkable\u000afibrous (40%) and fatty (60%) tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000almc/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 17, 2009 at 05:56:51PM\u000a[report_end]
