VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Skin biopsy (other than cyst, tag, debrid or repair\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ABRAR A QURESHI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Samuel P. Wyche, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Elsa F. Velazquez, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SKIN, LEFT BREAST, PUNCH:\u000a- Ulcer with acute suppurative dermal infiltrate.\u000a- Gram stain reveals scattered Gram-positive cocci. No fungi are seen with\u000aPAS-D and MSS stains. AFB is negative for mycobacteria.\u000a- Immunostains for HSV I/II and VZV are negative.\u000aAltogether, we favor an infectious etiology and cultures are recommended.\u000aA differential diagnosis includes pyoderma gangrenosum.\u000aThere are no features of calciphylaxis in this biopsy (no calcium\u000adeposition seen with a Von Kossa stain). However, the subcutaneous\u000atissue is not well represented in this biopsy. If the clinical suspicion\u000aof calciphylaxis persists, a deeper biopsy is advised.\u000aDr. Hollmann contacted Dr. Ibrahimi with the preliminary results on REMOVED_DATE \u000aCase reviewed at Dermatopathology Division Staff Conference.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 64-year-old female ESRD on HD, multiple atypical breast bx, has ulcers\u000aon bilateral breasts.\u000aOperation: 4-mm Punch.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Calciphylaxis vs Paget's vs infectious vs other.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Skin: L breast (peri-ulcer)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit\u000anumber only, and consists of REMOVED_DATE cm diameter x REMOVED_DATE cm depth variably pigmented\u000alight tan to dark brown circular skin, inked and bisected.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Elsa F. Velazquez M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 24, 2009 at 09:52:29AM\u000a[report_end]
