VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Vijay K Vanguri, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA: LEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, multiple foci (multiple levels examined).\u000aCalcium oxylate is present in apocrine cysts.\u000aNo calcifications are associated with atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aB: LEFT SUPERIOR BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aSEVERLY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA BORDERING ON DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU,\u000acribriform type (low nuclear grade) with focal single cell necrosis, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afocus (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000a(Multiple levels examined).\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, multiple foci.\u000aCalcium oxylate is present in apocrine cysts.\u000aNo calcifications are associated with atypical ductal hyperplasia or severe\u000aatypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aThe focus of severely atypical ductal hyperplasia is less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainferior margin with cautery artifact in atypical cells.\u000aNOTE: A re-excision of the inferior margin is recommended to exclude a larger,\u000amore severe lesion. Case was also reviewed with Dr. A. Richardson (of Breast\u000aPathology Service), who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Status post reduction mammoplasty x 20 years. New calcifications in\u000atwo sites.\u000aOperation: Left needle breast biopsy x 2.\u000aOperative Findings:\u000aClinical Diagnosis:\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Left breast inferior - short superior, long lateral.\u000a2. Left breast tissue superior - short superior, long lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aCalcifications in specimen #1, calcifications in specimen #2.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "Left breast inferior, short-superior, long-lateral", consists of a\u000awire localized excision of breast tissue (4.3 cm from superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from medial to lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior) with two\u000aorienting sutures (short-superior, long-lateral) and an embedded localization\u000awire. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. An accompanying radiograph demonstrates an\u000aembedded localization wire adjacent to a cluster of calcifications. Wire\u000alocalized sections are in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Sectioning reveals an ill-defined\u000aare of fibrous tissue (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with no obvious lesions.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aPart B, "Left breast superior tissue, short-superior, long-lateral", consists\u000aof a wire localized excision of breast tissue (3.5 cm from superior to\u000ainferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior)\u000awith two orienting sutures (short-superior, long-lateral) and an embedded\u000alocalization wire. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. An accompanying radiograph\u000ademonstrates an embedded localization distant from a cluster of calcifications.\u000aSectioning reveals no focal lesions, with unremarkable fibrofatty tissue (0.8 x\u000a0.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm), with no obvious lesions.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 frags, ESS.\u000aVIV/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Vijay K Vanguri M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aPrelim Dx Release by Vijay K Vanguri M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aNo Action - Prelim Sent by Vijay K Vanguri M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/6/2005\u000a[report_end]
