VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Tanya Rege, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Robert D Odze, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aBenign breast tissue with apocrine change, adenosis, and calcifications\u000aassociated with benign epithelium.\u000aCore biopsy site is present.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 51-year-old perimenopausal woman S/P REMOVED_DATE  R breast core Bx's\u000arevealing ADH - Exc. recommended.\u000aOperation: R breast wire-loc bx.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast tissue; short stitch - superior; long stitch - lateral;\u000amammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip, calcs, + intact wire are in the specimen. Dr. Yeh spoke with\u000aDr. Rhei in OR 12:20 p.m./EY.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name and\u000amedical record number, and "#1. Right breast tissue, short stitch superior,\u000along stitch lateral", and consists of one REMOVED_DATE g breast excision (3.8 cm\u000asuperior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm medial to\u000alateral), oriented with a short stitch designated superior and a long stitch\u000adesignated lateral. The specimen is received previously inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A localization\u000awire is present which enters the anterior aspect of the specimen and exits the\u000aposterior aspect. An accompanying radiograph demonstrates a clip, wire, and\u000acalcifications. A biopsy cavity with a clip (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is present at\u000athe superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ato the lateral margin. The breast parenchyma is approximately 90% white/tan\u000aand fibrotic and 10% yellow/tan and fatty. No additional lesions are\u000aidentified. The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast excision, medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE frags each. The clipped\u000abiopsy site is present in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on Thursday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 09, 2009 at 12:46:18PM\u000aADDENDUM:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aThe final diagnosis remains unchanged.\u000aAddendum #1 by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH\u000a28, 2009 at 02:22:19PM\u000a[report_end]
