VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Paula C Abreu-e-Lima, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A PALPABLE MASS (INCLUDING FROZEN SECTION):\u000aIntraductal papillomas with atypia (blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) (see note).\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies show a well developed myoepithelial cell layer within\u000athe papillomas.\u000aNote: The patient had a palpable breast mass that correlated with a\u000a0.6 cm grossly evident lesion. The palpable mass correlates microscopically\u000awith an area of intraductal papillomas. Although the cell population appears\u000amonomorphic and there are thin fibrovascular cores, the presence of a well\u000adeveloped myoepithelial cell layer favors classification as a papilloma with\u000aatypia rather than carcinoma in situ.\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Andrea Richardson who concurs with this\u000ainterpretation.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, INFERIOR MARGIN:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aNote: No intraductal papillomas are seen.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, SUPERIOR MARGIN:\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aNote: No intraductal papillomas are seen.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, MEDIAL MARGIN:\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aNote: No intraductal papillomas are seen.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, LATERAL MARGIN:\u000aFocal secretory changes.\u000aNote: No intraductal papillomas are seen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast mass.\u000aOperation: Right breast excisional biopsy wide local excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right breast tissue with palpable mass (fs @ 9:18).\u000aB/2) right new inferior margin adjacent to right breast.\u000aC/3) new right superior margin.\u000aD/4) new medial right.\u000aE/5) new right lateral.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1 - RIGHT BREAST TISSUE WITH PALPABLE MASS" (FSA):\u000aPapillary lesion, best evaluated on permanent sections.\u000aOR Consultation by: SUSAN LESTER, M.D., PH.D.\u000aResident: PATRICIA A. R. BRUNKER, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in five parts, each labeled with the patients\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A is received fresh in the frozen section lab, labeled "#1 - right breast\u000atissue with palpable mass", and consists of a portion of fibroadipose tissue\u000a(4.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is received previously inked by the surgeon\u000aaccording to the pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange (please note, sutures are not present on the specimen and\u000adefinitive blue ink (anterior margin) is not grossly identifiable). The\u000aspecimen is sectioned in the frozen section lab, revealing a tan/white, well\u000acircumscribed nodule (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with surrounding fibrosis, which\u000agrossly abuts the green inked margin (probable inferior margin), REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000aposterior margin (black ink), REMOVED_DATE cm of the nearest medial margin (orange ink),\u000a1.7 cm of the nearest superior margin (red ink), and REMOVED_DATE cm of the nearest\u000alateral margin (yellow ink). A representative section of the nodule is frozen\u000aas FSA. The remaining tissue consists predominantly of pale yellow adipose\u000atissue and scant tan/white fibrous stroma. No other gross lesions are\u000aidentified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSA remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: remaining non-frozen breast tissue, sequentially from medial\u000ato lateral with remaining lesion in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, multiple\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2 - R new inferior margin adjacent to right breast", and\u000aconsists of a portion of previously inked fibroadipose tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), which is inked black on one surface and green on the opposing surface. No\u000asutures are identified. The tissue is serially sectioned revealing\u000apredominantly dense tan/white fibrous stroma and scant pale yellow adipose\u000atissue. There is a moderate amount of pale yellow, friable substance exuding\u000afrom the ducts. No other gross lesions are identified. The entire specimen is\u000aexamined microscopically.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "#3 - new R superior margin", and consists of a portion of\u000apreviously inked irregular fibroadipose tissue (4.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000aspecimen is received inked red along one surface and black upon the opposing\u000asurface. The tissue is serially sectioned revealing predominantly tan/white,\u000adense fibrous stroma admixed with scant pale yellow lobulated adipose tissue.\u000aA pale yellow, friable substance exudes from the fibrous stroma. No other\u000agross lesions are identified. The entire specimen is examined microscopically.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: breast tissue, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart D, labeled "#4 - new medial R", and consists of a disrupted, previously\u000ainked portion of fibroadipose tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is\u000ainked yellow along one surface and black upon the opposing surface. The tissue\u000ais serially sectioned revealing a predominantly tan/white, dense fibrous stroma\u000awith scant pale yellow fibroadipose tissue. No definitive lesions are\u000aidentified grossly. The entire specimen is examined microscopically.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: breast tissue, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart E, labeled "#5 - new R lateral", and consists of an irregular portion of\u000alobulated fibroadipose tissue (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is inked orange along\u000aone surface and black upon the opposing surface. The tissue is sectioned\u000arevealing a predominantly pale yellow, lobulated adipose tissue with scant\u000afibrous stroma. No gross lesions are identified. The entire specimen is\u000aexamined microscopically.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID+REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: breast tissue, multiple frags, ESS.\u000adfi/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Paula C Abreu-e-Lima M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aPrelim Dx Release by Paula C Abreu-e-Lima M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aResident Review by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a3/7/2006\u000a[report_end]
