VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: RAYMOND J REILLY MB,BCH,BAO\u000aCASE: BG-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Li Chen, M.D., Ph.D.; Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aColumnar cell change with associated microcalcifications.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aSclerosing adenosis with associated microcalcifications.\u000aNote: There is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the entire\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 65 year old female with atypical ductal hyperplasia on breast core\u000abiopsy.\u000aOperation: Left needle localized breast mass excision.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: Abundant residual calcifications. Marked on specimen\u000aradiograph. Called to Dr. Reilly in OR.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Left breast mass, short at 12:00, long at 9:00\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in one part, labeled with the patient's name and\u000amedical record number.\u000aPart A, "left breast mass; short 12 o'clock, long 9 o'clock." consists of a\u000asingle fragment of fibroadipose tissue oriented with two sutures; the short\u000adesignating 12 o'clock, the long designating 9 o'clock. Based on the\u000aorientation of the specimen as "left", "12:00" is interpreted as superior, and\u000a"9:00" is interpreted as medial. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE \u000a(medial to lateral) x REMOVED_DATE (superior to inferior) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior).\u000aOn the accompanying specimen radiograph, the specimen contains a localization\u000awire, dense calcifications, and a clip. The specimen is received with the wire\u000aremoved.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from medial (slice 1) to lateral (slice 9)\u000ainto nine slides. There is a REMOVED_DATE cm hemorrhagic area adjacent to fibrous\u000atissue in slice 4. The remainder of the tissue consists of 50% fibrous tissue\u000aand 50% adipose tissue, that is entirely submitted in serial sections.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicular sections, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slices REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BG-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/5/2007\u000a[report_end]
