VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Derek K Marsee, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION:\u000aNo residual carcinoma identified including examination of margins.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid extension.\u000aDuctal hyperplasia with extensive duct ectasia.\u000aAdenosis.\u000aBiopsy site changes with foreign body giant cell reaction\u000aand fat necrosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 80 year old woman with DCIS on wire-localized excisional biopsy for\u000acalcifications.\u000aOperation: Right re-excision partial mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1 - right breast re-excision, short suture/superior, long suture/medial.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "#1 - right breast re-excision, short suture/superior, long suture/medial",\u000aand consists of a portion of fibrofatty breast tissue (3.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with\u000aa short designating "superior", and a long suture designating "medial". There\u000ais a red/tan, smooth, focally hemorrhagic/necrotic cavity (2.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aopening to and communicating with the anterolateral margins. The specimen is\u000ainked according to the breast pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior.\u000aThe aforementioned cavity grossly extends to the lateral and anterior margins,\u000acomes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the nearest medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior and\u000ainferior margins, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin. A gray/white, cystic,\u000aill-defined area (2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is present at the inferior aspect of the\u000acavity, grossly extending to the inferior, medial, anterior margins, and coming\u000ato within REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm of the superior margin. The remaining breast tissue consists of\u000apredominantly golden yellow lobulated fat with scant fibrous stroma. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted sequentially from superior to inferior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: breast tissue, sequentially from superior to inferior,\u000agray/white ill-defined lesional tissue in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, multiple\u000afrags, ESS.\u000adfi/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Derek K Marsee M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
