VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DAVID I SOYBEL M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Anna Laury, M.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS":\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Solid, cribriform, and clinging\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Inferior, superior, medial\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - Posterior (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, focal)\u000aVery close(<0.1 cm from margin)- Lateral (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aPositive (ink on carcinoma) - Anterior (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aPapilloma\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Pending\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Microcalcifications L breast.\u000aOperation: Not provided.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left breast lumpectomy (stitch: short/superior, long/lateral), to mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aIntact wire and calcifications are in specimen. Reviewed by Dr. Peters, Dr.\u000aOei. Dr. Whitener was called in the OR by Dr. Tamara Oei @ 3:50 pm 0m\u000a10/18/2007.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. Left breast lumpectomy, short superior, long lateral", and consists of\u000aan ovoid fragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (4.7 M - L x REMOVED_DATE S - I x\u000a2.5 A - P cm) which exhibits two sutures per surgeon: Short equals superior\u000aand long equals lateral. Adherent to the anteromedial aspect of the specimen\u000ais a tan granular skin ellipse (1.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm) through which enters a\u000aneedle-localization wire. The wire tip is embedded within the specimen, with\u000ano clear exit site. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen was\u000apreviously radiographed, confirming the presence of an intact wire and\u000acalcification within the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned from\u000alateral to medial. In the lateral aspect of the specimen, around the\u000aneedle-localization wire tip, is an ill-defined gritty yellow/tan firm lesion\u000a(1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) corresponding to the area of calcifications as seen on the\u000aaccompanying radiograph. The ill-defined lesion is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, and\u000a1.9 cm from the medial margin. The remainder of the cut surface is composed of\u000ayellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue with minimal delicate white/tan fibrous\u000astroma. The specimen is entirely sequentially submitted from lateral to\u000amedial.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central specimen from lateral to medial (ill-defined\u000agritty lesion corresponding to calcifications in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin to include skin ellipse perpendicularly sectioned,\u000amulti frags, ESS.\u000alm/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (10/25/07):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) WEAKLY POSITIVE (EQUIVOCAL) (2+)\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
