VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROBERT T OSTEEN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Paula C Abreu-e-Lima, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION, WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR A CLIP MARKING AN AREA OF\u000aBIOPSIED CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, micropapillary and cribriform types\u000a(low nuclear grade) present in twelve of fifteen (12:15) blocks\u000a(likely measuring at least 4 cm). No necrosis or calcifications are associated\u000awith DCIS.\u000aDCIS is very close (< REMOVED_DATE cm) to the superior and medial margins, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and > REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior and inferior margins.\u000aPrevious core biopsy site changes are present.\u000aNOTE: Immunoperoxidase studies will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aThis carcinoma would be classified as AJCC (6th Edition): Tis NX MX.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Right needle directed wide excisional breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Right breast mass - FS mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aClip and wire are within the specimen. Dr. Gombos.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "#1 Right breast mass", and consists of 5 x 4 x 2 cm fibrofatty tissue\u000afragment, received previously inked per surgeon per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins, as follows: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is\u000areceived with a radiograph showing localizing wire and surgical clip in place\u000awithin the specimen (localizing wire enters inferiorly and extends superiorly\u000awithin the specimen). Sectioning in the area of the localizing wire\u000ahead/surgical clip demonstrates a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, hemorrhagic cavity with\u000asurrounding fat necrosis, REMOVED_DATE cm from closest anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from closest\u000ainferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from closest posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from closest medial, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom closest lateral, and is remote from the superior margin. The surrounding\u000atan/white fibrous tissue is dense and granular without definitive lesions\u000aidentified, and radiates from the cavity to the anterior and medial margins.\u000aRemaining specimen is predominantly soft, lobulated, tan/yellow adipose (60%)\u000awith associated tan/white fibrous tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Submitted sequentially (tissue surrounding localizing wire head,\u000aclip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), ESS.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Paula C Abreu-e-Lima M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/6/2005\u000aFIRST SURGICAL ADDENDUM REMOVED_DATE  DR. DEBORAH DILLON\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) POSITIVE (2+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
