VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST MASS":\u000aBreast tissue with abundant adipose tissue, small sclerosed fibroadenoma\u000aand focal fat necrosis.\u000aCalcifications associated with breast epithelium.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 71 year old female with breast cancer in left breast.\u000aOperation: Breast biopsy with needle localization\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast mass - long stitch deep, medium stitch\u000asuperior, short stitch inferior\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KINDELBERGER,DAVID W.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen, received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and\u000a"left breast mass (short stitch inferior, long deep, medium superior), consists\u000aof a single fragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (6.5 cm medial to\u000alateral by REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior by REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior). There\u000aare three black surgical sutures placed by the surgeon for orientation, such\u000athat the long stitch marks the deep margin, the short stitch marks the inferior\u000amargin and the medium stitch marks the superior margin. A metal localizing\u000awire was submitted separately with the specimen, but was not embedded in the\u000abreast tissue. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange and serially sectioned. No nodules,\u000aareas of hemorrhage or other lesions are grossly identified. The breast is\u000acomposed of approximately 60% adipose tissue and 40% fibrous tissue.\u000aAn accompanied radiogram of the specimen shows a localizing wire, presumably\u000aembedded in the specimen and a single focus of calcification away from the\u000alocalizing wire.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - left breast mass, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: SOYBEL, DAVID, IRA M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
