VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGRANTER, SCOTT, R., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GRANTER,SCOTT R.,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR AN MRI ENHANCING LESION AT THE SITE OF\u000aA PRIOR EXCISION:\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia associated with complex sclerosing lesion.\u000aNodular focus of granulation tissue and fibrosis with hemosiderin (0.7 cm)\u000aconsistent with prior biopsy site.\u000aCase reviewed by Dr. Lester, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 69 year old female s/p REMOVED_DATE excision of mammographic architectural\u000adistortion. MRI (12/6/01) with persistence of a 9 mm retroareolar mass.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localization excision\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left abnormal mammogram\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Tissue from left breast (short suture/superior; long\u000asuture/lateral)\u000aRADIOLOGY: This is an MRI only lesion. JL.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BROWNE,TARA-JANE,MB,BCH,BAO\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. tissue from left breast", and consists of an oriented\u000aportion of fibroadipose tissue (3.5 x 3 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an ellipse of skin on\u000athe anterior surface (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) which contains a central linear scar (2\u000acm). There is one long and one suture attached to the skin ellipse to\u000adesignate lateral and superior respectively. A localization wire is in place.\u000aThe specimen is received inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Also received with the specimen is\u000aa specimen radiograph which is reported as "this is an MRI only lesion" and\u000ademonstrates a localization wire in the center of the specimen, the skin\u000aellipse, and a central, stellate opacity surrounding the wire. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned at 3 mm intervals from medial to lateral to reveal tissue\u000awhich is 80% normal lobulated adipose tissue and 10% firm white fibrotic\u000atissue. A cavity (0.4 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm) is present in the posterior superior\u000aportion of the specimen, and has a hemorrhagic wall and adjacent hemorrhage and\u000afat necrosis in the soft tissue. There are no lesions suspicious for invasive\u000acarcinoma grossly. The specimen is entirely submitted in series from medial to\u000alateral for histological examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, 12 frags, ESS\u000aeab\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
