VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Agoston Tony Agoston, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA (see NOTE).\u000aFibroadenoma (0.6 cm) associated with core biopsy site changes.\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aCalcifications associated with cysts & columnar cell change.\u000aPseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia, focal.\u000aNOTE: An E-cadherin immunostain performed highlights absent membrane staining\u000ain the atypical lobular cells. The margins were inked and evaluated for the\u000afinal diagnosis.\u000aRIGHT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aSEVERELY ATYPICAL COLUMNAR CELL CHANGE, associated with necrosis and\u000amicrocalcifications (see NOTE).\u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA\u000aAn E-cadherin immunostain performed highlights absent membrane staining in the\u000aatypical lobular cells.\u000aColumnar cell change and florid epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aNOTE: The atypical focus measures REMOVED_DATE cm within an area of columnar cell change\u000aand shows a clinging proliferation, with marked nuclear atypia, central lumen\u000anecrosis and microcalcifications. This area appears to be the targeted lesion\u000aand is located < REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest medial margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). An adjacent area\u000aof DCIS cannot be excluded. Dr. S. Lester also reviewed the slides and agrees\u000awith the diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Non palp mass, lt with ADH/micro calcs, lt micro calcs, rt/breasts.\u000aOperation: Wire direct excision.\u000aOperative Findings: See op note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Micro calcs lt & rt.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Tissue, lt. breast, wire has a double bend at the end, short suture\u000asuperior, long lateral - mammo.\u000aB/2. Tissue, rt. breast, short suture superior, long suture lateral - mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000a1. 2 wires, few calcifications, 1 clip are contained in the specimen. Called\u000aOR. Georgian-Smith.\u000a2. Intact wire, Ca++ are in specimen. Georgian-Smith.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and medical\u000arecord number, and consists of two parts.\u000aPart A, "#1. Tissue, left breast", consists of a wire-localized breast excision\u000a(2.0 cm SI, REMOVED_DATE cm ML, REMOVED_DATE cm AP) that is oriented with a short suture\u000adesignating superior and a long suture designating lateral. The specimen is\u000areceived with a radiograph which demonstrates two wires, a clip and an area of\u000acalcifications in it. Within the specimen, there are two wires noted, wire #1\u000ahas a double bend and enters anterolaterally and exits anteromedially near a\u000aclip as designated by the radiograph. Wire #2 has a corkscrew bend and enters\u000aposterolaterally and exits posteromedially near calcifications as demonstrated\u000aby radiograph. There is a firm white fibrotic area (2.0 cm SI, REMOVED_DATE cm ML, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm AP) between the two wires abutting the superior, inferior, medial, anterior\u000aand posterior margins, and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. Wire #1 has an\u000aassociated core biopsy site. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for\u000athe evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, 4 frags per block, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serially sectioned specimen from anterior to posterior, 1 frag\u000aper block, ESS. Note: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID contains slices near wire #1 and core biopsy\u000asite, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID contains sections near wire #2.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE frags per block, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Tissue, right breast", consists of a wire-localized excision (3.3\u000acm SI, REMOVED_DATE cm ML, REMOVED_DATE cm AP) that is oriented with a short suture designating\u000asuperior and a long suture designating lateral. The specimen is received with\u000aa radiograph which demonstrates a wire and an area of calcifications in it. The\u000aspecimen has a wire that enters laterally and exits medially. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins as follows:\u000aRed/superior, green/inferior, orange/medial, yellow/lateral, black/anterior,\u000aand blue/posterior. There is a firm white fibrotic area (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000athat abuts the medial, anterior, posterior and inferior margins, and is REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the lateral and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margins.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serially sectioned specimen from inferior to superior, REMOVED_DATE frags\u000aper block, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aNote: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID contains slices near wire.\u000aTA/ajb/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/25/2008\u000a[report_end]
