VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-10-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Vinodh Pillai, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR AN ABNORMAL MAMMOGRAM:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, extensive, see NOTE.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aCalcifications in normal epithelium.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aNote: The specimen is predominantly adipose tissue. Per LMR, the mammographic\u000alesion of interest is a REMOVED_DATE cm lobular mass in the upper inner quadrant and a\u000adefinite histological correlate of this is not clearly identified (specimen\u000aentirely submitted for histological evaluation). Radiologic correlation is\u000aadvised to ensure the biopsy is representative of the radiologic lesion.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 59 year-old post menopausal female not on hormones who's sister had\u000ainflammatory breast cancer in her 50's. Screening mmg REMOVED_DATE  demonstrates a\u000aLLIQ focal asymmetry with ultrasound correlate wire localized excision is\u000arecommended\u000aOperation: L breast wire localized biopsy\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal L mammogram\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA. Left breast tissue - short suture superior, long suture lateral, whip stitch\u000adeep margin\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "left breast tissue short suture superior, long suture lateral, whipstitch\u000adeep margin", consists of an oriented portion of fibrofatty tissue that\u000ameasures as follows; REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to\u000alateral and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior dimension. Specimen is received\u000apreviously inked per pathology protocol as follows; anterior blue, posterior\u000ablack, superior red, inferior green, lateral yellow and medial orange.\u000aSpecimen is received with a needle localization wire that enters the specimen\u000asuperior laterally and does not exit the specimen. The specimen radiograph\u000areviewed on Centricity image displays diffuse areas of dense white fibrous\u000atissue surrounding the widened portion of the needle localization wire.\u000aSpecimen is serially sectioned perpendicular to the long axis from superior to\u000ainferior. Sectioning reveals glistening yellow/tan homogeneous lobulated\u000aadipose tissue with a minimal amount of diffuse white fibrous tissue. A\u000adiscrete mass, lesion or nodule is not noted grossly. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin of resection taken perpendicularly, 2 frags\u000aper cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sections through the mid portion of the specimen moving from\u000ainferior to superior, 1 frag per cassette, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections of the area of diffuse dense white\u000afibrous tissue on the radiograph, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections through the mid portion of the\u000aspecimen moving towards the superior margin, 1 frag per cassette, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin of resection taken perpendicularly, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining breast parenchyma, multi frags, ESS\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aPDF/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 02, 2010 at 11:02:10AM\u000a[report_end]
