 inferior\u000ato superior, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral) and\u000aextends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm of the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral margin. There are two possible tan/brown lymph nodes in the lateral\u000amargin of the resection.\u000aMicro 1: Right breast deep margin with fibrous tissue, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Fibrous tissue, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 4: Superior outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 5: Inferior outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 6: Superior inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 7: Inferior inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 8: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 9: Two lymph nodes, 2 frags, ESS\u000aPart 2, "L breast - short superior long lateral", consists of a 510 gm left\u000asimple mastectomy specimen (22 x 15 x REMOVED_DATE ) with a white/tan skin ellipse (20.7\u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm) without an attached axillary tail. The areola measure REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000adiameter and the nipple measures REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter and REMOVED_DATE cm in length. There\u000ais a scar (1.1 cm) above the nipple, along the areola, from 9:00 to 12:00.\u000aThere is a biopsy cavity noted deep to the areola scar (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE c REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThe cavity is REMOVED_DATE cm form the deep margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the inferior margin, 7 cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral margin, and 1 cm from the anterior skin. REMOVED_DATE cm inferior to the biopsy\u000acavity is a firm nodular area (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aMicro 10: Inferior border of biopsy cavity, including firm, nodular area, 1\u000afrag, RSS\u000aMicro 11: Deep border of biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 12: Superior border of biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 13: Anterior border of biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 14: Lateral border of biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 15: Medial border of bipsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 16: Biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 17: Deep margin deep to cavity, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 18: Nodular firm area, 1 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 19: Superior outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 20: Inferior outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 21: Superior inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 22: Inferior inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 23: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
