VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000a1) SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT SIMPLE MASTECTOMY":\u000aFibrocystic changes including apocrine metaplasia.\u000aFocal ductal hyperplasia.\u000aHealing prior biopsy cavity.\u000aNOTE: No residual atypical ductal hyperplasia identified. There is no evidence\u000aof malignancy.\u000a2) SPECIMEN LABELED "MASTECTOMY SKIN, LEFT BREAST":\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: L simple mastectomy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. L simple mastectomy. Short stitch superior, long stitch\u000aaxillary tail.\u000a2. Mastectomy skin, L breast.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by ABBOTT,DEREK W,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, medical record\u000anumber in two parts.\u000aPart one, "left simple mastectomy, received is a 223-gram simple mastectomy\u000aspecimen (16.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with skin (4.9 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and nipple (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm). The deep surface of the specimen contains a smooth fascial plane\u000awith a small fragment of skeletal muscle (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The deep\u000asurface also contains an opened biopsy cavity (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and is\u000ainterpreted to be a fascial defect but not a deep margin. The fascial plane\u000aincluding the skeletal muscle is inked in black and the specimen is serially\u000asectioned to reveal the aforementioned biopsy cavity with area suspicious for\u000afat necrosis. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal multicystic breast.\u000aThere a single REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm area of nodularity in the upper inner\u000aquadrant. No other areas of gross pathology are appreciated. The entire\u000abiopsy cavity is sampled and generous sections are taken from the remainder of\u000athe breast.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  entire biopsy cavity including deep margin, REMOVED_DATE frags each\u000acassette, ESS.\u000aMicro 10: area of nodularity in the upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: additional section from inner upper quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections from the lower inner quadrant, 1 frag,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro 14&15: representative sections from the upper outer quadrant, 1 frag\u000aeach cassette, RSS.\u000aMicro 16&17: representative sections from the lower outer quadrant, 1 frag\u000aeach cassette, RSS.\u000aMicro 18: nipple, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 19: skin with scar, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart two, "mastectomy skin, left breast", received are four fragments of skin\u000aand underlying soft cutaneous tissue (6.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro 20: skin from mastectomy site, 3 frags, RSS.\u000adwa\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000a[report_end]
