VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Consult material\u000aProcedure Date:\u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Stephanie Schulte, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM NASHOBA VALLEY MEDICAL CENTER, AYER, MA:\u000aLEFT BREAST, STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR CALCIFICATIONS (09:REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID;\u000a2/18/09):\u000aSeverely ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA bordering on low-grade DCIS, with\u000aassociated calcifications (see note).\u000aNOTE: Two atypical foci with low-grade nuclear features are present, each\u000ameasuring approximately REMOVED_DATE cm. One focus shows cribriform features. The other\u000ashows a more solid architecture. Based on the limited sizes of the foci and\u000adifferences in histologic appearance, classification as atypical ductal\u000ahyperplasia is favored. Slides also seen by Dr. Susan Lester, who concurs.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is best classified following excision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast mass w/Ca++\u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aConsult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived from Nashoba Valley Medical Center, Pathology Department, 200 Groton\u000aRoad, Ayer, MA REMOVED_DATE  are ten (10) glass slides.\u000aThe slides are labeled "09:REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "1 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "1 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID"", "2 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through\u000a"2 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID","REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/6"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and "NEG", corresponding to a left breast core\u000abiopsies 1) with calcifications (2.0 X REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE cm) 2) remaining tissue (1.3 x\u000a0.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology\u000areport bearing the patient's name.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 03, 2009 at 08:54:20PM\u000a[report_end]
