VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Oname O. Burlingame, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP MARKING A PRIOR CORE NEEDLE\u000aBIOPSY SITE:\u000aColumnar cell change with flat atypia (e.g. blocks 10 and 12).\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aFibroadenomatoid changes.\u000aCore needle biopsy site.\u000aNote: The patient underwent a prior core needle biopsy for\u000acalcifications which showed atypical ductal hyperplasia associated with\u000acolumnar cell change and calcifications (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). No residual ADH is seen\u000ain the excision. The entire specimen is examined microscopically, including\u000amargins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast calcifications - core needle biopsy showed ADH.\u000aOperation: L breast excision with wire localization.\u000aOperative Findings: Specimen mammogram.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. L breast tissue with wire.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aClip and wire in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "left breast tissue with wire", and consists of a breast specimen (3.6 cm\u000aanterior-posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial-lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior-inferior) with a\u000asurgical stitch attached to the anterior margin and a needle localization wire\u000athat enters at the anterior-inferior margin and travels posteriorly without\u000aexiting the specimen. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A region of\u000ahemorrhagic, foreign material (2.3 cm medial-lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aanterior-posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm superior-inferior) representing the clip site is\u000apresent. The foreign material abuts the anterior and inferior margins and is\u000a0.5 cm from the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margins. A white/yellow, chalky, well-circumscribed\u000aregion is present (0.6 cm anterior-posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm superior-inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000amedial-lateral) is REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the lateral margins). The remainder of the breast parenchyma is\u000aapproximately 80% adipose and 20% fibrous tissue. The specimen is received\u000awith a radiograph showing a clip adjacent to the tip of a needle localization\u000awire. The entire specimen is submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin (perpendicular), 4 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential sections, each cross section submitted in two\u000acassettes with white/yellow mass in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and foreign material in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000amass with respect to foreign material in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin (perpendicular), REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast parenchyma to include posterior and superior margins, 3\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aoob\u005cpab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/11/2008\u000a[report_end]
