VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ELISABETH P FROST M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Eric J Burks, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, 11 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A REMOVED_DATE \u000aCM IRREGULAR MASS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA with ductal and lobular features, moderately differentiated\u000a(modified Bloom-Richardson grade II/III) measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size in\u000athis limited specimen.\u000aCalcifications are associated with invasive carcinoma.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aNo in situ carcinoma is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aCalcifications present in association with benign epithelium.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 62 y o female with mass, left UOQ - 13 mm. Hx Lt Bx (UOQ) in 1988\u000aFound LCIS.\u000aBreast Imaging Findings: irregular\u000aOperation: 11 G Ultrasound.\u000aOperative Findings: Cores obtained.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Carcinoma\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aCores in PINK cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aPart A, received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and\u000a"Left breast", is a one (1) pink cassette, labeled "Left", which contains\u000amultiple, yellow/white fibrofatty soft tissue cores (2.1 X REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Pink cassette contents, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aLMB/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Veerle I.J. Bossuyt M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (10/7/05): DR. DEBORAH DILLON\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for INVASIVE carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
