\u000aand fat necrosis is REMOVED_DATE cm to the nearest anterior margin and REMOVED_DATE to the\u000anearest inferior margin. The breast tissue is composed of approximately 50%\u000afibrous tissue with no obvious masses or gross lesions identified. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from inferior to superior and entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID including first area of calcifications and\u000aassociated ADH, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID including the clip site, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID including the second area\u000aof calcifications, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aelc/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
