cimen is received in four parts.\u000aPart one, labeled "ECC", consists of multiple fragments of tan hemorrhagic\u000atissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate.\u000aSection Code:\u000aMicro #1 - multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "EMC", consists of multiple fragments of tan/red soft tissue\u000asuggestive of endometrial polyp, measuring 3 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aMicro #2 - multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart three, labeled "right breast subareola", consists of a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afragment of fibro-fatty tissue with localized needle.\u000aMicro #3-5 - multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart four, labeled "right breast mass superior, consists of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afibro-fatty tissue fragments with two localized needles which has been removed\u000afrom the specimen by the time of processing.\u000aMicro #6-11 - multiple frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: FEDERSCHNEIDER, JEROME, MILES M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
