VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, 12:00, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A LOBULATED\u000aILL-DEFINED MASS:\u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR, measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size.\u000aThe stroma is moderately cellular with mild nuclear pleomorphism.\u000aMitoses are present but are < 1 per 10 HPF's.\u000aStromal overgrowth is present.\u000aFocal invasion into the surrounding breast tissue is present.\u000aSEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA is present within the phyllodes\u000atumor. Single cell necrosis is present.\u000aNote: In this biopsy, the phyllodes tumor would be most consistent with\u000aan intermediate grade tumor. However, final classification should be made\u000aafter excision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 43 year old female with a very rapidly growing left breast mass.\u000aHighly suspicious. R/O cancer. 12:00 left breast.\u000aBreast Imaging Findings: Lobulated, ill-defined.\u000aOperation: 11g stereotactic breast core biopsy\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 11g core biopsy specimens, 7 specimen (1 blue cassette)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SHAH,RAJSHRI N.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast", in a blue cassette, and consists of multiple, soft,\u000afragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000atr\u000aReports to: GOUGOUTAS, CHRISTINA M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
