VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000a1) RIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aAtypical Ductal Hyperplasia, multifocal, focally bordering\u000aon DCIS. No residual invasive tumor identified.\u000aFibrocystic changes including microcysts and calcifications in benign\u000aepithelium.\u000aFibrosis and foreign body giant cell reaction (status post prior\u000aexcision).\u000a(The specimen was extensively sampled for histologic examination and level\u000asections were examined.)\u000a2) SKIN, RIGHT BREAST:\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aNo residual carcinoma identified.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of right breast cancer. Original surgery was at Faulkner\u000aHosptial, lump/axillary dissection in Sept. 2000; +16/16 nodes. Today patient\u000ais having completion right mastectomy.\u000aOperation: Right simple mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast (long lateral, short superior).\u000a2. Additional breast tissue.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HENDERSON,JOEL M.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, right breast", consists of a 269 gram right simple\u000amastectomy (15.5 cm medial to lateral x REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aanterior to posterior). There is a tan-pink skin ellipse (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm), which\u000aincludes a tan-pink areola (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and an unremarkable nipple (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm high). The deep margin consists of a smooth surface with a few strands of\u000askeletal muscle around the periphery and a few central vertical strands (11 x 4\u000acm). At the superior aspect of the skin ellipse is a circumferential\u000awell-healed scar (4.0 cm in length). Deep to the scar is a prior biopsy site\u000a(2.0 cm medial/lateral x REMOVED_DATE cm superior/inferior x REMOVED_DATE cm anterior/posterior)\u000aconsisting of tan-gray, contracted fibrous tissue with no true cavity\u000aidentified, and coming to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep margin. Adjacent to this\u000aand deep and lateral to the nipple is a large area of firm fibrous tissue (6.0\u000acm medial/lateral x REMOVED_DATE cm superior/inferior x REMOVED_DATE cm anterior/posterior). The\u000aremainder of the breast parenchyma consists of 80% yellow adipose tissue and\u000a20% tan-gray fibrous tissue. No lymph nodes are grossly identified in upper\u000aouter quadrant breast parenchyma. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro 1: biopsy site and deep margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy site, deep margin, and prior scar, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: upper outer quadrant, fibrous tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: lower outer quadrant, fibrous tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: lower inner qaudrant, fibrous tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: upper inner quadrant, fibrous tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  upper outer quadrant tissue near axillary tail (rule out\u000alymph nodes), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "additional breast tissue", consists of a tan-pink,\u000aring-shaped skin excision (8.0 cm in diameter, REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm in width). No\u000ascars or other lesions are identified. The deep margin consists of tan-yellow\u000afibroadipose tissue (0.3 to REMOVED_DATE cm in depth). Representative sections are\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro 11: additional breast tissue, skin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aAdditional sections from part I are submitted:\u000aMicro 12: biopsy cavity, lateral aspect, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 13: biopsy cavity, medial aspect, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous tissue deep to nipple, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous tissue lateral to biopsy cavity, 5 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous tissue medial to biopsy cavity, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous tissue deep and inferior to biopsy cavity, 3 frags, RSS.\u000ajmh\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000a[report_end]
