VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCIBAS, EDMUND, SAULIUS, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by CIBAS,EDMUND SAULIUS,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST TISSUE, NEEDLE-DIRECTED BIOPSY:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (see note).\u000aFibrocystic change, proliferative, with florid duct hyperplasia.\u000aBenign perineural glandular inclusions (blocks 6 and 8).\u000aMicrocalcifications are associated with benign terminal duct/lobular\u000aunits.\u000aNOTE: In block 5 there is a solid proliferation of atypical ductal cells\u000awith mitotic activity. In block 6 there is a cribriform proliferation\u000aof monomorphic cells that partially involves two adjacent duct spaces.\u000aThese features, although reminiscent of ductal carcinoma in situ, are\u000aquantitatively insufficient for that diagnosis. The overall findings\u000aare most consistent with atypical duct hyperplasia. Dr. Stuart Schnitt\u000a(Beth Israel Hospital) has reviewed this case and concurs with the\u000adiagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left needle-directed breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram, left breast microcalcifications.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast tissue.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aA REMOVED_DATE cm cyst and a REMOVED_DATE cm firm area, too small to freeze; diagnosis\u000adeferred to permanents.\u000aGross examination only.\u000aRADIOLOGY: The mass is in the specimen J. Meyer, MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by GULIZIA,JAMES MARTIN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen, received fresh and labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "left breast tissue", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, unoriented,\u000ayellow/tan fragment of fibrofatty tissue with a REMOVED_DATE cm cyst and a REMOVED_DATE cm firm\u000aarea that is too small to freeze.\u000aMicro 1: Firm area, 4 frag, 1 cass.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Remainder of specimen, ESS, multi frag, 7 cass.\u000ajmg\u000aReports to: GARCIA, JOSE, PEREZ M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
