VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1) LEFT BREAST, QUADRANTECTOMY (INCLUDING FSA):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA present as two (2) discrete nodules measuring\u000a3.3 cm and at least REMOVED_DATE cm (see NOTE).\u000aThe larger tumor is poorly differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson\u000agrade II/III) and is not present at the surgical resection margins.\u000aThe smaller tumor is well differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson grade\u000aI/III) (tubular carcinoma) and is present at ink in an en face section\u000aof the inferior margin (block #6).\u000aLymphovascular invasion is identified adjacent to the larger tumor.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, comedo type, is present in association with the\u000alarger tumor, comprises ten per cent (10%) of the invasive tumor, and is\u000anot found away from the invasive tumor.\u000aIn-situ carcinoma is present in two of eight blocks (blocks #2, #6) and\u000ais not present at the margin.\u000aNOTE: The tumor masses were approximately 2 cm from one another and are\u000ahistologically dissimilar; thus, they probably represent two distinct\u000aprimaries. This case was reviewed at departmental staff conference.\u000aTumor from the larger tumor was sent for hormone receptor and flow\u000acytometry analysis.\u000a2) AXILLARY LYMPH NODE:\u000aEleven (11) lymph nodes with no tumor seen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left core needle biopsy (showing infiltrating cancer).\u000aOperation: Left Quadrantectomy, Axillary lymph node dissection\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Quadrantectomy - left\u000a#2. Axillary lymph node\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST QUADRANECTOMY (FSA):"\u000aTumor REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension.\u000aInfiltrating ductal carcinoma by FS.\u000aTumor extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the inked margin.\u000aTumor submitted for ERICA and flow cytometry.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHU,GERALD CHEN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. Quadrantectomy - left", consists of a tan/yellow\u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue (7.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with attached skin ellipse\u000a(4.5 cm x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen contains a long stitch which is designated as\u000aanterior-superior, and a short stitch which is designated anterior-inferior.\u000aThere is a firm, spiculated, white/tan/yellow mass (3.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which\u000ais closest to the deep margin (0.3 cm). The mass is also REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aof the inferior margin. The remainder of the breast contains white/tan breast\u000atissue with several blue-domed cysts. A portion of the tumor was submitted for\u000aintraoperative analysis as FSA. The FSR was submitted for ERICA. A\u000arepresentative section of the tumor was also submitted for flow cytometry.\u000aMicro 1, skin, 1 fragment, RSS.\u000aMicro 2, deep margin, perpendicular, 1 fragment, RSS.\u000aMicro 3, lateral margin, perpendicular, 1 fragment, RSS.\u000aMicro 4, medial, en face margin, 1 fragment, RSS.\u000aMicro 5, superior, en face margin, 1 fragment, RSS.\u000aMicro 6, inferior, en face margin, 1 fragment, RSS.\u000aMiro REMOVED_DATE  tumor, 2 fragments, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. axillary lymph node", consists of one fragment of\u000ayellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (8.5 x 6 x REMOVED_DATE cm). Thirteen lymph nodes are\u000aidentified within the specimen.\u000aMicro 9, 1 lymph node, 3 fragments, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  1 lymph node, 5 fragments, ESS.\u000aMicro 12, 1 lymph node, 2 fragments, ESS.\u000aMicro 13, 2 lymph nodes, 4 fragments, ESS.\u000aMicro 14, 2 lymph nodes, 3 fragments, ESS.\u000aMicro 15, 1 lymph node, 3 fragments, ESS.\u000aMicro 16, 2 lymph nodes, 4 fragments, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  1 lymph node, 8 fragments, ESS.\u000aReports to: EBERLEIN, TIMOTHY, JOSEPH M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODES REGIONAL RESECTION\u000a[report_end]
