VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: GREGORY J KANE M.D.\u000aCASE: BG-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Vijay K Vanguri, M.D.; Martin C Chang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Christopher P Crum, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, RETROAREOLAR, EXCISION FOR NIPPLE DISCHARGE ("A", ONE SPECIMEN):\u000aIntraductal papilloma (0.5 cm) with focal apocrine metaplasia.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the entire\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 10:00 (2 CM FROM NIPPLE), WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A REMOVED_DATE CM\u000aSONOGRAPHIC/MAMMOGRAPHIC ABNORMALITY, AND ADDITIONAL EXCISIONAL TISSUE ("B"\u000aTHROUGH "E", FOUR SPECIMENS):\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aSclerosing adenosis (forming an ill-defined REMOVED_DATE cm nodule) with epithelial\u000ahyperplasia and associated microcalcifications. See NOTE.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia and cysts, with columnar cell change and apocrine\u000ametaplasia.\u000aMicrocalcifications are associated with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the entire\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aNOTE: Four specimens are received, representing tissue targeting a reported\u000asonographic abnormality. The wire-localized specimen ("B") contains no\u000aspecific histologic evidence of a mass lesion. A radiographic lesion is\u000aidentified in specimen "D", corresponding to a small nodule of sclerosing\u000aadenosis. All specimens are entirely submitted.\u000aThis specimen has been reviewed by Dr. Richardson (Breast Pathology),\u000awho concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Bloody nipple discharge -> mammo and ultrasound. Dilated duct right\u000anipple area and suspicious lesion on ultrasound (separate) from\u000adilated duct seen.\u000aOperation: Right breast resection - wire localization.\u000aOperative Findings: Diffuse nodularity\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Lesion right breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Intraductal papilloma\u000a2. Right breast tissue (wire loc) - mammo\u000a3. Additional right breast tissue\u000a4. Additional right breast tissue\u000a5. Additional right breast tissue\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in five parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Intraductal papilloma", consists of an unoriented fragment of\u000atan/pink fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is\u000ainked black and sectioned to reveal a hemorrhagic-filled cavity (0.2 cm).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Intraductal papilloma sections, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Right breast tissue (wire localized)", consists of three\u000aunoriented fragments of tan/pink fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. A localization wire is visible\u000awithin the largest fragment. No mass or radiographic abnormality is associated\u000awith the wire in the accompanying specimen radiograph. The tissue consists of\u000atan/pink unremarkable, predominantly adipose (90%) tissue. The specimen is\u000ainked black, serially sectioned and entirely submitted for histologic review.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Largest fragment, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Second largest fragment, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Smallest fragment, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Additional right breast tissue", consists of multiple fragments of\u000atan/pink/yellow adipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate. No\u000aabnormality is identified in the accompanying specimen radiograph. The\u000aspecimen is inked black, sectioned and entirely submitted for histologic\u000areview.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections of additional right breast tissue, multi frags,\u000aESS.\u000aPart D, "#4. Additional right breast tissue", consists of six fragments of\u000atan/yellow/pink fibroadipose tissue (4.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate), which on\u000asectioning reveals tan/pink predominantly adipose tissue (85%). The\u000aaccompanying specimen radiograph shows an area of shadowing likely correlating\u000ato the reported sonographic abnormality. The fragments are inked black,\u000asectioned and entirely submitted for histologic review.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fragments of additional right breast tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart E, "#5. Additional right breast tissue", consists of a fragment of\u000atan/pink fibroadipose tissue (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is inked and entirely\u000asubmitted for histologic review.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional right breast tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BG-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMDH/am\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Christopher P Crum M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a6/12/2007\u000a[report_end]
