VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Rachel E Factor, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Tan A Ince, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aFibroadenoma with one focus of epithelial hyperplasia with atypia and apocrine\u000ametaplasia.\u000aAtypical Lobular Hyperplasia.\u000aCore biopsy site changes.\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory:\u000a1. A 48-year-old postmenopausal female with right breast mass in upper inner\u000aquadrant seen on mammo, REMOVED_DATE  status post R breast core Bx at 3 o'clock,\u000aretroareolar revealed breast tissue with fibroadenomatoid changes.\u000a2. US showed REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm solid mass.\u000aOperation: R breast WL excision Bx.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast mass, short suture superior, long lateral, whipstitch deep\u000amargin.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aRad-mass & clip in specimen.\u000a---(unsigned)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast mass, short superior, long lateral, whipstitch deep\u000amargin", and consists of irregular tan/yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose\u000abreast tissue (3.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a short suture designating the superior\u000amargin, long suture designating the lateral margin, and whipstitch designating\u000athe deep margin. There is a needle localization wire in place entering through\u000athe anterior medial aspect of the specimen and exiting through the posterior\u000ainferior aspect of the specimen. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000a(superior red, inferior green, lateral yellow, medial orange, anterior blue and\u000aposterior black) and inferiorly sectioned from anterior to posterior. There is\u000aa dense well-circumscribed fibrous nodule (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which abuts the\u000amedial and anterior margin, and is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe anterior margin. Remainder of the breast parenchyma is tan/yellow and\u000ahomogeneous with no additional lesions or areas of disruption identified. The\u000aspecimen is radiographed and displays a clip adjacent to the previously\u000adescribed lesion. The specimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections anterior to posterior block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to\u000ainclude nodules encrypt designated area, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Tan A Ince M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/26/2006\u000a[report_end]
