VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Stefan Kraft, M.D., Ph.D.; Rachel L Rucker-Schmidt, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Robert D Odze, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aMultifocal atypical ductal hyperplasia (blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000ain a background of columnar cell hyperplasia with associated\u000amicrocalcifications.\u000aDuctal epithelial hyperplasia\u000aCystic changes.\u000aMicrocalcifications associated with normal breast epithelium.\u000aFat necrosis consistent with prior biopsies.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. Andrea Richardson, Breast Pathology Service, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 43-year-old premenopausal female with abnormal L mammo/ultrasound\u000ademonstrating "two 10 mm groups of punctate" and amorphus calcifications in UOQ\u000aposteriorly - suspicious abnormality - unable to be cored - attempted\u000a03/12/2007.\u000aOperation: None given.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue (short superior, long lateral, whipstitch on chest\u000awall margin).\u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcs and wire in specimen. OR called. L. B. Smith.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand consists of a portion of fibroadipose tissue (7.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with\u000athree orientating sutures (short - superior; long - lateral; whipstitch on\u000achest wall margin), a needle localization wire in place (entering at the\u000asuperior aspect). The specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from inferior to superior, exhibiting approximately equal proportions\u000ayellow lobulated adipose tissue and white/pink, diffusely cystic (cyst\u000ameasuring up to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension) fibrous stroma. As confirmed by\u000athe accompanying radiograph and radiology "calcs and wire are in specimen".\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast, fibrous tissue, sequentially from superior to inferior,\u000amulti frags, ESS.\u000aDFI/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aADDENDUM:\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including the margins.\u000aAddendum #1 by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
