VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY, NEEDLE WIRE LOCALIZATION":\u000aATYPICAL ductal hyperplasia bordering on Ductal Carcinoma In Situ; the\u000alesion fulfills cytological and architectural criteria for DCIS\u000a(cribriform type, low nuclear grade), but involves only a\u000asingle space (<2mm). The lesion is present within REMOVED_DATE cm of a margin.\u000aFibrocystic change, focally proliferative, with extensive sclerosis.\u000aCalcifications are present in association with benign breast tissue.\u000aChronic inflammation, fibrosis, fat necrosis, foreign body giant cell\u000areaction and hemosiderin deposition consistent with prior needle biopsy\u000asite.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aThe ATYPICAL ductal hyperplasia bordering on ductal carcinoma in situ is\u000apresent within REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral margin.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 68 year old postmenopausal female, not on ERT, with family\u000ahistory of breast cancer in three sisters. Right breast\u000aretroareolar calcification. REMOVED_DATE  stereo-core bx showing\u000aADH.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization partial mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis:\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast biopsy wire localization, short\u000asuture=superior, long suture=lateral.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZATION BREAST BX" (GROSS ONLY):\u000aNo areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcification in specimen.\u000aD. SMITH M.D\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by ZEMBOWICZ,ARTUR , M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labelled with the patient's name\u000aand number and "right breast wire localization breast biopsy", consists of a\u000asingle fragment of pink/yellow fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000awith a needle localization wire in place and two orienting sutures, indicating\u000athe superior margin (short suture), and the lateral margin (long suture). The\u000aspecimen was inked and sectioned to reveal no areas grossly suspicious for\u000ainvasive carcinoma.\u000aMicro #1: Superior margins, en face, RSS, 1 frag.\u000aMicro #2: Inferior margin, en face, RSS, 1 frag.\u000aMicro #3: Lateral margin, en face, RSS, 1 frag.\u000aMicro #4: Medial margin, en face, RSS, 1 frag.\u000aMicro #5: Superficial margin, en face, RSS, 1 frag.\u000aMicro #6: Deep margin, en face, RSS, 1 frag.\u000aMicro #7: Area of calcifications, RSS, 1 frag.\u000aMicro #8: Superior/medial, RSS, 1 frag.\u000aMicro #9: Inferior/medial, RSS, 1 frag.\u000aMicro #10: Lateral, RSS, 4 frags.\u000aMicros #11-15: Remainder of specimen, ESS, 7 frags.\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
