VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: George Lin, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Vania Nose, MD, PhD\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT NIPPLE, BIOPSY":\u000aPAGET'S DISEASE OF THE NIPPLE.\u000aPlease see Part B.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, EXCISION WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS AND LEFT NIPPLE BIOPSY (including Part A and Part B):\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH PAGET'S DISEASE OF THE NIPPLE\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Comedo, solid,\u000aPaget?s Disease of the Nipple\u000aNuclear grade - High\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Superior\u000aVery close(<0.1 cm from margin)- Anterior (multifocal block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aMedial (multifocal block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aLateral (multifocal block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aInferior (multifocal REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aPositive (ink on carcinoma) - Posterior (focal block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - Tis (DCIS) Tis (Paget's) Nx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Pending\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 79 year old woman with history of right breast (1997) ADH > DCIS with\u000aexcision and negative re-excision - present with left breast mammo REMOVED_DATE \u000arevealing fine pleomorphic calcification distributed segmentally @ 3:00,\u000aexcision recommended.\u000aOperation: Left breast wl biopsy, L nipple.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left nipple biopsy.\u000aB/2. Left breast tissue, whip - deep margins, short - superior, long -lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcification and wire (piece of it was broken per. Dr. R. OR\u000acalled. SR.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Left nipple Bx", consists of a gray-tan irregular portion of skin\u000aand soft tissue (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is inked blue and is\u000asubmitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left breast tissue", consists of an irregular portion of\u000afibrofatty tissue (3.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a long suture designating lateral,\u000aa short suture designating superior, and a whipstitch designating deep margin.\u000aThere is a smoothly attached needle-localization wire, as displayed on the\u000aaccompanying radiograph, along the anterior margin. The specimen is inked as\u000aanterior blue, posterior black, superior red, inferior green, lateral yellow\u000aand medial orange. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal 90% yellow\u000alobulated adipose tissue, and 10% white fibrous tissue, with no discrete masses\u000aor lesions identified. The specimen is sequentially submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margins, radially, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections from anterior to posterior, with the\u000apossible area of concern on the accompanying radiograph in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID towards the\u000asuperior margin, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, radially, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aCP/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE (rare cells, < 1%)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) POSITIVE (3+)\u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen\u000aand progesterone receptors.\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
