VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kristin S. Ricci, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, PARTIAL MASTECTOMY, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS":\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA - Absent\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Comedo, solid, Paget?s Disease of the\u000anipple\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate to high\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent, see NOTE\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - 16:36 blocks\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Medial, superior, posterior, anterior,\u000askin margin (negative for Paget's)\u000aVery close(<0.1 cm from margin)- Lateral (multifocal), inferior\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aBiopsy cavity\u000aComplex sclerosing lesion\u000aPapilloma\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - Tis Nx MX\u000aNOTE: A single area of concern for possible microinvasion (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) was\u000aimmunostained for keratin/p63, and additional levels were examined, which did\u000anot demonstrate microinvasion. The same focus was also stained for\u000aER/PR/HER-2/neu, with results: ER=positive, PR=negative, HER-2/neu=positive\u000a(3+); these results are in accord with the prior studies (performed on\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 79 year old woman s/p L nipple biopsy REMOVED_DATE  "Paget's" disease of\u000athe nipple and s/p L B wire loc exc revealing high nuclear grade DCIS and\u000aclose/positive margins. History of right breast ADH/DCIS '97.\u000aOperation: L breast re-excision with 2 bracketing wires.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue short suture superior, long suture lateral, whip stitch\u000aon deep margin with mammography\u000aRADIOLOGY: Specimen 12 intact wires/targeted ca++ in specimen. Called to Dr.\u000aRhei REMOVED_DATE  @ 11:25 am.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part with the patient's name and unit\u000anumber and "left breast tissue, short suture superior, long lateral, whipstitch\u000aon deep margin", and consists of a left breast reexcision (394-g, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aanterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm inferior to superior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral)\u000awith two bracketing wires. The specimen has an attached skin ellipse (11.5 x\u000a5.5 cm) of tan/brown skin with a well-healed scar (4.5 cm), areola (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), and nipple (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is received inked by the\u000asurgeon for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange and has a long\u000astitch indicating lateral, short stitch indicating superior, and a whipstitch\u000aindicating deep. A radiograph demonstrates two localizing wires entering the\u000asuperior aspect of the specimen. The first localizing wire indicates\u000acalcification in the enlarged aspect of the localization wire (3.0 cm to the\u000aposterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin, and greater than REMOVED_DATE cm to the\u000amedial, lateral, inferior and skin margin). The second localizing wire\u000aindicates the wire head within the prior biopsy cavity (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) and\u000aadditional calcification adjacent to the cavity which is adjacent to the skin\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior margins, and greater than REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial, lateral, superior, and posterior margins. A fibrous area of tissue\u000asurrounds the biopsy cavity with depth of REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm in the\u000asuperior/posterior aspect of the specimen (3.0 cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the posterior margin); 40% of the specimen consists of fibrous tissue.\u000aThe remainder of tissue consists of adipose tissue. Gross photographs are\u000ataken of the specimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, perpendicular sections, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, en face section, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy site in relation to inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy site, lateral aspect, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy site, medial aspect of site, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy site in relation to skin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy site, superior aspect, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy site, posterior aspect, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue surrounding biopsy site, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000a1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area of wire localization for calcification, 2 frags\u000aeach, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area lateral to wire localization site, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area medial to wire localization site for calcification,\u000a1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral resection margin, perpendicular section, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial resection margin, perpendicular section, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Unoriented fragments of biopsy cavity, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections of breast parenchyma, 1 frag\u000aeach, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aKRI/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
