VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aMUELLER, JAMES, D, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by MUELLER,JAMES D,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST TISSUE, EXCISION:\u000aBreast tissue with dense stroma and epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aMicrocalcifications are seen in association with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aADDITIONAL LEFT BREAST TISSUE, EXCISION:\u000aBreast tissue with a focus of atypical ductal hyperplasia and dense\u000astroma.\u000aMicrocalcifications are seen in association with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aAdditional levels are performed and selected slides are reviewed by Dr. James\u000aConnolly and Dr. Susan Lester.\u000aThere are multiple foci of atypical hyperplasia and some areas are difficult to\u000aevaluate due to cautery artifact. In addition, some of the cytologic atypia\u000amay be due to the patient's prior treatment with radiation therapy. Diagnostic\u000afeatures of DCIS are not seen.\u000aThere is fibrosis and chronic inflammation. These changes may be related to\u000athe prior surgical excision in this area and/or to the more recent core needle\u000abiopsy. A definitive core needle biopsy site cannot be identified with\u000acertainty.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 67 year-old female not on ERT\u000aStatus post left breast for Stg. I breast cancer 1981 (parenthesis) xrt,\u000abut no chemo tx). Now has increased scarring on mammogram at\u000alumpectomy site. (L) breast wire loc. bx.\u000a* Clip not in specimen - please look for core biopsy tract -\u000awill obtain mammogram to ensure removal.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Left breast tissue to mammo\u000a2) Additional left breast tissue.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HONG,XUEFEI,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart 1, "left breast tissue", consists of four fragments of yellow/tan breast\u000atissue (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). No wire is identified. Sectioning\u000areveals 30% of the specimen is fibrous tissue. The specimen is inked and\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Breast tissue, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart 2, "additional left breast tissue", consists of three fragments of\u000atan/yellow fibroadipose soft tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm om aggregate). The\u000aspecimen is inked and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Additional breast tissue, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
