VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDILLON, DEBORAH, A, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by DILLON,DEBORAH A,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, 1:00, ADJACENT TO PRIOR BIOPSY CAVITY, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE\u000aNEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A NEW MASS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA with ductal and lobular features, moderately\u000adifferentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson grade II/III), measuring at\u000aleast REMOVED_DATE cm in size in this limited specimen.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aNo in situ carcinoma is present in this limited specimen.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by DILLON,DEBORAH A,M.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 1):\u000aEstrogen receptor - POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor - POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 69-year-old female with history of left lumpectomy and radiation\u000atherapy 20 years ago, status post biopsy 2002 for ADH, now with new\u000amass, left 1:00, adjacent to cavity.\u000aOperation: 11g stereotactic.\u000aOperative findings: Cores obtained.\u000aBreast Imaging Findings: Irregular.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Suspected recurrence, rule out fat necrosis.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Cores in orange cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMO,LESLEY C.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "Left breast", in an orange cassette, labeled "Left", and\u000aconsists of multiple, soft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (2.0 x\u000a1.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Left cores, multiple frags, ESS.\u000adb\u000aReports to: FROST, ELISABETH, PEPPERELL M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
