VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM DEACONESS HOSPITAL, BOSTON, MA.\u000aRIGHT BREAST BIOPSIES (96-S-5902; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000a9 O'CLOCK:\u000aSEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA BORDERING ON DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN\u000aSITU, present in 3 of 7 blocks (blocks 2, 3, and 4) and extending to the\u000asuperior lateral margin. Microcalcifications are associated with one\u000afocus of the atypical proliferation (block 3).\u000aCellular fibroadenoma (1.2 cm).\u000aFibrocystic changes including apocrine metaplasia, cysts, and stromal\u000asclerosis.\u000a12 O'CLOCK:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, single focus in one slide (slide 11), not\u000aat the margin.\u000aFibrocystic changes including small cysts, stromal sclerosis, and rare\u000aassociated microcalcifications.\u000aRIGHT BREAST RE-EXCISION (96-S-6222; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aFlorid ductal hyperplasia, focal, with mild atypical hyperplasia.\u000aFibrocystic changes including apocrine metaplasia and small cysts.\u000aHealing biopsy site.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 41 year old female with a positive family history for breast cancer\u000aand a right breast mass.\u000aOperation: Right breast biopsies.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Consult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aReceived from Deaconess Hospital, Boston, MA are 27 glass slides.\u000aSeventeen (17) slides are labeled 96-S-REMOVED_CASE_ID and sublabeled as follows: 1, 2,\u000a3 (1L through 4L), 4, 5, 6, 7 (1L and 2L), 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, and 13.\u000aThese slides correspond to two right breast biopsies from 9 o'clock (slides 1\u000athrough 9) and from 12 o'clock (slides 10 through 13) from a procedure\u000aperformed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the\u000apatient's name.\u000aAlso received referring to these slides (96-S-REMOVED_CASE_ID; REMOVED_DATE ) is a consultation\u000areport from Beth Israel Hospital, Boston, MA, signed by Dr. James Connolly, and\u000adated REMOVED_DATE  (outside diagnosis: "Foci of highly atypical ductal\u000aproliferation-low grade ductal carcinoma in situ in blocks 2 and 3.\u000aCalcifications are not identified. The ductal carcinoma in situ is present\u000aadjacent to blue inked margin (superior-lateral). Atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aCellular fibroadenoma.")\u000aTen (10) slides are labeled 96-S-REMOVED_CASE_ID and sublabeled 1 through 10.\u000aThese slides correspond to a right breast re-excision from a procedure\u000aperformed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the\u000apatient's name.\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000a[report_end]
