VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Justine A Barletta, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION:\u000aBreast tissue with atypical lobular hyperplasia, complex sclerosing\u000alesion, macrocyst with mural fibrosis (1.0 cm), and cystic change with\u000aapocrine metaplasia.\u000aCalcifications in association with benign breast tissue.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Atypical lobular hyperplasia, on core needle biopsy as MRI\u000aabnormality.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire-localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast ALH on core.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast wire localized excision, stitches: short=superior,\u000along=lateral, whip=none.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aClip in specimen (MRI lesion with prior MRI core bx). Also note calcs in\u000aspecimen.\u000a---C. Denison, MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, in a container labeled with the\u000apatient's name, medical record number, and "left breast wire localized\u000aexcision", and consists of one oriented wire localized breast excision specimen\u000a(4.7 cm anterior to posterior x REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral and REMOVED_DATE cm superior to\u000ainferior) oriented with two sutures designated by the surgeon as follows:\u000ashort=superior and long=lateral. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A localization wire enters the\u000aanterior aspect of the specimen. The specimen is sectioned from posterior to\u000aanterior in 13 slices. The localization wire ends in slice #5. A clip is in\u000aslice #7. A hemorrhagic biopsy cavity (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) extends through\u000aslices #5, #6, #7, and #8 and is located at the inferior, lateral, and superior\u000amargins and extends to REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior and 3\u000acm from the anterior margin. There is a hemorrhagic cyst (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aabutting the inferior and lateral margins and located REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior,\u000a2.0 cm from the medial, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior and 4 cm from the anterior\u000amargin. A radiograph is received with the specimen that shows a clip in the\u000aspecimen and calcifications. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin (perpendicular sections), 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2 and #3, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5 and #6, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7 (with clip), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slices #8 and #9, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slices #10 and #11, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #12, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin (perpendicular sections), 4 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aJUB/jp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
