VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ELISABETH P FROST M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Ann K Folkins, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, CENTRAL, 8 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform and solid types (high nuclear\u000agrade) with apocrine features, central necrosis, and calcifications, is\u000apresent.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor,\u000aprogesterone receptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an\u000aaddendum.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 60 year old female with a history of left breast invasive carcinoma\u000aand DCIS in 2002. Now with new right heterogenous calcifications in the mid\u000acentral breast.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: Nonpalpable calcifications.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: Central\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 8 G Stereotactic Vacuum-assisted\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 8 G Stereotactic Vacuum-assisted - fuchsia\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast", and consists of two fuchsia cassettes. First\u000afuchsia cassette "A CA++" contains multiple pink/tan tissues (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in aggregate). Second fuchsia cassette "B" contains multiple pink/tan\u000atissues (1.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fuchsia cassette A contents (CA++), multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fuchsia cassette B contents, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000alm/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/13/2008\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) WEAKLY POSITIVE (EQUIVOCAL) (2+)\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
