VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Cheryl Adackapara, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP, WIRE,\u000aAND CALCIFICATIONS":\u000aBreast tissue with columnar cell changes, and core biopsy site changes.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium\u000aFibroadenoma (0.9 cm).\u000aNo atypical ductal hyperplasia is identified.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000a(Multiple levels examined).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 48-year-old female with ADH on core biopsy, left breast.\u000aOperation: Left needle core biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast calcifications.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue short superior long lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aClip, residual calcifications and hookwire present.\u000aSignature: C. Dennison, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "left breast tissue", consists of a wire localized breast excision (4.1 cm\u000asuperior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior)\u000awith a stitch designating the superior aspect of the specimen and a long stitch\u000adesignating the lateral aspect of the specimen. The specimen is received\u000apreviously inked per surgeon. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for\u000athe evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. An accompanying radiograph\u000ademonstrates a localization wire entering the lateral aspect of the specimen\u000aand exiting the medial aspect of the specimen. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned in ten slices from superior to inferior to reveal dense white fibrous\u000atissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that abuts the superior, medial, inferior, lateral,\u000aanterior and posterior margins. Slice #4 is associated with the metallic clip\u000aand small biopsy cavity (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is located REMOVED_DATE cm to the\u000alateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm to the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm to the\u000ainferior margin. The specimen is entirely submitted for histological\u000aexamination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, perpendicular, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen serially sectioned from superior to inferior, 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS (micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID correspond to biopsy cavity, micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID correspond to\u000aarea of clip, micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, correspond to one slice transected\u000ain half).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, perpendicular, 10 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adcp/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
