/orange. The accompanying\u000aspecimen radiograph shows a single clip and the localization wire, both present\u000awithin a dense area containing microcalcifications. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm core biopsy\u000acavity, filled with beads and surrounded by areas of hemorrhage. It extends to\u000awithin REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior,\u000a1.1 cm of the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral margin.\u000aNo masses are grossly identified. 95% of the specimen is submitted, including\u000aall fibrous tissue. The area containing the clip is placed in cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Prior core biopsy site to anterior and inferior margins, 1 frag,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Core biopsy site to anterior, inferior, and posterior margins,\u000a1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Core biopsy site to anterior, inferior, and posterior margins,\u000a1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional core biopsy site, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue present in the specimen to include margins,\u000amulti frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining fibrous tissue, mult frags, ESS.\u000aPal/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/5/2005\u000a[report_end]
