VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Tanya Rege, M.D., Ph.D.; Justine A Barletta, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION OF A MASS:\u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR, LOW GRADE (2.8 CM), see NOTE.\u000aThe tumor is <0.1 cm from the unoriented resection margin (scant fat\u000aintervening).\u000aNote: The tumor has an irregular border and areas of stromal overgrowth. The\u000astroma is pauci to mildly hypercellular without nuclear atypia, and stromal\u000amitoses number 2 per 10 high power fields. No necrosis, hemorrhage or\u000aheterologous differentiation is present.\u000aThis tumor is best classified as a low grade phyllodes tumor.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast mass. Core bx (BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) --> fibro-epi lesion.\u000aOperation: Excision.\u000aOperative Findings: See Op Note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) rt breast mass.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "Rt breast mass", and consists of an unoriented ovoid yellow/tan to\u000apink/tan soft tissue (4.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is inked black and serially\u000asectioned to exhibit a partially circumscribed pink/tan lobulated solid mass\u000a(2.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which grossly extends to the black-inked margins in\u000amultiple areas. The mass occupies approximately 80% of the cut surface. The\u000aremaining specimen is composed of yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue with no\u000aadditional discrete lesions grossly identified. The specimen is entirely\u000asequentially submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: (Perpendicular sections in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags total, ESS.\u000alm/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/28/2007\u000a[report_end]
