VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, fibroadenoma\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: J. GREGORY KANE M.D.\u000aCASE: BG-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: George Lin, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Michelle S Hirsch, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aQ\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST FIBROADENOMA":\u000aBenign breast tissue with dense fibrous stroma and calcifications in\u000abenign epithelium.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST EXCISION WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR\u000aMICROCALCIFICATIONS.\u000aBenign breast tissue with dense fibrosis, core biopsy site and\u000acalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aC. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE LATERAL TO LOWER CLIP AREA":\u000aBenign breast tissue with dense fibrosis, core biopsy site and\u000acalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aNOTE: There is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Microcalcifications left breast -> core biopsy -> atypical ductal\u000ahyperplasia on core. Excision recommended.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localization, breast resection\u000aOperative Findings: 2 wires/2 microcalcifications\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast atypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1/A. Left breast fibroadenoma\u000a2/B. Left breast tissue - 2 wires, 2 microcalcifications (short suture\u000ainferior; long suture medial)\u000a3/C. Left breast tissue lateral to lower clip area\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand medical record number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Left breast fibroadenoma", consists of two fragments of\u000afibroadipose tissue with white nodularity (1.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibroadipose tissue with white nodularity, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Left breast tissue, two wires, two microcalcifications -\u000ashort suture inferior, long suture medial", consists of a fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue (2.4 cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm anterior to posterior). There are two orienting sutures: a short suture\u000adesignating inferior and a long suture designating medial per surgeon. The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. There are two wires entering the specimen with wire #1 entering\u000athe lateral aspect going towards the anterior aspect and wire #2 entering the\u000asuperior aspect going to the posterior aspect. Wire #1 is associated with a\u000aclip. A radiograph accompanies the specimen showing wire #1 associated with\u000aclip and microcalcifications in wire #2 associated with microcalcifications.\u000aThe specimen is sectioned into seven slices going from anterior to posterior\u000awith slice #1 as anterior and slice #7 as posterior. A clip is identified\u000aassociated with wire #1 and with surrounding hemorrhage and white fibrous\u000atissue (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) and located from margins as follows: REMOVED_DATE cm\u000asuperior, REMOVED_DATE cm inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial, abutting lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior,\u000aand abutting posterior. No lesions are grossly associated with wire #2. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #1 with anterior margin perpendicular, 4 frags in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and 3\u000afrags in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7 with posterior margin perpendicular, 3 frags in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and 4\u000afrags in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, ESS.\u000aNote: Hemorrhagic/white fibrous area associated with clip is in slices #5\u000athrough #7 and in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The clip is in micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aPart C, labeled "#3. Left breast tissue lateral to lower clip area", consists\u000aof an unoriented fragment of fibroadipose tissue (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000aouter aspect of the specimen is inked blue. The specimen is entirely submitted\u000afor histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibroadipose tissue sectioned, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BG-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aGL/am\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aThursday May 14, 2009 at 06:20:55PM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aAddendum #1 by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 10, 2009 at 01:37:24PM\u000a[report_end]
