VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: KATHARINE CARTER M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Paul A. VanderLaan, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST EXCISION, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Solid\u000aNuclear grade - High\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks (blocks 18 and 29)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Superior, inferior, medial, posterior\u000aAnterior\u000aVery close(<0.1 cm from margin)- <0.1 cm to lateral\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aCalcifications in association with sclerosing adenosis and apocrine cysts\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Pending\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition): Tis NX MX.\u000aCase was also reviewed by D. Dillon, Breast Service, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: See prior BWH core biopsy REMOVED_DATE  ADH.\u000aNOTE: Radiologist feels clips is no longer adjacent to area of calcification.\u000aOperation: Left mammographically-directed breast biopsy\u000aOperative Findings: Not given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram, left breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue, left upper outer breast; short = superior, long =\u000alateral. Medial part of biopsy is in old scar (see previous report).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSpecimen: Wire, clip, calcifications. OR called.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, and labeled with the patient's name and medical\u000arecord number, and "#1. Left breast tissue, left upper outer breast, short\u000asuperior, long lateral". The specimen consists of one left breast excision of\u000ayellow/pink fatty tissue that was oriented per the surgeon such that a long\u000astitch designated the lateral margin, and a short stitch designated the\u000asuperior margin. The breast excision dimensions are REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral,\u000a6.0 cm superior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior. A single wire\u000ais seemed to be entering the specimen at 12 o'clock and exiting the specimen at\u000a6 o'clock. An accompanying radiograph demonstrates the wire localizing a clip\u000anear an ill-defined mass in addition to multiple calcifications. The posterior\u000asurface of the specimen is a smooth and shiny surface whereas the rest of the\u000atissue is irregular fatty lobulated tissue. The specimen is six-inked per\u000aprotocol such that the superior is inked red, the inferior is inked green, the\u000alateral is inked yellow, the medial is inked orange, the anterior is inked\u000ablue, and the posterior is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000afrom medial to lateral revealing multiple areas of white/tan fibrous tissue\u000athat spread throughout the specimen. There is an area of hemorrhage in the\u000acenter of the specimen that is located from block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000apredominantly. The clip was found and corresponds to block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Multiple\u000acalcifications were apparent on sectioning. Representative sections are\u000asubmitted for histology.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicularly sectioned, 3 frags per cassette,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 slice, bisected, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 slice, bisected, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 slice, trisected, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 slice, trisected, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 slice, trisected, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 slice, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 slice, bisected, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 slice, bisected, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 slice, bisected, 1 frag per cassette, ESS; note, clip in\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 slice, bisected, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicularly sectioned, 3 frags per cassette,\u000aESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000apva/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/22/2008\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (9/23/08):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) POSITIVE (3+)\u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen\u000aand progesterone receptors.\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
