re localization in place\u000aalong with a mass. The specimen consists of breast parenchymal tissue (3.5 x\u000a3.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm), received with two sutures that have been designated short\u000asuperior, long lateral and whip stitch = deep. Sectioning of the specimen\u000areveals a white, fibrotic area interspered with possible core biopsy site that\u000ameasure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and appears to come to less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000agreen inked, red inked, yellow inked margins. No further lesions are\u000aidentified in the remaining breast parenchyma which consists entirely of\u000ayellow adipose tissue. The specimen is sectioned and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  area of fibrosis/core biopsy site, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remaining specimen, 9 frags, ESS.\u000ajhl\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
