VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Vinodh Pillai, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND A REMOVED_DATE CM MASS:\u000aBiopsy site with adjacent fibroadenoma (0.4 cm), see NOTE\u000aSclerosing adenosis with calcifications.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aNOTE: No residual papillary lesion is seen similar to that present on the prior\u000acore needle biopsy (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID slides re-reviewed). A small fibroadenoma is\u000apresent adjacent to the biopsy site.\u000aB. RIGHT BREAST MRI WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR AN AREA OF MRI ENHANCEMENT:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, focal, see NOTE\u000aApocrine cysts cluster (0.7 cm, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), see NOTE\u000aOther findings:\u000aColumnar cell change with calcifications & cysts.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aNOTE: A small focus of LCIS is present which appears to be an incidental\u000afinding (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). E-cadherin stain confirms absent membranous staining in lesional\u000acells. An ER and PR stain are strongly positive and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu is negative (1+).\u000aThe area of cysts (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) is quite prominent and is associated with sclerotic\u000astroma; this may represent the MRI area of interest, however radiologic\u000acorrelation is advised to ensure the specimen is representative of the\u000aradiologic lesion.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 69 yo/o female with right breast atypical hyperplasia after core\u000abiopsy, 2nd area of MRI enhancement\u000aOperation: 1. Right breast mammo guided wire excision.\u000a2. Right breast MRI guided wire excision\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided\u000aClinical Diagnosis: 1. Right breast atypical hyperplasia.\u000a2. Right breast abnormal MRI\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast mammo wire localized excisional biopsy (short superior, long\u000alateral)\u000aB/2. Right breast MRI wire localized excisional biopsy (short superior, long\u000alateral)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in two parts, labeled with the patient's name and\u000amedical record number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Right breast wire localized excision biopsy (short suture\u000asuperior, long lateral)", consists of a right breast wire localized excision\u000aspecimen oriented by the surgeon as short suture superior, long suture lateral\u000a(superior to inferior REMOVED_DATE cm, medial to lateral REMOVED_DATE cm, anterior to posterior\u000a1.9 cm) with the wire running from lateral to medial. The specimen radiograph\u000ais reviewed on Centricity and shows a wire and clip in the specimen. The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol as anterior-blue, posterior-black,\u000amedial-orange, lateral-yellow, superior-red and inferior-green. The specimen\u000ais serially sectioned from lateral to medial margin to reveal an ill-defined\u000afirm area (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) abutting the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm to medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to anterior\u000amargin and REMOVED_DATE cm to posterior margin. No other lesions can be identified.\u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted for histological examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin radial sections, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast parenchyma, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Ill-defined area/area of biopsy cavity, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast parenchyma, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Right breast MRI wire localized excision biopsy (short\u000asuperior, long lateral), consists of a right breast wire localized excision\u000aspecimen oriented as per surgeon as short suture superior and long suture\u000alateral (superior to inferior - REMOVED_DATE cm, medial to lateral - REMOVED_DATE cm, and\u000aanterior to posterior - REMOVED_DATE cm) with the wire running medial to lateral. The\u000aspecimen radiograph on centricity is reviewed and shows a wire in the specimen\u000awith additional possible density and calcification. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol as anterior-blue, posterior-black, medial-orange,\u000alateral-yellow, superior-red and inferior-green. The specimen is sectioned\u000afrom lateral to medial to reveal an ill-defined fibrous area abutting the\u000alateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to\u000aanterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to superior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm to inferior margin. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted for histological examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin radial sections, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Firm area, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast parenchyma, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast parenchyma, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis\u000ausing the following criteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not\u000ayet been determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor\u000acells but only a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >30% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for\u000ainvestigational use only.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aVIP/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 20, 2009 at 06:27:44PM\u000a[report_end]
