VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP MARKING A PRIOR SITE OF\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia, florid.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aNote: No carcinoma is seen after complete microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy for a REMOVED_DATE cm area of calcifications of the right\u000abreast showed ADH. Patient has a history of MS.\u000aOperation: Right breast, wire localized excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Mammographic calcifications with prior needle biopsy.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: The clip is in the specimen. Dr. S. Durfee.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast, wire localized excision (inked per protocol).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aReceived labeled with the patient's name and unit number and "right breast\u000abiopsy" is a 3 cm (medial to lateral) x REMOVED_DATE cm (superior to inferior) x 4 cm\u000a(anterior to posterior), fragment of fibrofatty tissue with a localization wire\u000ain place.\u000aThe specimen radiograph reveals a clip adjacent to the localization wire.\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol by the surgeon for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aThe wire enters through the anterior portion of the specimen. There is a REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.5 cm biopsy site along the wire. The remainder of the tissue consists of\u000afibrous white tissue admixed with adipose tissue with no focal lesions. The\u000aentire specimen is submitted for microscopic examination.\u000aCass 1: Anterior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aCass 2,3: Lateral margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCass 4: Medial margin, area of clip, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aCass 5: Deep margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCass 6,7: Superior margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aCass 8,9,10: Inferior margin, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
