VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Consult material\u000aProcedure Date:\u000aOrdering Provider: ANN H PARTRIDGE M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Qinghong Yang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM UNIVERSITY OF UTAH HEALTH SCIENCES CENTER, SLC, UT:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION AND ADDITIONAL MARGINS (SP-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID,\u000a12/05/2008):\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid and cribriform types (intermediate nuclear\u000agrade), with necrosis, is present adjacent to biopsy site changes in two of\u000aseven blocks reviewed.\u000aDCIS is present <0.1 cm from the lateral margin (inked blue, block 1D) and at\u000aleast REMOVED_DATE cm from other margins in the main excision.\u000aSeparately submitted additional deep inferior, medial, deep superior and\u000alateral margins with no carcinoma seen.\u000aNOTE: By report, a previous core needle biopsy showed DCIS (OSH SP-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast DCIS\u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aConsult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived from University of Utah Health Sciences Center, Pathology Department,\u000a500 Chipeta Way, SLC, UT REMOVED_CASE_ID, are one hundred sixty-one (161) glass slides\u000a(127 slides are unstained).\u000aThe slides are labeled ?SP-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID" and sublabeled "1A-1"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), "1A\u000aunstained"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "1B"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), "1B unstained"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), "1C-1"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), "1C\u000aunstained"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), "1C-2", "1D", "1D-1", "1D"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), "1D MUSA", "1D SMA", "1D\u000aNEGATIVE", "1E", "1E-1", "1E unstained"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), "1F", "1F unstained"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), "1G",\u000a"1G-1", "1G unstained"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), "2A", "2A-1", "2A unstained"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), "3A", "3A\u000aunstained"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), "4A", "4A-1", "4A unstained"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), "4B", "4B-1", "4B\u000aunstained"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), "5A", "5A-1", "5A unstained"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), "6A", "6A-1" and "6A\u000aunstained"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), corresponding to 1) right breast excision (3.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000a2) right breast, clips, excision (0.3 x REMOVED_DATE cm, and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE in\u000aaggregate) 4) right breast, medial margin, excision (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) 5)\u000aright breast, deep superior margin, excision (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) 6) right\u000abreast, lateral margin, excision (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aaccording to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on Sunday\u000aAugust 09, 2009 at 04:37:39PM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: (8/12/09)\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block 1D):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following\u000acriteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not\u000ayet been determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells or moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a< 30% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>30% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aThe immunoperoxidase, immunofluorescence and in-situ hybridization tests\u000aperformed at Brigham and Women's Hospital were developed and their performance\u000acharacteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the\u000aDepartment of Pathology at BWH. They have not been cleared or approved by the\u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such\u000aclearance or approval is not necessary.\u000aAddendum #1 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday August 12, 2009 at 04:18:27PM\u000a[report_end]
