VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Dick Guang-Iong Hwang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Hejin P Hahn, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread.\u000aColumnar cell change.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 54 y/o female S/P image-guided core biopsy of the right breast for\u000amicrocalcifications revealing columnar cell changes with atypia.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire-localized excisional biopsy.\u000aPREVIOUS SURGERY: Yes\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: right breast abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast wire-localized excisional biopsy; short suture - superior;\u000along suture - lateral, to mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip in specimen. - Meyer\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy, short suture superior,\u000along suture lateral to mammo", and consists of an ovoid yellow/tan fibroadipose\u000atissue (4.4 M-L x REMOVED_DATE S-I x REMOVED_DATE A-P cm), which is oriented per surgeon with two\u000asutures: Short equals superior, long equals lateral. The specimen is inked\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThere is one needle localization wire in place entering the anteroinferior\u000aaspect of the specimen and exiting the inferolateral aspect of the specimen.\u000aThe specimen was previously radiographed, confirming the presence of a clip\u000awithin the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral\u000ain the central/medial aspect of the specimen, there is a well-circumscribed\u000abulging tan granular solid mass (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which extends to the\u000ainferior and posterior margins, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral margin.\u000aEmbedded within the nodular mass is a silver metal clip as consistent with\u000aprior core biopsy procedure. The remainder of the cut surface is composed of\u000agreater than 75% dense white/tan fibrous stroma and less than 25% yellow/tan\u000alobulated adipose tissue with no additional discrete lesions grossly\u000aidentified. The specimen is entirely sequentially submitted from medial to\u000alateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central specimen from medial to lateral (mass in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, clip in\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aLM/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/4/2008\u000a[report_end]
