VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Oname O. Burlingame, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, ANTERIOR, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR\u000aA CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS":\u000aNo residual atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia and sclerosing adenosis with calcifications.\u000aCore biopsy site changes.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, POSTERIOR, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR\u000aA CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS":\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (0.25 cm, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and flat epithelial\u000aatypia, involving adenosis and not associated with biopsy site.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aSclerosing adenosis with calcifications.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aBiopsy site.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 54 year old with right nipple discharge and core biopsy REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, revealing\u000aseverely atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast abnormal mammogram, atypical ductal\u000ahyperplasia REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right breast wire localized - excisional biopsy (anterior wire), short\u000astitch/superior, long stitch/lateral.\u000aB/2) right breast wire localized - excisional biopsy (posterior wire), short\u000astitch/superior, long stitch/lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSpecimen #1: Anterior wire with clip and some calcifications, entire wire. OR\u000acalled by Dr. R. Galvin @ 2:10 pm.\u000aSpecimen #2: Posterior - clip, entire & mass seen in specimen. Called to OR\u000a34 @ 2:30 pm.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast, wire-localized excision biopsy, anterior wire",\u000aconsists of one breast lumpectomy specimen (3.9 cm anterior-posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000amedial-lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior-inferior) oriented with a short stitch\u000adesignating superior and a long stitch designating lateral. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A\u000alocalization wire enters at the superior-lateral aspect of the specimen and\u000atravels anteriorly exiting at the junction of the medial, inferior and anterior\u000amargins. The specimen is sectioned from anterior to posterior approximately\u000aparallel to the center of the wire. The parenchyma is approximately 40%\u000afibrous tissue and 60% adipose tissue with a biopsy cavity (0.6 cm greatest\u000adimension) containing a small metal cylinder (0.25 cm length x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000adiameter). No discrete masses are identified. The specimen is accompanied by\u000aa radiograph and radiograph report confirming that a wire, clip and\u000acalcifications are within the specimen. The entire specimen is submitted for\u000ahistologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin (perpendicular), REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial section to include biopsy cavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast parenchyma to include margins, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin (perpendicular), 5 frags each, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Right breast wire-localized excisional biopsy, posterior wire",\u000aconsists of a breast lumpectomy specimen (3.6 cm medial-lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aanterior-posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm superior-inferior) oriented with a short stitch\u000adesignating superior and a long stitch designating lateral. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A\u000alocalization wire enters the specimen at the center of the inferior margin and\u000atravels superiorly and posteriorly but does not exit the specimen. The\u000aspecimen is sectioned from medial to lateral approximately parallel to the\u000awire. The breast parenchyma is 80% adipose tissue and 20% fibrous tissue with\u000aa biopsy site (1.1 cm greatest dimension) containing a clip. No discrete\u000amasses are identified. The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph and\u000aradiograph report confirming that a clip and wire are within the specimen. The\u000aentire specimen is submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin (perpendicular), 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections sequentially submitted from medial to lateral with\u000athe clip site in B__, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin (perpendicular), 4 frags each, ESS.\u000aOOB/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
