VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Andrew G. Evans, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrew M. Bellizzi, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION (CORE BIOPSY DIAGNOSIS OF ADH):\u000aFocal atypical ductal hyperplasia (see NOTE).\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aSclerosed fibroadenoma (0.4 cm) with associated calcifications.\u000aSclerosing adenosis, focal epithelial hyperplasia, columnar cell change,\u000aapocrine metaplasia, and microcysts.\u000aMicrocalcifications in benign duct profiles including columnar cell\u000achange and in arterial walls.\u000aNOTE: Dr. D. Dillon has reviewed select sections from this case and concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 67 yo woman with bilateral mammographic calcifications, with L UOQ\u000aanterior calcifications for which she had REMOVED_DATE  core needle biopsy at Faulkner\u000aHospital revealing ADH. Excision is recommended.\u000aPrevious Surgery: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aOperation: L breast wire-localized biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal L mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast tissue; short - superior; long - lateral; whipped stitch -\u000achest wall margin; to mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Specimen contains targeted mass, 2 clips and an intact wire.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand unit number, and "left breast tissue, short - superior, long - lateral; to\u000amammo, whipped stitch chest wall margin", and consists of one wire-localized\u000alumpectomy specimen (31.0g; REMOVED_DATE superior to inferior x REMOVED_DATE medial to lateral x\u000a1.8 anterior to posterior cm). The wire is identified at the inferior margin.\u000aShort and long sutures have been placed per surgeon to designate the superior\u000aand lateral positions, respectively. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The cut surface\u000areveals one white/tan firm lesion consistent with a biopsy cavity which abuts\u000athe superior margin coming to within REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin. The remaining breast\u000atissue is 90% adipose tissue. A whipped stitch has been placed per surgeon to\u000adesignate the posterior aspect(skeletal muscle). The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted for microscopic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative biopsy cavity to superior margin, 2 frags\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional biopsy cavity to medial and lateral margins, 1\u000afrag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional serial sections of breast tissue, 1 frag each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aSWY/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrew M. Bellizzi M.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday August 05, 2009 at 05:29:36PM\u000aADDENDUM:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION:\u000aMargins were examined for the final diagnosis.\u000aAddendum #1 by Andrew M. Bellizzi M.D., Electronically signed on Thursday\u000aAugust 06, 2009 at 11:32:21AM\u000a[report_end]
