VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-04-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS, SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY, AND\u000aSUPERIOR SHAVE MARGIN (including REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)(specimens #1-#3 of 3\u000aspecimens):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA\u000aNEGATIVE LYMPH NODES\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - no\u000aHistologic Type - ductal\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - intermediate\u000aEIC - N/A\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - absent\u000aSkin invasion - absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - all margins (including superior shave\u000amargin)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel Lymph Nodes - negative (3 HE levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 3\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- 0:3\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aSkin with scar\u000aFibroadenoma\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(sn) MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - performed previously\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Non-palpable CA, right breast\u000aOperation: (R) sentinel lymph node bx.\u000a(R) breast wire directed lumpectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given\u000aClinical Diagnosis: (R) breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a#1. (R) sentinel lymph nodes - FS.\u000a#2. Tumor site (R) breast, short superior, long lateral (to mammo).\u000a#3. Superior shave margin whip stitch superior.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aSpecimen radiograph contains targeted lesion and hookwire.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. (R) SENTINEL LYMPH NODE" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2, 3):\u000aThree lymph nodes with no tumor seen.\u000aOR Consultation by: Alessandra Nascimento, MD.\u000aResident:\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. (R) sentinel lymph nodes", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afragment of fatty tissue containing three lymph nodes (0.6 cm, REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ain greatest dimension). Two smaller lymph nodes have been previously entirely\u000afrozen as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and the largest lymph node has been bisected and entirely\u000afrozen as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Non-frozen tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Tumor site (R) breast, short superior, long lateral", consists of\u000aa REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fibrofatty tissue fragment, oriented by sutures\u000adesignating superior (short suture) and lateral (long suture) margins. The\u000aattached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan/white skin demonstrates a possible REMOVED_DATE cm linear\u000awell-healed scar. The specimen is received with a radiograph demonstrating a\u000alocalizing wire in place within a central stellate mass. The specimen has been\u000apreviously inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The specimen is sectioned from anterior/posterior, revealing a\u000afairly well circumscribed firm tan/white mass (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which abuts\u000athe superior margin and approaches within REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm medial, and is greater than REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior\u000aand posterior margins. The remaining specimen is comprised of predominately of\u000asoft, lobulated, tan/yellow adipose with occasional intervening tan/white\u000afibrous septae. There are no additional lesions noted grossly.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire mass and surrounding fibrous tissue, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial, lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior, posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining fibrous tissue, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aAll fibrous tissue submitted. Localizing wire in place, section represented by\u000amicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aPart C, labeled "#3. Superior shave margin, whip stitch superior", consists of\u000aa REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fibrofatty tissue fragment, oriented by single suture\u000adesignating superior. This superior surface has been previously inked per\u000asurgeon in blue. The remaining tissue is inked black. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned and is submitted entirely.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, multi frags, ESS.\u000adb/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aMicroscopic/Diagnostic Dictation by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., on\u000a12/10/2004\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/13/2004\u000a[report_end]
