VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM FAULKNER HOSPITAL, BOSTON, MA:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, is present in one of 11 slides (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID;\u000alevels examined) (see note). The involved area measures approximately\u000a0.1 cm in size and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest (lateral) margin. A\u000acalcification is present associated with the ADH, but the majority of\u000acalcifications are present in cysts.\u000aApocrine cysts and calcifications are present.\u000aNote: The involved area consists of eight spaces involved by cells with a\u000acribriform pattern. The cell population does not appear completely\u000amonomorphic and some streaming of nuclei is present. The diagnosis of ADH\u000ais favored due to both qualitative and quantitative features.\u000aDr. Andrea Richardson also reviewed this case and concurs with the\u000adiagnosis of ADH.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Consult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BAI,HONGWEI,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aReceived from Faulkner Hospital, Pathology Department, 1153 Centre Street,\u000aBoston, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are twelve (12) slides.\u000aThe slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (2)", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (4)"\u000aand "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", corresponding to a left breast guided wire needle\u000alocalization excision (5.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to\u000athe accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000a[report_end]
