VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report *********** Resident: Joseph Woodward Carlson,\u000aM.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jonathan N Glickman, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Solid\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total: REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) superior, medial, lateral, anterior, posterior\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm) inferior (focal, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aOTHER FINDINGS Columnar cell change and hyperplasia.\u000aCysts and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - Tis pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Pending\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Microcalcifications, right breast.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire-directed excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Microcalcifications, right breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA. Tissue from right breast.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aWire and calcifications are in the center of the specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "Tissue from right breast", and consists of a wire-localized excision (4.0\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen has been inked by the surgeon per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A specimen\u000aradiograph accompanies the specimen, which demonstrates wire and calcifications\u000ain the center of the specimen. Approximately 50% of the breast tissue consists\u000aof firm white fibrous tissue with no discrete masses. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, multiple frags, ESS.\u000ajoc/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Joseph Woodward Carlson M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/8/2005\u000aFIRST ADDENDUM REMOVED_DATE  DR. DEBORAH DILLON\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (0.35 cm focus) (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) POSITIVE (2+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
