ast tissue wire-localized biopsy, short - superior, long -\u000alateral, whip stitch - chest wall margin", and consists of a previously inked\u000aand oriented wire-localized excision of breast tissue (4.5 cm from superior to\u000ainferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior)\u000awith an embedded localization wire and three orienting sutures (short -\u000asuperior, long - lateral, whip suture - posterior/chest wall). An accompanying\u000aradiograph shows an embedded localization wire along a cluster of\u000acalcifications with a nearby surgical clip. Sectioning from medial to lateral\u000areveals no discrete lesions; however, the area around the embedded wire appears\u000aheterogenous with approximately 70% fibrous tissue admixed with minority of\u000aadipose tissue. The entire specimen is examined microscopically.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial with some inferior, 8 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag each, ESS (wire-localized area in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags each, ESS,\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral with some superior, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aVKV/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-8455.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
