VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1) SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aComplex collection of apocrine microcysts and cysts correlating with\u000aradiographic masses (see NOTE).\u000aFlorid ductal hyperplasia.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aProbable hamartoma.\u000aBiopsy site.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000a2) SPECIMEN LABELED "SUPEROLATERAL LEFT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aBenign breast tissue with fibrosis and microcysts.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aNOTE:\u000aCase reviewed by Dr. A. Richardson, Breast Pathology Service.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 59 year old postmenopausal female, currently weaning prempro. REMOVED_DATE \u000amammogram supplemented by ultrasound demonstrates a left breast 3:00 axis\u000acomplex cyst. REMOVED_DATE  aspiration under u/s guidance for 1 ml of fluid with\u000adecrease in size of cyst. Cytology with atypical cells. Wire localization and\u000aexcision is recommended.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localization excision\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left mammogram\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Left breast tissue\u000a#2) Superolateral left breast tissue\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass(es) in specimen. Dr. Meyer.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HONG,XUEFEI,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. left breast tissue", consists of a wire localized\u000aexcision (5.2 cm from medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior, and\u000a2 cm from anterior to posterior) with short stitch denoting superior and long\u000astitch denoting lateral. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue;\u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aSectioning the specimen superior to inferior reveals 30% of the tissue is\u000afibrous tissue. No masses are grossly identified. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast with superior and posterior margins, mult frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast with inferior margin, mult frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast with medial, inferior margins, mult frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast with lateral margin, mult frags, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. superolateral left breast tissue", consists of a breast\u000aexcision (5.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is not oriented. The specimen is\u000ainked in black. Sectioning reveals 70% of the tissue is fibrous tissue. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast tissue, mult frags, ESS\u000axh\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
