d. The specimen is\u000asequentially submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, radially, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential bisected cross section, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential bisected cross section, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential bisected cross section, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, radially, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/19/2007\u000a[report_end]
