VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLEE, KENNETH, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LEE,KENNETH ROBERT,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY":\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia, single focus in one slide (slide 13).\u000aFibrocystic change with microscysts and sclerosing adenosis.\u000aMicrocalcifications associated with benign breast tissue.\u000aPrior biopsy site.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Needle localization left breast biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast calcification\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast tissue (mammo/FS)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HENDERSON,JOEL M.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen, received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and\u000a"left breast tissue", consists of four unoriented fragments of yellow/tan\u000afibroadipose tissue (from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000aspecimen is accompanied by a specimen radiograph which shows a localization\u000awire adjacent to an area of microcalcification which has been circled by a\u000aradiologist. Also present in the radiograph is an another wire adjacent to an\u000aarea of dense fibrosity. The localization wire is in place in the large\u000atissue fragment, which is approximately 50% firm, tan/white, fibrous tissue\u000aand 50% yellow adipose tissue. There is a small wire corresponding to the 2nd\u000awire described in the specimen radiograph, in place in the smallest tissue\u000afragment, which is 80% tan/white fibrous tissue and 20% yellow adipose tissue.\u000aThe remaining two fragments are 80% yellow adipose tissue and 20% tan/white\u000afibrous tissue. No discrete masses or othe lesions are identified in any of\u000athe tissue fragments. The specimen is inked and is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - largest fragment (area of calcification in #3&4), 6 f, ESS.\u000aMicro 7 - smallest fragment, bisected, 2 f, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - 2nd largest fragment, 7 f, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - 3rd largest fragment, 6 f, ESS.\u000aReports to: KANE, GREGORY, J. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: CYST - OTHER, NON-NEOPLASTIC\u000a[report_end]
