VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBROWN, FELIX, MARCEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BROWN,FELIX MARCEL,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED RE-EXCISION BIOPSY FOR 2 CLIPS:\u000aAtypical columnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and\u000asecretions.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aNo tumor seen.\u000aNOTE: Because of preoperative clinical or radiologic concern regarding the\u000apossibility of tumor, the margins of this specimen were inked, sampled, and\u000aexamined microscopically.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 44-year-old premenopausal female whose REMOVED_DATE mammogram demonstrates\u000anew left breast UOQ calcifications. REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy revealed columnar\u000aalteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions with atypia,\u000aexcision recommended.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localization excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast wire localized re-excision biopsy.\u000aRadiological exam - clip in specimen. JL.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by RIVERA,MIGUEL N,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name and\u000aunit number. The specimen consists of a single fragment of tissue that is\u000ainked by the surgeon. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen measures\u000a4.5 cm from superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom medial to lateral. There is a single wire in the specimen and a\u000aradiograph that shows the wire in relation to clips and calcifications. The\u000aspecimen is approximately 90% fibrous tissue and 10% fat. No defined masses\u000aare identified. Two (2) clips are present and are removed. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted for histologic evaluation. The clips are present in\u000amicro's 8 and 11.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  contain entire specimen from superior to inferior, multi frags,\u000aESS.\u000amir\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
