VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Michael H Roh, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Robert D Odze, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST MRI LOCALIZED EXCISION BIOPSY":\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, focal, within a papilloma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aBreast tissue with intraductal papillomas, apocrine cysts, CAPSS, and\u000acalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aDuctal hyperplasia.\u000aThe case was reviewed by Dr. A. Richardson (Breast Pathology), who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: right breast mammogram with architectural distortion. Right breast\u000aabnormal MRI.\u000aOperation: Right breast MRI-localized excision bx.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right breast MRI.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/#1. Right breast MRI-localized excision biopsy; short suture - superior,\u000along suture - lateral. To mammo/ FS rm.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Lesion wire in specimen. OR called/SL\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patients name, unit number,\u000aand "1. Right breast MRI-localized excision biopsy; short suture - superior,\u000along suture - lateral", and consists of a portion of yellow/pink focally\u000acauterized fibroadipose tissue (4.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with two (2) orienting\u000asuture (short - superior; long - lateral) and a needle-localization wire in\u000aplace (entering laterally). The specimen is inked by the prosector according\u000ato the breast inking protocol: The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: Posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from medial to lateral, revealing approximately 80% white/tan,\u000adiffusely dense, focally cystic (cyst measuring up to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest\u000adimension) stroma and 20% yellow lobulated adipose tissue. A definitive gross\u000alesion is not identified in the region of the wire. However, the accompanying\u000aradiograph and radiology consults states, "Lesion in wire in specimen; OR\u000acalled/SL". The needle-localization wire traverses the specimen from the\u000alateral/superior aspect and exits at the inferior aspect. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted sequentially from medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, sequentially from medial to lateral,\u000amultiple frags, ESS.\u000aDFI/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Michael H Roh M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
