VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aHORNICK, JASON, L., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by HORNICK,JASON L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1) RIGHT BREAST INFERIOR LOWER LOWER OUTER QUADRANT, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION\u000aFOR MICROCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia involving sclerosing adenosis.\u000aCalcifications in association with sclerosing adenosis.\u000a2) RIGHT BREAST SUPERIOR UPPER OUTER QUADRANT, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR\u000aMICROCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia involving sclerosing adenosis.\u000aCalcifications in association with benign breast tissue and sclerosing\u000aadenosis.\u000aCysts.\u000aNOTE: Dr. J. Connolly (Breast Pathology Service) has also reviewed this case\u000aand agrees with the diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Patient with history of ALH in right upper outer quadrant, now with\u000atwo new areas of microcalcification, right upper outer quadrant and\u000aright lower outer quadrant.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization x 2.\u000aOperative findings: Normal appearing tissue, positive specimen mammo,\u000apositive calc.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast calcification, 2 areas, right upper outer\u000aquadrant/right lower outer quadrant.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Right breast inferior lower outer quadrant\u000amicrocalcifications\u000a2) Right breast superior upper outer quadrant microcalcifications\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aCalcifications in each of two specimens.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HAHN,HEJIN P.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is recieved fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart 1, "Right breast inferior lower outer quadrant microcalcifications",\u000aconsists of a piece of breast tissue (5 cm from superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom medial to lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior). The specimen\u000ais received inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green;\u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen contains a wire, protruding\u000afrom the inferior/anterior portion of the specimen. The specimen is\u000aaccompanied by a radiograph which shows a wire and an area of\u000amicrocalcifications. Serial sectioning reveals that the specimen is 40% firm,\u000awhite fibrous tissue. No lesions are grossly identified. The entire specimen\u000ais submitted serially from inferior to superior.\u000aMicro 1: Inferior margin, perpendicular, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Serial sections, multiple frags, ESS\u000aMicro 8: Superior margin, perpendicular, 2 frags, ESS\u000aPart 2, "Right breast superior upper outer quadrant microcalcifications",\u000aconsists of a piece of breast tissue (4 cm from medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000asuperior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior). The specimen is\u000areceived inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green;\u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen contains a hook wire which\u000aruns along the lateral aspect of the specimen. The specimen is accompanied by\u000aa radiograph which demonstrates a wire and a focal area of\u000amicrocalcifications. Serial sectioning reveals that the specimen is 80% firm,\u000awhite fibrous tissue. No lesions are grossly identified. The entire specimen\u000ais submitted serially from medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Medial margin, perpendicular, 6 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Serial sections, multiple frags, ESS\u000aMicro 17: Lateral and posterior margin, perpendicular, 2 frags, ESS\u000ahph\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
