VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Peter M Sadow, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jonathan N Glickman, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY (253 GM):\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar cell changes with focal atypia.\u000aIntraductal papillomas.\u000aFibroadenomatoid changes.\u000aAdenosis.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aNo invasive carcinoma seen, including deep margin.\u000aB. LEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY (217 GM):\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU with pagetoid spread.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia with associated calcifications.\u000aColumnar cell changes with focal atypia.\u000aAdenosis.\u000aFibroadenomatoid changes.\u000aIntraductal papilloma.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aNo invasive carcinoma seen, including deep margin.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: FHx breast CA, pos. hx LCIS, mammo with new microcalcifications, pt.\u000arequests bilateral mastectomies.\u000aOperation: Bilat simple mastectomies.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Bilateral breast CA\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. R breast tissue - marking stitch - short=superior, long=lateral\u000aB/2. L breast tissue marking stitch - short=superior, long=lateral\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. R breast tissue - marking stitch - short=superior, long=lateral",\u000aconsists of a 253 g right mastectomy specimen (14.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), oriented\u000aby sutures designating superior (short suture) and lateral (long suture)\u000aportion of the specimen. The attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan/white skin is almost\u000aentirely comprised of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm areola and central unremarkable REMOVED_DATE cm\u000anipple. Immediately lateral to and abutting the lateral quater of the nipple\u000ais a REMOVED_DATE cm curve of linear tan/white discoloration, likely scar. Deep surface\u000acomprised of a smooth fascial plain (inked black). The specimen is sectioned,\u000arevealing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fibromembranous, retracted area in the right\u000aupper radial quadrant (? Prior biopsy cavity), REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin. In\u000aaddition, there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm cystic lesion filled with a thick\u000atan/yellow amorphous material, REMOVED_DATE cm lateral to the previously described\u000alesion and REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin in this area (right upper radial\u000aquadrant). Remaining specimen is comprised of extremely dense granular fibrous\u000atissue (maximally REMOVED_DATE cm, medial to lateral), with occasional dilated ducts\u000afilled with a deep tan yellow fluid. There are no additional discreet masses.\u000aDense fibrous tissue comprises at least 60% of specimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, possible lateral scar, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Possible cavity (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is closest to deep margin), 5 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_DATE cm cyst, lateral to possible cavity, with closest deep\u000amargin, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central breast, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS\u000aNOTE: Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID are sequential representative sections from irregular\u000afibrous dense tissue (medial to lateral)\u000aPart B, "#2. L breast tissue, marking stitch short superior, long lateral",\u000aconsists of a 217 gm, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm left mastectomy specimen. The\u000aattached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan/white ovoid skin is almost entirely comprised of a\u000a3.0 cm diameter, areola and central REMOVED_DATE cm everted, unremarkable nipple. There\u000aare no scars grossly. Deep surface is comprise of a smooth fascial plain\u000a(inked black). The specimen is sectioned, revealing diffusely dense, granular,\u000acystic fibrous tissue (maximally REMOVED_DATE cm, medial to lateral), with occasional\u000adilated ducts filled with a thick, tan/yellow fluid. Closest overlying freely\u000amobile deep margin is within REMOVED_DATE cm of the dense fibrous tissue. There are no\u000adiscreet lesions grossly. Fibrous tissue comprises of at least 60% of the\u000aspecimen. There is scant grossly uninvolved fibrous tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential representative sections from lateral to medial (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is\u000alateral most fibrous tissue, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is upper outer quadrant, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is\u000alower outer quadrant, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is central breast, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is lower inner\u000aquadrant, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is upper inner quadrant, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is medial most fibrous\u000atissue), multiple frags, RSS\u000aDB/cdm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Peter M Sadow M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/26/2005\u000a[report_end]
