VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Priscilla S Chang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: None\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR TWO CLUSTERS OF CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aSingle focus of atypical ductal hyperplasia present in a background of florid\u000ausual hyperplasia (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, levels examined).\u000aFlorid usual hyperplasia with associated microcalcifications.\u000aExtensive sclerosing adenosis and apocrine cysts.\u000aMicrocalcifications present in association with benign epithelium.\u000aDr. Susan Lester has reviewed slides REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localized biopsy x 2 wires.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast calcifications.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Left breast wire localized biopsy x 2 wires - short suture superior, long\u000asuture lateral - to mammo via frozen section room.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aBoth clusters of calcifications are in the specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "#1 Left breast wire localized biopsy x 2 wires - short suture superior,\u000along suture lateral", and consists of a single fragment of breast tissue (4.5 x\u000a9.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm), received with two orienting sutures and two wires. The specimen\u000ais accompanied by a radiograph, which demonstrates two wires in the specimen,\u000aadjacent to two areas of calcifications. The calcifications are located next to\u000athe inferior and superior margins. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. Serial sectioning demonstrates\u000athat the specimen is approximately 90% composed of firm, white fibrous tissue.\u000aCorresponding to the two areas of calcifications are two areas of small cysts\u000awith cheesy white secretions and calcifications. The first area is located REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the closest superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the anterior margin, 2 cm from the inferior margin, approximately 1 cm\u000afrom the medial margin, and greater than 5 cm from the lateral margin. The\u000asecond area is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, 2 cm from the superior\u000amargin, approximately 2 cm from the medial margin, and approximately 4 cm from\u000athe lateral margin. The specimen is entirely submitted. Approximately REMOVED_DATE %\u000aof the specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicular, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections from medial to lateral including first (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aand second area of calcifications (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 12 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of specimen from medial to lateral, multiple frags,\u000aESS.\u000apsc/elw\u000apsc/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Priscilla S Chang M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Tan A Ince M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a6/23/2005\u000a[report_end]
