VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Elgida Radoncipi, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia, focal (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aCalcifications associated with columnar cell change, cysts and apocrine cysts.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aE-cadherin stain highlights absent membranous staining in ALH (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 76 yo F whose REMOVED_DATE  mammogram demonstrated L UOQ calcifications;\u000abiopsy is recommended for one group of calcifications; pt was unable to\u000atolerate core biopsy (pt is on HRT)\u000aOperation: L breast wire-localized excision\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal L mammogram\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue (short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral,\u000awhip stitch/chest wall margin)\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aExam Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Specimen Image\u000aDate/Time: REMOVED_DATE  14:23\u000a(TRANSCRIBED FROM RADIOLOGY REPORT IN LMR) Specimen radiography confirmed that\u000athe target tissue and clip were contained in the specimen. The findings were\u000acalled to OR by Dr Shadpour Demehri at 2:25 pm on the date of exam.\u000aIMPRESSION: Left mammographic (crosshair) localization for surgical biopsy of\u000athe clustered micro-calcifications in the 2 o'clock region at a middle depth\u000acompleted.\u000aRADIOLOGISTS: SIGNATURES:\u000aDEMEHRI, SHADPOUR\u000aGIESS, CATHERINE S GIESS, CATHERINE S\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "left breast tissue", and consists of an irregular fragment of fibroadipose\u000atissue (5.4 cm M-L x REMOVED_DATE cm S-I x REMOVED_DATE cm A-P) with a short suture designating\u000asuperior, long suture designating lateral, and a whipstitch designating chest\u000awall margin. Centricity review of the specimen radiograph reveals a wire in the\u000aspecimen with associated calcifications. The specimen is received with a needle\u000alocalization wire entering the anterosuperior aspect of the specimen, with no\u000adefinitive exit. Specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to\u000aexhibit 98% dense white fibrous tissue to 2% yellow lobulated adipose tissue.\u000aNo definitive masses or lesions can be grossly appreciated. The specimen is\u000asubmitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular medial margin, multi frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Body, sequentially submitted from medial to lateral to include\u000aarea designated by needle localization wire (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular lateral margin, 2 frags in each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000ajc\u005cpab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aFriday REMOVED_MONTH 06, 2009 at 03:18:56PM\u000a[report_end]
