VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aTRESELER, PATRICK, ANDREW, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by TRESELER,PATRICK ANDREW,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST MASS":\u000aBreast tissue with dense interlobular fibrosis and a single microscopic\u000afocus of benign ductal hyperplasia.\u000aNo tumor seen.\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aBreast tissue with dense interlobular fibrosis.\u000aNo tumor seen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Mass left breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Mass left breast (FS if indicated).\u000a#2. Left breast tissue (permanent).\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000a#1. LEFT BREAST MASS:\u000aNo areas suspicious for invasive carcinoma.\u000aNo areas suitable for frozen section. Gross only.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KRAUS,MADELEINE,M.D.\u000aReceived fresh, labeled with the patient's name, number and "#1. left breast\u000amass", is a 3 x 3 x 2 cm mass of dense fibrous connective tissue and scant\u000aadipose tissue. The cut surface of the specimen is homogeneous, white and\u000apliable; there are no areas suspicious for invasive carcinoma, and no areas\u000asuitable for frozen section. The specimen is inked, step sectioned, and\u000asubmitted in sequential cassettes.\u000aMICRO #1-10: Left breast mass (Specimen #1), mult frags, 10 cass, ESS.\u000aSpecimen #2, received fixed, labeled with the patient's name, number and "#2.\u000aleft breast tissue", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of dense white\u000afibrous connective scant adipose. The specimen is inked, step sectioned, and\u000asubmitted in the same cassette.\u000aMICRO #11: Left breast tissue (Specimen #2), 3 frags, 1 cass, ESS.\u000aReports to: KOFSKY, EDWARD, R. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
