VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aHORNICK, JASON, L., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by HORNICK,JASON L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aBreast tissue with atypical ductal hyperplasia (block 6) not associated\u000awith calcifications, and calcifications associated with benign\u000aepithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aNOTE: This case was also reviewed with Dr. Susan Lester (Breast Pathology\u000aService), who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 39 year old premenopausal female with a family history of breast\u000acancer whose REMOVED_DATE  mammogram demonstrate a 4 mm cluster of\u000acalcifications in the L subareolar region, not amenable to core biopsy.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localization excision\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal L mammogram\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left breast tissue for mammo\u000aRADIOLOGY: Ca++ are in specimen. D.N. Smith,MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SADOW,PETER MARK,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. left breast tissue (long lat, short superior, whip stitch\u000adeep margins)", and consists of a breast excision specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm that has a short suture placed by the surgeon indicating the superior\u000amargin and a long suture indicating the lateral margin. The specimen is inked\u000aby the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. There is a localizing wire entering the specimen at the lateral\u000amargin and coursing through towards the anterior pole of the specimen. On\u000asection, there is white fibrous tissue (20% of the specimen) running along the\u000alateral margin towards the anterior pole. The remainder of the specimen is\u000acomposed of unremarkable, focally hemorrhagic, yellow lobulated adipose tissue.\u000aThe path of the wire and wire localized area is submitted in micros one to\u000athree. The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial and is\u000aentirely submitted. The specimen radiograph as read by radiology shows\u000acalcifications localized by the wire.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  wire, localized area, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of fibrous portion of specimen, 5 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, lateral to medial, 12 frags, ESS\u000assa\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
