VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: GREGORY J KANE M.D.\u000aCASE: BG-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Justine A Barletta, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Kenneth R Lee, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aSclerosing papilloma with apocrine adenosis and focal areas of flat\u000aepithelial atypia.\u000aNo in situ carcinoma or atypical ductal hyperplasia present.\u000aB. SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE INFERIOR TO SPECIMEN #1":\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aNote: Case reviewed by Andrea Richardson in breast pathology.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Core biopsy of microcalcifications R breast -> atypical lobular\u000ahyperplasia. Surgical excision recommended.\u000aOperation: Right breast resection\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Atypical lobular hyperplasia\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a#1) Right breast tissue with wire\u000a#2) Breast tissue inferior to #1\u000aRADIOLOGY: #1) Calcifications and needle localization wire identifed.\u000a#2) No lesions identified. DIR.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "R. breast tissue, short stitch lateral, long stitch inferior",\u000aconsists of oriented breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior,\u000a0.5 cm from medial to lateral and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior. A needle\u000alocalization wire traverses the center of the specimen. The specimen is inked\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe tissue consists of dense fibrous tissue. The specimen is sectioned from\u000asuperior to inferior. There are no grossly identifiable lesions. The specimen\u000ais entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 12 frags (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, superior; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID inferior), ESS\u000aPart B, labeled "tissue inferior to specimen", consists of one unoriented\u000afragment of fibrofatty tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is\u000ainked black, serially sectioned, and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 5 frags, ESS\u000ajub/jl\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Justine A Barletta M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Kenneth R Lee M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
