VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNUCCI, MARISA, ROSE, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NUCCI,MARISA ROSE,M.D.\u000a1) RIGHT BREAST, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS:\u000aFibroadenoma (1.5 cm) with adjacent atypical lobular hyperplasia\u000awith pagetoid spread.\u000aIntraductal papilloma.\u000aCore biopsy site with repair reaction.\u000aMargins examined microscopically.\u000aSlides reviewed by Dr. A. Richardson, breast pathology, who concurs.\u000a2) RIGHT BREAST TISSUE, BREAST REDUCTION (2970 gms):\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aSkin with seborrheic keratosis.\u000a3) LEFT BREAST TISSUE, BREAST REDUCTION (3070 gms):\u000aBenign breast tissue with columnar alteration of lobules with prominent\u000asnouts and secretions, cysts, and epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aIntramammary lymph node with no significant pathologic change.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Bilateral enlarged breast.\u000aOperation: Bilateral breast reduction.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Bilateral breast hypertrophy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Fibroadenoma, from right breast.\u000a2. Right breast tissue.\u000a3. Left breast tissue.\u000aRadiology Report:\u000aA mass is in the specimen. JM.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by REIMANN,JULIE DYLAN REGAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, fibroadenoma", consists of a piece of fibroadipose\u000atissue (6.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is unoriented as submitted. There is\u000aa wire protruding from one (1) aspect of the breast, and the specimen is\u000aaccompanied by a radiograph and is red, and a mass is present in the specimen.\u000aThe specimen is inked in black and serially sectioned to reveal firmly adipose\u000atissue with an area of lobulated, cystic, well-circumscribed tissue (1.5 cm in\u000alongest dimension) which is grossly consistent with fibroadenoma.\u000aRepresentative sections are taken of the specimen and submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  area of breast consistent with fibroadenoma, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: uninvolved breast, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, right breast tissue", consists of skin and breast\u000atissue, weighing 2970 grams, and measures 54 x 35 x 5 cm in depth. There are\u000aeight (8) separate fragments of fibroadipose tissue and one (1) separate\u000afragment of skin measuring 26 x 11 cm. There is a brown-pigmented portion of\u000athe skin, REMOVED_DATE cm in length, which is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the nearest skin\u000aellipse edge. This skin ellipse edge is inked in black, and the lesion is\u000asectioned and representative segments are submitted. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned to reveal fibroadipose tissue (approximately 10% of which is fibrous\u000atissue, and the rest is adipose tissue). There are no lesions grossly\u000aidentified.\u000aMicro 5: brown-pigmented lesion on skin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous breast tissue, REMOVED_DATE frags each, RSS.\u000aPart three, labeled "#3, left breast tissue", consists of skin and attached\u000abreast tissue weighing 3,070 grams. There are thirteen (13) pieces of tissue in\u000aall; ten of which are fibroadipose tissue, one of which is a large piece of\u000afibroadipose tissue with attached skin, measuring 53 x 13 x 5 cm deep, and two\u000a(2) fragments of skin, measuring 17 cm and 24 cm in length. There are no\u000aidentifiable skin lesions, grossly.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000ajdr\u000aReports to: ORGILL, DENNIS, PAUL M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY\u000a[report_end]
