VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: SARA RUSSELL M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Stacey A. Simons, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST WIRE LOCALISED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia with apocrine features, associated with\u000acalcifications, is present as a single focus (0.15 cm) in one of 9 slides\u000a(block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). Immunoperoxidase studies reveal that the ADH is positive for\u000ae-cadherin, positive for estrogen and progesterone receptors and only weakly\u000apositive for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu. No necrosis is present.\u000aADH is REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present. An immunoperoxidase study confirms that\u000athe LCIS is negative for e-cadherin and positive for ER and PR.\u000aColumnar cell change associated with microcalcifications\u000aNote: No invasive carcinoma is seen after complete microscopic examination of\u000athe specimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Right breast needle directed biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: Targeted microcalcifications and the wire are within the\u000aspecimen. Dr. Twohig.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Right breast tissue short superior, long lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue short superior/long lateral", and consists of an\u000airregular tan/white to tan/yellow portion of breast tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000athat has a short suture marking superior and long suture marking lateral.\u000aThere is a needle localization wire entering the lateral aspect of the\u000aspecimen. The specimen radiograph shows the wire and a small cluster of\u000acalcifications. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol (blue equals\u000aanterior, black equals posterior, red equals superior, green equals inferior,\u000ayellow equals lateral, and orange equals medial). The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from lateral to medial to show parenchyma with focally dense\u000atan/white fibrous tissue (45%). There is a cystic space REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest\u000adimension, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin,\u000a0.2 cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. The remaining\u000aparenchyma consists of tan/yellow adipose tissue. The entire specimen is\u000aexamined microscopically.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen sequentially sectioned from lateral to medial,\u000amulti frags, ESS.\u000aDRD/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/26/2006\u000a[report_end]
