rface is tan/yellow and\u000ahomogeneous with focal areas of dense white fibrous tissue constituting\u000aapproximately 10% of the breast parenchyma. No discrete lesions or areas of\u000adisruption are grossly identified. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin and breast tissues, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional sections of breast tissue, mult frags, RSS.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/23/2008\u000a[report_end]
