VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Christian J. Davidson, M.D.; Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.; Vania Nose, MD, PhD\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A REMOVED_DATE CM HYPOECHOIC MASS:\u000aFibroadenoma (0.6 cm; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aOther findings:\u000aDiffuse columnar cell change with calcifications and focal atypia, including\u000ainvolving fibroadenoma epithelium.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aB. RIGHT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR AN AREA OF ARCHITECTURAL DISTORTION\u000aAND MICROCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA, focal, involving a nodule of columnar cell change\u000awith calcifications, sclerosis, and cysts (1.5 cm; see NOTE).\u000aOther findings:\u000aFibroadenoma (0.3 cm)\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aNOTE: The REMOVED_DATE cm area of columnar cell change and sclerosis correlates well\u000awith the radiological findings of architectural distortion (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). Within\u000athis lesion a very small focus of ALH is present (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID double\u000aimmunohistochemical stain performed on the sclerotic lesion shows myoepithelial\u000acells are present in all sclerotic duct profiles.\u000aC. LEFT BREAST DUCT EXCISION:\u000aIntraductal papilloma (0.5 cm).\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 45 year old woman with architectural distortion on screening mammogram\u000aright separate complex cystic lesion incidental found on right which had\u000aaspiration and returned atypia; on clinical exam had single poor clear\u000adischarge from left nipple.\u000aOperation: Right needle localization, breast biopsy two lesions left duct\u000aexcisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left nipple discharge, right abnormal mammogram.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000a1. Mass in specimen. EP Frost, MD\u000a2. Architectural distortion and calcification in specimen. EP Frost, MD\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue cystic lesion short suture superior, long lateral.\u000aB/2. Right breast tissue architectural distortion short suture superior, long\u000alateral.\u000aC/3. Left breast duct suture in on the duct.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "right breast tissue cystic lesion, short suture superior, long\u000alateral", consists of an irregular tan/yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose\u000abreast tissue (3.5 cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm anterior to posterior) with a short suture designating superior margin, and\u000aa long suture designating lateral margin. There is a needle localization wire\u000ain place which enters through the lateral aspect of the specimen and exits\u000athrough the medial posterior aspect of the specimen. The specimen has been\u000apreviously inked per pathology protocol (superior red, inferior green, medial\u000aorange, lateral yellow, anterior blue, posterior black) and is serially\u000asectioned from superior to inferior. The cut surface is tan/yellow and\u000ahomogenous with focal areas of dense white fibrous tissue constituting\u000aapproximately 20% of the breast parenchyma. No discrete lesions are grossly\u000aidentified. The specimen is submitted in its entirety. The specimen is\u000areceived with a radiograph which shows a wire and a density in the specimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections superior to inferior, 1 frag each, ESS,\u000ablock REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include designated area in specimen radiograph.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "Right breast architectural distortion, short superior, long\u000alateral", consists of an irregular tan/yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose\u000abreast tissue (3.8 cm anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, and\u000a2.4 cm medial to lateral) with a short suture designating the superior margin,\u000aand a long suture designating the lateral margin. There is a needle\u000alocalization wire in place which enters through the superior aspect of the\u000aspecimen and exits through the inferior aspect of the specimen. The specimen\u000ahas been previously inked per the surgeon per pathology protocol (anterior\u000ablue, posterior black, superior red, inferior green, medial orange, lateral\u000ayellow) and is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior. There are focal\u000aareas of dense white fibrous tissue constituting approximately 90% of the\u000abreast parenchyma. No discrete lesions or areas of disruption are grossly\u000aidentified. The specimen is submitted in its entirety. The specimen is\u000asubmitted in its entirety. The specimen is received with a radiograph which\u000ashows a wire, calcifications and an area of architectural distortion in the\u000aspecimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, 4 frags, ESS,\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections anterior to posterior, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to\u000ainclude area designated per specimen radiograph, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "left breast tissue duct", consists of an irregular tan/yellow\u000alobulated portion of fibroadipose breast tissue (3.0 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm superior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior). There is a suture\u000apresent designating "duct". The specimen has been previously inked per\u000apathology protocol (superior red, inferior green, medial orange, lateral\u000ayellow, anterior blue, and posterior black). The suture is located on the\u000aanterior surface of the specimen. The cut surface is tan/yellow and homogenous\u000awith focal areas of dense white fibrous tissue constituting approximately 90%\u000aof the breast parenchyma. No discrete lesions are grossly identified. The\u000aspecimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS,\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections medial to lateral, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include\u000aduct, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aSEK/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/7/2008\u000a[report_end]
