VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: RAYMOND J REILLY MB,BCH,BAO\u000aCASE: BG-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Stacey A. Simons, M.D.; Martin C Chang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A\u000aCLIP:\u000aFocal atypical ductal hyperplasia (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia and columnar cell change with associated\u000amicrocalcifications.\u000aCore biopsy site changes.\u000aNo residual papilloma is identified.\u000aNote: By report, the patient underwent a prior core needle biopsy for\u000acalcifications showing an intraductal papilloma. There is no malignancy seen\u000aupon microscopic examination of the entire specimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Right needle localized breast excision.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Right breast mass (to mammo) via FS room\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "right breast mass", and consists of an unoriented right\u000abreast biopsy (5.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a localization wire in place and no\u000aorienting sutures. An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates scattered\u000acalcifications near the hook-wire tip, and shows the clip within a separate\u000aregion that corresponds to dense fibrous tissue. The specimen is inked blue\u000aover the entire surface and serially sectioned. The tissue consists of 90%\u000ayellow adipose tissue and 10% dense fibrous tissue. There is hemorrhage along\u000athe wire tract, and no masses or lesions are identified. The region of the clip\u000acorresponds to block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, although the clip is not identified (blocks have been\u000aradiographed). The region of the wire tip is in blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast biopsy with all fibrous tissue submitted (wire localized\u000ato REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, clip region corresponds to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining adipose tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BG-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aSAS:lc:sas\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a3/5/2007\u000a[report_end]
