VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Travis J Hollmann, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST NEEDLE - LOCALIZED EXCISION:\u000aBreast epithelium with columnar cell change within calcifications.\u000aCalcifications in benign breast epithelium.\u000aDense fibrous stroma.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aThe entire specimen was submitted and reviewed microscopically.\u000aNOTE: Dr. Ince, Breast Pathology service, reviewed the case and agrees.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 44 year old with abnormal mammo - right; family history of breast\u000acancer (sister diagnosed at age 31). REMOVED_DATE - outside mammo - (illegible)\u000aMedical Center - granular calcs in right upper quadrant; REMOVED_DATE  - right breast\u000acore biopsy - UOQ - "ADH" associated with calcs.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized excision, biopsy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right needle localized --> paint to protocol.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aLocalization targeting the clip. Intact wire contained in specimen. The clip\u000ais not seen. S. Nielsen REMOVED_DATE  11:00 A.M.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patients name, unit number,\u000aand "#1 - right needle loc - paint to protocol", and consists of a single\u000awire-localized breast excision specimen, received pre-inked with a localization\u000awire intact and entering the lateral aspect of the specimen. The specimen also\u000acontains a short suture and a long suture located on the superior and lateral\u000amargins, respectively. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE cm\u000am-l, REMOVED_DATE cm s-i, and REMOVED_DATE cm a-p. The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph,\u000awhich shows a wire in place and no evidence of a surgical clip. The specimen\u000ais serially sectioned from superior to inferior into twelve slices, whereby the\u000alocalization wire passes through slices five and six. Styrofoam beads are\u000apresent in slices four through seven. The cut parenchyma is comprised of\u000aapproximately 85% dense, white/tan fibrous tissue and 15% fibrofatty tissue.\u000aThere is no evidence of discrete mass. Cystic change is located in slices\u000athree and four. The entire specimen is submitted for histological review,\u000aconsecutively from superior to inferior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice one, superior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice two, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice three, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice four, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID+REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice five, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice six, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice seven, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice eight, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice nine, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice ten, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice eleven, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice twelve, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aNOTE: The entire specimen is submitted for histological review.\u000aTH/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
