VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLEE, KENNETH, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LEE,KENNETH ROBERT,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform and solid types (low to intermediate\u000anuclear grade), present in 4 of 9 blocks (best seen on the deeper levels\u000aof blocks 5 and 7). No necrosis or calcifications are associated with\u000aDCIS.\u000aDCIS is < REMOVED_DATE cm from the margin in multiple blocks (not oriented).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present.\u000aCalcifications are associated with cysts and columnar alteration of\u000alobules with prominent snouts and secretions.\u000aNote: The DCIS is intermingled with areas of atypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aand appears to be incidental to the mammographic findings.\u000aThere is an area of extravasated cells in stroma in the original level of\u000ablock 1. This area is not present on deeper levels and appears to be an\u000aartifact.\u000aThis carcinoma would be classified as AJCC Tis NX MX.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION:\u000aSeverely atypical ductal hyperplasia is present in one of one block. The\u000aADH is < REMOVED_DATE cm from the margin.\u000aNote: Focal involvement by DCIS cannot be excluded.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Microcalcifications of right breast, 2 separate clusters.\u000aOperation: Wire localization and right breast resection.\u000aOperative findings: No palpable masses.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Microcalcifications right breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue\u000a2. Right breast tissue\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aBoth groups of calcifications are in the specimen, C. Denison, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BAILEY,GERALD P.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, "right breast tissue microcalcifications", consists of four fragments\u000aof unoriented fibroadipose tissue (5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate), with a\u000asingle fragment containing a wire (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The fragments are\u000ainked in black, serially sectioned and entirely submitted.\u000aA specimen radiograph reveals two clusters of calcifications and a localization\u000awire.\u000aMicro sections:\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fragment of tissue, containing the wire, 3 frags each cass, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of right breast tissue, 4 frags each cass, ESS.\u000aPart two, "right breast tissue", is one fragment of unoriented fibroadipose\u000atissue (2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 9: right breast tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aReports to: KANE, GREGORY, J. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
