VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: EREN D YEH M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-10-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Elizabeth M. Manion, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, LOWER INNER, 10G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aINVASIVE TUBULAR CARCINOMA, well differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson\u000agrade I/III) (tubule score=1, nuclear score=1, mitoses score=1, total=3), is\u000apresent, at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size in this limited specimen.\u000aAn immunohistochemical stain for p63 and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID confirms the absence of\u000amyoepithelial cells in the invasive carcinoma.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is present in this limited specimen.\u000aNo carcinoma in situ is present in this limited specimen.\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA arising in the background of columnar cell change\u000aand flat epithelial atypia with associated microcalcifications.\u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 71 year old woman with clustered MOC and amorphous ca++ in the right\u000aslightly lower, slightly inner quadrant. History of ADH on the right in 2005.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: Nonpalpable and calcifications.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: lower inner\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 10G Stereotactic Vacuum-assisted\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 10G Stereotactic Vacuum-assisted A with ca++, B without ca++ - Orange\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, MRN\u000anumber, and "right", consists of tan/yellow breast biopsy cores. The specimen\u000ain cassette A is marked with calcifications. The specimen in cassette B is\u000amarked without calcifications. The specimen is entirely submitted for\u000ahistological examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette A, with calcifications, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette B, without calcifications, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: 6733.\u000aklv/ag\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following\u000acriteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not\u000ayet been determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor\u000acells but only a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >30% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for\u000ainvestigational use only.\u000aThe immunoperoxidase, immunofluorescence and in-situ hybridization tests\u000aperformed at Brigham and Women's Hospital were developed and their performance\u000acharacteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the\u000aDepartment of Pathology at BWH. They have not been cleared or approved by the\u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such\u000aclearance or approval is not necessary.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aThursday February 18, 2010 at 08:50:32AM\u000a[report_end]
