VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, well differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson\u000agrade I/III), REMOVED_DATE cm. Calcifications are present in tumor stroma.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is present.\u000aInvasive carcinoma is present at the lateral and anterior margins and is\u000a< REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin. The remaining margins appear free of\u000ainvasive carcinoma.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present as multiple foci in multiple blocks.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is associated with the invasive carcinoma\u000a(levels examined). ADH is associated with calcifications.\u000aBenign calcifications are present.\u000aNote: This carcinoma would be classified as AJCC REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc NX MX with multiple\u000afoci of invasion (see also specimen below).\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results (block 9):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE - LOW\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu NEGATIVE (0)\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, well differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson\u000agrade I/III), REMOVED_DATE cm (block 19; seen only on the original slide).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is present.\u000aInvasive carcinoma is present < REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin. The\u000aremaining margins appear free of carcinoma.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present as multiple foci in multiple blocks.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is present as multiple foci in multiple\u000ablocks and is associated with calcifications (levels examined).\u000aCalcifications are associated with benign epithelium.\u000aNote: Immunoperoxidase studies were attempted on the invasive carcinoma.\u000aHowever, carcinoma was no longer present on the deeper levels.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast calcifications.\u000aOperation: Right needle directed breast biopsies x 3.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast calcifications.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue at 12 o'clock with wires 1 and 2.\u000a2. Right breast tissue lateral around wire #3 (short = superior,\u000along = lateral).\u000aRadiology report #1: Mass and calcifications in specimen. J. Meyer MD.\u000aRadiology report #2: Calcifications in specimen. J. Meyer, MD.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHAN,JENNIFER A.,M.D.,C.M.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, sublabeled "#1, right breast tissue at 12 o'clock", consists of a\u000asingle fragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with two\u000a(2) orienting sutures and two (2) needle localization wires in place. The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral\u000a= yellow; medial = orange. There are no masses grossly suspicious for\u000acarcinoma. The entire specimen is submitted including all margins.\u000aMicro 1: superior margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior half of specimen including anterior, posterior, medial\u000aand lateral margins, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior half of specimen including anterior and lateral margin, 1\u000afrag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior half of specimen includng medial and deep margins, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, sublabeled "#2, right breast tissue, lateral around wire #3",\u000aconsists of a single fragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.0 cm) with two (2) orienting sutures in place. A needle localization wire is\u000anot received with the specimen. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior =\u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. There are no areas\u000agrossly suspicious for carcinoma. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral half of specimen serially submitted from superior to\u000ainferior, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial half of specimen serially submitted from superior to\u000ainferior, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 24: inferior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
