VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1) RIGHT BREAST, MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY:\u000aRESIDUAL INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA (0.2 cm), well differentiated\u000a(modified Bloom-Richardson grade I/III), present as a single microscopic\u000afocus adjacent to the most superior and anterior of two (2) biopsy\u000acavities in the upper outer quadrant.\u000aLymphatic/vascular invasion is not identified.\u000aSecond biopsy site with no residual invasive tumor identified.\u000aRESIDUAL LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU.\u000aSkin with cicatrix.\u000aFibrocystic change with microcysts.\u000aFourteen (14) lymph nodes with no tumor seen.\u000a2) SPECIMEN LABELED "ADDITIONAL AXILLARY NODE", BIOPSY:\u000aOne (1) lymph node with no tumor seen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 49-year-old with right breast cancer. Previous path report shows that\u000aa biopsy on REMOVED_DATE showed well-differentiated invasive lobular carcinoma on 2\u000abiopsies.\u000aOperation: Right modified radical mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast with nipple, stitch on axillary tail.\u000a2. Additional axillary node.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by RODIG,SCOTT J.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "Right breast with nipple" and consists of a 485 gram\u000amodified radical mastectomy specimen with overall dimensions 17 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. There is an ellipse of tan-white skin measuring 12 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There\u000ais a scar measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in the upper outer quadrant. There is an areola\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter and a nipple measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter. The\u000aaxillary tail measures 8 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm in total. Sectioning the specimen\u000areveals areas of hemorrhage consistent with prior biopsy cavity located in the\u000aupper outer quadrant. The first biopsy site (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is located in\u000athe upper outer quadrant deep to the skin ellipse. The second biopsy site of\u000ahemorrhage measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm is located inferior and posterior to\u000athe first biopsy cavity and is closer to the resection margin (0.2 cm from\u000adeep resection margin). The closest of the two (2) biopsy cavities approach\u000aone another is REMOVED_DATE cm. In addition, careful sectioning reveals in the lower\u000ainner quadrant additional area of hemorrhage, which may or may not represent\u000abiopsy site measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. This site is located REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe other site(s) of biopsy. Careful sectioning of the axillary tissue\u000areveals the presence of fourteen (14) candidate lymph nodes which are entirely\u000asubmitted for analysis.\u000aMicro 1: 1st biopsy site in relation closest to skin surface, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 2: 1st biopsy site in relation to deep margin perpendicular, 2 frags,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro 3: 1st biopsy site, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  2nd biopsy cavity (closer to deep margin), and lower outer\u000aquadrant, perpendicular, 2 frags per cass., RSS.\u000aMicro 6: biopsy site versus hemorrhage located in lower inner quadrant,\u000a2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: deep margin perpendicular, lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: deep margin perpendicular, upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: upper outer quadrant, deep margin perpendicular, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: skin with cicatrix, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: skin with nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  4 candidate lymph nodes per cass., 4 frags per cass., ESS.\u000aMicro 15: 2 candidate lymph nodes, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, additional axillary node", and consists of a single\u000afragment of tan-white soft tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro 16: additional axillary node, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
