VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Edilberto G Bauza, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY:\u000aComplex sclerosing lesion with atypical lobular hyperplasia and\u000acalcifications; see NOTE.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aB. SUPERIOR SHAVED MARGIN, RIGHT BREAST:\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aNOTE: This case was also reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester (Breast Pathology\u000aService), who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Area of architectural distortion, right breast, with\u000amicrocalcifications. Tissue from right breast.\u000aOperation: Right breast by localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Tissue from right breast - long suture = lateral, short suture = superior.\u000aB/2. Superior shaved margin from right breast, suture = superior.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aLesion and hookwire contained in specimen.\u000aDr. A. Elman\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "Tissue from right breast, long suture = lateral, short suture =\u000asuperior", consists of a REMOVED_DATE (medial to lateral) x REMOVED_DATE (inferior to superior) x\u000a1.8 (anterior to posterior) cm breast biopsy with a localization wire in place\u000aand a short suture marking the superior margin and along suture marking the\u000alateral margin. An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates an apparent\u000alesion and the localization wire. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The\u000atissue consists of fibroadipose tissue without a discrete palpable mass.\u000aSectioning of the specimen reveals a diffuse white fibrous mass with\u000anon-distinct borders (2.6 cm from inferior to superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to\u000alateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior) that grossly abuts each margin.\u000aSections of each margin are submitted for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superiormost and posterior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior, inferior, medial and lateral margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial, anterior, and posterior margins (bisected), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior, posterior, and anterior margins (bisected), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior, anterior, and medial margins (bisected), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior, posterior, and lateral margins (bisected), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial, lateral, and posterior margins (bisected), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior, anterior, and lateral margins (bisected), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial and inferior margins (bisected), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferiormost margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart B, "Superior shaved margin from right breast, suture = superior", consists\u000aof a fragment of fibroadipose tissue (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an embedded\u000astitch and a blue-inked surface. The specimen has a non-distinct REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.3 cm fibrous mass, which grossly abuts the resection margins. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior shaved margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aEUB/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Edilberto G Bauza M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/19/2005\u000a[report_end]
