VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aRICHARDSON, ANDREA, L., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 3:30, 11 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS AND A MASS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA with ductal and lobular features, measuring at least\u000a0.7 cm in size in this limited specimen.\u000aThe carcinoma is moderately differentiated (modified Bloom Richardson\u000aGrade II/III).\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform, solid and clinging types,\u000a(intermediate nuclear grade) is present.\u000aMicrocalcifications and necrosis are associated with DCIS.\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions,\u000aassociated with microcalcifications.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 1):\u000aEstrogen receptor - POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor - POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast 7 mm hypoechoic mass at 3:30. Associated with nearby\u000amicrocalcifications. Likely IDC.\u000aOperation: 11G ultrasound guided core.\u000aOperative findings: 8 cores.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: ? IDC.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast tissue in brown/tan cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by PREISINGER,ELIZABETH ANN,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast", in a single tan cassette labeled "right", and\u000aconsists of multiple, soft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (2.4 x\u000a1.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000adfi\u000aReports to: TWOHIG, LORRAINE, BERNADETTE, MB\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
