VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aHIRSCH, MICHELLE, S., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by HIRSCH,MICHELLE S.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST MASS, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA lining cystic spaces and associated with\u000acopious mucin production (a REMOVED_DATE cm mucocele-like lesion) (see Note).\u000aExtensive mucin is extravasated into stroma and is present at the medial\u000aand inferior resection margins.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe mucocele-like lesion correlates with the mammographic density.\u000aAlthough definite diagnositic features of an invasive mucinous carcinoma\u000aare not seen, due to the extent of mucin at the resection margins, a wide\u000aexcision may be helpful to exclude this possibility.\u000aThe specimen was entirely submitted.\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester (BWH Breast Pathology) and Dr.\u000aSturat Schnitt (BIDMC Breast Pathology), who conur with this\u000ainterpretation.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left abnormal mammogram.\u000aOperation: Breast biopsy, left.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast mass on mammo.\u000aLesion and wire in specimen. OR called. SR.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BAILEY,GERALD P.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen, received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1, left breast mass", is an excisional biopsy specimen (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) which contains a localization wire. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue;\u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The\u000alocalization wire runs inferolateral to superomedial. There is a small nodule\u000a(0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that abuts the inferior and medial margins, and is located\u000a1.8 cm from the posterior margin, 1 cm from the superior margin and greater\u000athan 2 cm from the lateral and anterior margins. An x-ray was received with the\u000abreast tissue, which is reviewed by the pathologist. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro 1: nodule with inferior and medial margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: posterior and inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posterior, medial and inferior margin, 1 frag each cass., ESS.\u000aMicro 6: superior, medial and inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 7: superior, medial and inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 8: superior and lateral margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 9: superior, anterior and lateral margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 10: superior, anterior and lateral margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000ageb\u000aReports to: LOCKHART, DIANE, CATHERINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
