VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Stephanie Schulte, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS":\u000aBreast tissue with dense fibrosis, epithelial hyperplasia, columnar cell\u000achanges, and sclerosing adenosis.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aBiopsy site changes with foreign body giant cell reaction to polarizable\u000amaterial.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast calcifications, history of ADH.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localized biopsies.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast calcification.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast wire localized excision (FS) - mammo (short stitch equals\u000asuperior, long stitch equals lateral).\u000aRADIOLOGY: Many Ca++ in specimen. The two groups of concern are included.\u000aE. P. Frost\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Left breast wire localized excision", and consists of an irregular\u000atan/pink to tan/yellow fibrofatty portion of breast tissue (5.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000athat has a long stitch marking lateral and a short stitch marking superior.\u000aSpecimen was previously radiographed (per radiologist "new calcifications in\u000aspecimen"). The prosector concurs and notes that there are calcifications\u000afound throughout the specimen with a particularly dense cluster found\u000aimmediately adjacent to the localization wire. The specimen is inked (The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange). The localization wire enters the specimen in the lateral\u000aaspect and leaves the specimen in the superior anterior aspect. Specimen is\u000asectioned from anterior to posterior to show a parenchyma consisting of\u000atan/white fibrous tissue that is focally cystic with focal calcifications,\u000aalong with tan/yellow lobulated adipose tissue. No other lesions are grossly\u000aidentified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen sectioned with perpendicular section of anterior aspect\u000ain REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and perpendicular section of posterior aspect in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, multi frags,\u000aESS.\u000aDRD/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/25/2007\u000a[report_end]
