VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a#1. LEFT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS, WIRE NEEDLE LOCALIZATION:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aBenign breast tissue with epithelial hyperplasia, cysts, apocrine\u000ametaplasia and microcalcifications.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000a#2. LEFT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aSEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA BORDERING ON DUCTAL CARCINOMA\u000aIN-SITU, with associated calcifications, REMOVED_DATE cm area, present in 2 of 6\u000ablocks and less than REMOVED_DATE cm from inked margin in both blocks (blocks 10,\u000a11) (see NOTE).\u000aBenign breast tissue with epithelial hyperplasia, cysts, apocrine\u000ametaplasia and microcalcifications.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread.\u000aThere is no evidence of invasive carcinoma.\u000aNOTE: Additional surgical excision may be warranted to exclude a more severe\u000alesion.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Lt needle directed breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Lt breast mass.\u000a2. Lt breast mass.\u000aRadiology: Ca++ in specimen. OR called.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HIRSCH,MICHELLE S.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aBoth specimens are received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit\u000anumber.\u000aSpecimen #1, labeled "#1 left breast mass", consists of a single, unoriented\u000afragment of tan/yellow, fibroadipose tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a\u000alocalization wire in place, but it does not correspond to any suspicious\u000alesions in the accompanying specimen radiograph. There are isolated\u000acalcifications noted in the specimen radiograph. Sectioning reveals the\u000aspecimen to consist of approximately 70% yellow adipose tissue and 30% firm\u000atan/gray fibrous tissue, predominantly composing a fibrous nodule (1.0 cm in\u000agreatest dimension) near one edge of the specimen. The specimen is inked in\u000ablack and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  #1 left breast mass, 13 frags, ESS.\u000aSpecimen #2, labeled "#2 left breast mass", consists of a single fragment of\u000atan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (3.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is\u000aunoriented and is accompanied by a specimen radiograph which shows a small\u000acluster of calcifications near one edge of the specimen. The cut specimen\u000aconsists of 80% yellow adipose tissue and 30% tan/white firm fibrous tissue\u000awith a firm cystic fibrous tissue mass (0.8 cm in greatest dimension) present\u000aat one end. The specimen is inked in black and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  #2 left breast mass (firm nodule in cassette 8), 13 frags, ESS.\u000ajmh\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
