in. The specimen is accompanied\u000aby a radiograph of the specimen and a pink form signed by the radiologist\u000aindicating that the proximal wire is in mass or in the speciemn. The specimen\u000ais entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 1: inferior, anterior, superior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: inferior, anterior, superior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 3: lateral, superior, posterior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 4: superior, posterior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 5: anterior, inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 6: anterior, inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 7: superior, posterior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 8: posterior, inferior, superior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 9: inferior, anterior, superior, posterior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 10: medial, anterior, posterior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000ajdr\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
