ior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the anterior margin, 2 cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainferior margin, and at least 4 cm from the lateral margin. The specimen is\u000aapproximately 25% composed of firm white fibrous tissue. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted from medial to lateral.\u000aMicro #1+2: Medial margin, perpendicular, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #3+4: Slice with clip, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #5+6: Slice adjacent to clip, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #7-12: Serial sections, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #13+14: Possible area of calcifications, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #15-17: Serial sections, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #18+19: Lateral margin, perpendicular, 10 frags, ESS.\u000apsc/\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
