VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Eleanor Y. Chen, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE" (Wire-localized excisional biopsy for a\u000amass and calcifications):\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, florid epithelial hyperplasia, extensive\u000aadenosis and sclerosing adenosis with microcalcifications, intraductal\u000apapillomas, pseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia, and microcysts with\u000aapocrine metaplasia.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, multifocal.\u000aNOTE: No ductal carcinoma in situ or invasive carcinoma is present, including\u000aevaluation of resection margins.\u000aCase reviewed by Dr. T. Ince, of the Breast Pathology Service, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Abnormal R mammogram. Rule out CA.\u000aOperation: Right node loc br biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnl right mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue - mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aCalled to Dr. Shoji @ 11:48 a.m. REMOVED_DATE \u000aCalcifications, architectural distortion and spiculated mass in specimen, as\u000awell as entire wire. R. Birdwell, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "Right breast tissue", and consists of an irregular, previously inked\u000a(according to pathology protocol: blue equals anterior, black equals\u000aposterior, red equals superior, green equals inferior, yellow equals lateral,\u000aorange equals medial) irregular portion of breast tissue (6.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThere is a needle localization wire entering the anteromedial aspect. The\u000aspecimen is previously radiographed (per radiologist "calcifications,\u000aarchitectural distortion and spiculated mass in specimen as well as entire\u000awire"). The prosector concurs and notes that there are focal calcifications\u000athroughout the specimen with focal dense fibrous tissue concentrated around the\u000aneedle. The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to show an\u000aill-defined, firm, spiculated mass (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that grossly extends to\u000athe posterior and superior margins, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin. The remaining parenchyma consists of tan/white, dense fibrous\u000atissue that is focally cystic (75%). The fibrous tissue appears to be most\u000adense nearest the superior margin. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass and calcifications, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 2 frags total, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sections of dense fibrous stroma at superior margin, 1 frag\u000aeach, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: The remainder of the breast tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000adrd/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
