0aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags in each, RSS.\u000aPart B, labeled "left breast tissue", consists of an aggregate of fibrofatty\u000asoft tissue (460 g; REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) partially surfaced by tan-white\u000aunremarkable skin. The specimen is serially sectioned to exhibit 20% dense\u000awhite fibrous tissue and 80% yellow lobulated adipose tissue. Several dome\u000acysts are identified (ranging from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension). No\u000amasses or lesions are grossly appreciated.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags in each, RSS.\u000aPart C, labeled "lump, lateral aspect of left breast", consists of an\u000aunoriented multifocally disrupted irregular fragment of fibroadipose tissue\u000a(6.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is inked and serially sectioned to exhibit 10% dense\u000awhite fibrous tissue and 90% yellow lobulated unremarkable adipose tissue. No\u000adefinitive masses or lesions are grossly appreciated.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nearly all fibrous tissue, multi frags total, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aJC/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on Friday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 05, 2008 at 04:58:35PM\u000a[report_end]
