n and\u000aexits inferomedially. The specimen is received with a radiograph demonstrating\u000athe localizing wire in place within a scattered area of calcifications. The\u000aspecimen is, on inspection, vaguely from superior to inferior at least REMOVED_DATE %\u000atan/white fibrous tissue without palpable or visible masses, lesions, or other\u000aabnormalities grossly. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely\u000asequentially submitted, vaguely from superior to inferior, with the\u000aperpendicular end in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and the area of interest (per localizing wire)\u000ain REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aDB/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/18/2008\u000a[report_end]
