VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DAVID I SOYBEL M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Elizabeth A. Steensma, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA/1) LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA is present in association with calcifications and\u000aintraductal and extravasated mucin, see note.\u000aCluster of benign cysts with associated mucin and calcifications (0.5 cm).\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aNote: Multiple levels are examined. A focus of ADH with micropapillary\u000afeatures is present <0.1 cm from the lateral margin (best seen in block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000alevels 2 and 3).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Needle-loc excision, left breast nodule.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Breast nodule left.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast tissue.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived fresh labeled with the patient's name and medical record number only\u000ais an irregular fragment of yellow/tan to pink/tan fibroadipose tissue (4.6 x\u000a3.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an adherent brown wrinkled skin ellipse (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm). Per\u000asurgeon, there are two sutures (per attached pink sheet, short stitch superior\u000aand long stitch lateral). The specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange. There is\u000aaspect/skin ellipse and exiting the posterolateral aspect of the specimen.\u000aHowever, a radiograph did not accompany the specimen (her note by SK on REMOVED_DATE \u000aat 9:05 p.m.), "surgeon tried to reach Radiology unsuccessfully and decided\u000athat x-ray is not necessary (wire in mass) - specimen fixed and processed for\u000apathology." The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial. In the\u000alateral/central aspect of the specimen, there is a poorly delineated irregular\u000acystic/gelatinous tan mass (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is traversed by the\u000aneedle localization wire. The mass comes within REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin,\u000a0.4 cm of the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000aanterior/skin margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm at the medial\u000amargin. The remainder of the cut surface is composed of approximately 90%\u000ayellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue and 10% delicate white/tan fibrous stroma\u000awith no additional discrete lesions identified. The specimen is entirely\u000asequentially submitted from lateral to medial.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central specimen from lateral to medial (mass in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aLMB/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/3/2007\u000aSurgical addendum:\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Deborah Dillon and Dr. Susan Lester, Breast\u000aPathology Service, who concur.\u000aAddendum #1 by Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
