 ellipse without any gross\u000alesions at the anterior/superior/medial aspect of the specimen. Two\u000alocalization wires enter through the skin ellipse with the tips embedded within\u000athe specimen. An accompanying radiograph shows the tip of one wire embedded\u000anear the lateral aspect, associated with a clip and calcifications. The second\u000awire tip is located centrally and is associated with calcifications. There is\u000aa hemorrhagic biopsy site associated with the clip near the lateral aspect of\u000athe specimen (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). This area is REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000aposterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from medial. The specimen is serially sectioned from\u000alateral to medial and entirely submitted for microscopic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Core biopsy site, each slice bisected clip (in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections from lateral to medial, each slice bisected, 1\u000afrag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area associated with tip of wire #2, each slice bisected, 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional sections from lateral to medial, each slice bisected,\u000a1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional serial section, 1 slice, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aDH/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/22/2008\u000a[report_end]
