ioned from inferior to superior. The localization wire\u000aenters the specimen in anterior/inferior aspect. Cut surface shows a\u000atan/white, firm nodule (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that abuts the posterior aspect, is\u000a1.6 cm from the lateral aspect, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial aspect, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior aspect, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior aspect and REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000aaspect. This tan/white nodule is surrounded by focally dense tan/white,\u000afocally cystic fibrous tissue that is primarily concentrated at the posterior\u000aaspect (40% of the parenchyma), while the remaining parenchyma consists of\u000atan/yellow, focally hemorrhagic lobulated fat.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nodule to medial, anterior and posterior margins, 2 frags total,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nodule to posterolateral and anterior margins, 2 frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, multi frags total, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sections of random fibrous tissue, multi frags, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aDRD/jp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/20/2006\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aAddendum #1 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/29/2006\u000a[report_end]
