 the posterior\u000amargin. A clip is present within the gelatinous beads at the anterior-most\u000aaspect of the cavity, and the wire traverses the lesion. The accompanying\u000aspecimen radiograph confirms the presence of a wire and clip in the tissue. No\u000aresidual calcifications are noted on the accompanying radiograph. The remaining\u000abreast tissue consists of yellow lobulated fat with scant fibrous stroma. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: breast tissue, multiple frags, ESS\u000aDFI/jp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Ann K Folkins M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/2/2005\u000a[report_end]
