VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aHIRSCH, MICHELLE, S., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by HIRSCH,MICHELLE S.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, TISSUE, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCIISON FOR A CLIP:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread and\u000ainvolvement of large ducts.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aFibroadenoma (0.3 cm).\u000aMicrocalcifications associated with benign breast epithelium.\u000aFat necrosis, chronic inflammation, and a foreign body giant cell\u000areaction, consistent with prior biopsy site.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 64-year-old post menopausal female whose REMOVED_DATE mammogram demonstrates\u000aright breast UOQ calcifications, core biopsy performed REMOVED_DATE  revealed\u000afragments of a fibroadenoma with calcifications and atypical lobular\u000ahyperplasia for which excision is recommended.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right abnormal mammogram. ALH.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue, short/superior, long/lateral,\u000awhipstitch/deep margin. Color markers per path protocol.\u000aRadiology Report:\u000aClip is in the specimen. (DNS).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by FACTOR,RACHEL E.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1, right breast tissue", and consists of a fragment of fibroadipose\u000atissue. An xray film is also received which demonstrates a clip in the\u000aspecimen. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Sutures were placed by\u000athe surgeon: short for the superior margin, long for the lateral margin, and a\u000awhipstitch for a deep margin. Prior localization was done, and a wire was\u000apresent in the specimen. A radiograph was submitted showing a wire, a clip,\u000aand possible microcalcifications. The specimen measures 6 x 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm and\u000aconsists of fibroadipose tissue, which is 85% adipose. On sectioning, an\u000airregular, white-tan lesion is noted measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. It measures REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral\u000amargin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin. The entire specimen was submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue from lateral to superior margin to medial,\u000ainferior margins, multi frags, ESS.\u000aref\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
