nt, 1 frag,\u000aRSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: additionally submitted skin segments, 3 frag, ESS\u000aPart B, "#2 right simple mastectomy, stitch at axilla," consists of a 285-gram\u000aright simple mastectomy specimen (17.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with areola (3.7 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) and everted nipple (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm (depth)). The deep margin is inked\u000ablack. The cut surface demonstrates focal fibrosis. There is no evidence of\u000anecrosis, hemorrhage, or mass. The specimen also contains two unoriented\u000afragments of skin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag each, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag each, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag each, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lower outer quadrant, 1 frag each, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: additional fibrous areas (central), 1 frag each, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: separate skin segment, 1 frag, ESS\u000aESN/jp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Peter M Sadow M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/8/2005\u000a[report_end]
