VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aFibroepithelial lesion (4.5 cm) (see note).\u000aThe stroma is mildly cellular with mild nuclear atypia.\u000aFocal stromal overgrowth is present.\u000aMitoses average 1 per 10 HPF's (range 0 to 2; 50 HPF's counted).\u000aThe lesion is well circumscribed and no stromal invasion is seen.\u000aThe lesion is present at the margin.\u000aNo heterologous elements are present.\u000aScant adjacent breast tissue with no significant pathologic change.\u000aNote: The differential diagnosis includes a cellular fibroadenoma and a\u000alow grade phyllodes tumor. A cellular fibroadenoma is favored. However,\u000aclose clinical follow-up is suggested.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Biopsy proven fibroadenoma of left breast, now enlarging.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Mass, lt breast.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by MILNER,DANNY A.,JR.,M.D.\u000aReceived in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, medical record number\u000aand designated "#1 left breast mass", is a single fragment of pink, soft,\u000anodular tissue with a scabrous coating. The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a2.5 cm. There is a single white suture in one aspect of the specimen which is\u000anot further oriented. The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to\u000areveal a well circumscribed nodule of pink, lobulated, glistening material with\u000aan adjacent band of fibrous tissue. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  1 frag each, ESS.\u000adam\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
