VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Consult material\u000aProcedure Date:\u000aOrdering Provider: JULIA WONG M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Rachel E Factor, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM FAULKNER HOSPITAL, BOSTON, MA:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION, ADDITIONAL SUPERIOR MARGIN, AND LEFT\u000aSENTINEL LYMPH NODES (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified Bloom-\u000aRichardson grade II/III), present as at least fifteen foci, measuring REMOVED_DATE cm,\u000a0.9 cm, REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_DATE cm (five foci) and REMOVED_DATE 2 cm (seven foci) (see note).\u000aLymphovascular invasion is present (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform and solid type (intermediate to high\u000anuclear grade), with necrosis and calcifications, is present in seven of nine\u000aslides reviewed (EIC positive, by report).\u000aIn the main specimen, INVASIVE CARCINOMA is present at or <0.1 cm from the\u000ablue, black, yellow, and red-inked margins (by report, these correspond to the\u000aanterior, superior, lateral, and deep margins, but specific designations are\u000anot indicated). By report, invasive carcinoma is present <0.1 cm from the\u000ainferior margin on slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (not received for review). The orange-inked margin\u000ais negative for carcinoma (>0.3 cm).\u000aDCIS is present <0.1 cm from the black-inked margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; deep, by\u000areport), <0.1 cm from a yellow-inked margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), REMOVED_DATE cm from a green-inked\u000amargin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), REMOVED_DATE cm from a blue-inked margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), REMOVED_DATE cm from a red-inked\u000amargin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and >0.3 cm from orange-inked margins on slides received for\u000areview.\u000aSeparately submitted "final superior margin" shows a REMOVED_DATE cm focus of invasive\u000acarcinoma present in association with several foci of lymphovascular invasion.\u000aInvasive carcinoma is present REMOVED_DATE cm from the yellow-inked deep aspect and at\u000aleast REMOVED_DATE cm from the black-inked "peripheral" margin on the single slide\u000areceived for review.\u000aBiopsy site changes are present.\u000aBy report, two of two sentinel lymph nodes with no carcinoma seen on H&E or\u000akeratin immunohistochemistry.\u000aNOTE: By report, a REMOVED_DATE 0 cm mass was seen grossly, comprising multifocal\u000ainvasive carcinoma and associated DCIS (40-50% of the mass). Radiologic\u000acorrelation is suggested for best determination of tumor size.\u000aThis carcinoma could be classified as AJCC (6th edition) at least REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(sn)\u000aMX, with numerous foci of invasion.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast invasive carcinoma\u000aClinical Diagnosis: IDC\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aConsult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived from Faulkner Hospital, Pathology Department, 1153 Centre Street,\u000aBoston, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are nine (9) glass slides.\u000aThe slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through\u000a"REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", corresponding to C) left breast, superior\u000amargin, excision (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm) D) left breast partial mastectomy (3.5 x\u000a4.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology\u000areport bearing the patient's name.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/25/2006\u000a[report_end]
