VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Elizabeth A. Steensma, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Shuji Ogino, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA/1. SPECIMEN LABELED "1 = LEFT BREAST, SHORT = PREVIOUS BREAST CANCER\u000aRESECTION, LONG = BREAST TAIL":\u000aNo residual carcinoma identified.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aChronic inflammation, fat necrosis, foreign body giant cell reaction\u000aand fibrosis, consistent with prior surgical site.\u000aCalcifications in benign breast epithelium, extensive.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 60-year-old woman with left invasive ductal cancer, excised\u000a09/15/2006 at Faulkner Hospital, multifocal with DCIS, close at superior margin\u000aand deep margin, REMOVED_DATE SLN positive. Recommended for mastectomy.\u000aOperation: Left simple mastectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left invasive multifocal ductal cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. = equals left breast, short = previous breast cancer resection, long =\u000abreast tail.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "One equals left breast, short equals previous breast cancer resection,\u000along equals breast tail", and consists of 206 g, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm simple\u000amastectomy specimen, with a short suture just superior to the nipple,\u000adesignating prior resection, and a long suture designating lateral tissue. The\u000aanterior surface of the specimen is inked blue, the deep (smooth fascial plane)\u000ais inked black. The attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm areolar skin exhibits an eccentric\u000a1.3 cm everted nipple and a REMOVED_DATE cm curvilinear scar, just superior to the\u000anipple. Sectioning in this area demonstrates a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm scarred area\u000aof breast parenchyma, REMOVED_DATE cm from the overlying freely mobile deep margin (12\u000ao'clock). The closest anterior margin is within REMOVED_DATE cm. Surrounding tissue is\u000agranular and fibrous, without mass lesions noted grossly. Remaining specimen\u000ais comprised predominantly of soft, lobulated tan/yellow adipose tissue, with\u000aoccasional tan/white granular fibrous dense tissue (predominantly in the\u000ainferior half of the specimen, comprises less than 15% of parenchyma). There\u000aare no additional abnormalities grossly. There are no lymph nodes palpated\u000awithin the lateral soft tissue. Additionally received in the specimen\u000acontainer is a freely floating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan/white skin fragment,\u000agrossly unremarkable. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire scar and surrounding fibrous tissue, closest deep and\u000aanterior margins, sequentially from lateral to medial, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant (adjacent to scar tissue), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, 4 frags total, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Severally received skin, sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: 3864.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Shuji Ogino M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/29/2007\u000a[report_end]
