VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Li Chen, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA/1). LEFT INFERIOR MEDIAL BREAST TISSUE, EXCISION:\u000aPapillomatous changes.\u000aColumnar cell change with architectural distortion.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aBiopsy site changes, present at the cauterized lateral and anterior\u000amargins.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aB/2). LEFT SUPERIOR BREAST TISSUE, EXCISION:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is present as a single duct profile (slide\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, levels examined) adjacent to biopsy site changes, located REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the nearest margin (posterior).\u000aColumnar cell change.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aC/3). INFERIOR SHAVED MARGIN, LEFT BREAST, EXCISION:\u000aBenign epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 64-year-old female S/P L breast UIQ core bx on REMOVED_DATE  revealing ADH,\u000aneeding evaluation/excision.\u000aOperation: L breast WL bx x 2.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left inferior medial tissue; short - superior; long - lateral; whip\u000astitch on deep margin.\u000aB/2) Left superior breast tissue; short - superior; long - lateral; whip\u000astitch on chest wall.\u000aC/3) Inferior shaved margin with stitch of new margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY: U-shaped clip, a few Ca++ and wire. RB phoned ER in OR.\u000aLeft 2nd specimen of posterior upper inner clip present. Called to OR, Dr.\u000aRhei. Ayo Odulate, MD REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aSoft tissue and wire but no clip. RB phoned to OR to Dr. Rhei, who will take\u000amore tissue superficially.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, all labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Left inferior medial tissue", consists of a REMOVED_DATE (medial to\u000alateral) x REMOVED_DATE (superior to inferior) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior) cm breast\u000aexcision specimen and a short suture marking the superior margin and the long\u000asuture marking the lateral margin and accompanying radiograph shows cluster of\u000acalcification and a clip close to the medial margin. The specimen is inked for\u000athe evaluation of the margins: posterior equals black, anterior equals blue,\u000asuperior equals red, inferior equals green, and lateral equals yellow, medial\u000aequals orange. There is an ill-defined, firm, white/tan lesion at the clip site\u000a(2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) located less than REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior\u000amargin. The specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior. About\u000a80% of the specimen are submitted including all fibrous tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mammographic microcalcification area with medial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest anterior and posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Section with additional medial, posterior, and anterior margin,\u000amulti frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining fibrous tissue, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left superior breast tissue", consists of a REMOVED_DATE (superior to\u000ainferior) x REMOVED_DATE (medial to lateral) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior) cm breast\u000aexcision specimen with a localization wire present but no clip showed on the\u000aaccompanying radiograph. The specimen is inked for the evaluation of the\u000amargins: posterior equals black, anterior equals blue, superior equals red,\u000ainferior equals green, lateral equals yellow, medial equals orange. No gross\u000alesion or calcification are identified along the plane the localization wire.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial margin. Two sections\u000aof each margin are submitted for microscopic evaluation. The margin consists\u000aof unremarkable adipose tissue. 90% of the specimen is fatty adipose tissue and\u000aless than 10% is fibrous tissue. About 40% of the specimen was submitted\u000aincluding all fibrous tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining fibrous tissue, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Inferior shave with margin", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000abreast excision specimen with a suture marking the new inferior margin (inked\u000ain black) and an accompanying radiograph shows a clip. There is an\u000aill-defined, firm, white fibrotic area (0.9 cm in greatest dimension)\u000aconsistent with possible previous biopsy sites located within REMOVED_DATE cm to the\u000ainked margin. The specimen consists of 85% fatty adipose tissue, about 10%\u000afibrous tissue, and 5% muscular tissue. All fibrous tissues are submitted for\u000amicroscopic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sections of all fibrous tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aLC/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/31/2007\u000a[report_end]
