VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Anna Laury, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), associated with columnar\u000acell change, adjacent to core biopsy site.\u000aSurgical resection margins are uninvolved (>0.3 cm).\u000aMicrocalcifications are present in the areas of columnar cell change.\u000aDuctal epithelial hyperplasia, sclerosing adenosis and calcifications in benign\u000abreast epithelium are present.\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. J. Connolly, Breast Pathology, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 51 yo women s/p new microcalcs seen on screening L mammogram -s/p core\u000abx (+) columnar change with atypia recommended for excision.\u000aOperation: L needle localization breast bx.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L abnl mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast needle localization breast mass, orange border -> medial,\u000aorange border with stitch = lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSpecimen X-ray with Ca++ + clip + 2 wires/DG.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "left needle localization breast mass", and consists of a portion of\u000alobulated fibroadipose tissue (4.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with two needle localization wires\u000ain place (wire #1 entering at the lateral aspect and exiting at the superior\u000aaspect; wire #2 entering at the lateral aspect and exiting at the medial\u000aaspect). The specimen is received previously inked by the surgeon as follows:\u000aOrange border with stitch equals lateral, orange border - medial, blue -\u000aanterior, black - posterior, red - superior, and green - inferior. The lateral\u000aaspect is over inked yellow by the prosector. The specimen is accompanied by a\u000aradiograph, which exhibits two intact needle localization wires, a clip, and\u000amultiple foci of calcifications, some of which grossly abut the inferoposterior\u000aaspect. The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial, exhibiting\u000aan area of dense, focally cystic fibrous tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), extending\u000ato the medial, inferior, superior, anterior, and posterior margins. The areas\u000aof calcification are present within the dense fibrous region. Just lateral to\u000athe fibrous region is the aforementioned clip. The remaining breast tissue\u000aconsists of predominantly yellow lobulated adipose tissue. No other gross\u000alesions identified and the specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue sequentially from lateral to medial, multi frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - area of clip, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense cystic fibrous area (calcifications probable in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID),\u000amulti frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aDFI/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/31/2007\u000a[report_end]
