VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGRANTER, SCOTT, R., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GRANTER,SCOTT R.,M.D.\u000a1. RIGHT BREAST, BIOPSY:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU, several foci.\u000aNo invasive carcinoma identified.\u000a2. RIGHT BREAST, SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aFocal atypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aCase reviewed by Dr. Lester, who concurs, and at Surgical Pathology\u000aStaff Conference.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Non-palpable mass, right breast.\u000aOperation: Right breast localized breast biopsy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast mass.\u000a#2. Tissue at closest margin (suture marks inner\u000aapex).\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000a1. SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST MASS":\u000aTissue inked per request.\u000aGross only.\u000a2. SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST CLOSEST":\u000aTissue inked per request.\u000aGross only.\u000aRadiology: Mass in in specimen #1.-----Dr. Dennison.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by STONE,JAMES ROBERT,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two (2) parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart #1, "right breast mass," consists of a single fragment of yellow/tan\u000afibroadipose tissue (6.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). No orienting sutures are present. The\u000aspecimen is inked in black. Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE cm firm mass, less than\u000a0.2 cm from one (1) margin. Other margins are\u000agrossly negative.\u000aMicro 1 : mass, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart #2, "right breast, closest margin," consists of a single fragment of\u000ayellow/pink/red fibroadipose tissue (5.5 x 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a whip stitch on\u000aone (1) flat surface. The side with the whip stitch is inked black; the other\u000aside is inked blue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  shave margin, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
