VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Elizabeth Amy Morgan, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, DOUBLE WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND\u000aMICROCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aFocal atypical ductal hyperplasia (Block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; levels examined).\u000aMicrocalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aBiopsy site changes are transected at the medial margin.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the entire\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aNOTE: Part A is reviewed by Dr. S. Lester, Breast Pathology Service, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aB. 2ND WIRE:\u000aGross examination only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 52 year old post-menopausal female, S/P R breast core bx on REMOVED_DATE \u000arevealing ADH associated with calcifications - but review of films, few\u000apunctate calcifications within 2 cm posterior to clip - recommendation --> 2\u000awire WL excision. Previous surgery: REMOVED_DATE  - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aOperation: R breast WL bx REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right breast tissue, *short stitch - superior, long - lateral, whipstitch\u000a- chest wall margin*.\u000aB/2) 2nd wire.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aMass with clip; + separate area with calcifications with an intact hookwire,\u000aare within the specimen. Other wire is separately submitted. Dr. Gombos.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue", and consists of a 50 gram breast biopsy specimen\u000a(6.5 cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to\u000aposterior) with intact localization wire entering at the inferior border. The\u000aspecimen is inked per the surgeon according to the pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange, and there is a short stitch at\u000athe superior margin, and a long stitch at the lateral margin. The accompanying\u000aradiograph shows a clip and tiny cluster of calcifications adjacent to the\u000alocalization wire, medially. There is a well-circumscribed, red/brown nodule\u000aat the medial border (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) consistent with biopsy cavity,\u000aalthough the surgical clip is not identified in this area. The breast is\u000acomposed of approximately 70% fibrous tissue. The specimen is sectioned\u000asuperior to inferior and the entire specimen is submitted for histologic\u000aevaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sectioned superior to inferior, 1 frag each, ESS\u000a(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - biopsy cavity; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - wire tip).\u000aPart B, "#2. Second wire", consists of an additional localization wire. Please\u000anote that this wire was not noted on the form 86 by the surgeon. The specimen\u000ais submitted for gross examination only.\u000aEM/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/30/2007\u000a[report_end]
