VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP MARKING A PREVIOUSLY BIOPSIED\u000aMASS:\u000aSEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, involving an intraductal papilloma\u000ain two of 24 slides (slides 5 and 6) (see note). The ADH is REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe anterior and superior margins.\u000aA biopsy site is associated with the papilloma.\u000aNote: The ADH is confined to the papilloma over a REMOVED_DATE cm area and is not\u000aseen in adjacent tissue after microscopically examining all the adjacent\u000atissue. Although the ADH closely approaches a diagnosis of DCIS, ADH is\u000afavored as this cellular proliferation is only present within the\u000apapilloma. However, re-excision of the close margins would be helpful to\u000aexclude more extensive involvement of the adjacent breast tissue.\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. Stuart Schnitt and Dr. Susan Lester who\u000aconcur with this interpretation.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 64-year-old female with left breast mass.\u000aOperation: Left needle localized breast biopsy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left needle localized breast biopsy.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: Clip in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BENNETT,MICHAEL W.,M.B.,B.C.H\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1, left needle localized breast biopsy", and consists of a piece of\u000afibrofatty tissue, which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and is marked by the\u000asurgeon with two (2) sutures (short = superior, long = lateral). A localizing\u000awire protrudes from the medial aspect of the specimen.\u000aThe specimen radiograph reveals a clip within an area of vague density and a\u000alocalization wire.\u000aAt the anterosuperior margin of the specimen is an indurated white mass, which\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The mass abuts the superior border of the\u000aspecimen microscopically. Lateral to the mass is a linear biopsy track, which\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter extending from the superior aspect of the\u000aspecimen. Adjacent and medial to the mass is an area of indurated fibrous\u000atissue, which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aThe entire specimen is submitted for histological examination. The surgical\u000aclip is identified radiographically in cassette #4.\u000aMicro 1: lateral border, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: superior lateral margin including wire tip localization, 1 frag,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro 3: linear scar, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass and adjacent fibrotic area, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 8: section to include anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  sections to include inferior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  sections to include medial margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, mult frags, ESS.\u000amwb\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
