feriorly. Specimen is received along with a\u000aradiograph demonstrating the localizing wire in place centrally within the\u000aspecimen, adjacent to a small focus of calcifications. Sectioning demonstrates\u000adense tan/white fibrous tissue (60-70% of the specimen), admixed with\u000aunremarkable tan/yellow soft, lobulated adipose tissue. There are no obvious\u000amasses, lesions or other abnormalities grossly. The entire specimen is\u000asequentially submitted from lateral to medial, with perpendicular lateral\u000amargin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, perpendicular medial margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and area of interest (per\u000alocalizing wire) in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sequentially from lateral to medial,\u000amulti frags, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/30/2006\u000a[report_end]
