VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, best seen in slides 8, 19, and 23 (levels\u000aexamined).\u000aCalcifications are associated with one area of ADH.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present (e.g., block 7).\u000aBreast tissue with cysts, fibrosis, sclerosing adenosis and epithelial\u000ahyperplasia.\u000aMicrocalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 44 year old female with REMOVED_DATE  mammogram with right breast UIQ 5 cm\u000aarea of calcifications for which wire localization and excision is\u000arecommended. Past history of left breast DCIS.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization excision x 2\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right abnormal mammogram\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Right breast tissue (short stitch superior; long\u000astitch lateral, whip stitch chest wall margin)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcifications in specimen. Dr. Meyer.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BENNETT,MICHAEL W.,M.B.,B.C.H\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. R. breast", and consists of a portion of fibrofatty tissue\u000awhich measures REMOVED_DATE x 5 x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen has been marked by the surgeon\u000awith sutures as indicated on the form 86. The specimen has been inked by the\u000asurgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. (The area of the long suture in addition to that of the whip\u000astitch has been inked black). A single wire localizing needle enters the\u000aspecimen at the superior margin. The second wire which is present on the\u000aincluded specimen radiograph is not present in the specimen or container. The\u000aspecimen appears to have been focally incised at the anterior border after\u000ainking. The specimen is divided in two and radiographed. The first part\u000a(superomedial) is serially sectioned from superior to medial (inferior) . This\u000aarea contains focal white poorly defined fibrotic areas which extend to the\u000asuperior and posterior margins of the specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm. The\u000asecond portion of the specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial and\u000aincludes white fibrotic areas which measure approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000awhich extend to the inferior and focally the lateral margins of the specimen.\u000a100% of fibrotic areas are submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior to medial (inferior), 1st part of specimen, 10 frags,\u000aESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  2nd part of specimen, lateral to medial, 16 frags, ESS\u000amwb\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
