VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: COLLEEN MURPHY M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Paul A. VanderLaan, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A PRIOR EXCISION SITE AND AN ADDITIONAL\u000aFOCUS OF CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - 16:40 blocks, associated with prior\u000aexcision site and with an additional separate focus of calcifications\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Lateral, superior, anterior, posterior\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000a- Medial (0.1 cm focus located REMOVED_DATE cm from the margin, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000a- Inferior (0.2 cm focus located REMOVED_DATE cm from the margin and multifocally\u000abetween REMOVED_DATE 3 cm from the inferior margin)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aSclerosing adenosis\u000aFibroadenoma\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - Tis\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Performed previously at the outside\u000ainstitution\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: L DCIS (+) margins.\u000aOperation: Breast needle-loc lumpectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: Calcs in specimen.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast needle-localized lumpectomy; sutures - short - superior/ long\u000a- lateral (to mammo)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Specimen shows Ca++, clips and 2 wires. Called to Dr. Murphy by\u000aDr. Lizer.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, medical record\u000anumber, and "#1. Left breast needle localized lumpectomy sutures short\u000asuperior, long lateral", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE gram lumpectomy specimen that\u000ais oriented per the surgeon with a short stitch designating superior and a long\u000astitch designating lateral. The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to\u000aposterior, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral. The\u000aposterior/deep surface of the specimen is smooth consistent with a deep tissue\u000aresection plane. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. Accompanying the specimen are\u000atwo radiographs showing two wires localizing areas of calcification. The wires\u000aenter on the anterior surface of the specimen (at 6 and 9 o'clock), but do not\u000aexit the specimen. There are four surgical hemostasis clips identified on the\u000aradiograph and found in the center of the specimen. No biopsy clips are seen\u000aon the mammogram or identified in the specimen. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from lateral to medial to reveal approximately 85% yellow lobulated\u000afatty tissue and approximately 15% white fibrous tissue. Located within the\u000aspecimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm white/tan firm area that abuts the\u000alateral/inferior margin. This area is REMOVED_DATE cm to the anterior resection margin,\u000a3.0 cm to the posterior resection margin, and greater than REMOVED_DATE cm to the other\u000aresection margin. Additionally, there is a smooth walled cavity consistent\u000awith a previous biopsy cavity with vascular hemostasis clips present in and\u000anear the wall. This biopsy cavity measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and is near the\u000atwo localizing wires. The biopsy cavity is REMOVED_DATE cm to the anterior resection\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the posterior resection margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior\u000aresection margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior resection margin, and greater than REMOVED_DATE \u000acm to the lateral and medial resection margin. The remainder of the lumpectomy\u000aspecimen has scattered white fibrous areas but no other discrete masses or\u000alesions. Approximately 50% of the entire specimen is submitted for histology,\u000aincluding the entire biopsy cavity, all the fibrous tissue, and representative\u000asurgical resection margins.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral end, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral/inferior fibrous area, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin near lateral/inferior area, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin near lateral/inferior area, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area lateral to biopsy cavity, 1 frag per cassette, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy cavity, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial edge of biopsy cavity and medial margin fibrous tissue, 2\u000afrags per cassette, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional tissue including margins and additional area of\u000acalcifications, multiple frags, RSS.\u000aPVA/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aMonday REMOVED_MONTH 29, 2009 at 07:03:55PM\u000a[report_end]
