VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000a1) "RIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY":\u000aBreast tissue with fibroadenoma (0.2 cm), columnar alteration of lobules\u000awith prominent snouts and secretions, and epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aBiopsy site changes are present.\u000aSkin with scar.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000a2) "LEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY":\u000aHealing biopsy site changes.\u000aBreast tissue with focal atypical ductal hyperplasia, multiple small\u000afibroadenomas (up to REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aSkin with scar.\u000aNo residual DCIS.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of DCIS left breast (see BWH path REMOVED_DATE ). Patient requested\u000acompletion left mastectomy and prophylactic right mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS left breast\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Right breast (stitch: short/superior, long/lateral; 300g)\u000a#2) Left breast (stitch: short/superior, long/lateral)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by RUCKER-SCHMIDT,RACHEL L.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. right breast - stitch: short superior, long lateral",\u000aconsists of a right simple mastectomy specimen (15.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a\u000atan/pink skin ellipse (8.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm) including a REMOVED_DATE cm nipple. The specimen\u000aincludes two sutures placed by the surgeon to designate the lateral and\u000asuperior orientation of the specimen. A thin, well-healed periareolar scar\u000a(2.8 cm in length) is present in the lower medial portion of the skin, grossly\u000a0.3 cm from the closest skin resection margin. Immediately deep to the scar in\u000athe lower inner quadrant there is a tan/white, fibrous stellate area (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm) which is grossly consistent with a well-healed previous excision\u000asite. This area extends to the skin and within REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep, black inked\u000amargin, which is a smooth fascial plane. The remainder of the breast is\u000aapproximately 70% fatty tissue and 30% fibrous tissue. Representative sections\u000aare submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro 1: deep margin over excision site, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  previous excision site, (#3 and 4 include skin with scar), 3\u000afrags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  UOQ, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  UIQ, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  LOQ, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  LIQ, 3 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 13: nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. left breast, stitch: short superior, long lateral",\u000aconsists of a 352 gram left simple mastectomy specimen (15.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000awith a tan/pink skin ellipse (8.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm), including a REMOVED_DATE cm nipple. The\u000aspecimen includes two sutures placed by the surgeon to designate the lateral\u000aand superior orientation of the specimen. The deep margin is a smooth, fascial\u000aplane, without skeletal muscle and is inked in black. There is a REMOVED_DATE cm thin,\u000awell-healed, periareolar scar present on the lower middle aspect of the skin\u000aellipse, coming to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest skin margin. REMOVED_DATE cm deep to\u000athe scar, there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, tan/white, cystic biopsy cavity\u000afilled with a clear serous fluid. The cavity is surrounded by punctate chalky\u000ayellow discoloration, grossly suspicious for fat necrosis. The biopsy cavity\u000ais located REMOVED_DATE cm deep to the black inked margin. The remainder of the tissue\u000ais approximately 80% fatty tissue and 20% fibrous tissue. No lymph nodes are\u000aidentified after thin sectioning of the upper outer quadrant. Representative\u000asections, including the entire biopsy cavity, are submitted for histologic\u000aexamination.\u000aMicro 14: deep margin over biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy cavity, including nipple and scar, mult frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  UOQ, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  UIQ, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  LOQ, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  LIQ, 2 frags, RSS\u000arlr\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
