VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A PALPABLE MASS:\u000aAtypical Ductal Hyperplasia (block 8; levels examined).\u000aDuctal hyperplasia and papilloma.\u000aFibrocystic change with dense nodular interlobular fibrosis.\u000aAdenosis.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. S. Lester (Breast Pathology Service) who\u000aagrees with the above diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 42-year-old female with left breast mass without mammographic or\u000aUS correlate.\u000aOperation: Left excisional breast biopsy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast excisional biopsy, short stitch superior,\u000along stitch lateral, and whipstitch chest wall margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BRINSTER,NOOSHIN K.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1, left breast excisional biopsy", and consists of a breast excision\u000aspecimen with three (3) orienting sutures: short stitch superior, long stitch\u000alateral, and whipstitch deep margin. The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE cm from medial\u000ato lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior.\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. A firm mass is palpated along the lateral, superior and\u000ainferior aspects of the specimen. The cut surface of this mass reveals white\u000afirm fibrous tissue, which has ill-defined borders and extends across the\u000aposterior aspect of the mass and blends into the remainder of the breast\u000aparenchyma as it approaches the medial aspects. The most discrete portion of\u000athe mass measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Approximately 80% of the specimen is\u000asubmitted for histologic evaluation. The entire mass and all fibrous\u000aportions of the tissue are submitted fo rhistologic evaluation.\u000aMicro 1: mass to lateral, inferior, and superior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass to superior, posterior, inferior and lateral margins, 1 frag,\u000abisected, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass to include anterior margin, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro 6: closest approach of mass to medial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of mass, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous tissue most medially, 1 frags each, ESS.\u000anb\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
