VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWEINBERG, DAVID, S., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WEINBERG,DAVID S.,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY":\u000aBreast tissue and skin with fibrosis, fat necrosis, foreign body reaction,\u000aand polarizable suture material consistent with previous biopsy site.\u000aNo tumor is seen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Borderline ductal carcinoma-in-situ.\u000aOperation: Right breast biopsy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast biopsy. Short stitch - superior.\u000aLong stitch - medial (per surgeon).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by TURNER,JERROLD ROSS,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe unfixed specimen, "right breast biopsy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. mass of\u000afibrofatty tissue (medial and lateral, superficial to deep, superior to\u000ainferior, respectively), containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. skin ellipse. The\u000aspecimen contains a short stitch designated "superior" by the surgeon and a\u000along stitch designated "medial". The superior margin is inked in yellow, the\u000ainferior margin is inked in green, the medial and lateral margins are inked in\u000ablack, and the deep margin has overlapping yellow/green. Within the specimen\u000ais a single, firm, white nodule with a tan central core measuring REMOVED_DATE cm. in\u000agreatest dimension. It is approximately REMOVED_DATE cm. deep to the skin surface and\u000a2 cm. from the lateral margin and does not approach the deep margin. It is\u000asubmitted primarily in cassettes 9 and 10. This may represent old biopsy\u000acavity and fat necrosis.\u000aMicross #1-5: The specimen is submitted from medial to lateral, with micros\u000a1-3 containing the medial margin, micro 15 containing the lateral margin, the\u000aintervening cassettes containing the remainder of the specimen, with skin\u000aprimarily attached to superficial margins, and deep margins without skin, ESS.\u000aReports to: SMITH, BARBARA, LYNN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
