VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (block 6; original level only) associated\u000awith columnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and\u000asecretions with calcifications.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia, fibroadenoma, cysts, and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Hx calcs LUOQ.\u000aOperation: Left mammographically directed biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast tissue (short = superior, long = lateral).\u000aRADIOLOGY: Ca++/hookwire in specimen.\u000a(illegible signature)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SHEN,JIAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "left needle directed breast biopsy", and consists of a fragment of breast\u000atissue (6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is oriented by surgeon. Breast tissue\u000ais inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. The specimen contains 50% areas of fibrosis with focal area\u000aof hemorrhage (0.5 cm diameter) which is located within REMOVED_DATE cm of closest\u000aposterior margin. The specimen is entirely submitted for microscopic\u000aexamination.\u000aThe specimen radiograph reveals a large cluster of calcifications and the\u000alocalization wire.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  entire breast tissue from medial margin to lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000afrags per cassette, ESS.\u000ajis\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
