VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Dominique P. Coco, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Tan A Ince, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (see note).\u000aFocal atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar cell hyperplasia, fibroadenomatous changes, and calcifications in\u000abenign epithelium.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemistry for E-cadherin is non-contributory.\u000aDr. Susan Lester has reviewed the case and concurs with the diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 53-year-old premenopausal woman with r breast mammogram on REMOVED_DATE \u000anoting clustered punctate and amorphous calcifications in UIQ posteriorly; not\u000aamenable to core bx.\u000aOperation: R breast WL bx.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast tissues; stitches - Short --> superior; long --> lateral;\u000awhip --> chest wall margin. *Sent to FS Rm --> Remammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Both sets of calcifications along with both intact hookwires are\u000aseen with the specimen. Findings d/w Dr. Rhei by Dr. Jeanmenne at 2:45 PM on\u000a12/7/07\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue", and consists of an ovoid fragment of yellow/tan\u000alobulated fibroadipose tissue (4.0 M - L x REMOVED_DATE S - I x REMOVED_DATE A - P cm) which is\u000aoriented per surgeon with three stitches: short equals superior, long equals\u000alateral, and whip equals chest wall margin. The specimen is inked by the\u000asurgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange.\u000aThere are two needle-localization wires in place, arbitrarily designated wire\u000a#1 and #2 per prosector. Wire #1 enters the superomedial aspect of the\u000aspecimen with no clear exit point. Wire #2 enters the anteromedial aspect of\u000athe specimen with no clear exit point. The specimen was previously\u000aradiographed confirming three sets of calcifications within the specimen,\u000acorresponding to the aforementioned needle-localization wires. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from lateral to medial to exhibit approximately 80%\u000adense/nodular white/tan fibrous stroma and 20% yellow/tan lobulated adipose\u000atissue. The dense fibrous stroma extends to all six-inked margins. No\u000adiscrete masses or lesions are identified. The area of calcification #1 and #2\u000a(please see orientation and radiograph) corresponds to the tip of the\u000aneedle-localization wire #1. Area of calcifications #3 (please see orientation\u000aof accompanying radiograph) corresponds to the tip of needle-localization wire\u000a#2. The specimen is entirely sequentially submitted from lateral to medial.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central specimen sequentially submitted from lateral to medial\u000a(area of calcification #1 in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, area of calcification #2 in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, area of\u000acalcification #3 in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags in each,\u000aESS.\u000aLM/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Tan A Ince M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/20/2007\u000a[report_end]
