 wire localizing vague calcification.\u000aThe portion of breast tissue which contains the calcifications is entirely\u000asubmitted for histologic examination. Representative sections of the remainder\u000aof the tissue are also submitted. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior =\u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. On sectioning, no\u000aarea suspicious for invasive carcinoma is identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue at REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, multiple fragments, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of breast tissue, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
