VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: HOPE E PETERS M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Kevin B Long, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, LOWER INNER, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH MICROINVASION.\u000aDCIS, comedo, cribriform, and solid types (high nuclear grade), with\u000acentral necrosis and calcifications, is present.\u000aA focus of microinvasion (< REMOVED_DATE cm) is present.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aFragments of a fibroadenoma are present.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor,\u000aprogesterone receptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an\u000aaddendum.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 58 year old female with history of left lower excisional biopsy of\u000acalcifications in 2000 yielding ADH. New coarse heterogeneous calcifications\u000ain same quadrant, segmental distribution. Differential diagnosis - DCIS,\u000abenign less likely. Time in formalin - 9:30 am.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: Non-palpable calcifications.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: lower/inner.\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 11G Stereotactic.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast core biopsy in two pink cassettes - A/calcs and B/no calcs.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast 9:30 AM", and consists of multiple yellow/white\u000afocally hemorrhagic fibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which\u000aare received in two pink cassettes, labeled "A Ca++" and "B". The specimens\u000aare submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "A Ca++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000acp/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Friday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 11, 2009 at 01:05:56PM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: (12/15/09)\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS and microinvasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following\u000acriteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not\u000ayet been determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells or moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a< 30% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>30% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate immunoreactivity.\u000aThe immunoperoxidase, immunofluorescence and in-situ hybridization tests\u000aperformed at Brigham and Women's Hospital were developed and their performance\u000acharacteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the\u000aDepartment of Pathology at BWH. They have not been cleared or approved by the\u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such\u000aclearance or approval is not necessary.\u000aAddendum #1 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 15, 2009 at 04:35:50PM\u000a[report_end]
