 is inked blue. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000aand entirely submitted for microscopic examination. Also included is a skin\u000aellipse (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with underlying subcutaneous tissue excised to a depth\u000aof REMOVED_DATE cm. This is serially sectioned and entirely submitted for microscopic\u000aexamination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular serial sections, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular serial sections, 2 frags in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular serial section, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular serial sections, 2 frags in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular serial sections, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular serial sections, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular serial sections, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular serial sections, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin perpendicular serial sections, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B is labeled "#2. Left breast inferior shave margin - whip-stitch on new\u000amargin", and consists of one fragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (4.5 x\u000a4.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with suture marking the new margin (inked black). The opposite\u000asurface is smooth and red consistent with lining of prior excision cavity (this\u000aside is inked blue). The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted\u000afor microscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular serial sections, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular serial sections, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 perpendicular serial section, cut in half, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular serial section, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 perpendicular serial section, cut in half, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular serial section, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 perpendicular serial section, cut in half, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular serial section, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular serial sections, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aerv/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lynette M Sholl M.D., Electronically signed on Thursday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 21, 2010 at 11:32:44AM\u000a[report_end]
