VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-10-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: John W. Hanna, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Solid\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks, adjacent to excision cavity in UIQ\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Deep\u000aOTHER FINDINGS:\u000aSkin and nipple are negative for tumor.\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Performed previously\u000aB. LEFT BREAST SKIN:\u000aSkin and subcutis with no significant pathologic change.\u000aC. RIGHT BREAST, REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY (469 g):\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aBenign breast tissue with focal epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 58 year old postmenopausal female status post REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy\u000arevealing DCIS with microinvasion, REMOVED_DATE  excision and SLNB; reexcision\u000arevealing DCIS with close margins and 2 negative lymph nodes, and REMOVED_DATE \u000areexcision revealing residual DCIS.\u000aOperation: Left simple mastectomy with tram flap and right reduction.\u000aOperative Findings: Not given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast - short superior, long lateral - 1,1167 g\u000aB/2. Left breast skin\u000aC/3. Right breast tissue - 469 g\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each part labeled with the\u000apatient's name and medical record number.\u000aPart A, "left breast, short superior, long lateral", consists of an 1165-gram\u000asimple mastectomy specimen (31.5 cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to\u000alateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior). A short stitch designates superior and\u000aa long stitch designates lateral per the surgeon. Also present is a skin\u000aellipse (10.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a nipple areolar complex (6.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a\u000aflat nipple. The deep surface of the specimen is inked black.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a previous biopsy cavity (5.5 x\u000a5.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) characterized by volume loss and surrounding fibrosis. The\u000abiopsy cavity is located in the upper inner quadrant and abuts the deep margin.\u000aNo other masses or lesions are noted. The breast is approximately 95% fatty\u000atissue and 5% fibrous tissue. The lateral breast tissue is searched for lymph\u000anodes but none are found.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area surrounding previous biopsy cavity, REMOVED_DATE frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart B, "left breast skin", consists of a circular fragment of skin (11.0 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm with a central punched out area of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The skin is unremarkable.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Left breast skin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart C, "right breast tissue", consists of 469 grams of breast tissue and skin\u000aare represented by eight fragments (16.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The\u000abreast tissue and skin are unremarkable. Representative sections are taken.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Right breast and skin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aJWH/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aThursday February 25, 2010 at 07:26:03PM\u000a[report_end]
