_DATE cm and contains a\u000aserosanguineous to pus-like fluid. No invasive lesions are grossly\u000aidentified. Four (4) possible lymph nodes are identified ranging from REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aup to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension. Representative sections are submitted as\u000afollows.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of fibrosed tissue subjacent to skin scar\u000afrom medial to lateral, 10 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of upper outer quadrant, 2 frags each,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of lower outer, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of inner upper quadrant, 2 frags each,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of lower inner quadrant, 2 frags each,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of each skin scar, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro 17: representative radial section of nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 18: 4 possible lymph node candidates, 4 frags, ESS.\u000akks\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODES REGIONAL RESECTION\u000a[report_end]
