ow/tan to pink/tan fibroadipose tissue and brown wrinkled skin\u000a(21.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The fragments are sectioned to exhibit\u000aapproximately 30% focally dense white/tan fibrous stroma and 70% yellow/tan\u000aadipose tissue lobulated adipose tissue with no discrete masses ore lesions\u000agrossly identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections of fibrous stroma and skin, 3 frags in\u000aeach, RSS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Lymph node right breast", consists of an irregular fragment of\u000ayellow/tan to pink/tan fibroadipose tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is\u000adissected to exhibit two pink/tan rubbery lymph node candidates (0.6 and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ain greatest dimension respectively).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 bisected lymph node candidate, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node candidate, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aLMB/LP\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/13/2006\u000a[report_end]
