VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNUCCI, MARISA, ROSE, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NUCCI,MARISA ROSE,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, NEEDLE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A DENSITY:\u000aComplex sclerosing lesion (0.3 cm).\u000aFibroadenoma (0.8 cm) present at inferomedial margin with extensive\u000acautery artifact.\u000aFibrocystic changes including apocrine cysts, intraductal papilloma,\u000aand focal epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aPrevious core biopsy site.\u000aNOTE: Extensive cautery artifact of breast tissue limits evaluation.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Right needle-localized breast biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right mammographic abnormality\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right needle-localized breast mass (to mammo)\u000a(long/lateral; short/superior; whip/deep margin)\u000aRadiology Report:\u000aTargeted density in specimen.\u000aE.P. Frost, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BENNETT,MICHAEL W.,M.B.,B.C.H\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "1) right needle-localized breast mass (to mammo)(short/superior;\u000along/lateral; whip/deep margin)", and consists of a portion of fibrofatty\u000atissue (4.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen has been marked by the surgeon with\u000athree (3) sutures: short/superior, long/lateral, and whip/deep margin. The\u000aspecimen has been inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. A localizing needle\u000aenters at the deep/lateral margin and exits the specimen at the median margin.\u000aAt the inferior and lateral aspect of the specimen is an area of white\u000afibrosis (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) that extends to involve the margins in these areas.\u000aAdjacent immediately to this area, is an area of yellowish discoloration (0.4 x\u000a0.3 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with adjacent hemorrhage. This area extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe deep margin of the specimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  entire specimen, lateral to medial (area of yellow discoloration\u000ain #6, 7, 8), 18 frag, ESS\u000amwb\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
