VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Anna Laury, M.D.; Eleanor Y. Chen, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION":\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia, columnar cell change and apocrine\u000ametaplasia.\u000aChanges consistent with core biopsy site.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast atypia on core biopsy of calcifications.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire-localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast atypia on core biopsy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast wire-localized excision, short stitch - superior, long -\u000alateral (to mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aIntact wire, clip and calcifications present in the sample.\u000a(No radiologist's signature)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000amedical record number, and "#1. Left breast wire localized excision, short\u000astitch superior, long lateral", and consists of a wire localized lumpectomy\u000aspecimen (3.4 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000asuperior to inferior). The specimen is received with a radiograph\u000ademonstrating a clip with a wire transversing a marked area. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a well-circumscribed soft, tan\u000anodule (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE ) which is; REMOVED_DATE cm to superior, REMOVED_DATE cm to inferior, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm to anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral resection margin. A clip is identified at the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the nodule. The specimen is entirely submitted for histology.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicular, 3 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of specimen (clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aAL/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/28/2007\u000a[report_end]
