VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGENEST, DAVID, RAYMOND, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GENEST,DAVID RAYMOND,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "POSTERIOR UPPER LEFT BREAST":\u000aFocal DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU arising in an area of florid ductal\u000ahyperplasia and atypical ductal hyperplasia (see note).\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU is present within REMOVED_DATE cm of the resection margin.\u000aMicrocalcifications in association with benign ductal epithelium.\u000aBiopsy site with repair reaction.\u000aNote: The diagnostic area of DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU measures less than REMOVED_DATE \u000acm.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "ANTERIOR LOWER LEFT BREAST":\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aMicrocalcifications in association with benign ductal epithelium.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Two areas of microcalcifications left breast upper outer\u000aquadrant. One of which had cone biopsy done showing DCIS\u000a(Faulkner Hospital). History of DCIS of left breast (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aOperation: Wire localization and breast resection (2 sites).\u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS left breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Posterior upper left breast\u000a2. Anterior lower left breast\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "POSTERIOR UPPER LEFT BREAST" (GROSS ONLY):\u000aNo areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "ANTERIOR LOWER LEFT BREAST" (GROSS ONLY):\u000aNo areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma,\u000abut tissue is slightly irregular. Await permanents.\u000aCalcifications are in both specimen. Jack Meyer, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by ENGELSGJERD,MARC C.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, "posterior upper left breast", consists of one, unoriented fragment\u000aof yellow/tan soft tissue (1.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with one needle localization\u000awire in place. The specimen is inked black. Sections showing remarkable\u000afibroadipose tissue with no areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma.\u000aMicro sections:\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, "anterior lower left breast", consists of one unoriented fragment of\u000ayellow/tan soft tissue (3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with one needle localization wire in\u000aplace. The specimen is inked black and section showed a linear area of\u000aindurated hemorrhagic tissue (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), possibly representing a\u000abiopsy needle biopsy tract. There are no areas grossly suspicious for invasive\u000acarcinoma.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  multiple frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: KANE, J.GREGORY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
