d around ducts/calcs associated with\u000abenign epithelium; REMOVED_DATE  - left breast ultrasound-guided core biopsy -\u000a"invasive mucinous cancer", well-diff - BR I/III - no lymphovascular invasion,\u000ano carcinoma in-situ. ER/PR+ - Her2Neu-.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left axillary tissue.\u000aB/2) left sentinel lymph nodes (fs).\u000aC/3) left breast.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2 - LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE(S)" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aTwo (2) lymph nodes; no tumor present.\u000aOR Consultation by: WILLIAM ROBERT WELCH, M.D.\u000aResident: JUSTINE BARLETTA, M.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patients\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1 - left axillary tissue", consists of two irregular\u000afragments of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (4.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate),\u000acontaining two pink/tan firm lymph node candidates (1.8 cm and REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000agreatest dimension, respectively), which are entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: one lymph node candidate serially sectioned, multiple frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: one lymph node candidate serially sectioned, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B is received in the frozen section room, labeled "#2 - left sentinel\u000alymph nodes", and consists of two fragments of pink/yellow soft tissue (3.0 cm\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension, respectively), which exhibit two pink/tan\u000alymph node candidates (2.2 cm and REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension, respectively).\u000aThe larger lymph node was previously bisected and entirely frozen as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, with\u000athe second lymph node candidate also previously bisected and frozen as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "#3 - left breast", consists of a 440 gram left simple\u000amastectomy specimen (16.5 m-l x REMOVED_DATE s-i x REMOVED_DATE a-p cm) with an attached\u000atan/white, wrinkled skin ellipse (13.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a central tan/pink\u000aeverted nipple (1.0 cm in diameter) and tan areola (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm). Per\u000asurgeon, the specimen exhibits two sutures (short suture superior, long suture\u000alateral). Located REMOVED_DATE cm inferolateral to the nipple is a well-healed linear\u000ascar (4.2 cm in length). The superomedial aspect of the areola exhibits a\u000awell-healed retracted curvilinear scar (3.2 cm in length). The deep margin\u000a(inked black) is predominantly a smooth fascial plane with a central, focally\u000adisrupted blue/green dyed (? sentinel node mapping procedure) area (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral. At\u000aapproximately 12 o'clock (at the junction of the upper/inner and upper/outer\u000aquadrant), there is an indurated tan/pink, lobulated, poorly delineated mass\u000a(1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the black-inked deep\u000amargin. Within the central portion of the mass is a yellow/tan\u000amucinous/gelatinous focus (0.8 cm in greatest dimension). Located REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ainferolateral to the aforementioned mass is a poorly delineated firm tan/white\u000avaguely nodular fibrous lesion (? biopsy cavity from prior excision procedure,\u000a1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the black-inked deep\u000amargin.\u000aThe remainder of the specimen is composed of approximately 30% dense, nodular,\u000alumpy, tan/white fibrous stroma and approximately 70% yellow/tan lobulated\u000aadipose tissue with multiple foci of blue/green discoloration as consistent\u000awith prior node mapping procedure.\u000aWithin the most-lateral breast tissue, one pink/tan rubbery intramammary lymph\u000anode candidate (0.9 cm in greatest dimension) is identified. An axillary tail\u000ais not present.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: nipple and areola with curvilinear scar, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: deep margin closest to mass, 12 o'clock, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: mass 12 o'clock sequentially submitted from lateral to\u000amedial (sections to exhibit greatest dimension of mass), 3\u000afrags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: ill-defined vaguely nodular lesion, inferolateral to mass to\u000ainclude deep margin, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: grossly unremarkable intervening tissue between 12 o'clock\u000amass and inferolateral lesion, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: dense/lumpy fibrous stroma, upper/outer quadrant, 4 frags,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: dense/lumpy fibrous stroma, upper/inner quadrant, 4 frags,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: dense/lumpy fibrous stroma, lower/outer quadrant, 4 frags,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: dense/lumpy fibrous stroma, lower/inner quadrant, 4 frags,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: one bisected lymph node candidate, 2 frags, ESS.\u000almb/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Ann K Folkins M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Shuji Ogino M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/6/2006\u000a[report_end]
