VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: KATHARINE CARTER M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Jian Shen, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, 2:00, 11 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR AN\u000aILL-DEFINED MASS:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, well differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson grade\u000aI/III), measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size. Numerous calcifications are\u000aassociated with the invasive carcinoma.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type (low nuclear grade), associated with\u000acalcifications, is present. No necrosis is seen.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 56 y/o female h/o left breast ALH and ADH; left breast ultrasound\u000alesion at 2:00, 5 cm from nipple vague, hypoechoic area.\u000aBreast Imaging Findings ill-defined.\u000aOperation: 11 G Ultrasound.\u000aOperative Findings: Cores obtained.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast lesion at 2:00, 5 cm from nipple; Blue cassette- Ca++ in "A".\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "Left\u000abreast", are two (2) blue cassettes.\u000aOne cassette is labeled "A. Ca++" and contains multiple, yellow/white\u000afibrofatty soft tissue cores (1.5 X REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aThe other cassette is not labeled and contains similar tissue fragments (1.5 X\u000a1.0 X REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "Ca++", multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: No calcifications, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aWP/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Jian Shen M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aResident Review by Jian Shen M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aPrelim Dx Release by Jian Shen M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aNo Action - Prelim Sent by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/14/2006\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
