VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Matthew D. Stachler, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Lynette M Sholl, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA/1) SENTINEL LYMPH NODE, LEFT\u000aSEE PART B.\u000aB/2) LEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY AND SENTINEL NODE BIOPSIES:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - Yes (see note)\u000aHistologic type - Ductal\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - III (Poor) (8 or 9 points)\u000aTubules - < 10% (3 points)\u000aNuclear grade - High (3 points)\u000aMitotic counts - 2 points\u000aEIC - Positive\u000aLVI - Absent\u000aDermal LVI - Absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - Not applicable\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - Deep (0.2 cm)\u000aNOTE: The invasive ductal carcinoma is present as two foci arising from an\u000aarea of high grade DCIS. Both foci measure REMOVED_DATE cm. Immunohistochemical\u000astudies performed on blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID at BWH confirm absence of p63 staining in\u000athe areas of invasion.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Comedo, Solid, Cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate to High\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - Deep (0.2 cm)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel lymph nodes - Negative (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 1\u000aAxillary lymph nodes - Negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 1\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- REMOVED_DATE \u000aOTHER FINDINGS:\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aPapilloma, involved by DCIS\u000aNipple skin with focal marked acute and chronic inflammation and giant cell\u000areaction\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Pending\u000aAJCC Classification (7th edition): REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX (with multiple foci of invasion)\u000aC/3) RIGHT BREAST TISSUE:\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 62 year old woman with mammogram mass L breast s/p U/S core biopsy\u000awith clip placement. She was followed in high risk clinic after ALH found on\u000abiopsy and was taking Evista\u000aOperation: Left simple mastectomy left SLN biopsy\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left invasive breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. SLN, left - FS\u000aB/2. Left breast tissue - long stitch at 3 o'clock, short stitch and documented\u000acancer site\u000aC/3. Right breast tissue\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "1. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE LEFT" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID AND REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aLymph node; negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: William Robert Welch, M.D.\u000aResident: Andrew G. Evans, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, specimen labeled "#1. Sentinel lymph node, left", consists of one lymph\u000anode (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen was bisected and entirely submitted as\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart B, specimen labeled "#2. Left breast tissue", consists of a 162-gram\u000asimple mastectomy (13.8 cm medial to lateral x REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior x\u000a3.1 cm anterior to posterior) with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm skin ellipse (a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000astrip of skin attached to a side of skin ellipse), a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm areola, and a\u000a1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm everted nipple. The specimen is oriented per the surgeon as long\u000aat 3 o'clock and short at documented cancer site. The deep margin is a smooth\u000afascial plane (inked black). Near the short stitch is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000apink/tan area of firmness, REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin. Within this area of\u000afirmness is a biopsy cavity and a metal clip. There is a second slightly firm\u000aarea (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is REMOVED_DATE cm posterior (toward 6 o'clock, if\u000ashort stitch is at 12 o'clock) and REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin. The second\u000amass is tan/white and protruding. The specimen is 60% adipose tissue and 40%\u000afibrous tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass by stitch, biopsy cavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Second described mass, with nipple in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue from 12 o'clock to 3 o'clock, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue from 9 o'clock to 12 o'clock, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue from 6 o'clock to 9 o'clock, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue from 3 o'clock to 6 o'clock, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aPart C, specimen labeled "#3. Right breast tissue", consists of an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm focally disrupted skin excision with an excision depth of up to REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Section to the skin, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aTAC/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lynette M Sholl M.D., Electronically signed on Thursday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 31, 2009 at 04:32:06PM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aNote: By report, ER, PR and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu studies were performed on the prior HVMA\u000acore biopsy that also demonstrated carcinoma that was negative for all three\u000amarkers (reviewed as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aNormal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen and\u000aprogesterone receptors.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following\u000acriteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells or moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a< 30% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate immunoreactivity.\u000aThe immunoperoxidase, immunofluorescence and in-situ hybridization tests\u000aperformed at Brigham and Women's Hospital were developed and their performance\u000acharacteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the\u000aDepartment of Pathology at BWH. They have not been cleared or approved by the\u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such\u000aclearance or approval is not necessary.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 05, 2010 at 09:07:36PM\u000a[report_end]
