VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR TWO CLUSTERS OF CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPEPLASIA, with associated adenosis and mucin production\u000awith calcifications, is present as a < REMOVED_DATE cm focus in block 6 (levels\u000aexamined) (see note).\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is also present in block 8 (levels examined).\u000aAdenosis and calcifications.\u000aNote: There is focal area of necrosis associated with the ADH present on\u000athe first level of the recut slides. There is an area of duct rupture\u000awith extravasation of mucin associated with the area of ADH. Small\u000aepithelial cell nests are present within the mucin. This area is\u000ainterpreted as most consistent with epithelial displacement into stroma\u000aassociated with the ruptured duct.\u000aNo ink is present on the tissue section containing the ADH.\u000aThe entire specimen was examined histologically, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Calcifications right breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Tissue right breast. The wire with the curl is the medial\u000awire.\u000aRADIOLOGY: 2 points of calcification in specimen. J. Leung, MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CORBO,JOSEPH,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "tissue right breast", and consists of a portion of yellow/tan\u000afibroadipose tissue (6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an two localizing wires in the\u000acentral portion of the specimen, one of which is curled at one end. The curled\u000awire designates the medial aspect of the specimen per surgeon. The specimen is\u000aotherwise unoriented. The medial half of the specimen is therefore inked in\u000ablue and the lateral half of the specimen is inked in black for the evaluation\u000aof margins. The specimen demonstrates some vague fibrous nodularity but there\u000aare no areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMICRO #1-7: Central area of specimen (where two localizing wires were located),\u000amult frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO #8-10: Portion of specimen lateral to central region of breast, mult\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMICRO #11-13: Portion of specimen medial to central region of breast, mult\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
