ring 17 cm from lateral to medial by REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior by\u000a1.9 cm from anterior to posterior. A short black suture is placed by the\u000asurgeon to indicate the superior aspect of the specimen, and a long black\u000asuture is placed by the surgeon to indicate the lateral aspect of the specimen.\u000aThere is a pink/tan skin ellipse measuring 15 cm from lateral to medial by 5 cm\u000afrom superior to inferior, containing an eccentrically placed nipple (1.4 x\u000a1.4 cm), surrounded by areolar tissue (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm). A biopsy cavity is\u000aidentifed (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which approaches to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep\u000amargin. No additional lesions are grossly identified. The breast parenchyma\u000ais composed of approximately 70% adipose and 30% fibrous tissue. No lymph\u000anodes are identified. Representative sections are submitted for histologic\u000aevaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Biopsy cavity and deep margin, 2 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 3: Upper outer quadrant sample, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 4: Lower outer quadrant sample, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 5: Upper inner quadrant sample, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 6: Lower inner quadrant sample, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 7: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000aPart 2, "Right breast tissue" consists of 426 g right simple mastectomy\u000ameasuring 19 cm from lateral to medial by 19 cm from superior to inferior by\u000a2.2 cm from anterior to posterior. A short black suture was placed by the\u000asurgeon to indicate the superior aspect of the specimen and a long black suture\u000awas placed by the surgeon to indicate the lateral aspect of the specimen.\u000aThere is a pink/tan skin ellipse measuring 14 cm from lateral to medial by REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from superior to inferior. It contains a centrally placed nipple (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) surrounded by areolar tissue (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE cm). No lesions are grossly\u000aidentified. The breast parenchyma is composed of approximately 60% adipose and\u000a40% fibrous tissue. No lymph nodes are identified. No lesions are grossly\u000aidentified. Represenative sections are submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro 8: Upper outer quadrant sample, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 9: Lower outer quadrant sample, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 10: Upper inner quadrant sample, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 11: Lower inner quadrant sample, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 12: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
