VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM FAULKNER HOSPITAL, BOSTON, MA:\u000aLEFT BREAST, MEDIAL, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (by report, present in 2 of 17 blocks), REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the inked superior margin (see note).\u000aIntraductal papilloma.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aNOTE: The ADH involves five duct profiles in two slides (slides REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). The cells form arcades in four of the ducts and micropapillae in\u000aone duct. Although the findings approach a diagnosis of low grade DCIS,\u000adue to the limited extent and incomplete involvement of spaces, a\u000adiagnosis of ADH is favored.\u000aThe ADH is REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin. By report, a separate wire\u000alocalized excision of the left breast, "superior" showed no evidence of\u000amalignancy. Clinical correlation is necessary to determine if this second\u000aspecimen would be considered the superior margin of the first specimen.\u000aIf not, re-excision could be considered to exclude an adjacent area of\u000aDCIS. The ADH is also REMOVED_DATE cm from yellow inked tissue (the deep margin).\u000aIt is difficult to determine if this is the true deep margin, or ink\u000aleakage into tissue.\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. Andrea Richardson who concurs with the\u000adiagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast atypical papilloma.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Consult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by YANG,TAO,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aReceived from Faulkner Hospital, Pathology Department, 1153 Centre Street,\u000aBoston, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are three (3) slides.\u000aThe slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID",\u000acorresponding to a left breast, medial, partial mastectomy with wire\u000alocalization (5 x 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the\u000aaccompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aIncluded is a pathology report from the same institution numbered "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID",\u000acorresponding to a left breast ultrasound guided core biopsy (0.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report\u000abearing the patient's name, (outside diagnosis: intraductal papilloma, columnar\u000aaltered hyperplastic ducts, several).\u000aReports to: SADOWSKY, NORMAN, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000a[report_end]
