VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Cheryl Adackapara, M.D.; Eleanor Y. Chen, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (best seen in block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aCore needle biopsy site changes.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar cell changes.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aNote: The patient had a prior core needle biopsy in the central outer\u000abreast showing atypical ductal hyperplasia (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). Clinical and\u000aradiologic correlation is needed to determine if this specimen is an excision\u000aof this site.\u000aThere is no malignancy or atypical ductal hyperplasia seen upon\u000amicroscopic examination of the entire specimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 58 year old woman with recent abnormal mammogram which showed an area\u000aof microcalcifications in the lower inner quadrant of the right breast. A\u000abiopsy of this area showed columnar cell change with calcifications. However,\u000aa core needle biopsy of the central outer breast showed ADH.\u000aOperation: None given.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Tissue marker and faint residual ca++ in specimen. Hookwire also\u000apresent. C. Denison, MD.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "R breast tissue", and consists of a fragment of fibroadipose\u000atissue (5.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE 