tion\u000ashows invasive lobular carcinoma present in association with stromal changes\u000acompatible with treatment effect in six of six slides reviewed. By report, an\u000aestimated 80% reduction in tumor volume is present, corresponding to a\u000aMiller-Payne Grade 3 response to chemotherapy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: S/P right sentinel node mapping and completion right axillary node\u000adissection at BWH REMOVED_DATE  +1/7 nodes, s/p TAC chemo REMOVED_DATE  - REMOVED_DATE  for\u000alocally advanced ILC. Initial estimates of tumor size were 6 cm, clip was left\u000ain breast at time of core biopsy. Pt requests right mastectomy and\u000aprophylactic left mastectomy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: ILC and LCIS\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aConsult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived from Faulkner Hospital, Pathology Department, 1153 Centre Street,\u000aBoston, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are six (6) glass slides.\u000aThe slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through\u000a"REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", corresponding to a right breast total mastectomy (18.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aperformed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing\u000athe patient's name.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
