VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Li Chen, M.D., Ph.D.; Stephanie Schulte, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP:\u000aNo residual atypical proliferation present.\u000aExcision site changes.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar cell change with cysts and calcifications.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aFocal lactational change.\u000aFibroadenomatoid change.\u000aAn immunohistochemical double stain for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID demonstrates the presence\u000aof myoepithelial cells in ducts around the biopsy site.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aB. LEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION:\u000aBenign breast tissue and nipple ducts with biopsy site changes.\u000aAn immunohistochemical double stain for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID demonstrates the presence\u000aof myoepithelial cells in ducts around the biopsy site.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aC. RIGHT BREAST, EXCISON FOR A LATERAL DENSITY:\u000aBenign breast tissue with prominent thick walled cysts (covering a REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aarea).\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Wire directed excision.\u000aOperation: Re-excision.\u000aOperative Findings: See Op-Note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Excision biopsy of left breast -> ADH - present at anterior\u000amargin for re-excision. Core biopsy of right breast - ADH.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue (long stitch lateral, short stitch superior) -> mammo.\u000aB/2. Re-excision left breast.\u000aC/3. Lateral density (long suture medial, short suture posterior nipple) open\u000afor situ right breast.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Biopsy clip and intact wire in specimen. Phoned to Dr. Cristian by\u000aDr. Lizer 2:08 pm\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand medical record number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast tissue", consists of a REMOVED_DATE (superior to inferior) x\u000a4.0 (lateral to medial) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior) cm breast excision\u000aspecimen with localization wire in place and short suture marking the superior\u000amargin and a long suture marking the lateral margin. An accompanying specimen\u000aradiograph demonstrates metal clip within the specimen, adjacent to the\u000alocalization wire. The specimen is inked for the evaluation of margins:\u000aPosterior equals black, anterior equals blue, superior equals red, inferior\u000aequals green, lateral equals yellow, and medial equals orange. No gross lesion\u000aat the clip site can be identified. The specimen consists of unremarkable\u000afibroadipose tissue. The entire specimen is submitted for histological\u000aexamination with clip site in cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Clip site, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tissue surrounding the clip site, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of the specimen, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Reexcision left breast", consists of REMOVED_DATE (lateral to medial) x REMOVED_DATE \u000asuperior to inferior) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior) cm breast excision specimen\u000awith a short suture marking the posterior nipple and the long suture marking\u000athe medial margin. The specimen is inked for the evaluation of margins:\u000aPosterior equals black, anterior equals blue, superior equals red, inferior\u000aequals green, lateral equals yellow, and medial equals orange. No gross lesion\u000acan be identified. The specimen is submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Lateral density at operation site right breast", consists of\u000ayellow/pink unoriented fibroadipose tissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen\u000ais inked, bisected and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-09-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aLC/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 14, 2009 at 04:53:26PM\u000a[report_end]
