VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D.; Scott Lovitch, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER INNER, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A\u000aCLIP:\u000aCalcifications are associated with small cysts and benign epithelium.\u000aCore biopsy site changes are present.\u000aNote: The patient underwent a prior core needle biopsy for\u000acalcifications that showed atypical ductal hyperplasia (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). All\u000afibrous tissue is examined, including margins, and no additional areas of\u000aatypical hyperplasia are seen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 52 year old post-menopausal woman, whose REMOVED_DATE  mammogram of REMOVED_DATE \u000amag views demonstrated L UIQ calcifications. REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy revealed\u000aatypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: L breast wire-localization biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left breast tissue, short suture/superior, long/lateral, whipstitch on\u000adeep margin (to mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aLeft clip, hookwire, density, few faint calcifications. Called to OR. Dr.\u000aPeters.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in a single container, labeled with the\u000apatient's name, medical record number, and "#1. Left breast tissue, short\u000asuture superior, long lateral, whipstitch on deep margin". It consists of a\u000asingle wire-localized breast excision specimen, which measures REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000asuperior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral to medial, and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior\u000ato posterior. A short suture marks the superior aspect of the specimen, a long\u000asuture marks the lateral aspect, and a whipstitch marks the deep margin. The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. Please note, the specimen is received inked by the surgeon.\u000aThere is a single localization wire in the specimen, which enters at the\u000aanteromedial margin and terminates in the specimen. The entry point of the\u000awire is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin.\u000aThe specimen radiograph provided shows the wire passing through an ill-defined\u000amass, as well as a clip adjacent to the wire within the mass. Faint\u000acalcifications are present in this area. Serial sectioning reveals a firm,\u000awell-circumscribed, pink/white mass, which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, located\u000aadjacent to the wire and containing the clip site. Grossly, it extends to\u000awithin REMOVED_DATE cm of the nearest medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the nearest inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the nearest lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the nearest superior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the nearest anterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the nearest\u000aposterior margin. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass and closest medial and inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass and closest anterior, superior, and lateral margins, 1 frag, ESS\u000a(please note: The section is contiguous with the section in cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional mass and anterior and inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional mass and lateral margin, 1 frag, ESS (please note: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID represent a contiguous section).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional mass and superior, inferior, anterior, medial, and\u000alateral margins (contiguous section), 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional lateral margin, and inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional superior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional medial, and inferior margin and posterior margin, 1 frag,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest posterior margin, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remaining fibrous breast tissue and additional lateral, superior,\u000aand posterior margins, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aPlease note: The entire mass is submitted in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, with the clip\u000asite located in cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (clip removed prior to processing). In total, the\u000aspecimen consists of approximately 90% yellow-white adipose tissue and 10%\u000afibrous tissue. All of the fibrous tissue in the specimen is submitted. In\u000atotal, approximately 70% of the tissue in the specimen is submitted.\u000aSBL/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a6/30/2008\u000a[report_end]
