VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000a1] SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST EXCISION WITH WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS":\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA - not present\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Cribriform, apocrine.\u000aNuclear grade - Low\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (<0.3 cm) - superior, posterior, medial\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) - Lateral, anterior, inferior\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present, extensive\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia,atypical lobular hyperplasia, fibroadenoma,\u000acalcifications in benign epithelium, cysts, apocrine metaplasia.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - Tis pNX MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Pending\u000a2] SPECIMEN LABELED "FRAGMENTS OF CALCIUM":\u000aFibroadenoma.\u000aNOTE: No calcifications present.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block 6):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) VARIABLE\u000aNote: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu immunoreactivity varies from weakly to focally strongly\u000apositive.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast calcifications.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire directed excisional biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast calcifications\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a#1) Tissue from left breast (stitch markings: short/superior; long/lateral)\u000a#2) ? fragments of calcium (taken by Dr. Christian to mammo)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcs in specimen. CD/JMS\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SCHMIDT,JASON F.,M.D.\u000aTwo specimens are received fresh, each labeled with the patient's name and unit\u000anumber.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. left breast tissue", consists of a single portion of\u000abreast tissue (4.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Accompanying the specimen is a specimen\u000aradiograph demonstrating multiple calcifications scattered throughout the\u000aspecimen. Two orienting sutures are present designated as follows:\u000along/lateral, short/superior. The specimen has been previously inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior =\u000ablue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral. The specimen is\u000acomposed primarily of heterogenous tan/white to yellow rubbery tissue\u000a(approximately 80%) which extends to the inked margins. The remainder of the\u000atissue is composed of yellow lobulated adipose tissue)approximately 20%). No\u000adiscrete lesions are identified. The specimen is entirely submitted for\u000ahistologic examination.\u000aMicro 1: breast tissue, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 2: breast tissue, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 3: breast tissue, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 4: breast tissue, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 5: breast tissue, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 6: breast tissue, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, 1 level bisected, 1 frag each, RSS\u000aMicro 9: breast tissue, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 10: breast tissue, 1 frag, RSS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. fragments of calcium", consists of two portions of\u000atan/white to tan/brown soft tissue (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aAn accompanying specimen radiograph does not demonstrate any calcifications.\u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro 11: soft tissue, 2 frags, ESS\u000ajfs\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
