VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNOSE, VANIA, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NOSE,VANIA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION WIRE-LOCALIZATION (SPECIMEN 1):\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Cribiform, clinging, apocrine\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate to high\u000aCalcification with DCIS - Present\u000aNecrosis with DCIS - Absent\u000aMargins DCIS:\u000aNegative: - Superior, lateral, posterior\u000aClose (0.1 cm): - Medial and inferior: multifocal\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - present\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aBiopsy cavity\u000aSkin with scar\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - performed previously\u000aNOTE:\u000aSkin with seborrheic keratosis.\u000aDr. Susan Lester concurs.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATION (SPECIMEN 2):\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aOther findings: Atypical ductal hyperplasia, sclerosing adenosis, fibroadenoma\u000aand calcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: DCIS left breast microcalcification, left breast. DCIS, resected, but\u000aclose margins.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localized excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS, left breast; microcalcifications, left breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Site of DCIS, left breast to FS.\u000a2. Area of microcalcifciations, left breast. Suture short margin. Long\u000alateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Ca++ in specimen - site #1, UOQ posterior. epf\u000aCA++ in specimen - site #2, anterior. epf\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHEN,JEY-HSIN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aReceived fresh in the Frozen Section Room in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit 