panying specimen radiograph demonstrates the distal end of the\u000alocalization wire adjacent to a clip and vague calcifications. The specimen is\u000asectioned into nine slices from inferior to superior with the area around the\u000awire being present in slices 6 and 7 at the superior aspect. There is a piece\u000aof gel foam (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) in slices 6 and 7, which comes to within REMOVED_DATE \u000acm of the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE of the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial margin, 2 cm of the superior margin and greater\u000athan 2 cm from the inferior margin. No masses are grossly identified, and the\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen is entirely submitted from inferior to superior\u000a(Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID area around wire with gel foam, 30 frags,\u000aESS).\u000aAF/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
