l/orange. The accompanying\u000aradiograph is examined. There is an excision cavity present in the specimen\u000a(3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm depth). There is a localization wire entering the specimen\u000ain the prior excision cavity. The orientation of the wire cannot be clearly\u000aidentified as it is partially dislocated, but it appears to be entering the\u000aspecimen on the lateral aspect. Upon sectioning, the specimen contains\u000aapproximately 40% fibrous and 60% adipose tissue. The fibrous tissue is\u000apredominantly located adjacent to superior and anterior margins (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a2.0 cm) as well as surrounding the prior excision cavity. The fibrous tissue\u000ais entirely submitted from medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial and inferior margins, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Small anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior and posterior margins, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior and lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral, superior, and posterior margins, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aAWE/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/24/2008\u000a[report_end]
