JCC CLASSIFICATION - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Performed previously\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 56 year old female with right breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Right wire (local excision) breast (short/superior;\u000along/lateral)\u000a#2) Right sentinel node biopsy\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass and clip in specimen. JL\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BUNDOCK,ELIZABETH A.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. right wire local excision breast", consists of a portion\u000aof fibroadipose tissue (7.5 x 5 x 2 cm) with a localization wire and two\u000asutures (short to designate superior, long to designate lateral) in place. The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral\u000a= yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is sectioned serially at 3 mm\u000aintervals from medial to lateral to reveal tissue which is 75% rubbery white\u000afibrosis which extends to the inferior, medial and posterior margins, is REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the superior margin, and more than 1 cm from the lateral margin. The clip\u000ais found in the lateral aspect of a firm white mass (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which\u000ais apparent on the accompanying specimen radiograph. The mass extends to the\u000adeep and inferior margins and is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior, 2 cm from\u000athe anterior, and 2 cm from the lateral margin. The mass is submitted\u000aentirely in series in cassettes one through four. Representative sections of\u000athe remaining fibrous tissue and margins are submitted. The specimen is also\u000areceived with a specimen radiograph which is reported as mass and clip in\u000aspecimen. A separate specimen radiograph is taken in pathology to localize the\u000aclip in the sectioned specimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass surrounding clip, clip in #4, 5 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of dense fibrosis (approximately 75%), 8\u000afrags, RSS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. rt sentinel node biopsy", consists of one fragment of\u000ayellow/tan adipose tissue (2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which contains one lymph node (0.6\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aMicro 10: 1 lymph node, 1 frag, ESS\u000aeab\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000a[report_end]
