VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR A CLIP MARKING AN AREA OF PRIOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aApcrine metaplasia and microcysts.\u000aCalcifications are present associated with benign epithelium.\u000aA prior biopsy site is present.\u000aNOTE: No malignancy is seen after microscopic examination of the entire\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Prior core needle bx for calcifications, showed columnar alteration of\u000alobules with prominent snouts and secretions associated with numerous\u000acalcifications.\u000aOperation: R needle directed breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. R breast mass.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip in specimen. OR called.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HENDERSON,JOEL M.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1 right breast mass", and consists of a single fragment of tan/yellow,\u000afibroadipose tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) containing a localization wire, and\u000apreviously oriented by the surgeon and inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is\u000aaccompanied by a whole specimen radiograph, which shows the localization wire\u000amarking a central clip with no densities or calcifications identified. The\u000aspecimen is sliced from medial to lateral to reveal uniform tan/yellow fibrous\u000atissue with a central core needle biopsy site. No distinct lesions are\u000aidentified. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 1: slice 1, medial margin, sectioned perpendicularly, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2&3: slices 2&3, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slices REMOVED_DATE  each split into superior and inferior segments, 10\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro 9: slice 9, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 10: slice 10, lateral margin, sectioned perpendicularly, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aNOTE: The clip was identified in slice 6.\u000ajmh\u000aReports to: WHANG, EDWARD, E. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
