\u000aThe specimen, Part C, is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit\u000anumber, and "Left breast", received in a white, mesh cassette, labeled "Left",\u000aand consists of multiple fibrofatty cores aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Left breast cores, multiple frags, ESS.\u000adb/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aMicroscopic/Diagnostic Dictation by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/6/2005\u000a[report_end]
