VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: David C. Park, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jonathan N Glickman, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, EXCISION WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS":\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Cribriform, micropapillary\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - 4:13 blocks\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Anterior, posterior, superior, inferior,\u000amedial\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - Lateral (0.1 cm; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, focal)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - Tis Nx MX.\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Pending\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 78 year old female with abnormal left mammo.\u000aOperation: None given.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast needle loc, stitch long lateral short superior to mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcifications in specimen. Hookwire present. C. Denison, MD.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. L breast needle loc, stitch long lateral, short superior", consists of\u000aa yellow/tan portion of fibroadipose tissue (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with two\u000aorienting sutures ("long stitch lateral, short stitch superior") and an intact\u000ahookwire (ensuring at the lateral aspect). The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from superior to inferior, exhibiting approximately equal\u000aportions of yellow lobulated adipose tissue and tan/white dense stroma. Focal\u000ahemorrhage is present adjacent to the insertion site of the localization wire.\u000aThe specimen is accompanied by a radiograph, exhibiting an intact hookwire and\u000aprobable calcifications adjacent to the hookwire head. No other gross lesions\u000aare identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue sequentially from superior to inferior (probable\u000acalcifications in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adl/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/22/2008\u000aADDENDUM (01/28/08):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE-LOW\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) POSITIVE (3+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/28/2008\u000a[report_end]
