VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, MASTECTOMY:\u000aRESIDUAL INVASIVE MUCINOUS CARCINOMA, well differentiated (modified\u000aBloom-Richardson grade I/III) is present adjacent to the prior biopsy site\u000a(0.4 cm).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is present.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type (low nuclear grade) is present in one\u000aslide, adjacent to the prior biopsy site. No calcifications or necrosis\u000aare present.\u000aThe deep margin is free of carcinoma.\u000aThe skin shows a cicatrix but no tumor is seen.\u000aLactational changes are present.\u000aTen lymph nodes with no tumor seen. Immunoperoxidase studies for\u000acytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID are performed on all of the nodes and no carcinoma is\u000aidentified.\u000aNote: A prior excision (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) revealed a REMOVED_DATE cm invasive carcinoma.\u000aThe AJCC classification is REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast (505 kg).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BAILEY,GERALD P.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1, left breast", and is an 18 x 16 x REMOVED_DATE cm with an axillary tail\u000a(4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) marked by suture). A nipple (1.3 cm in diameter) and\u000aareola (4.5 cm in diameter) are present. A skin ellipse (3.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a\u000acentral scar (2.1 cm in length) is located REMOVED_DATE cm inferior to the edge of the\u000aareola. The posterior surface of the specimen is inked black. There is dense\u000afibrosis throughout 70% of the specimen with diffuse white granular punctate\u000aareas mixed within the fibrosis. There is fibrosis underlying the biopsy site\u000abut there is no obvious gross tumor mass.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  contiguous portions of skin, biopsy site and posterior margin,\u000a1 frag each cass., RSS.\u000aMicro 4: biopsy site, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  central, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 13: 6 potential lymph nodes, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 14: 4 potential lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 15: 1 lymph node, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 16: 1 lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 17: 1 lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000ageb\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
