VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aODZE, ROBERT, DANIEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by ODZE,ROBERT DANIEL,M.D.\u000a1) RIGHT BREAST, POSTERIOR SHAVE MARGIN, RE-EXCISION:\u000aBreast tissue with apocrine metaplasia and cysts and fibrosis.\u000aSkin with scar.\u000aPrior biopsy site is present.\u000aNo residual atypical ductal hyperplasia or atypical papilloma is present.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 65 year old postmenopausal female s/p right retroareolar duct\u000aexcision of the right nipple discharge and negative breast imaging\u000awith unsuccessful attempt at ductogram. Pathology revealed severely\u000aatypical ductal hyperplasia with an atypical papilloma within 1 mm of\u000athe posterior margin, re-excision is recommended.\u000aOperation: Right breast excision\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right severely atypical ductal hyperplasia, atypical\u000apapilloma\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Posterior shave margin - whip stitch on new margin\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMO,LESLEY C.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. posterior shave margin - whip stitch on new margin", and\u000aconsists of a single yellow/tan, focally hemorrhagic fragment of fibrofatty\u000abreast tissue (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a whip stitch along one aspect\u000adesignating new margin. The opposite surface is smooth, red/tan, and granular,\u000agrossly consistent with prior biopsy site. The surface is inked in blue, and\u000athe surface designated with the whip stitch is inked black. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned to reveal focal hemorrhagic areas and areas of fat necrosis\u000asubjacent to the biopsy site. Also received in the same container are two\u000afragments of white/pink/yellow soft tissue; the first fragment, which measures\u000a1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm is unoriented, is inked in black, and serially sectioned to\u000areveal unremarkable white fibrous tissue, and a small amount of what appears to\u000abe pink tissue consistent with prior biopsy site. The second detached\u000afragment, is also unoriented, and contains fragments of skin (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm,\u000aexcised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm). The skin ellipse has been longitudinally cut\u000afrom one edge to a length of REMOVED_DATE cm. No scar is definitively identified. The\u000adeep margin is inked in black, the specimen serially sectioned, and entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast posterior shave margin, 2 or 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 6: detached soft tissue fragment, 6 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 7: skin ellipse tips of second detached fragment, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 8: detached soft tissue fragment of skin, mult frags, ESS\u000alcl\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
