VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: EVA C. GOMBOS M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Rachel L Rucker-Schmidt, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 12:00, MRI-GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR CLUMPED LINEAR\u000aENHANCEMENT:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform and papillary types (low nuclear grade) is\u000apresent. No necrosis or calcifications are associated with DCIS. An\u000aimmunoperoxidase study for p63 confirms the presence of myoepithelial cells\u000aaround the periphery of areas of DCIS, and not in fibrovascular cores.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aDCIS LCIS\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aE-cadherin POSITIVE NEGATIVE\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: Right clumped enhancement in linear distribution at 12 o'clock in\u000apatient with h/o right duct excision in 2001 --> path ADH.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: 4 mm, Nonpalpable, linear, clumped and non-mass forming.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: 12:00\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. MRI\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. MRI - Blue/white - 2 cassettes\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber and "Blue and white, two cassettes, right breast", and consists of two\u000acassettes both with white bases and blue tops. The first white base blue top\u000acassette contains multiple tan/pink tissues that aggregate to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. The second unlabeled white base blue top cassette contains multiple\u000atan/yellow tissues that aggregate to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: The first-described white base blue top unlabeled cassette contents,\u000amulti frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: The second-described white base blue top cassette contents, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aPF/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a3/24/2008\u000a[report_end]
