VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST COMPREHENSIVE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM NAPLES PATHOLOGY, NAPLES, FL:\u000aLEFT BREAST MASS (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR (3 cm) with focal areas of LIPOSARCOMA.\u000aMitoses in the majority of the tumor range from REMOVED_DATE per 10 HPF's (average\u000a1 per HPF's; 50 HPF's, counted).\u000aIn the sarcomatous areas, mitoses number up to 6 per HPF.\u000aNuclear pleomorphism ranges from moderate to marked.\u000aStromal overgrowth is present.\u000aSingle cell necrosis is present.\u000aThe tumor invades into the surrounding stroma.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia is present.\u000aMonckeberg's medial calcific sclerosis is present in blood vessels.\u000aNOTE: The majority of the lesion would be considered intermediate grade.\u000aHowever, in two blocks (11 and 14) liposarcoma is present. Thus, this\u000ashould be considered a high grade tumor.\u000aAccording to the original report, the specimen was received incised and\u000athe final margin status could not be determined. A wide local excision is\u000arecommended.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Consult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by MANTEL,MICHELLE HAVA,M.D.\u000aReceived from Naples Pathology Associates, 366 Goodlette Road, South, Naples,\u000aFL, REMOVED_CASE_ID are fourteen glass slides.\u000aThe slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "01" through "14",\u000acorresponding to excision of left breast mass (6 x 6 x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed on\u000a07/27/1999, according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the\u000apatient's name.\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST COMPREHENSIVE\u000a[report_end]
