is received in three parts, each labeled with the patient's name\u000aand unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "left breast mass", consists of a single fragment of\u000ayellow/tan fibrofatty tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with three orienting\u000asutures: short=superior, long=lateral and whipstitch=deep. There is an\u000aattached pink/white skin ellipse with a scar (4.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000aspecimen is inked for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior =\u000ablue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aSections of margins are submitted for microscopic examination. Sectioning\u000areveals dense fibrous tissue (4.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is grossly less than\u000a0.1 cm from the black/anterior, red/superior, and orange/medial margins. The\u000aspecimen is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the yellow margin and greater than REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe green margin. Representative sections are submitted. No areas are grossly\u000asuspicious for invasive carcinoma.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous area, mult frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  uninvolved breast parenchyma including all margins, mult frags,\u000aRSS\u000aPart two, labeled "inferior shave margin", consists of a single fragment of\u000atan/yellow adipose tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is marked with a\u000awhipstitch which designates the new margin. The new margin is inked in blue.\u000aThe side opposite the new margin has tan/white fibrous cauterized area\u000aconsistent with previous surgery. Sectioning reveals dense fibrous tissue and\u000atan/yellow fat necrosis which extends to the inked margin. Representative\u000asections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  new inferior margin, perpendicular sections with respect to new\u000amargin, 4 frags, RSS\u000aPart three, labeled "medial shave margin", consists of a single fragment of\u000atan/yellow/white fibrofatty tissue (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which a whipstitch that\u000ais designated the new margin. The side opposite the margin has tan/yellow fat\u000anecrosis consistent with previous surgery. The specimen consists of tan/white\u000adense fibrous tissue which grossly extends to the new margin. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted and perpendicular sections with respect to the new margin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  new margin, mult frags, ESS\u000ajd\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
