ATE \u000acm tan/white cystic mass containing purulent white cloudy material extending\u000ato within REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm to the\u000asuperior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial, and REMOVED_DATE cm to the\u000alateral resection margin. In addition there is a REMOVED_DATE cm simple cyst extending\u000ato within REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000asuperior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial resection margin.\u000aNo other gross masses or lesions are present. The greatest dimensions of the\u000aspecimen are medial to lateral, followed by superior to inferior; the specimen\u000ais submitted in its entirety in serial sections from the medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial edge, mult frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  specimen in serial sections from medial to lateral, cyst in 4\u000athrough 6, 8, and 9, mult frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral edge, mult frags, ESS\u000amcc\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
