VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kevin B Long, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST NEEDLE-LOCALIZATION EXCISIONAL\u000aBIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS:"\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aClinical History: Status post core biopsy with atypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: Left needle localization, breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Needle directed left breast mass - mammo (for confirmation of needle\u000alocalization) toward surgical superior, long stitch equals lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aClip, calcs and wire in specimen. M Segal/Rad.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number\u000a"#1, needle directed left breast mass" and consists of a REMOVED_DATE (posterior to\u000aanterior) x REMOVED_DATE (lateral to medial) x REMOVED_DATE (superior to inferior) cm breast\u000abiopsy with a localization wire in place and short suture marking the superior\u000amargin and a long suture marking the lateral margin. An accompanying specimen\u000aradiograph demonstrates a clip, calcifications, and the wire in the specimen.\u000aThe specimen is inked for evaluation of margins: Posterior equals black;\u000aanterior equal blue; superior equals red; inferior equals green; lateral equals\u000ayellow; and medial equals orange. There is a white/tan skin ellipse measuring\u000a1.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm yellow/tan well-defined mass with\u000afocal areas of red/pink/brown central hemorrhage. The lesion comes to within\u000a0.4 cm from the lateral and superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin/skin.\u000aRed/brown hemorrhage consistent with needle tract is present focally throughout\u000athe specimen. One brown/red possible intraparenchymal lymph node is identified\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension. The entire lesion and approximately\u000a75% of the specimen is submitted for histologic evaluation. The uninvolved\u000abreast parenchyma consists of predominantly (greater than 90%) grossly\u000aunremarkable yellow adipose tissue. The specimen is submitted according to a\u000aspecimen diagram.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lesion and posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lesion and superior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lesion and superior and lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lesion and superior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lesion and superior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin of skin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional medial and inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aKEL/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/12/2006\u000a[report_end]
