VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Marian H Harris, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - no\u000aHistologic Type - lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - intermediate\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - absent\u000aSkin invasion - absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - deep\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aBiopsy cavity\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa MX (from previous excision\u000aBS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - previously ordered\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Ca of lt breast, large tumor\u000aOperation: (L) simple mastectomy\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: (L) breast CA\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a(31) Left breast stitch marks tail.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "1. Left breast, stitch marks tail", and consists of a 998-gm (25 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a4.0 cm) simple mastectomy specimen. There is a tan/white skin ellipse,\u000ameasuring a 19 x REMOVED_DATE cm with a REMOVED_DATE cm healing scar apparently running through\u000aan inverted nipple. The remaining areola/nipple measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There\u000ais a suture designated by the surgeon to mark "tail". The posterior surface of\u000athe specimen is a smooth, fascial plane except for an area of\u000apuckering/firmness subjacent to the nipple. The posterior surface is inked\u000ablack. The previous biopsy cavity is identified, subjacent to the nipple and\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The cavity and surrounding firmness abuts the\u000adeep margin. The remainder of the specimen consists of grossly unremarkable,\u000afibroadipose tissue. No lymph node candidates are identified within the\u000alateral portion of the specimen. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy cavity to deep margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional biopsy cavity, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Firm area adjacent to biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple with scar and biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper/outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower/outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper/inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower/inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional firm area adjacent (lateral) to biopsy site,\u000a1 frag, RSS.\u000amah/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Marian H Harris M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
