VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Consult material\u000aProcedure Date:\u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Martin C Chang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM LEONARD MORSE HOSPITAL/METROWEST, NATICK, MA:\u000aLEFT BREAST, RETROAREOLAR, CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR AN ASYMMETRIC DENSITY\u000a(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia with atypical features involving an area of\u000agynecomastia.\u000aNOTE: Some areas of epithelial hyperplasia have a discohesive round-cell\u000aappearance, closely resembling lobular neoplasia in situ. An immunoperoxidase\u000astudy performed at the outside institution shows strong cytoplasmic\u000aimmunoreactivity for e-cadherin (reviewed). This would be an unusual result\u000afor lobular neoplasia. It is possible the appearance of the cells is due to\u000afixation artifact. However, an unusual form of atypical hyperplasia cannot be\u000acompletely excluded.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of melanoma.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Gynecomastia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aConsult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived from Metrowest Medical Center, Inc., Leonard Morse Hospital, Pathology\u000aDepartment, 67 Union Street, Natick, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are six (6) glass slides.\u000aThe slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "E-CAD"\u000aand "(-)", corresponding to a left breast, retroareolar, core biopsy (2.0 x\u000a0.15 cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report\u000abearing the patient's name.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a3/20/2007\u000a[report_end]
