VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Juan-Miguel Mosquera, M.D., M.S.C.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, BIOPSY FOR A PALPABLE MASS:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, consisting of cells with enlarged pleomorphic\u000anuclei in a pagetoid pattern (best seen in block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; levels examined). There\u000aare very focal areas with a cribriform pattern.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed with the following results for the\u000aatypical cells:\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aHER-2/neu HETEROGENEOUS (1+ to focal 2+)\u000aE-Cadherin: POSITIVE\u000aGynecomastia.\u000aNote: The patient had a prior core needle biopsy that showed epithelial\u000ahyperplasia with atypical features (reviewed as BWH REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). The excision\u000ashows similar findings. The positivity for e-cadherin excludes classification\u000aas lobular neoplasia. The findings are unusual in a male and would be best\u000aclassified as atypical ductal hyperplasia. The entire specimen, including\u000amargins, is examined microscopically.\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Andrea Richardson, who concurs with this\u000ainterpretation.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Core biopsy of the breast showed "hyperplasia with atypical\u000afeatures". History of malignant melanoma of the left thigh in 1994.\u000aOperation: Left breast mass, left breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast mass.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast mass", and consists of an unoriented yellow/tan/white,\u000afocally cauterized to hemorrhagic portion of fibroadipose tissue (1.9 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.2 cm). Specimen is inked and serially sectioned, exhibiting a predominantly\u000awhite/tan, focally cystic fibrous stroma admixed with scant adipose tissue. No\u000aother gross lesions identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000adfi/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/24/2007\u000a[report_end]
