areas of red, yellow, blue,\u000agreen, and black ink as wells as a focus of uninked tissue. The surface of\u000athe smaller portion of tissue has areas of black, blue, and orange ink as well\u000aas a focus of uninked tissue. No discrete lesions or masses are identified.\u000aThe specimen is composed primarily of yellow, lobulated adipose tissue\u000a(approximately 95%) with interwoven strands of tan/white fibrous tissue (5%).\u000aThe specimen is submitted in its entirety for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Larger portion of tissue from lateral to anterior, 19 frags\u000a(slices bisected in REMOVED_DATE ), ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Smaller portion of tissue, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aPart 2, "2 Additional Anterior Tissue", consists of consists of a breast shave\u000amargin specimen (5.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) without orienting sutures. An\u000aaccompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates no lesions or\u000amicrocalcifications. The surface of the specimen has been previously inked\u000ablack and blue by the surgeon. The specimen is composed primarily of yellow,\u000alobulated adipose tissue (approximately 80%) and focal areas of tan/white\u000afibrous tissue (approximately 20%). No discrete lesions are identified.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Additional anterior tissue, 6 frags, ESS.\u000ajfs\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
