and a whip stitch designating the superior,\u000alateral and deep margins, respectively. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue;\u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The\u000ainterior of this specimen is uniformly fibrofatty without discreet masses or\u000asuspicious lesions. Core biopsy site is grossly identified. A clip is not\u000agrossly identified. A mammogram accompanies the specimen demonstrating the\u000apresence of a surgical clip. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 1: anterior, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: posterior, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, anterior and posterior, (core biopsy site\u000achanges in 7 through 10), ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, superior lateral shave margin", consists of multiple\u000aunoriented fragments of yellow-tan fibroadipose tissue, measuring in aggregate\u000a4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is uniformly fibrofatty, without discreet\u000amasses or suspicious lesions. A mammogram accompanying the specimen is grossly\u000aunremarkable. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  multi frags, ESS.\u000afsd\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
