VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: EVA C. GOMBOS M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Stephanie Schulte, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, 12:00, ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR AN IRREGULAR\u000aMASS (0.4 CM):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, well differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson grade\u000aI/III), measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in this limited specimen.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aNo carcinoma in situ is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aNote: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported as an addendum.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: Hx of left breast; ADH; currently 2 masses seen on MRI and US (2.1 cm\u000aapart).\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: REMOVED_DATE cm and irregular mass.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: 12:00; REMOVED_DATE cm apart.\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 4 core samples - white cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "Left breast", and consists of cores of fibroadipose tissue,\u000areceived in a white cassette with a white lid and aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Left breast white cassette cores, multi frags, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aThursday REMOVED_MONTH 22, 2009 at 01:06:24PM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (1/30/09):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemistry for p63/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID confirms absence of myoepithelium\u000aaround foci of invasive carcinoma.\u000aMethod for Hormone receptor analysis:\u000aEstrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual\u000amorphometric analysis using the following criteria:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on Friday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 30, 2009 at 04:14:24PM\u000a[report_end]
