VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aHIRSCH, MICHELLE, S., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by HIRSCH,MICHELLE S.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, AND SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Solid\u000aNuclear grade - Low\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000a- Number of blocks - REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000a- Negative (>0.3 cm) - Deep\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000a- Number of positive nodes - 0\u000a- Number of nodes examined - 1\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens) - REMOVED_DATE \u000aOTHER FINDINGS:\u000aCalcifications benign epithelium.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - Tis pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(sn) MX.\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Performed previously.\u000aRIGHT BREAST TISSUE, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aBreast tissue with microcalcifications associated with benign epithelium,\u000aapocrine metaplasia.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 50 yo female with left breast DCIS.\u000aOperation: Bilateral simple mastectomies with placement of bilateral\u000asilicone implants.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS, left breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. L sentinel lymph node.\u000a2. L breast - stitch marks axilla.\u000a3. Right breast - stitch marking -> axilla.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHANG,MARTIN C,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aReceived in three parts, all of which are received fresh, labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1 L sentinel lymph node", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion\u000aof yellow/tan lobulated fat, within which a single tan/pink, rubbery lymph node\u000a(2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is identified and bisected.\u000aMicro 1&2: sentinel lymph node, 2 frags total, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2 L breast - stitch marks axilla", is a 680-gram, REMOVED_DATE x\u000a18.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm left simple mastectomy specimen to include a tan/pink skin\u000aellipse (6.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm), tan areola (5.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm), and an everted nipple (1.5\u000acm in diameter). Five tan/pink, raised lesions (? scar vs papule), are\u000aadjacent to the nipple, each averaging approximately REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest\u000adimension. A single stitch is present along the lateral aspect, designated as\u000a"axilla" per the surgeon. A definitive axillary tail is not identified. The\u000adeep margin/fascial plane is inked in black. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from medial to lateral. A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, tan, slightly\u000amembranous lesion (? biopsy cavity), is present between the lower outer and\u000alower inner quadrants, REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin and is devoid of any fat\u000anecrosis or gross tumor. An xray of the specimen is taken and a clip is\u000aidentified cetnrally, REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep resection margin. Adjacent to and\u000asurrounding the aforementioned cavity is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm area of\u000atan/white, dense cystic fibrous stroma extending into all quadrants with focal\u000anodularity. The remaining breast tissue consists of yellow/tan lobulated fat\u000aadmixed with strands of tan/white fibrous stroma. No lymph nodes are\u000aidentified within the lateral breast tissue. No other lesions are identified.\u000aMicro 3: nipple and adjacent lesion, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 4&5: probable biopsy cavity in relationship to deep, 2 frags total, RSS.\u000aMicro 6&7: additional probable biopsy cavity, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tissue near clip, multi frags, RSS.\u000aPart three, labeled "#3 right breast, stitch marks axilla", consists of an\u000a850-gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm right simple mastectomy specimen, to include an\u000aoverlying tan/pink skin ellipse (5.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm), a pink/tan areola (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) and an everted nipple (1.3 cm in diameter). A single stitch is present at\u000athe lateral most aspect designating "axilla" per the surgeon. Axillary tissue\u000ais not identified grossly. The deep/fascial plane is inked black and the\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral. A tan/white, dense\u000acystic, lumpy fibrous lesion is present within the central aspect of the\u000abreast, extending to all quadrants and coming to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep\u000amargin. No other lesions grossly consistent with invasive carcinoma are\u000aidentified. Remaining breast tissue consists predominantly of yellow/tan\u000alobulated fat with tan/white strands of fibrous stroma. No lymph nodes are\u000aidentified within the lateralmost aspect of the breast.\u000aMicro 12: nipple and areola, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 13: upper outer quadrant fibrous tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 14: lower outer quadrant fibrous lesion, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 15: lower inner quadrant fibrous lesion, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 16: upper inner quadrant with relationship to deep, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 17: lateral breast tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000adfi\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
