VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Scott Lovitch, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aNo residual atypical lobular hyperplasia identified.\u000aCalcifications associated with columnar cell change in area of prior\u000abiopsy.\u000aBenign epithelium with associated calcification.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aImmunostains for p63/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID were examined and show the presence of basal\u000acells.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 49 yo female with right breast atypical lobular hyperplasia with\u000acalcifications; s/p image-guided core biopsy\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast atypical lobular hyperplasia\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. R breast wire localized excisional biopsy\u000ashort stitch - superior; long stitch - lateral\u000aRADIOLOGY COMMENT:\u000aCa++/specimens and wire within tissue.\u000aDB\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, medical record\u000anumber, and "#1. Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy short stitch\u000asuperior long stitch lateral", and consists of a single wire localized breast\u000aexcision specimen (5.3 cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm anterior to posterior). There are two orienting sutures designating the\u000asuperior margin (short) and the lateral margin (long). The specimen is\u000aaccompanied by a radiograph which shows a clip, and calcifications in the\u000aspecimen. The clip upon correlation of the radiograph with the gross specimen\u000aappears to be in the mid to inferior portion of the specimen. There is a\u000asingle localization wire entering the specimen inferiorly, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior and posterior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral and medial margins.\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The specimen is bisected along the wire. There is a white,\u000afocally hemorrhagic firm area grossly consistent with prior biopsy site and\u000aassociated with a clip (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The fibrous area abuts the medial\u000aand superior, and is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior,\u000a0.6 cm from the posterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted for microscopic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of the specimen serially sectioned from lateral to\u000amedial (fibrous area/possible core biopsy site from REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, area of clip and\u000apossible calcifications in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, medial margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags, ESS.\u000ask\u005cpab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/16/2007\u000a[report_end]
