D_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm overall. Sectioning\u000areveals unremarkable tan lobulated tissue with no discrete mass lesion or\u000anodule present. The approximate specimen composition is REMOVED_DATE % unremarkable\u000ayellow adipose tissue interspersed with REMOVED_DATE % diffuse white fibrous tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 4 frags, RSS.\u000aPart C, "Left breast capsule", consists of a partially fragmented aggregate of\u000asoft pink/tan membranous tissue with a minimal amount of adherent grossly\u000aunremarkable yellow adipose tissue that aggregates to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aoverall. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal no discrete mass lesion\u000aor nodule present.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections of the specimen, 3 frags per cassette\u000aeach, both RSS.\u000aPF/lp/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a3/10/2008\u000a[report_end]
