VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Kristin S. Ricci, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODES (including FSA):\u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor (0:1; nine levels examined).\u000aB. LEFT AXILLARY TISSUE:\u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor.\u000aC. LEFT BREAST, INCISION SITE:\u000aSkin and subcutis with no significant pathologic change.\u000aD. LEFT BREAST, EXCISION WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS, A MASS, AND A\u000aCLIP, AND SENTINEL NODE BIOPSIES:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aNEGATIVE LYMPH NODES\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - at least two foci, largest focus REMOVED_DATE cm\u000a(see NOTE)\u000aMultifocal - Yes\u000aHistologic type - Ductal\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - II (Moderate) (6 to 7 points)\u000aTubules - < 10% (3 points)\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate (2 points)\u000aMitotic counts - 2 points\u000aEIC - Positive\u000aLVI - Absent\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Medial, lateral, anterior, posterior,\u000asuperior, inferior\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Cribriform, micropapillary\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate and high\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - 10:23 blocks\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Medial, lateral, superior, inferior,\u000aanterior\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - Posterior (0.2 cm; focal, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aSclerosing adenosis\u000aComplex sclerosing lesion with epithelial hyperplasia\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aCalcifications associated with columnar cell change and flat epithelial\u000aatypia\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa at least 2 foci REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(sn) MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Pending\u000aNOTE: From imaging studies a 3 cm to 4 cm area of suspicious calcifications was\u000anoted in the upper outer quadrant. Grossly a REMOVED_DATE cm mass was appreciated and\u000ahistologically 6 slides of 8 representing this mass contain small foci of\u000ainvasive carcinoma within a REMOVED_DATE cm area of DCIS. These invasive foci range from\u000a0.3 to REMOVED_DATE cm in size with at least two separate foci on one slide (0.4 cm and\u000a0.3 cm; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and single foci on remaining slides, all close to biopsy site.\u000aIt's not possible to be sure whether all these foci of invasion are separate,\u000aor are part of the same invasive focus seen on consecutive slides. But, the\u000alargest single focus measures REMOVED_DATE cm and at least two separate foci are\u000apresent. DCIS extends beyond the grossly appreciated mass lesion as scattered\u000afoci associated with calcifications in grossly unremarkable breast tissue (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) covering a total estimated area of 3 to 4 cm. Many calcifications are\u000aalso present in benign breast tissue.\u000aE. LEFT BREAST SUPERIOR MEDIAL MARGIN:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar cell change with calcifications and flat epithelial atypia.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for final diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Ca left breast.\u000aOperation: SNB, Left ax, wire directed excision, ? ax dissection.\u000aOperative Findings: see op note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis:\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left sentinel lymph node - FS.\u000aB/2. Left axillary tissue.\u000aC/3. Left breast incision site.\u000aD/4. Primary tumor site, left breast - FS.\u000aE/5. Superior medial margin, left breast.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Called to Dr. Christian at 5:30 PM by Dr. Gerlach.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aLymph node. negative for tumor\u000aOR Consultation by: MICHELLE S. HIRSCH, M.D., PH.D.\u000aResident: Christopher P. Elco, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in five parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Left sentinel lymph node", consists of a red/tan irregular soft\u000atissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is trisected and submitted in its entirety\u000afor frozen section as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left axillary tissue", consists of a focally cauterized irregular\u000aportion of yellow lobulated adipose tissue (1.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is\u000asubmitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Left breast incision site", consists of an unoriented tan skin\u000aellipse (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE (depth) x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a pink irregular macule, consistent\u000awith a well-healed scar (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm), less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest\u000aradial margin. The deep margin is inked blue and the specimen is serially\u000asectioned and submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tips, en face, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central cross sections, 3 frag, ESS.\u000aPart D, "#4. Primary tumor site left breast", consists of a an irregular\u000aportion of fibrofatty tissue (6.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a long suture\u000adesignating lateral, and a short suture designating superior, as per the\u000aoperative report. The specimen is received previously inked per pathology\u000aprotocol as anterior blue, posterior black, superior red, inferior green,\u000alateral yellow, and medial orange. There are two inserted needle localization\u000awires, as displayed on the accompanying radiograph. The wires both enter along\u000athe lateral margin, and extend towards the medial margin, however do not exit\u000athe specimen. The wires are located REMOVED_DATE cm apart from each other at the\u000alateral margin. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a white focally\u000ahemorrhagic irregular ill-defined mass (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which contains a\u000abiopsy cavity (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). A surgical clip is identified within the\u000abiopsy cavity. The mass is REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin.\u000aThe remaining cut surface displays 85% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, and 15%\u000awhite fibrous tissue, with no additional discrete masses or lesions identified.\u000aApproximately 95% of the fibrous tissue is submitted. Representative sections\u000aare sequentially submitted from superior to inferior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, radially, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, with white fibrous tissue, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, bisected, with white fibrous tissue, 1\u000afrag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross sections from the same slice, with the mass in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag\u000aeach, RSS (mass ESS).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross sections from the same slice, with the mass in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag\u000aeach, RSS (mass ESS).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross sections from the same slice, with the mass in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag\u000aeach, RSS (mass ESS).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross sections from the same slice, with the mass in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and the biopsy cavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, RSS (mass ESS).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross sections from the same slice, with the mass in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aand the biopsy cavity with the surgical clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, RSS (mass and\u000acavity ESS).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross sections from the same slice, with the mass and the biopsy\u000acavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, RSS (mass and biopsy cavity ESS).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections of white fibrous tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, radially, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart E, "#5. Superior medial margin left breast", consists of an irregular\u000aportion of fibrofatty tissue (4.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a long suture\u000adesignating lateral, and a short suture designating superior (per the operative\u000areport). The specimen is received previously inked red at the superior (short\u000asuture) margin and orange (medial margin). The opposite margin, which is\u000aconsistent with previous cavity site, is inked yellow (long suture lateral).\u000aThe specimen is additionally inked posterior black, anterior blue and inferior\u000agreen. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal 80% yellow lobulated\u000aadipose tissue, and 20% white fibrous tissue, with no discrete masses or\u000alesions identified. The specimen is sequentially submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, radially, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections from posterior to anterior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, radially, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCP/mgd/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 26, 2008 at 04:54:12PM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 12, 14):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) WEAKLY POSITIVE (EQUIVOCOAL) (2+)\u000aNote: FISH analysis for amplification of REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and\u000areported in an addendum.\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 03, 2008 at 04:53:10PM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: (12/9/08)\u000aFISH was performed by Clarient using the PathVysion HER-2 DNA Probe Kit with\u000athe following (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aResults: NOT AMPLIFIED\u000aHER-2/CEP-17 ratio = REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average of HER-2 copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average centromere 17 copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aREFERENCE RANGE:\u000aNOT AMPLIFIED HER-2/CEP-17 ratio < REMOVED_DATE \u000aEQUIVOCAL HER-2/CEP-17 ratio REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE \u000aAMPLIFIED REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/CEP-17 ratio > REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #2 by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 09, 2008 at 02:40:29PM\u000a[report_end]
