VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Edilberto G Bauza, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Robert D Odze, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT NEEDLE-DIRECTED BIOPSY":\u000aCalcifications present in association with benign\u000abreast tissue (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (slides REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), apocrine\u000ametaplasia, ductal hyperplasia without atypia.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "MORE ANTERIOR MEDIAL LEFT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia without atypia.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is present REMOVED_DATE cm from the new margin.\u000aThere were no calcifications identified in the specimen.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Deborah Dillon of the Breast Pathology\u000aService.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left needle directed breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast biopsy (needle directed); long - lateral, short - superior.\u000aB/2. More anterior medial left breast tissue - stitch on new margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aA/1. Calcifications in specimen.\u000aB/2. One calcification.\u000a(Radiologist's signature is illegible)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "Left needle directed biopsy", consists of a fragment of fibroadipose\u000atissue (4.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with two embedded stitches (short = superior, long\u000a= lateral) and an embedded wire that enters laterally. The specimen is inked\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aSectioning of the specimen reveals a tan/white fibrous interior that is diffuse\u000awith focal areas of cystic change. There are no other gross abnormalities\u000aidentified. The specimen was serially sectioned from medial to lateral and\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateralmost, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections (lateral to medial), 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial-most, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart B, "More anterior medial left breast tissue - stitch on new margin",\u000aconsists of a fragment of white/tan fibroadipose tissue (3.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000awith an embedded stitch demarcating the new margin (inked black). The specimen\u000ais grossly unremarkable. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely\u000asubmitted. The specimen was re-radiographed, revealing no areas of\u000acalcification.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional tissue with new margin, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aeub/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Edilberto G Bauza M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
