hibiting approximately 40% white/tan, focally cystic,\u000adense, focally hemorrhagic fibrous stroma and 60% yellow lobulated adipose\u000atissue. As confirmed by the accompanying radiograph and radiology,\u000acalcifications, core biopsy clips, and hookwire are present within the\u000aspecimen. No other gross lesions identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue sequentially from medial to lateral, multi frags,\u000aESS [NOTE: area of calcification and clip are present within\u000amicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID].\u000adfi/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
