VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY (1410 grams):\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY (1305 grams):\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (blocks 3 and 4).\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aSuture material, consistent with a prior surgical site. The adjacent\u000aductal epithelium shows focal squamous metaplasia and reactive nuclear\u000achanges (block 18).\u000aFibroadenoma (0.6 cm).\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aNOTE: There is a small focus of adenosis in block 9 which is confirmed by\u000aan immunoperoxidase study on the H&E slide revealing myoepithelial cells\u000a(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 50 year old female with complaints of neck and back pain secondary\u000ato bilateral mammary hypertrophy.\u000aOperation: Bilateral breast reduction.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Bilateral mammary hypertrophy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast tissue - 1410 g.\u000a2. Right breast tissue - 1305 g.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HASKELL,HENRY D.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number\u000ain two parts.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1 left breast tissue", consists of a 1410-gram, 25 x 23 x\u000a5 cm aggregate of hemorrhagic, fibrofatty breast tissue and multiple fragments\u000aof tan unremarkable skin. Serial sectioning of the breast tissue reveals\u000aapproximately 60% yellow/tan lobulated fat and 40% tan/white, focally cystic,\u000afibrous stroma. No other lesions are grossly identified.\u000aMicro 1: skin and breast stroma, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 2: breast stroma, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast, additional sections, mult frags, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2 right breast tissue", consists of a 1305-gram, 25 x 22 x\u000a4 cm aggregate of hemorrhagic, fibrofatty breast tissue and multiple fragments\u000aof tan irregular skin. Serial sectioning of the breast tissue reveals\u000aapproximately 60% yellow/tan lobulated fat and 40% tan/white to red, focally\u000ahemorrhagic, focally cystic, fibrous stroma. A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, tan/white,\u000arubbery, circumscribed, fibrous nodule is identified within the stroma\u000aconsistent with a fibroadenoma. No other lesions are grossly identified.\u000aThe breast is re-examined grossly and additional sections were submitted.\u000aMicro 3: skin and circumscribed fibrous nodule, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: breast stroma, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast, additional sections, mult frags, RSS.\u000adfi\u000aReports to: HERGRUETER, CHARLES, A. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY\u000a[report_end]
