VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aRICHARDSON, ANDREA, L., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aPART 1) LEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR A DENSITY:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, involving an intraductal papilloma and also\u000apresent in several foci away from papilloma (blocks 9, 10, and 12;\u000amultiple levels examined).\u000aIntraductal papillomas, largest measuring REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aApocrine cysts and sclerosing adenosis.\u000aCalcifications in papillomatous stroma and in cysts.\u000aPART 2) DEEP MARGIN\u000aIntraductal papilloma.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left wire localized breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Left breast biopsy (mammo at 125 )\u000a2) Deep margin (mammo at 125 )\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aDensity in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by YOU,MINGJIAN JAMES,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand unit number.\u000aPart 1, "Left breast biopsy", consists of one fragment of yellow/tan adipose\u000atissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). When the specimen received, it was inked by the\u000asurgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. The specimen was radiographed interoperatively, revealing\u000aincreased density in the center of the specimen. The specimen is sectioned,\u000arevealing approximately 95% yellow/tan adipose tissue and approximately 5%\u000awhite/tan fibrous tissue. There is a tan, semi-solid area (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000awhich is less than REMOVED_DATE cm from inferior, less than REMOVED_DATE cm from posterior,\u000aless than REMOVED_DATE cm from medial, less than REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000asuperior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral margin. The specimen is entirely submitted in\u000aseries from superior to inferior margins.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Left breast biopsy, 36 frags, ESS\u000aPart 2, "Deep margin", consists of an unoriented soft tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). When the specimen was received it was inked in blue and the blue color is\u000ainked one surface and the black color is inked on the rest of the surface. An\u000ainteroparative radiograph was taken which does not reveal any localized dense\u000atissue. The specimen is sectioned, which does not reveal any solid nodule,\u000ahemorrhic or necrotic areas. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Deep margin, 16 frags, ESS\u000amjy\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
