VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (e.g. block 3).\u000aBreast tissue with florid epithelial hyperplasia, califications in\u000aassociation with benign epithelium, intraductal papillomas, sclerosing\u000alesion, columnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and\u000asecretions, apocrine metaplasia and cysts.\u000aA prior biopsy site is present adjacent to a complex sclerosing lesion\u000a(block 10).\u000aNOTE: No malignancy is seen after complete microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins. Case reviewed with Dr. Lester, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 49-year-old female with abnormal mammogram, left breast.\u000aOperation: Left needle directed breast biopsy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left wire localized breast biopsy.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HAHN,HEJIN P.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1, left wire localized breast biopsy", and consists of a piece of breast\u000atissue (4.0 cm from superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to lateral, and\u000a2.0 cm from anterior to posterior, that has been inked by the surgeon. The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral\u000a= yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph, which\u000ademonstrates multiple punctate calcifications spread through two-thirds of the\u000aspecimen, which is adjacent to a clip, and hook wire. A clip is identified in\u000athe superolateral portion of the specimen. Serial sectioning reveals 70%\u000awhite-brown fibrous tissue. No lesions are grossly identified. Sections are\u000asubmitted serially from medial to lateral. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial margin, perpendicular, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections from medial to lateral, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  section containing clip, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral and anterior margins, perpendicular, multi frags, ESS.\u000ahph\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
