VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION:\u000aNo residual ductal carcinoma in situ identified.\u000aBenign breast tissue with fibrocystic changes including cysts, fibrosis\u000aand microcalcifications.\u000aPrevious biopsy site with giant cell reaction.\u000aSkin with scar.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of DCIS diagnosed at Faulkner (+ inferior margin). This\u000ais re-excision of left breast biopsy site. Please see Faulkner\u000areport.\u000aOperation: Re-excision left breast biopsy site.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS left breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast tissue, short = superior, long = lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by MAGI GALLUZZI,CRISTINA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "Breast", and consists of a segment of fibrofatty tissue,\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and weighing 26 grams. An ellipse of unpigmented\u000askin measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm is attached to the specimen. A REMOVED_DATE cm well-healed\u000ascar is present in the center of the skin. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue;\u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. A short\u000aand long stitch are present in the specimen in proximity to the red and yellow\u000aink, respectively. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral\u000ato show a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm hemorrhagic cavity in the mid-portion of the\u000aspecimen. The cavity is REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, 1 cm from the\u000ainferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the skin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral margin of resection. The tissue adjacent to the cavity shows focal\u000aareas of fat necrosis. A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm yellow-tan firm area is present\u000ain proximity to the superior resection margin. the specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  firm area in proximity to the superior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  hemorrhagic cavity, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 6: medial margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 7: lateral margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  skin and underlying parenchyma, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remaining portion of the specimen from medial to lateral,\u000a9 frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
