VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBOROWSKY, ALEXANDER, D., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BOROWSKY,ALEXANDER D.,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY FOR A LEFT HYPOECHOIC\u000aLESION:\u000aFOCAL ATYPICAL HYPERPLASIA (best seen on original levels),\u000a(Multiple levels examined). (See Note).\u000aAcute and chronic inflammation including sheets of macrophages and\u000aforeign body giant cell reaction to cholesterol crystals, consistent\u000awith ruptured cyst.\u000aNOTE: Focal atypical hyperplasia is present, involving ducts and lobules,\u000afavor atypical lobular hyperplasia. This is best classified on\u000aexcision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 62 year old female with left hypoechoic lesion - attempted cyst\u000aaspiration yielded no fluid.\u000aBreast Imaging Findings: Circumscribed.\u000aOperation: 14g U/S breast core biopsy\u000aOperative findings: Cores obtained\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Probable complex cyst; r/o malignancy\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Cores (1 orange cassette)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by MCMENAMIN,MAIRIN,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast", in an orange cassette, and consists of multiple,\u000asoft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000akks\u000aReports to: FROST, ELISABETH, PEPPERELL M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
