VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP MARKING AN AREA OF BIOPSIED\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia adjacent to the biopsy site (block 4; levels\u000aexamined).\u000aIntraductal papillomas.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent apocrine snouts.\u000aNote: No malignancy is seen after complete microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 46 year old premenopausal female with a family history of breast\u000acancer (mother and maternal grandmother), whose REMOVED_DATE  mammogram\u000ademonstrated a new R breast cluster of calcifications. REMOVED_DATE \u000acore biopsy revealed atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: R breast wire localization biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. R breast tissue, short stitch superior, long stitch\u000alateral, whip stitch deep margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip in specimen. OR called. Dr. P. Kornguth\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by WOLGAMOT,GREGORY M.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1 right breast tissue", and consists of a single fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). A wire protrudes from the specimen.\u000aA short stitch designates superior, a long stitch designates lateral and a whip\u000astitch designates posterior. The specimen is received inked in six colors\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black;\u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial =\u000aorange. Received with the specimen is a radiograph that reveals the specimen\u000acontaining a wire adjacent to a clip but no calcifications. The specimen is\u000acomposed of approximately 50% yellow adipose tissue and 50% tan fibrous tissue\u000athat grossly extends to all margins. A REMOVED_DATE cm diameter, hemorrhagic cavity is\u000aconsistent with a prior biopsy site. The specimen is entirely submitted for\u000ahistologic examination.\u000aMicro 1: superior pole, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  specimen superior to inferior, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 11&12: inferior pole, multi frags, ESS.\u000aNOTE: Micro 5 contains the clip.\u000agmw\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
