VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST COMPREHENSIVE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM COOLEY DICKENSON HOSPITAL, NORTHAMPTON, MA:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA BORDERING ON DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000apresent in two (2) of eleven (11) blocks (blocks B and E).\u000aBlock B contains two (2) small foci (each < REMOVED_DATE cm), best seen in\u000athe original slide. The closest margin is REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aBlock E contains one (1) focus (0.2 cm), best seen in the new levels,\u000awhich is REMOVED_DATE cm from the nearest margin.\u000aOther areas of atypical hyperplasia are present.\u000aCalcifications are associated with apocrine cysts and are not specifically\u000aassociated with the atypical hyperplasia.\u000aNote: The involved areas consist of a monomorphic population of small\u000acells forming cribriform spaces, bridges and rare micropapillae. Due\u000ato the small areas of involvement and the failure of the cells to\u000acompletely fill involved ductal spaces, this lesion is best classified as\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA.\u000aThe blocks of the most severely atypical areas were obtained and recuts\u000amade. The above diagnosis incorporates the results of the review of these\u000aadditional slides.\u000aDr. Stuart Schnitt reviewed the original slides and concurred with the\u000adiagnosis of atypical hyperplasia.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Family history of breast cancer. Now with mammographic\u000acalcifications.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Consult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by MANTEL,MICHELLE HAVA,M.D.\u000aReceived from Cooley Dickenson Hospital, Northampton, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are eleven (11)\u000aglass slides and three (3) paraffin blocks.\u000aThe slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "A" through "K", corresponding\u000ato a left breast wire localized biopsy performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the\u000aaccompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name. The specimen\u000aconsisted of two (2) fragments of tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE cm and was\u000acompletely submitted for histologic examination.\u000aSubsequently received from Cooley Dickenson Hospital are three (3) paraffin\u000ablocks labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "B", "E" and "J", corresponding to a\u000aleft breast wire localized biopsy performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the\u000aaccompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST COMPREHENSIVE\u000a[report_end]
