VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Eleanor Y. Chen, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Hejin P Hahn, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SENTINEL LYMPH NODES, BIOPSY (including REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA is present in two (2) of two (2) lymph nodes. See NOTE.\u000aMetastatic tumor is present as scattered nests of tumor throughout the lymph\u000anode (size of largest metastatic focus/tumor nest is REMOVED_DATE cm.)\u000aNo extranodal extension is identified.\u000aPerinodal lymphovascular invasion is present.\u000a(3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNOTE: The focus of metastatic carcinoma in the second sentinel lymph node, is\u000apresent only on permanent sections and is not present on the frozen section\u000aslide prepared at the time of intraoperative consultation.\u000aB. LEFT BREAST MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - Yes\u000aHistologic Type - Ductal\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (Moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - Intermediate\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Present, multi-focal\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - Absent\u000aSkin invasion - Absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive):\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) deep\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Solid, cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aExtent of DCIS:\u000aNumber of blocks/total: REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS):\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) deep\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aAXILLARY LYMPH NODES: Negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 12\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens including Part A above) - REMOVED_DATE \u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread, core biopsy site,\u000afibroadenoma, calcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa MX with multiple foci of invasion\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Pending\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left breast simple mastectomy and sentinel node biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Sentinel node (FS)\u000aB/2) Left breast, stitch - apex of axilla.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "1. SENTINEL NODE" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA in one (1) of two (2) lymph nodes.\u000aReport time: 1:59 PM\u000aOR Consultation by: HEJIN P. HAHN, M.D., PH.D.\u000aResident: ANN FOLKINS, M.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and medical record number.\u000aPart A, labeled "sentinel lymph node", consists of two lymph nodes (1.8 cm and\u000a1.0 cm in greatest dimension). The larger lymph node is bisected and is\u000aentirely submitted for frozen section analysis as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The smaller lymph node\u000ais bisected and entirely submitted for frozen section analysis REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "Left breast; stitch at apex of axilla", consists of a 385 g left\u000abreast mastectomy specimen (19.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a white/tan skin ellipse\u000a(16.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and an attached axillary tail (9.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). In the\u000alateral breast at approximately REMOVED_DATE o'clock, there is a white/firm/ill-defined\u000amass (2.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), marked by a blue clip, which comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the deep margin. There is a second white/firm/ill-defined mass (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm), located REMOVED_DATE cm inferior/posterior to the larger mass in the lateral\u000abreast, marked by a green clip, which comes within REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin.\u000aA third white/tan, well-circumscribed nodule (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), marked by a\u000apink clip, is centrally located. The deep margin is composed of a smooth\u000afascial plane. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is composed of\u000aapproximately 30% fibrous tissue and 70% of adipose tissue. There are sixteen\u000alymph node candidates identified in the axillary tail, the largest measuring\u000a1.7 cm in greatest dimension. Representative sections of the largest tumor\u000amass are submitted to Dr. Richardson's lab for research. Photographs are\u000ataken.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: The larger mass, marked by the blue clip, including adjacent\u000afibrous area, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Second mass, marked by the green clip, including adjacent\u000afibrous area, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Centrally located third mass, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 lymph node candidates, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 lymph node candidates, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 lymph node candidates, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aELC/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BG-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a6/26/2007\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (7/6/07):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aNOTE: By report, FISH analysis was performed on the prior core needle biopsy.\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
