en posteriorly. The specimen is received with a radiograph that displays\u000aan ill-defined area of firm dense white opacity located at the distal portion\u000aof the widened portion of the needle localization wire. Specimen is inked in\u000asix colors (different from standard protocol) as follows: superior blue,\u000ainferior green, medial red, lateral orange, anterior yellow and posterior\u000ablack. Specimen is serially sectioned perpendicular to the long axis from\u000alateral to medial. Specimen is serially sectioned to reveal focal areas of\u000adense white fibrous tissue consistent with fat on the radiograph located in the\u000amid portion of the specimen closest to the posterior margin of resection. This\u000acollection of dense white fibrous tissue measures over an area REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. Specimen is submitted entirely sequentially from the lateral to the medial\u000aaspects as follows:\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: The lateral margin taken perpendicularly, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: All the sections to contain the dense white fibrous tissue, 1\u000afrag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of the specimen, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: The medial margin taken perpendicularly, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aPDF/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 03, 2010 at 02:26:53PM\u000a[report_end]
