VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLODA, MASSIMO, F., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LODA,MASSIMO F.,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, DUCT EXCISION, PARTIAL MASTECTOMY:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (block 12).\u000aIntraductal papillomatosis with foci of florid epithelial hyperplasia,\u000asclerosing adenosis.\u000aBreast parenchyma with epithelial hyperplasia, sclerosing adenosis,\u000afibrosis, cysts, secretory changes, apocrine metaplasia, and\u000amicrocalcifications.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LODA,MASSIMO F.,M.D.\u000aPer the surgeon, the specimen received is from the LEFT breast.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 55 year old female with left breast single duct nipple discharge,\u000a7/99 ductogram was unreaveling. Left breast retroareolar thickening with\u000acompression eliciting nipple discharge. REMOVED_DATE  mammogram is unrevealing.\u000aOperation: Left breast duct excision, partial mastectomy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast nipple discharge, left breast mass\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast duct excision (stitch on divided duct at\u000anipple level)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by MAGI GALLUZZI,CRISTINA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "right breast duct (stitch on divided duct at nipple level)",\u000aand consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm segment of fibrofatty tissue received\u000ainked by the surgeon. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. A stitch is present at\u000aone end of the specimen to mark a duct (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned to show a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm white/gray, fairly\u000awell-circumscribed firm nodule less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the orange ink. The\u000anodule is REMOVED_DATE cm from the stitch present at the duct margin. The adjacent\u000aparenchyma is yellow/gray with focal gelatinous areas. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro 1: duct margin in proximity to the stitch, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 2: remaining portion of duct, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  nodule described, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remaining portion of specimen, mult frags, ESS\u000acmg\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
