ge, lateral yellow, anterior blue, and\u000aposterior black) and serially sectioned from medial to lateral. The cut\u000asurface is tan/yellow and homogenous with focal areas of dense white fibrous\u000atissue constituting approximately 70% of the breast parenchyma. Within the\u000afibrous tissue is a silver metallic surgical clip. The specimen is submitted\u000ain its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections from medial to lateral, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include\u000ametallic clip, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aSK/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/2/2008\u000a[report_end]
