VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Leona A. Doyle, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS":\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, present in two of twenty blocks (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread and associated\u000acalcifications.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar cell change with calcifications.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aFibroadenomatoid changes.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies demonstrate that the foci of ALH are negative for\u000aE-cadherin and that the foci of ADH are positive for E-cadherin.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000a(Select slides were also reviewed by Dr. J. Brock, Breast pathology service,\u000awho concurs)\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: None given.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue with wire - mammo at 15:00\u000aRADIOLOGY: Specimen radiograph shows calcifications and clip and wire intact.\u000aPhoned to OR. E. Lizer at 3:15 pm.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, and\u000amedical record number, and "#1. Left breast with wire", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE \u000agram breast excision specimen previously inked by surgeon for the evaluation of\u000amargins posterior black, anterior blue, superior red, inferior green, lateral\u000ayellow, medial orange. No orienting sutures are present. The specimen measures\u000a4.8 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to\u000aposterior. An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates a localization\u000awire entering the specimen and associated with both a metal clip and a cluster\u000aof calcification of the medial aspect of the specimen. The localization wire\u000aenters the specimen laterally and extends to the medial aspect. The\u000alocalization wire is associated with firm fibrous breast parenchyma with\u000ahemorrhage and biopsy site changes and a small metallic clip, extending over an\u000aarea of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, which is present at the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to\u000athe medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin. The\u000aremaining breast parenchyma is 50% fibrous and 50% adipose tissue with no\u000aadditional gross lesions identified. The entire specimen is submitted to\u000ainclude the clip site and closets margins and all remaining tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast parenchyma surrounding clip site (clip located in block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000ato include closest inferior and anterior margins, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest lateral margin, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep and inferior margins, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining anterior margin, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining medial margin, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining breast parenchyma, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aLDO/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed\u000aon Tuesday February 24, 2009 at 04:50:49PM\u000a[report_end]
