VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BG-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Eleanor Y. Chen, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type (low nuclear grade), is present as a\u000a0.3 cm focus in one of twenty-four blocks (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aColumnar cell change with associated microcalcifications, multifocal atypical\u000aductal hyperplasia and flat epithelial atypia (blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present focally.\u000aDCIS is present <0.1 cm from the lateral (yellow) margin (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). Atypical\u000aductal hyperplasia is present <0.1 cm from the inferior margin (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and\u000a<0.1 cm from the deep margin (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). DCIS is present >0.3 cm from anterior,\u000amedial and superior margins.\u000aNOTE: Selected slides (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) also seen by Dr. Susan Lester, who concurs.\u000aImmunohistochemistry for E-cadherin confirms membrane immunoreactivity in the\u000aDCIS.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 50-year-old female with abnormal left mammogram. On August 24, 2006,\u000aleft mammogram showed grouped heterogenous calcifications in axillary tail\u000aregion. History of right breast ALH, atypia.\u000aOperation: Left breast wide excision biopsy\u000aOperative Findings: Two wires in excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram with calcifications.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aLeft breast tissue to frozen room from mammography (short stitch - superior,\u000along stitch - lateral, whip stitch - chest wall margin).\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aSpecimen contains two (2) wires, each with associated calcifications.\u000aOR called/Sughra Raza, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen, received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and\u000a"left breast tissue", consists of an REMOVED_DATE cm (medial to lateral) x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000a(inferior to superior) x REMOVED_DATE cm (anterior to posterior) breast biopsy with\u000athree sutures: the long designating lateral, the short designating superior,\u000aand the whipstitch designating a chest wall margin. The specimen contains two\u000awires, each marks areas of calcifications corresponding to the accompanying\u000aradiograph. No obvious masses or other lesions are identified in the breast\u000atissue. Approximately 50% of the specimen is composed of fibrous tissue.\u000aPrior to sectioning, the specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The entire specimen is serially\u000asectioned from lateral to medial (long axis) and submitted for histological\u000aanalysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue with possible calcifications, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: The remainder of the breast tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BG-06-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aEC/am/PES\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/18/2006\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (10/18/06):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
