VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Oname O. Burlingame, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Michelle S Hirsch, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST TISSUE, EXCISION:\u000aBreast tissue with LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, core biopsy site,\u000aepithelial hyperplasia, a papilloma, prominent sclerosing adenosis,\u000aand calcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aNo invasive carcinoma is identified.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. M. Bennett (Breast Pathology Service), who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 41-year-old woman status post core right breast 8 o'clock LCIS,\u000ainvolving areas of sclerosing adenosis.\u000aOperation: Right breast mass excision.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass with LCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue, short stitch superior, long stitch lateral, BRBX.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen, Part A, is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "#1. Right breast tissue, short stitch superior, long stitch\u000alateral", and consists of an ovoid fragment of yellow/tan to pink/tan\u000afibroadipose tissue (3.8 S-I x REMOVED_DATE M-L x REMOVED_DATE A-P cm), which is oriented per\u000asurgeon with two sutures as indicated. The specimen is inked by the surgeon\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to exhibit\u000aapproximately 60% dense/nodular/cystic white/pink fibrous tissue extending to\u000aall inked margins, and approximately 40% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue.\u000aA small metal clip is identified within the dense fibrous tissue in the\u000ainferior portion of the specimen. No discrete masses are identified. The\u000aspecimen is entirely sequentially submitted from inferior to superior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin perpendicularly sectioned, 3 frags in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central specimen to include dense/nodular/cystic fibrous tissue\u000a(clip identified within tissue in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags total,\u000aESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aLMB/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/21/2007\u000a[report_end]
