VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000a1. RIGHT BREAST, LOWER INNER QUADRANT, EXCISIONAL BIOSY, FOR A MASS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia predominantly associated with a complex\u000asclerosing lesio (block #4).\u000aFibrocystic change with microcysts.\u000aMicrocalcifications in association with benign epithelium.\u000a2. RIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA (blocks #5,6).\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia involving a complex sclerosing lesion.\u000aFibrocystic change with microcysts and fibroadaenomatoid change.\u000aMicrocalcifications in association with benign epithelium.\u000aBiopsy site with repair reaction.\u000aSkin with cicatraix.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 32 year old female with ADH, right breast excised REMOVED_DATE (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aclose to margin. Additional new leson in the lower inner quadrant of the\u000aright breast.\u000aOperation: Re-excision right breast biopsy and excision mass right breast\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Atypical hyperplasia and breast mass on right\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) New lesion from lower inner quadrant of right breast\u000a#2) Right breast tissue (long suture/lateral; short suture/\u000asuperior), re-excision\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by WENG,ANDREW PHILIP,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "tissue from lower inner quadrant of right breast", consists\u000aof a single unoriented fragment of tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (3 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) with an unoriented traction suture in place. The specimen margins are\u000ainked in black. On sectioning, no masses or other lesions are identified. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 1: ends, 4 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  cross sections through body, 6 frags, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "right breast tissue", consists of a single oriented fragment\u000aof tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (2.4 cm from superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom medial to lateral, 4 cm from anterior to posterior) including a tan/white\u000askin ellipse (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm in length) surrounding a well-healed surgical scar\u000a(2.8 cm). The specimen margins are inked as follows: superior=red,\u000ainferior=orange, medial=green, lateral=yellow, anterior=blue, posterior=black.\u000aOn sectioning, the parenchyma is dense and uneven, but no masses or other\u000adiscrete lesions are identified. Approximately 75% of the specimen is\u000asubmitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro 5: lateral perpendicular margin, 3 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 6: medial perpendicular margin, 3 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial cross sections through body from lateral to medial\u000aincluding superior and inferior perpendicular margins, 7 frags,\u000aRSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posterior perpendicular margin, 4 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  anterior perpendicular margin including skin with scar, 4 frags,\u000aRSS\u000aapw\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
