ses or microcalcifications are identified. The unoriented specimen is inked\u000ain black and serially sectioned to reveal approximately 50% white fibrous\u000atissue with a small area of firmness (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is present in\u000aone slice. The remainder of the specimen is comprised predominantly of\u000aunremarkable adipose tissue and the specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right wire localized breast biopsy, 1, 2, or 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPlease note: the area of firmness is submitted in cassette #2.\u000alcl\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
