VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Scott Lovitch, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR TWO (2) CLIPS":\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia with calcifications (see NOTE).\u000aMucinous cysts.\u000aTwo (2) core biopsy sites.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe patient's prior core biopsies (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ) were reviewed for the\u000afinal diagnosis, and Dr. Susan Lester, Breast Pathology Service, has reviewed\u000athe case and concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 44 year old woman, s/p REMOVED_DATE  Right breast core bx revealing ADH with\u000aexcision recommended. Hx of ovarian ca.\u000aOperation: R breast Wire-localized bx x2\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Not provided\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue\u000a(short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral, whip stitch/chest wall\u000amargin)\u000aRADIOLOGY COMMENT:\u000aSpecimen: 2 wires, 2 clips, OR called.\u000aSR\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, medical record\u000anumber, and "right breast tissue, short stitch superior, long stitch lateral,\u000awhip stitch on chest wall margin", and consists of a double wire-localized\u000aright breast excision specimen. A short suture marks the superior margin, a\u000along suture marks the lateral margin, and a whip stitch marks the deep margin.\u000aThe specimen is received previously inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange, and measures REMOVED_DATE cm from medial\u000ato lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to\u000aposterior. Two wires are present in the specimen. The more lateral of the two\u000ais arbitrarily designated wire #1. This wire enters laterally, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior and inferior margins. It exits\u000alaterally, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior\u000amargin. A radiograph shows this wire passing through one ill-defined mass and\u000aadjacent to mammography clip. Wire #2 enters anteriorly, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin. It exits at the junction\u000aof the anterior and superior margins, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. A\u000aradiograph shows this wire passing adjacent to a mammography clip. There is no\u000aclear mass specimen in this area. The entire specimen is serially sectioned\u000afrom medial to lateral into eleven slices, such that slice #1 represents the\u000amedial margin and slice #11 represents the lateral margin. The specimen\u000aconsists of approximately 70% firm, pink/white, fibrous tissue and 30% yellow\u000aadipose tissue. Both mammography clips are identified and removed. Please\u000anote: While the clinical history describes two separate lesions, these grossly\u000aappear to be contiguous. The two clips are REMOVED_DATE cm apart. No discrete mass is\u000aidentified. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicular sections, 11 frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9 including clip site, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9, tissue adjacent to clip site, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9, tissue between clip site #1 and clip site #2, 1 frag\u000aper cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #10, clip site #2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #10, tissue adjacent to clip site #2, 1 frag per\u000acassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular sections, 5 frags total, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000asbl\u005cpab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/23/2008\u000a[report_end]
