VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Skin, L breast, punch\u000aProcedure Date:\u000aOrdering Provider: STEPHEN R. LYLE M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Matthew M Johnson, M.D.\u000aPathologist: George F Murphy, MD\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCONSULTATION RECEIVED FROM DERMPATH NEW ENGLAND; BRIGHTON, MA\u000a(Our ref. "GFM 11,063")\u000aA. SKIN, LEFT BREAST, PUNCH BIOPSY (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aAssessment: METASTATIC CARCINOMA consistent with the patient's known lung\u000aprimary.\u000aComment/Recommendation: The tumor is present in dermal vessels with extension\u000ainto perivascular dermis. Immunohistochemical stains show that tumor cells are\u000apositive for keratin 7, TTF-1 and Her2, and negative for keratin 20, ER, PR and\u000aGCDFP, supporting the above interpretation. Her2 has been shown to be\u000aexpressed by a minority of lung carcinomas.\u000aThe immunoperoxidase, immunofluorescence and in-situ hybridization tests\u000aperformed at Brigham and Women's Hospital were developed and their performance\u000acharacteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the\u000aDepartment of Pathology at BWH. They have not been cleared or approved by the\u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such\u000aclearance or approval is not necessary.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Patient is a 63-year-old female with a history of stage I breast\u000acancer on the right side and history of metastatic left lung cancer with bone\u000ametastases. She has a ? vascular lesion involving the left breast.\u000aAppropriate stains to determine lung vs. breast cancer are requested.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Infiltrating adenocarcinoma.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aConsult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived from Dermpath New England, 1380 Soldier's Field Road, Suite 100,\u000aBrighton, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID is one H&E-stained glass slide and a paraffin block both\u000alabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" (slide sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID"), which correspond to a punch\u000abiopsy of skin from the LEFT BREAST, collected on REMOVED_DATE  according to the\u000aaccompanying surgical pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by George F Murphy MD, Electronically signed on Friday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 20, 2009 at 04:48:37PM\u000a[report_end]
