its through the posterior aspect of the specimen. The\u000aaccompanying radiograph shows a focus of calcifications. The specimen has been\u000apreviously inked per pathology protocol (superior red, inferior green, medial\u000aorange, lateral yellow, anterior blue, and posterior black) and serially\u000asectioned from medial to lateral. The cut surface is tan-yellow homogenous\u000afocal area of dense white fibrous tissue constituting approximately 30% of the\u000abreast parenchyma. No discrete lesions are grossly identified. The specimen\u000ais submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections medial to lateral, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include\u000apossible area of calcification or specimen radiograph, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000asek/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 10, 2009 at 05:47:09PM\u000a[report_end]
