robable calcifications (associated with wire A). No other gross\u000alesions are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast, sequentially from lateral to medial (probable\u000acalcifications in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adl/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aADDENDUM:\u000aMargins of resection are negative for dysplasia or malignancy.\u000aAddendum #1 by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
