VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR TWO RADIOLOGIC MASSES:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, single focus (slide 6) measuring REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions.\u000aFibrocystic change including cysts, apocrine metaplasia and florid\u000aepithelial hyperplasia.\u000aSingle focus of calcification associated with benign epithelium.\u000aExtensive histiocytic reaction within duct spaces, with focal rupture and\u000achronic inflammation.\u000aPrior biopsy site changes.\u000aNOTE: Slides 5 and 6 were reviewed by Dr. Andrea Richardson.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 53 year old female with right breast 8 mm mass noted on mammogram\u000aand US with 4 mm lesion 2 cm medial. S/P REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy of the\u000a8 mm mass with pathology demonstrating ruptured ducts and fat necrosis,\u000a? with imaging findings - excision recommended.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization x 2\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass x 2\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Right breast mass tissue (short/superior; long/lateral;\u000awhip stitch/chest wall margin)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HENDERSON,JOEL M.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. right breast tissue, short superior, long lateral, whip stitch chest\u000awall margin", and consists of a single fragment of pink/yellow fibroadipose\u000atissue (5.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen arrives accompanied by a whole\u000aspecimen radiograph which shows a localization wire marking a central\u000aradiologic density with a localization clip in place, and an adjacent diffusely\u000aradiodense focus that is marked by the tip of the localization wire. The\u000aspecimen arrives with a localization wire in place, and is marked by the\u000asurgeon with a long suture to indicate lateral and a short suture to indicate\u000asuperior, as well as a whip stip to indicate the deep margin. The specimen has\u000abeen previously inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is sectioned to reveal\u000aa central biopsy site adjacent to the previously placed marking clip (0.8 cm in\u000agreatest dimension), surrounded by areas of pink/gray fibrous tissue. The\u000aremainder of the specimen (approximately 70%) consists of yellow lobulated\u000aadipose tissue, except for a small firm tan nodule (0.3 cm),\u000awell-circumscribed, adjacent to the inferomedial margin and corresponding to\u000athe location marked by the localization wire. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from medial to lateral and representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro 1: medial margin, perpendicularly sectioned, 5 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, serially sectioned from medial to lateral (nodule\u000ain #2 and 3, prior biopsy site in #4-7), 14 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 11: lateral margin perpendicularly sectioned, 5 frags, ESS\u000ajmh\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
