VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE", WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION:\u000aSclerosed fibroadenoma (0.6 cm) with dystrophic calcifications.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia, apocrine metaplasia, and benign\u000acalcifications.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Area of microcalcifications, right breast (no biopsy, however, patient\u000ahad biopsy of left breast REMOVED_DATE years ago, because not amenable to stereotactic\u000abiopsy - per Pathology resident).\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Breast CA.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Rt breast tissue, stitch short - superior, stitch long\u000alateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Ca++ in specimen. (no signature)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by REIMANN,JULIE DYLAN REGAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aReceived fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "#1 right\u000abreast tissue", is a fragment of breast tissue (7.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm deep) with\u000aattached skin ellipse (5.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue;\u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The\u000aspecimen is accompanied by a radiograph indicating microcalcification localized\u000aby a wire and an accompanying pink sheet which states that the calcium deposits\u000aare in the specimen. There are no grossly identifiable lesions on serial\u000asectioning. The breast consists of approximately 10% fibrous tissue, the rest\u000ais adipose tissue. There are no grossly identifiable lesions on the skin\u000aellipse.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  area localized by wire, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  adjacent fibrous tissue, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  contain remaining fibrous tissue from the specimen, 1 frag each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro 16: contain three representative sections from the skin ellipse\u000aincluding tip, 3 frags, RSS.\u000apsc\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
