VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MITRA NOROOZIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Xuefei Hong, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, 9:00, 11G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, associated with multiple calcifications (see note).\u000aColumnar cell change with calcifications.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies are performed and reveal the following results for\u000aLCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu NEGATIVE (0)\u000aE-cadherin NEGATIVE\u000aNote: The majority of the calcifications in the biopsy are associated with\u000aLCIS. There is no necrosis and the nuclei are low grade.\u000aThe immunoprofile supports classification as LCIS.\u000aThe association of calcifications with typical LCIS is an unusual finding.\u000aThis lesion would be evaluated best with excision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 49 y/o female with family history of breast cancer with a cluster of\u000aamorphous calcifications ~4 mm in left inner mid breast.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING: Mammo - Calcifications, Non-palpable.\u000aSize of lesion: 4 mm\u000aLOCATION: Left, 9:00\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY: 11 G, Stereotactic, Vacuum-assisted.\u000aBREAST CORE(S) SUBMITTED: Left breast - REMOVED_DATE cores (+) calcs in green "A".\u000a7/12 no calcs --> green "B".\u000aCassette color: Green\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "Left breast", and consists of multiple tan/yellow lobulated\u000afibroadipose breast tissue cores (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). A portion\u000aof the breast tissue cores received in a green cassette marked "A Ca+2" and the\u000aremainder of the breast tissue cores received in a green cassette marked "B".\u000aThe specimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette "A. Ca+2", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aSEK/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a6/26/2007\u000a[report_end]
