VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, NEEDLE DIRECTED BIOPSY:\u000aDuctal hyperplasia, focal, with associated microcalcifications, adjacent\u000ato healing prior core biopsy site and clip (block #2). See note.\u000aNo atypical ductal hyperplasia present in this specimen.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aNOTE: No other areas of microcalcifications identified histologically (levels\u000aexamined on selected blocks).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Right needle directed breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammo right breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue (short stitch superior, long\u000alateral).\u000aClip and calcifications in specimen. OR called. CG.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by FIRESTEIN,RON,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "#1, right breast tissue", consists of a single fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000aanterior to posterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior. The specimen is\u000aoreinted by the surgeon with a short stitch superior and long stitch lateral.\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral\u000a= yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is received with a radiograph that\u000ashows a wire and a clip. There are calcifications shown in relation to the\u000aclip. The specimen did not contain a wire when it was received. The area\u000acorresponding to the clip corresponds to an area of fibrous tissue. Adjacent\u000ato the area, there is a small focus of hemorrhage. This area is REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin. The lateral margin is 2\u000acm away and the medial margin is REMOVED_DATE cm away. Representative sections are\u000asubmitted for histologic evaluation. The specimen is 50% fibrous tissue and\u000a50% fat.\u000aMicro 1: lateral margin, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  area closest to clip, 14 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional areas of the specimen, 12 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 17: lateral margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000amir\u000aReports to: SHOJI, BRENT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
