VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Vinodh Pillai, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aRESIDUAL HIGHLY ATYPICAL DUCTAL PROLIFERATION, consistent with DCIS is present\u000ain 1 of 19 blocks associated with biopsy site, see NOTE\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU. An E-cadherin stain performed confirms absent\u000amembranous staining in lobular neoplasia.\u000aCalcifications associated with normal lobules, adjacent to biopsy site.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aNOTE: A single highly atypical focus is present which measures just REMOVED_DATE cm and\u000aconsists of a cluster of ducts containing highly atypical cells located\u000aadjacent to the biopsy site and probably represents a small residual focus of\u000aDCIS (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). This focus is present REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. The remaining\u000amargins are negative for DCIS (medial, superior, inferior, anterior,\u000aposterior). Dr. S. Lester also reviewed the selected slides and concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: DCIS - L breast. Hx of ADH --> DCIS in R side; ADH on left in past,\u000aetc.\u000aOperation: None provided.\u000aOperative Findings: None provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Lf bst. CA, DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left bst excision post needle-loc; short - superior; long - lateral; to\u000amammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Specimen radiograph shows the targeted clip, a few calcs, and the\u000awire. - Adam Wang.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled "#1. Left breast excision\u000awith needle loc, short superior, long lateral", and the patient's name and unit\u000anumber. The specimen consists of REMOVED_DATE cm (medial to lateral) x REMOVED_DATE cm (anterior\u000ato posterior) x REMOVED_DATE cm (superior to inferior) breast biopsy with a localization\u000awire in place and the short suture marking the superior margin and the long\u000asuture marking the lateral margin. The accompanying specimen radiograph shows\u000athe targeted clip, few calcifications, and the wire. The specimen margins are\u000ainked as per the pathology protocol; posterior-black, anterior-blue,\u000asuperior-red, inferior-green, lateral-yellow, and medial-orange. There is a\u000atan/red firm area consistent with biopsy cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm,\u000alocated REMOVED_DATE cm to lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the\u000aposterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm to inferior margin. The biopsy cavity is associated with calcifications.\u000aThe entire specimen is submitted for histological examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular sections of the lateral margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular sections of the medial margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Consecutive sections of the specimen to include biopsy site and\u000acalcifications in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy cavity and calcification, multi frags, ESS.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis\u000ausing the following criteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not\u000ayet been determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor\u000acells but only a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >30% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for\u000ainvestigational use only.\u000aVIP/mm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 08, 2009 at 04:52:59PM\u000a[report_end]
