cluded skin ellipse) is inked black.\u000aDeep to the scar is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm previous biopsy cavity with closest\u000ainked margin (0.3 cm). Nine candidate lymph nodes are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  old biopsy cavity and closest black inked margin, 4 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of biopsy cavity, 7 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 11: skin with underlying biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 12: uninvolved breast, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 13: 4 lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 14: 1 lymph node (bisected), 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 15: 1 lymph node (bisected), 2 frags ESS\u000aMicro 16: 1 lymph node, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 17: 1 lymph node (bisected), 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 18: 1 lymph node (bisected), 2 frags, ESS\u000aaji\u000aReports to: PILSON, KARL, D. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODES REGIONAL RESECTION\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
