in per the surgeon. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is accompanied by a\u000aradiograph, which a wire within the specimen as well as a spiculated area of\u000adensity. The cut surface is tan with coarse white strands of tissue throughout\u000athe parenchyma. No definite masses or nodules were identified. The specimen\u000ais entirely submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Left breast tissue, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Left breast tissue, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aTH/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Travis J Hollmann M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Review by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/11/2005\u000a[report_end]
