VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aHIRSCH, MICHELLE, S., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by HIRSCH,MICHELLE S.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A CYST:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, focal.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia, focal.\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions.\u000aBenign cyst and epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aGiant cell reaction consistent with prior aspiration.\u000aMargins evaluated.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: REMOVED_DATE aspiration of cyst. 11 o'clock breast, cytology\u000aatypical; F/U showed recurrence. Excisional biopsy: HVMA.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast (11 o'clock), short = superior margin, long\u000alateral margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aRIGHT BREAST CYST:\u000aCyst in specimen.\u000aSigned: GD/PK\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by ABREU-E-LIMA,PAULA C.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000a"#1. Right breast tissue at 11 o'clock, short = superior, long = lateral". The\u000aspecimen consists of a single fragment of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE \u000a(M-L) x REMOVED_DATE (A-P) x REMOVED_DATE cm (S-I). The specimen is oriented with two surgical\u000asutures: a short marking the superior, and long marking the lateral aspect.\u000aContained within the specimen is a single localization wire indicating a cyst\u000aon the accompanying specimen radiogram. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. Contained within\u000athe specimen, marked by the localization wire, is a REMOVED_DATE cm simple cyst filled\u000awith a gelatinous material. The cyst wall focally abuts the posterior margin.\u000aThe cyst also approaches the other margins as follows: REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior,\u000a0.4 cm of the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial, and\u000a2.2 cm from the lateral resection margin. The remainder of the breast\u000aparenchyma is composed of 60% adipose tissue and 40% fibrous tissue. There is\u000aa firmer/rubbery area of fibrosis near the medial edge that is poorly defined\u000a(2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). This area of fibrosis abuts the medial, superior,\u000aanterior, and posterior margins. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 1: Cyst in relation to inferior and posterior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: Cyst in relation to superior, posterior, and inferior margin, 1 frag,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro 3: Anterior margin closest cyst, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 4: Lateral edge, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 5: Medial edge, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 6: Rubbery firm area in relation to superior, medial, anterior and\u000aposterior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, multi frags, ESS.\u000amcc\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
