VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical Ductal Hyperplasia (blocks 10, 12, 14, 21; levels examined).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (block 10, level 3).\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia, apocrine metaplasia, fibrosis, and\u000amicrocalcifications.\u000aFibroadenoma (1.2 cm).\u000aMinute intraductal papilloma.\u000aMicrocalcifications are associated with benign epithelium.\u000aA biopsy site with repair changes is associated with the fibroadenoma.\u000aNOTE: No carcinoma is seen after complete microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 60 year old postmenopausal female, not on hormones, s/p REMOVED_DATE \u000acore biopsy for evaluation of calcifications on L mmg. Pathology revealed\u000aatypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: L breast wire localization excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L abnormal mammogram, atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. L breast tissue, short superior, long lateral, whipstitch\u000aon deep margin, red superior, black lateral, blue anterior, medial orange,\u000agreen inferior, yellow posterior.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aCalcifications in specimen.\u000aDr. J. Leung\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HONG,XUEFEI,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in one part, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber and "#1 left breast tissue, short superior, long lateral". It consists\u000aof one fibroadipose soft tissue with long suture denotes lateral, short suture\u000adenotes superior and localization wire. The specimen is previously inked by\u000athe surgeon as follows:red=superior, black=lateral, blue=anterior,\u000aorange=medial, green=inferior, yellow=posterior. It measures REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000asuperior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from medial\u000ato lateral. Sectioning reveals the specimen contains 95% tan/yellow adipose\u000asoft tissue. The biopsy cavity and surrounding fibrotic tissue (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.5 cm) is REMOVED_DATE cm from inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000aanterior and REMOVED_DATE cm from posterior margin. There is no gross evidence for\u000ainvasive carcinoma. The entire specimen is submitted. The enclosed radiograph\u000ashows microcalcifications in the specimen as documented by the radiologist.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior and lateral margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mid portion of the specimen with inferior, anterior and posterior\u000amargins, biopsy cavity in Micro 11, 12 & 13, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial portion of the specimen, multi frags, ESS.\u000axh\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
