VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Javad Beheshti, M.D.; Rachel L Rucker-Schmidt, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR ARCHITECTURAL DISTORTION:\u000aIntraductal papillomas, involving an area of at least REMOVED_DATE cm, with florid\u000aductal epithelial hyperplasia, apocrine metaplasia and focal\u000amicrocalcifications.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Abnormal mammogram right breast, architectural distortion.\u000aOperation: Right breast mass wire localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: See Op note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue: short superior, long lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Architectural distortion and clip in specimen. Wire intact. J. Riter\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "right breast tissue", consists of a REMOVED_DATE gram oriented lumpectomy specimen\u000athat is REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior and\u000a2.1 cm from medial to lateral. The specimen is received with a short suture\u000awhich denotes superior, and long suture which denotes the lateral. The\u000aspecimen is received with a needle-localization wire and accompanying\u000aradiograph that displays an area of architectural distortion where the\u000aneedle-localization wire enters the specimen which is on the superior aspect of\u000athe specimen. Both the needle-localization wire minimally exits the specimen\u000ain the inferior aspect of the specimen. There is a metal clip inserted\u000aadjacent to the entry point of the needle-localization wire in the superior\u000aportion of the specimen. The specimen is inked in six colors "per pathology\u000aprotocol" with superior red, inferior green, anterior blue, posterior black,\u000amedial orange and lateral yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned from\u000ainferior to superior. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a possible\u000aprevious biopsy site located in the mid portion of the specimen surrounded by\u000aan area of recent hemorrhage that measures over an area REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aAlso noted throughout the specimens are multiple smooth-lined cysts ranging\u000afrom REMOVED_DATE up to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension. There is no discrete mass, lesion\u000aor nodule associated with the specimen grossly. The approximate specimen\u000acomposition is 85% diffuse dense white fibrous tissue and 15% unremarkable\u000ayellow adipose tissue.\u000aThe specimen is submitted entirely sequentially from inferior to superior.\u000aNote also the area that contains the clip and the area of architectural\u000adistortion is in cassette 16, 17 and 18.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin perpendicularly sectioned, 3 frags per\u000acassette each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: One full thickness\u000asectioned divided into two pieces, 1 frag per cassette each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin perpendicularly taken with REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags,\u000aESS, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000acp/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/19/2008\u000a[report_end]
