n diameter and is adjacent to the medial margin,\u000a0.2 cm from the posterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin. The\u000asecond area of firmness is 1 cm away from the first one and is adjacent to the\u000aposterior margin, 1 cm from the medial margin, and 2 cm from the superior\u000amargin. This area measures REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter. The remainder of the tissue\u000aconsists of unremarkable fibroadipose tissue. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted for histologic analysis from superior to inferior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  entire specimen submitted from superior to inferior margins. The\u000aareas of firmness are contained in cassettes REMOVED_DATE \u000amir\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
