VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Qinghong Yang, M.D., Ph.D.; Ann K Folkins, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Tan A Ince, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER INNER QUADRANT, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR ARCHITECTURAL\u000aDISTORTION ON MAMMOGRAPHY:\u000aFocal atypical ductal hyperplasia, (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aExtensive adenosis associated with microcalcifications.\u000aComplex sclerosing lesion involved with epithelial hyperplasia and adenosis.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aArterial calcifications.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000aImmunohistochemical stains for p63-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID confirm the presence of\u000amyoepithelial cells in all the areas of the sclerosing lesion.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 58 y/o woman with new architectural distortion on mammogram, MRI read\u000aas negative. Recommended for biopsy.\u000aOperation: R needle-localization breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R abnl mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) R breast tissue. * short stitch - superior, long stitch - lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Targeted architectural distortion and intact wire are seen within\u000athe specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm excision of\u000afibroadipose tissue, oriented by sutures designating superior (short suture)\u000aand lateral (long suture) margins. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange (inked by surgeon).\u000aA localizing wire enters the superior aspect of the specimen and exits\u000ainferomedially. The accompanying radiograph demonstrates a localizing wire in\u000aplace within an encircled area of architectural distortion within the central\u000aaspect of the specimen. Sectioning in this area demonstrates tan/pink focally\u000ahemorrhagic fibrous tissue (involving an area that is maximally REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000agreatest dimension). Tissue along the anteromedial aspect of the specimen is\u000apalpably firm (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm area), and abuts the anterior, medial and\u000asuperior margins in this area. This palpably firm area is REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aclosest posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the nearest lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the nearest inferior margin. The entire specimen is sequentially\u000asubmitted, with perpendicular superior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, perpendicular inferior\u000amargin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and palpably firm tissue in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sequentially from superior to inferior, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Tan A Ince M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/17/2007\u000a[report_end]
