 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, "breast tissue lateral to specimen #1", consists of a single\u000aunoriented fragment of fibroadipose tissue (1.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). No firm\u000amasses are identified. The specimen is inked in black and entirely submitted\u000afor histologic examination.\u000aMicro 5: breast, 1 f, ESS.\u000aPart three, "breast tissue medial to specimen #1", consists of a single\u000afragment of unoriented yellow adipose tissue (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). No masses\u000aare grossly identified. The surgical margin is inked in black and the specimen\u000ais entirely submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro 6: breast, 1 f, ESS.\u000aReports to: KANE, GREGORY, J. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
