VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Christian J. Davidson, M.D.; Scott Lovitch, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Vania Nose, MD, PhD\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS":\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aBenign breast tissue with calcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aColumnar cell change.\u000aCysts.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 45 year old female with new right microcalcifications on mammogram too\u000afaint for stereotactic core biopsy.\u000aOperation: Right needle localized breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: R abnormal mammogram.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue short suture superior long lateral for mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Microcalcifications in specimen informed Dr. Lockhart.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "right breast tissue, short superior, long lateral", and consists of an\u000airregular tan/yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose breast tissue (3.1 cm\u000amedial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm superior to\u000ainferior) with a short suture designating the lateral margin, and a long suture\u000adesignating the superior margin. There is a needle-localization wire in place\u000awhich enters through the superior lateral aspect of the specimen and exits\u000athrough the medial inferior aspect of the specimen. The specimen has been\u000apreviously inked per the surgeon per pathology protocol (superior red, inferior\u000agreen, medial orange, lateral yellow, anterior blue, posterior black) and\u000aserially sectioned from medial to lateral. The cut surface is tan/yellow and\u000ahomogenous with focal areas of dense white fibrous tissue constituting\u000aapproximately greater than 90% of the breast parenchyma. There is an irregular\u000ared/brown hemorrhagic area (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which abuts the superior and\u000aposterior margins and extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral margin. No discrete lesions are grossly identified. The specimen is\u000asubmitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, medial to lateral, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to\u000ainclude hemorrhagic area, blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include designated area of\u000amicrocalcifications per specimen radiograph, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aSEK/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
