VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: AYODALE S ODULATE M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Dominique P. Coco, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, 12:00, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, cribriform and micropapillary patterns, is\u000apresent associated with columnar cell change with atypia, mucinous cysts,\u000aand numerous calcifications.\u000aNote: ADH would be evaluated best with excision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 51 y/o female with history of phyllodes tumor of right breast in\u000a2003. Now with 7-mm cluster of coarse and punctate Ca++ in the left breast.\u000aPlease rule out malignancy.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: 7 mm, Nonpalpable calcifications.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: upper outer 12:00\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 11G Stereotactic Vacuum-assisted\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 11G Stereotactic Vacuum-assisted; A = Specimen with Ca++; B = Specimen\u000awithout Ca++. - Blue cassettes\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "Left breast", and consists of multiple irregular tan/yellow to\u000atan/white lobulated fibroadipose breast tissue cores (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate). A portion of the breast tissue cores are received in a blue\u000acassette marked "A. Ca+2", and remainder of the breast tissue cores are\u000areceived in a blue cassette marked "B". The specimen is submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette "A. Ca+2", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aSEK/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/7/2007\u000a[report_end]
