VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: Esther Rhei M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Lynette M Sholl, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION WITH WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - solid, cribriform, micropapillary\u000aNuclear grade - low\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 6:13 blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - anterior, posterior, lateral, medial\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) - superior (0.2 cm)\u000ainferior (0.1 cm), see NOTE\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia\u000aBiopsy cavity\u000aSkin with scar\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - Tis NX MX\u000aNOTE: There is cautery artifact in areas of hyperplasia at the inferior margin,\u000aprecluding optimal evaluation.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 47 year-old female history (L) breast ADH, s/p right breast wire loc\u000abiopsy REMOVED_DATE  for calcifications (R) upper outer breast - severe ADH\u000abordering on DCIS, margins positive. Re-excision REMOVED_DATE  DCIS. Post\u000aexcisional mammogram REMOVED_DATE  demonstrated calcifications in right breast upper\u000ainner quadrant.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire directed re-excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Rt breast tissue - to mammo.\u000a(short superior, long lateral, whip stitch - chest wall, scar anteriorly.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aCalcifications in specimen (E.P. Frost).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "requisition states right breast tissue", and consists of "requisition\u000astates right breast tissue", and consists of an irregular fragment of firm\u000apink/tan to yellow/tan fibrofatty tissue (5.6 (M-L) x REMOVED_DATE (S-I) x REMOVED_DATE (A-P) cm)\u000awhich is oriented per surgeon as follows: short suture = superior, long suture\u000a= lateral. The specimen was previously inked per surgeon per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. Two needle\u000alocalization wires are in place. Wire 1 enters the superior/lateral aspect of\u000athe specimen and exits the superior/medial aspect of the specimen. Wire 2\u000aenters the superior/medial aspect of the specimen and exits the\u000ainferior/posterior aspect of the specimen. The specimen radiograph shows a\u000acentral lucent area corresponding to the biopsy site and scattered\u000acalcifications around the biopsy. The specimen is serially sectioned from\u000alateral to medial in a total of nine slices (slice 1 = lateral). In slices\u000a3-6, there is a well-delineated smooth walled fibrous biopsy cavity (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm), which is REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. The cavity is\u000acompletely surrounded by very dense, focally hemorrhagic white/tan fibrous\u000atissue with multiple focal areas of chalky yellow/tan fat necrosis. The dense\u000afibrous tissue extends to all surgical margins. A discrete mass is not grossly\u000aidentified. Wire 1 traverses the superior aspect of the biopsy cavity while\u000awire 2 traverses the inferior aspect of the biopsy cavity. A discrete mass is\u000anot grossly identified. The remainder of the specimen is composed of greater\u000athan 90% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue admixed with >10% unremarkable\u000awhite/tan fibrous stroma. The specimen is entirely submitted sequentially from\u000alateral to medial as follows:\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 1 (lateral), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 2, to include dense fibrous tissue, hemorrhage and fat\u000anecrosis, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slices REMOVED_DATE to include entire biopsy cavity with adjacent dense\u000afibrous tissue, hemorrhage and fat necrosis, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 7, bisected, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 8, bisected, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 9 (medial), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aLmb/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Lynette M Sholl M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/1/2005\u000a[report_end]
