VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLEE, KENNETH, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LEE,KENNETH ROBERT,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aResidual intraductal papilloma with focal areas of LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN\u000aSITU and atypical lobular hyperplasia with diffuse areas of epithelial\u000ahyperplasia, apocrine metaplasia, and sclerosing adenosis.\u000aSkin with scar and old biopsy site are present.\u000aReviewed by Dr. Susan Lester.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "UTERUS, CERVIX, TUBES AND OVARIES" (72gms):\u000aCervix:\u000aSquamous metaplasia.\u000aEndometrium:\u000aEndometrial Intraepithelial Neoplasia (atypical endometrial\u000ahyperplasia), focal.\u000aAtrophic endometrium.\u000aMyometrium:\u000aNo significant pathologic change.\u000aSerosa:\u000aNo significant pathologic change.\u000aLeft ovary:\u000aCortical (mesothelial) inclusion cysts, periovarian adhesions.\u000aRight ovary:\u000aCortical (mesothelial) inclusion cysts, periovarian adhesions.\u000aRight and left tubes:\u000aNo significant pathologic change.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Excision of left breast papillary - squamous metaplasia. Now for\u000awider excision of papilloma site.\u000aOperation: Re-excision papilloma\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Endometrial hyperplasia, atypical papilloma left breast\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast tissue (long stitch lateral, short superior)\u000a2. Uterus, cervix, both tubes and ovaries\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BAILEY,GERALD P.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in 2 parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart 1, "left breast tissue - long lateral, short superior", is one fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue (3.5 x 3 x 2 cm) with a skin ellipse (2 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a\u000awell healed REMOVED_DATE cm central scar. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior =\u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange and contains two\u000asutures: long = lateral and short = superior. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from medial to lateral and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - left breast tissue, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aPart 2, "uterus, cervix, both tubes and ovaries", is a 72g specimen including\u000auterus (8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), right fallopian tube (5 cm in length by REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000adiameter), right ovary (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), left fallopian tube (4.5 cm in\u000alength by REMOVED_DATE cn in diameter) and left ovary (2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The exocervix\u000a(3 x REMOVED_DATE cm) is covered by smooth, glistening, white mucosa. The external os\u000ais slit-like and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The endocervical canal (3 cm in\u000alength) has a tan herringbone mucosa. The endometrial cavity (2.5 cm from\u000acornu to cornu, REMOVED_DATE cm in length) has a tan/pink hemorrhagic endometrium (0.2\u000acm in average thickness). The myometrium measures REMOVED_DATE cm in maximum thickness.\u000aThe serosa is dull and there are no adhesions. Both fallopian tubes are patent\u000aand have fimbriated ends without paratubal cysts. Both ovaries have a\u000acribriform, glistening, tan surface.\u000aMicro 10 - anterior cervix, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11 - posterior cervix, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 12 - LUS, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - anterior endometrium, REMOVED_DATE f each cass, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - posterior endometrium, REMOVED_DATE f each cass, ESS.\u000aMicro 22 - left ovary & fallopian tube, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 23 - right ovary & fallopian tube, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aReports to: FARHAD, SAHBA M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: UTERUS 