VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1) SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST, UPPER INNER QUADRANT", WIRE-LOCALIZED\u000aINCISION:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions,\u000aintraductal papilloma, apocrine metaplasia, epithelial hyperplasia, and\u000acysts.\u000aMicrocalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000a2) SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST, LOWER INNER QUADRANT", WIRE-LOCALIZED\u000aEXCISION:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, apocrine metaplasia, epithelial hyperplasia,\u000aand adenosis.\u000aSkeletal muscle.\u000aCore biopsy site identified.\u000a3) SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION":\u000aCysts, apocrine metaplasia, epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aMicrocalcifications associated with benign epithelium\u000a4) SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST, UPPER INNER QUADRANT, RE-EXCISION":\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Lobular carcinoma in situ and adenosis.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast, abnormal mammo.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Left breast upper inner quad, short/superior, long/ lateral x core bx.\u000a2. Breast, lower inner quad, short/superior, long/lateral.\u000a3. Left breast, long/lateral, short/superior.\u000a4. Left breast, re-excision upper quad, inner, short/superior, long/lateral.\u000aRadiology Reports:\u000aSpecimen #1, Rad - 2 wires, no clip, discussed with Dr. Matory. SMS/SR.\u000aSpecimen #2, Rad - clip in specimen. SMS/SR.\u000aSpecimen #3, No clip in specimen discussed with Dr. Matory.\u000aSpecimen #4, No clip.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LIN,JONATHAN H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in four parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, left breast upper inner quadrant, short/superior,\u000along/lateral" is a breast biopsy specimen received with two (2) orienting\u000asutures designated short/superior and long/lateral by the surgeon along with\u000aone (1) wire in place. The breast biopsy measures 6 cm from medial to lateral,\u000a4.2 cm from anterior to superior and anterior to posterior and REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000asuperior to inferior. The breast biopsy consists of greater than 80% yellow\u000aadipose tissue. There is an irregular area of white fibrosis measuring REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ain greatest dimension that appears to approach to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the green\u000ainked margin. There is a also a REMOVED_DATE cm clear fluid filled cyst that appears to\u000aapproach to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the green inked margin. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast biopsy specimen, 25 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, left breast, lower inner quadrant, short/superior,\u000along/lateral", consists of a breast biopsy specimen oriented by two (2) sutures\u000adesignated as short/superior, long/lateral by the surgeon along with the wire\u000ain place measuring REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to\u000aposterior and REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior\u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aThe specimen consists approximately of 80% yellow adipose tissue, and the\u000aremaining tissue may consist of possible skeletal muscle admixed with bands of\u000airregular white fibrous tissue. A definite biopsy site is not identified. The\u000aclip is not grossly identified. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lower inner quadrant breast biopsy serially sectioned from\u000alateral to medial, entirely submitted, 23 frags, ESS.\u000aPart three, labeled "#3, left breast, long lateral, short superior", consists\u000aof a breast biopsy specimen received with two (2) sutures designated\u000along/lateral by the surgeon measuring REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom anterior to posterior and REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior. The specimen\u000ais inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. The specimen consists of 80% of yellow adipose tissue, and a\u000adiffuse area of white fibrosis (1.5 cm in greatest dimension) appears to\u000aimmediately abut both the green and red inked margins. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast biopsy specimen #3, serially sectioned and entirely\u000asubmitted from lateral to medial, 12 frags, ESS.\u000aPart four, labeled "#4, left breast, re-excision upper quadrant, long/lateral,\u000ashort superior", consists of a breast biopsy specimen received with two sutures\u000adesignated short/superior, long/lateral by the surgeon. The specimen is inked\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black;\u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial =\u000aorange and measuring REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to\u000ainferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior. The specimen consists of 80%\u000aadipose tissue with possible interspersed areas of fibrosis in the remaining\u000atissue. The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  re-excision breast biopsy specimen, 7 frags, ESS.\u000ajhl\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
