VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBROWN, FELIX, MARCEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BROWN,FELIX MARCEL,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions.\u000aBiopsy site changes including fibrosis, fat necrosis and hemosiderin\u000adeposition.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aCalcifications in association with benign epithelium.\u000aNOTE: Because of preoperative clinical or radiologic concern regarding the\u000apossibility of tumor, the margins of this specimen were inked, sampled,\u000aand examined microscopically.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 45 year old premenopausal female, not on hormones, whose REMOVED_DATE \u000amammograms demonstrate right breast UOQ calcifications. REMOVED_DATE core\u000abiopsy reveals DCIS and ADH.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized excision x 2\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast tissue (short/superior; long/lateral; whip\u000astitch/deep margin)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip in specimen. Dr. Smith.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by PADERA,ROBERT F.,JR.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. right breast tissue", and consists of a single fragment of\u000abreast tissue. The tissue is received with a double long suture indicating\u000alateral, a double short suture indicating superior, and whip stitch that is\u000adesignated as the deep margin. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior\u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aThe specimen is received with a wire in place. The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from inferior to superior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000aanterior to posterior. Within the breast tissue there are two areas of\u000anodularity. The more medial area measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and is present\u000awithin 1 mm of the inferior and posterior margin, is REMOVED_DATE cm from from the\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000amargin, and approximately 4 cm from the lateral margin. The second nodular\u000aarea measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, is associated with fat necrosis and\u000ahemorrhage, and is the area marked by the clip. This nodule is REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, 2 cm from the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the lateral margin. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is\u000acomprised of approximately 80% adipose tissue and 20% fibrous tissue. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted for histologic evaluation\u000afrom medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue, mult frags, ESS (the medialmost nodule is\u000ain cassettes REMOVED_DATE  and the nodule marked by the clip is in\u000acassettes REMOVED_DATE with the area of the clip present in cassette 9)\u000arp\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
