VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: CHRISTINE M DENISON M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Jane E Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, LOWER OUTER, 9 G MRI GUIDED VACUUM-ASSISTED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES\u000aFOR CLUMPED NON-MASS ENHANCEMENT:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA with predominantly lobular features, measuring at least REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in size in this limited specimen.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aCARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type (intermediate nuclear grade), with focal necrosis\u000aand calcification, is present.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemistry for p63/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID confirms absence of myoepithelium in\u000athe focus of invasive carcinoma. Immunohistochemistry for E-cadherin\u000ademonstrates loss of membrane immunoreactivity in both the invasive and in situ\u000acarcinoma.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 49 y. o. with segmental, clumped non-mass enhancement in the right mid\u000aand lower outer breast. High risk for breast cancer. Suspect DCIS.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: 9 cm (ant-post extent), Nonpalpable, segmental, clumped and non-mass\u000aforming.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: lower outer\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 9G MRI Vacuum-assisted\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 9G MRI Vacuum-assisted - 2 Grey cassettes.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in one part, labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number, and consists of multiple yellow-tan irregular fibrofatty\u000atissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are received in two unlabeled\u000agray cassettes. The specimens are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (9/23/07):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for INVASIVE carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aNOTE: The in situ carcinoma shows partial loss of progesterone receptor in the\u000afocus with necrosis and will be characterized best following excision.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
