VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP":\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, single small focus (block #7) adjacent to\u000ahealing prior core biopsy site.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia, columnar alteration of lobules with prominent\u000asnouts and secretions, cysts, apocrine metaplasia, fibroadenomatoid\u000achanges, and calcifications in association with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy, including evaluation of all resection\u000amargins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left breast needle localized biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram, left.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left breast tissue short stitch superior, long stitch\u000alateral to FS room for mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aSpecimen radiograph contains loc wire, core biopsy clip and\u000acalcifications.\u000a(Radiologist's signature illegible)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by GIBSON,JOANNA A,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "Left breast tissue", and consists of an oriented breast excision specimen\u000a(4.5 cm inferior to superior, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm medial\u000ato lateral). The specimen is received with two orienting sutures designating\u000athe superior (short suture) and lateral (long suture) margins. The specimen is\u000aaccompanied a radiograph showing a clip, hookwire, and REMOVED_DATE clusters of\u000acalcifications. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is sectioned into\u000aeleven slices and is radiographed to reveal a clip in slice 7, and\u000acalcification clusters located in slices 4, 5, 7, and 8. Surrounding the clip\u000ais a partially hemorrhagic, ill-defined, white firm area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.8 cm, which is located REMOVED_DATE cm to the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to\u000athe lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial margin. The entire slices 4, 5,\u000a7, 8, and 9 are submitted. The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of\u000aunremarkable yellow lobulated adipose tissue admixed with tan/white fibrous\u000atissue. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice 4, with superior, inferior, anterior, and posterior margins,\u000a2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice 5, with superior, inferior, anterior, and posterior margins,\u000a2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice 7, (includes clip), with superior, inferior, posterior,\u000aand anterior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice 8, including inferior, superior, posterior, anterior margin,\u000a2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice 9, including inferior, superior, posterior, and anterior\u000amargin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 11: Medial margin (slice 1), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: Lateral margin (slice 11), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Remainder of slice 1, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice 2, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice 3, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice 6, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 21: Remainder of slice 10, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice 11, lateral/inferior margins, 5 frags, ESS.\u000ajgi\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
