n width) within the expander. For ID only.\u000aPart B, "#2 right breast tissue expander ID only," consists of a deflated\u000adiscoid medical device (12.5 cm in diameter x REMOVED_DATE cm in width), consistent with\u000aa breast tissue expander. The capsule is tan-red, textured, and displays the\u000afollowing inscription: "McGhan style 133 FV 12 cm - 400 cc Lot REMOVED_CASE_ID." There\u000ais a small amount of clear fluid and a silver metal disc (3.7 cm in diameter x\u000a0.7 cm in width) within the expander. For ID only.\u000aPart C, "#3 breast scar tissue," consists of a tan unoriented skin (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.4 (depth) cm). There is a linear, well-healed scar that traverses the length\u000aof the specimen. No other lesions are identified. The specimen is inked and\u000asectioned.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 4 frags, ESS\u000aPart D, "#4 breast scar tissue," consists of tan unoriented skin (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.4 (depth) cm). A definitive scar is not grossly identifiable. The specimen is\u000ainked and bisected.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS\u000aDFI/jp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Samuel G Katz M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Christopher D. M. Fletcher M.D. FRCPath, Electronically\u000asigned on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
