y, at least REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin. The\u000abiopsy cavity measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is an additional dense,\u000awhite, fibrous area that is REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension towards the axilla and\u000a0.2 cm from the deep margin. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass with biopsy cavity and deep margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous area towards axilla, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Left breast, stitch on axillary tail", consists of a 253\u000agm left simple mastectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a\u000apink skin ellipse that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with a flesh-colored areolar that\u000ais indistinguishable from the surrounding skin. There is an everted nipple\u000athat measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is no scar present. On section, the\u000aspecimen contains heterogeneous yellow, fibrofatty breast tissue with focally\u000adense white fibrotic areas but no discrete masses. Representative sections are\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous areas, 1 frag in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 axillary lymph node candidates, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPes/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Peter M Sadow M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
