pect is designated with a long stitch, the\u000asuperior with a short stitch and the deep margin with a whip stitch. There is\u000aa wire entering the specimen on its inferior aspect and exiting the specimen\u000abetween anterior and medial aspect. The specimen is previously inked by the\u000asurgeon. It was accompanied by a radiology report reading "MR clip and intact\u000awire in specimen." The specimen was sectioned to reveal a biopsy cavity (1.5 x\u000a1.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) present REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the anterior margins. It is surrounded by firm, white fibrous tissue with\u000asporadic hemorrhagic areas. The specimen was entirely submitted from medial to\u000alateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lumpectomy specimen, sectioned from medial to lateral, 1 to 4\u000afrags, each, ESS. The biopsy cavity is present in cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, the\u000aclip is found in cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aAWE/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
