VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOGINO, SHUJI, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by OGINO,SHUJI,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a"SKIN":\u000aSkin with scarring.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000a"RIGHT BREAST":\u000aBreast tissue with calcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aGranulation tissue, fat necrosis, foreign body giant cell reaction, and\u000ahemosiderin deposition consistent with previous biopsy site.\u000aSkeletal muscle with no significant pathologic change.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: H/O severe atypia now with microcalcifications adjacent to biopsy site\u000aOperation: R wire loc biopsy\u000aOperative findings: Radiograph specimen (+) microcalcification.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast microcalcification.\u000aR breast microcalcification.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Skin\u000a2. Rt breast - mammo tissue with wire.\u000aRADIOLOGY REOPRT: Calcs in specimen.\u000aD. N. Smith/PT\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by ABREU-E-LIMA,PAULA C.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fixed in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "1. Skin", consists of two fragments of skin with\u000asubcutaneous tissue (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aMicro #1: Skin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "2. Right breast mass", consists of a previously-inked\u000abreast excision specimen containing a single localization wire. The\u000aaccompanying radiograph shows a localization wire within an area containing\u000amultiple microcalcifications. The specimen (3.2 cm from superior to inferior x\u000a3.1 cm from medial to lateral x REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior), is serially\u000asectioned from the medial to the lateral margin. Within the specimen is a\u000awell-circumscribed yellow-white nodule (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the medial, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin.\u000aMicro #2-4: Unremarkable breast parenchyma, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro #5-8: Breast nodule, Micro #5 likely containing calcifications,\u000a1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro #9-10: Inferior and posterior margins, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000apal/\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
