VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Consult slide(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Hejin P Hahn, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM NORTH SHORE PATHOLOGISTS, SALEM, MA:\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aExtensive ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, with focal severe atypia, bordering on\u000aDCIS (see note).\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread is present.\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aPapillomatosis.\u000aNOTE: There is extensive atypical ductal hyperplasia seen throughout this\u000aspecimen. The atypical epithelial proliferation approaches DCIS in slides REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aand REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Slides seen also by Drs. Stuart Schnitt and James Connolly, who\u000aconcur. Re-excision of this area would be recommended.\u000aLEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is present focally (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present.\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aNOTE: Slides also seen by Drs. Stuart Schnitt and James Connolly, who\u000aconcur.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast calcifications.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aConsult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived from North Shore Pathologists, P.C., Salem Hospital, Pathology\u000aDepartment, 81 Highland Avenue, Salem, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are thirty-six (36) glass\u000aslides.\u000aTwenty-four (24) slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through\u000a"REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", corresponding to a left breast excision with\u000ainked margin evaluation (7.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to\u000athe accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aTwelve (12) slides are labeled "SS-05-REMOVED_CASE_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through\u000a"REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", corresponding to a left breast re-excision with inked margin\u000aevaluation (8.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the\u000aaccompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Deborah A Dillon M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
