e is received free-floating within the specimen\u000acontainer. The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to\u000aexhibit approximately 40% dense white/pink, focally gritty fibrous stroma and\u000aapproximately 60% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. No discrete masses or\u000alesions are grossly identified. The specimen is entirely sequentially\u000asubmitted from superior to inferior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: specimen from superior to inferior, with dense, gritty\u000afibrous stroma containing probable calcification in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000aand additional dense stroma in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, multiple frags total,\u000aESS.\u000almb/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/18/2006\u000a[report_end]
