VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Douglas I. Lin, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION, NEW MEDIAL POSTERIOR MARGIN:\u000aBenign breast tissue and biopsy cavity.\u000aNo residual carcinoma seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aentire specimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: ? of the medial and posterior margin (see path report); this is a\u000are-excision along the medial and posterior sides of the cavity "Stitches are\u000aplaced on the new margin."\u000aOperation: Not specified.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: As above.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. New medial posterior margin - long suture medial margin; short suture\u000aposterior margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "new medial posterior margin, long suture medial margin and short suture\u000aposterior margin", consists of an irregular tan/yellow lobulated portion of\u000afibroadipose breast tissue (3.8 cm anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to\u000ainferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral) (lateral margin designates old margin).\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol (superior red, inferior green,\u000amedial orange, lateral yellow, anterior blue and posterior black) and is\u000aserially sectioned from anterior to posterior. The cut surface is tan/yellow\u000aand homogeneous with no discrete lesions grossly identified. There are focal\u000airregular tan/yellow chalky areas of discoloration consistent with possible fat\u000anecrosis which grossly abuts the lateral (old) margin. The specimen is\u000asubmitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections anterior to posterior, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aSEK/mgd/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed\u000aon Wednesday August 19, 2009 at 03:31:48PM\u000a[report_end]
