VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: SARA M DURFEE M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Xuefei Hong, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, 8 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia associated with columnar cell change, mucin\u000aproduction, and calcifications, is present.\u000aNote: ADH is best evaluated with excision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 55 year old woman with a history of non-Hodgkin's lymphoma, S/P BMT\u000aone year ago. Now with new coarse calcifications R UOQ.\u000aOperation: 8-G Stereotactic.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R/O DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) 8-G core sampling right upper/outer quadrant Ca++, blue cassette: A -\u000awith Ca++, B - no Ca++.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast", and consists of multiple tan/yellow to tan/white\u000alobulated portions of fibroadipose breast tissue (3.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate). The breast tissue cores are received in a blue cassette labeled "A\u000aCa++", and remainder of the breast tissue cores received in a blue cassette\u000amarked "B". The specimen is submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette "A Ca++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000asek/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/30/2007\u000a[report_end]
