VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Christopher P. Elco, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP MARKING A\u000aCORE NEEDLE BIOPSY SITE:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aCore needle biopsy site.\u000aLobules and cysts with calcifications.\u000aNotes: Immunoperoxidase studies were attempted to further characterize\u000athe ADH and ALH but the lesion were no longer present on deeper levels.\u000aNo carcinoma is seen after complete microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 57 year old postmenopausal female, not on hormones. Family history of\u000aher mother developing breast cancer at 50 years of age. Mammograms REMOVED_DATE \u000ademonstrated R UOQ calcifications, REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy revealed atypical ductal\u000ahyperplasia, excision recommended.\u000aOperation: R breast wire localized biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue - short stitch superior, long stitch lateral, whip\u000astitch at deep margin\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aClip, residual calcifications, plus intact wire in specimen.\u000aCalled to Dr. Rhei by Dr. Lizer 11:55 am.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "#1. Right breast tissue", consists of a REMOVED_DATE (medial to\u000alateral) x REMOVED_DATE (superior to inferior) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior) cm breast\u000abiopsy with localization wire in place, a short suture marking the superior\u000amargin, a long suture marking the lateral margin, and a whipstitch at the deep\u000amargin. An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates a clip in place in\u000athe central portion of the specimen adjacent to the localization wire and a\u000adensity with calcifications. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange.\u000aThere is a well-circumscribed white mass (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) located REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior\u000amargin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. A second white firm region (0.8 cm\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is located REMOVED_DATE cm away from the first mass, abutting the\u000aposterior margin, less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000amargin. The stroma intervening between the two masses is dense white fibrous\u000atissue, which may represent a contiguous process between the two masses. The\u000aremainder of the specimen is yellow adipose tissue devoid of additional\u000alesions. The entire specimen is examined microscopically.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 2 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass from medial to lateral (biopsy cavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, mass 2 in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aand REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 2 frag each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aCEL/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aThursday REMOVED_MONTH 18, 2009 at 04:45:37PM\u000a[report_end]
