VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: CHRISTINE M DENISON M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Elizabeth M. Manion, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA.LEFT BREAST LOWER INNER 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A REMOVED_DATE \u000aCM IRREGULAR MASS:\u000aCARCINOMA IN SITU with lobular features and signet ring cells, involving an\u000aintraductal papilloma (at least REMOVED_DATE cm), see NOTE.\u000aE-cadherin stain highlights reduced membranous expression in the carcinoma in\u000asitu consistent with lobular morphology.\u000aA p63/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID double stain highlights retained myoepithelial cells in the\u000aintraductal papilloma around fibrovascular cores.\u000aB. LEFT BREAST LOWER INNER 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A\u000a0.5 CM ILL DEFINED AREA OF ARCHITECTURAL DISTORTION:\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, well to moderately differentiated (modified\u000aBloom-Richardson grade I-II/III; tubules score 3, nuclei score predominantly 1,\u000afocally 2, mitoses score 1), with signet ring cells, measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in this\u000alimited biopsy.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aCARCINOMA IN SITU with lobular features and signet ring cells, see NOTE:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for INVASIVE CARCINOMA and CIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) HETEROGENEOUS (1+ to 2+)\u000aA block will be sent for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu FISH studies and the results reported in an\u000aaddendum.\u000aNOTE: The CIS in both biopsies has areas of slightly higher nuclear grade than\u000atypically seen in classic LCIS. No necrosis or calcifications are associated\u000awith the CIS.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: Site #1: Site 54 y. o. with strong family hx of breast cancer. Now\u000a7-mm mass with indistinct and angular margin LLIQ, 7:00, 3 cm from the nipple.\u000aAdditional site of concern 7:00, 8 cm from the nipple = biopsy site #2 (see\u000apage 2).\u000aSite #2: 54 with strong family hx breast cancer. new vague focal density\u000aposterior LLIQ with subtle distortion, shadowing on U/S @ 7:00, 8 cm from\u000anipple. Additional 7-mm mass @ 7:0, N+3 cm = biopsy site #1 (see page 1)\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: 7-mm, Nonpalpable and irregular mass.\u000a2. Left: ~5 mm, Nonpalpable, architectural distortion and ? ill-defined mass.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: lower inner\u000a2. Left: lower inner\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 14G Ultrasound\u000a2. 14G Ultrasound\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Biopsy site #1: 1:00 p.m. in formalin, 7:00 N+3 lesion round mass with\u000aangular margin. - 1 blue cassette.\u000aB/2. Biopsy site #2: vague mass density LLIQ + arch. distort/? mass on U/S\u000a7:00 N+8 cm; in formalin @ 1:30 p.m. - 1 pink cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name, unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "left breast", consists of a blue cassette containing multiple\u000acylindrical focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty soft tissues (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate), which are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of blue cassette, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "left breast #2", consists of a pink cassette containing\u000amultiple cylindrical focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty soft tissues (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.3 cm in aggregate), which are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of pink cassette, multi frags, ESS.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis\u000ausing the following criteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not\u000ayet been determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor\u000acells but only a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >30% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for\u000ainvestigational use only.\u000aJC/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 17, 2009 at 04:50:39PM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: (11/23/09)\u000aFISH was performed by Clarient using the PathVysion HER-2 DNA Probe Kit with\u000athe following (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aResults: NOT AMPLIFIED\u000aHER-2/CEP-17 ratio = REMOVED_DATE \u000aAverage HER-2 copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aAverage centromere 17 copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aREFERENCE RANGE:\u000aNOT AMPLIFIED HER-2/CEP-17 ratio < REMOVED_DATE \u000aEQUIVOCAL HER-2/CEP-17 ratio REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE \u000aAMPLIFIED REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/CEP-17 ratio > REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #1 by Amy Ly M.D., Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 23,\u000a2009 at 04:34:26PM\u000a[report_end]
