VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aRICHARDSON, ANDREA, L., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS (SL-02-REMOVED_CASE_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR, INTERMEDIATE GRADE, at least REMOVED_DATE cm by gross report (see\u000anote).\u000aTumor is present <0.1 cm from inked surgical margins (specimen not\u000aoriented).\u000aNOTE: The tumor has hypercellular stroma with severe cytologic atypia and a\u000amitotic rate of 2 per 10 hpf. Focal heterologous smooth muscle differentiation\u000ais present, but frank sarcomatous elements are not seen. There is no necrosis,\u000ahemorrhage or stromal overgrowth. The margins are mostly circumscribed but\u000awith focal infiltrative areas. The epithelium associated with the phyllodes\u000atumor is notable for extensive squamous metaplasia.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 35 y/o female diagnosed with phyllodes tumor.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Consult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by PREISINGER,ELIZABETH ANN,M.D.\u000aReceived from Southcoast **LIVE** Lab system, St. Luke's Hospital, Pathology\u000aDepartment, 101 Page Street, New Bedford, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are four (4) slides.\u000aThe slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "1", "2", "4" and "5",\u000acorresponding to a right breast excision (2.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm and REMOVED_DATE x 5 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report\u000abearing the patient's name.\u000aSubsequently received on REMOVED_DATE  is a single slide labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and\u000asublabeled "3".\u000aSubsequently received on REMOVED_DATE  is a single slide labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and\u000asublabeled "6".\u000aReports to: GEORGE, SUZANNE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000a[report_end]
