VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOGINO, SHUJI, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by OGINO,SHUJI,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIDE EXCISION OF PHYLLODES TUMOR SITE:\u000aBreast tissue with cysts, apocrine metaplasia, intraductal papillomas\u000a(2).\u000aPrior biopsy cavity.\u000aFibroadenomatous changes are present; however, no residual phyllodes\u000atumor is present.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of\u000athe specimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Phyllodes tumor right breast.\u000aOperation: Right simple mastectomy (right breast quadrantectomy).\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Phyllodes of right breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Wide excision Phyllodes site right breast, stitch\u000asubareola\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HAHN,HEJIN P.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1, Wide excision sarcoma right breast, stitch subareola", and consists of\u000aa piece of breast tissue (7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a tan-white skin ellipse (4.5\u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm) that contains a well-healed linear scar (3.6 cm). The specimen was\u000ainked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior = black;\u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial =\u000aorange, and contains a stitch on the anteromedial portion of the specimen to\u000adesignate subareola tissue. The prior excision cavity is identified and is\u000a0.2 cm from the closest anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest\u000ainferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest medial margin, and 3 cm from the\u000aclosest lateral margin. There is a well-circumscribed hematoma (0.7 cm) just\u000abelow the biopsy cavity. The medial portion of the specimen is composed dense\u000arubbery, white-tan tissue, the remainder of the specimen is 80% adipose\u000atissue. Approximately 80% of the entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy cavity, marked by stitch, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  sections lateral to biopsy cavity including hematoma, 10 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior margin, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial fibrous area, 8 frags, ESS.\u000ahph\u000aReports to: BERTAGNOLLI, MONICA, MARIE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
