VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia with associated microcalcifications\u000a(blocks #1 & #5, levels examined).\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 44-year-old premenopausal female whose REMOVED_DATE  mammogram demonstrated\u000aleft breast UOQ calcifications for which biopsy is recommended, not\u000aamenable to core biopsy.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localization biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast tissue, long lateral, short superior,\u000awhipstitch chest wall margin.\u000aCalcifications and wire in specimen/radiology.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by ABREU-E-LIMA,PAULA C.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1, left breast tissue", and consists of REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm medial to lateral and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior. The specimen is\u000areceived ink, with orienting sutures (long = lateral, short = superior, and\u000awhipstitch = deep margin. The specimen is received with a hook wire in the\u000asuperior/anterior area and exiting in the medial/posterior area. The specimen\u000ais received with an accompanying radiograph which shows a hook wire, and\u000amicrocalcifications within the specimen. Sectioning reveals 60% white firm\u000afibrous tissue admixed with yellow lobulated adipose tissue. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted from anterior to superior. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aMicro 1: superior margins and adjacent medial margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  anterior, posterior, medial, lateral margins, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 6: inferior margin, 5 frags, ESS.\u000ajgi\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
