VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ELISABETH P FROST M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Mariana A. Stoleru, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER OUTER QUADRANT, 8G STEREOTACTIC GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES\u000aFOR A REMOVED_DATE CM AREA OF CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA (see Note).\u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA (see Note).\u000aCalcifications are associated with columnar cell change, cysts and atypical\u000ahyperplasia.\u000aNote: Within an area of columnar cell change with calcifications and cysts\u000a(seen in block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) there is classic atypical lobular hyperplasia lacking\u000amembranous staining for E-cadherin. In addition there is a focus of atypical\u000ahyperplasia with low grade nuclei and a more ductal morphology associated with\u000acalcifications and necrosis (best seen in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) which shows retained weak\u000amembranous staining with E-cadherin, consistent with ADH. ADH is evaluated best\u000awith excision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: Clustered amorphous calcifications left upper/outer quadrant\u000astretching over 7 mm.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: 7 mm, non-palpable and calcifications.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: upper/outer.\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 8G Stereotactic and vacuum-assisted.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast core biopsy in two green cassettes - A/with calcs and B/no\u000acalcs.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast", and consists of multiple yellow-white focally\u000ahemorrhagic fibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are\u000areceived in two green cassettes, labeled "A Ca++" and "B". The specimens are\u000asubmitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "A Ca++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000acp/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aThursday REMOVED_MONTH 08, 2009 at 04:00:34PM\u000a[report_end]
