VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: Esther Rhei M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Patricia A. R. Brunker, M.D., D. Phil.\u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aFibroadenoma (0.9 cm).\u000aCalcifications in association with benign epithelium, apocrine\u000ametaplasia, and cysts.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Not provided.\u000aOperation: Needle directed left breast bx.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammo left breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue - short superior, long lateral, whip stitch deep\u000amargin.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aMass in specimen (EP Frost).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient?s name,\u000aunit number, and "#1. Left breast tissue - short superior, long lateral, whip\u000astitch clip margin", and consists of one fragment of red/yellow fibroadipose\u000atissue (5.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is oriented by the three sutures designated\u000aby the surgeon as short superior, long lateral, and whip stitch deep. The\u000aspecimen is pierced by a needle localization wire, which enters at the\u000asuperoanterior aspect and exits at the superolateral aspect. The whipstitch is\u000aconcordant and oriented such that is posterior (deep). Accompanying the\u000aspecimen, there is a radiograph bearing the patient's name and medical record\u000anumber and showing a radiodense mass of soft tissue, approximating specimen,\u000awith a needle localization wire, which is encircled by the radiologist. The\u000aspecimen is inked in the pathology department per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. Serial sectioning demonstrates\u000afibrous tissue without discrete nodules. Approximately 20% of the specimen is\u000aadipose tissue. The specimen is entirely and serially submitted for histologic\u000aevaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: left breast tissue, medial to lateral, 10 frags, ESS.\u000aPab/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Patricia A. R. Brunker M.D., D. Phil., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
