VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Reduction mamoplasty\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DENNIS P ORGILL M.D.,PH.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Leona A. Doyle, M.D.; Marianna B Ruzinova, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA/1. RIGHT BREAST, REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY (989 GM):\u000aBenign breast tissue with associated calcifications.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aB/2. LEFT BREAST, REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY (840 GM):\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present (see note).\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemistry for E-cadherin is negative in LCIS, supporting\u000alobular phenotype.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None specified.\u000aOperation: Bil breasts, reduction.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Bil. breasts, hypertrophy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast tissue 989.\u000aB/2) Left breast tissue 840.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast tissue", consists of multiple yellow lobulated\u000afibrofatty tissue, with overlying and separately received tan wrinkled\u000aunremarkable skin fragments (989 grams, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimens\u000aare serially sectioned to reveal 60% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, and 40%\u000afocally dense, nodular and cystic white fibrous tissue, with no discrete masses\u000aor lesions identified. Representative sections of the skin and fibrous tissue\u000aare submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin and fibrous tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional sampling, 10 frags, RSS\u000aPart B, "#2. Left breast tissue", consists of multiple irregular lobulated\u000afragments of fibrofatty tissue, with overlying and separately received tan\u000awrinkled unremarkable skin fragments (840 grams, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000aspecimens are serially sectioned to reveal 70% yellow lobulated adipose tissue,\u000aand 30% focally dense white, nodular, focally cystic white fibrous tissue, with\u000ano discrete masses or lesions identified. Representative sections of the skin\u000aand fibrous tissue are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin and fibrous tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional sampling, 10 frags, RSS\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/23/2008\u000a[report_end]
