VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Consult material\u000aProcedure Date:\u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Peter M Sadow, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM NORTH SHORE PATHOLOGISTS, SALEM, MA:\u000aLEFT BREAST, 2:00, ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY FOR A "SMALL" NODULE\u000a(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aAtypical hyperplasia is present involving lobules and ducts (see note).\u000aNote: The biopsy was performed to evaluate a "nodule". Histologic features of\u000aa mass forming lesion are not seen.\u000aThere are two lobular units involved by a proliferation of cells with some\u000asignet ring cells present. Although the histologic features are suggestive of\u000aa "lobular" type of lesion, the nuclear pleomorphism is somewhat higher than\u000atypical for this type of lesion.\u000aClinical and radiologic correlation are suggested to ensure that the biopsy is\u000arepresentative of the targeted lesion.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given\u000aClinical Diagnosis: LCIS\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aConsult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived from North Shore Pathologist, P.C., Pathology Department, 81 Highland\u000aAvenue, Salem, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are three (3) glass slides.\u000aTwo (2) slides are labeled "SS-06-REMOVED_CASE_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID",\u000acorresponding to a left breast, 2 o'clock, core biopsy (0.6 cm) performed on\u000a10/18/06, according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's\u000aname.\u000aOne (1) cytology slide is labeled "CS-06-REMOVED_CASE_ID" and sublabeled "A-1",\u000acorresponding to a left breast, 2 o'clock, 6 cm from areolar, fine needle\u000aaspiration performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying cytology report\u000abearing the patient's name. The cytologic preparations were not reviewed due\u000ato a lack of medical necessity (outside diagnosis: red cells/inflammatory\u000acells, scattered groupings of apocrine metaplasia cells, and scattered poorly\u000apreserved histiocytes).\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/1/2006\u000a[report_end]
