VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-10-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Paul A. VanderLaan, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST TISSUE, DOUBLE WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A PRIOR BIOPSY SITE\u000aAND A SECOND AREA OF CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aBiopsy site with adjacent intraductal papilloma(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aSeparate focus of microcalcifications associated with a complex-sclerosing\u000alesion, and with columnar cell change with cysts.\u000aApocrine cysts, columnar cell change and epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 41 y o woman with region coarse calcifications on screening R\u000amammogram. S/P core bx with clip placement, R resulted as LCIS, with atypia\u000arecommended for excision to better eval. On day of surgery, second area of\u000amicrocalcs noted within 1 cm and radiologist opted to place 2 wires.\u000aOperation: R wire-localized breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast LCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast tissue; one wire marks clip; one wire marks additional\u000acalcification (to mammo 1709).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue", consists of an irregular portion of yellow\u000alobulated fibrofatty tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a long suture\u000adesignating lateral and a short suture designating superior. The specimen is\u000areceived previously inked per pathology protocol as anterior blue, posterior\u000ablack, superior red, inferior green, lateral yellow, and medial orange. A\u000aradiograph reviewed on centricity shows the specimen with two wires in place,\u000aone marking a clip. The specimen is received with two inserted needle\u000alocalization wires. Both needle localization wires enter at the lateral margin\u000aand traverse towards the medial margin. The wires are placed REMOVED_DATE cm apart from\u000aone another. The needle localization wire closest to the superior margin is\u000aarbitrarily designated by the prosector as needle localization wire #1, and the\u000aneedle localization wire closer to the inferior margin is arbitrarily\u000adesignated by the prosector as needle localization wire #2. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned to reveal a well-healed biopsy cavity (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000awhich contains a surgical clip. This biopsy cavity and surgical clip is recent\u000ato the arbitrarily designated needle localization wire #2, towards the inferior\u000amargin. The biopsy cavity is REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. The\u000aremaining cut surface displays 80% focally dense white fibrous tissue, and 20%\u000ayellow lobulated adipose tissue, with no additional discrete masses or lesions\u000aidentified. The specimen is sequentially submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, radially, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, which may contain area of\u000acalcification adjacent to needle localization wire #1 (arbitrarily designated),\u000a1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, which may contain area of\u000acalcification adjacent to arbitrarily designated needle localization wire #1, 1\u000afrag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, which may contain the area of\u000acalcification adjacent to arbitrarily designated needle localization wire #1, 1\u000afrag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, with the biopsy cavity\u000acontaining the surgical clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, with the biopsy cavity in\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining sequential cross sections, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, radially, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aSaturday REMOVED_MONTH 09, 2010 at 02:38:08PM\u000a[report_end]
