VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Eric L Snyder, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA) RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY:\u000aBreast tissue with florid epithelial hyperplasia, sclerosing adenosis,\u000acalcifications associated with benign epithelium, and prior biopsy site\u000achanges.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aB) LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY:\u000aBreast tissue with focal atypical lobular hyperplasia, epithelial\u000ahyperplasia, and prior biopsy site changes.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast atypical ductal hyperplasia and left breast atypical\u000alobular hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: Bilateral breast wire localized excisional biopsies.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast atypical ductal hyperplasia and left breast\u000aatypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1 - rt breast wire localized excisional bx (stitch = short/superior,\u000along/lateral)\u000aB/2 - left breast wire localized excision bx (stitch = short/superior,\u000along/lateral).\u000aRADIOGRAPHY REPORT:\u000aSpecimen A/1: calcifications and wire are in the specimen, DEH (CD).\u000aSpecimen B/2: clip is seen in second specimen C. Denison, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A is labeled #1 - right breast wire loc", and consists of a single breast\u000aexcision specimen, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is oriented by\u000athe surgeon with a short stitch indicating the superior margin, and a long\u000astitch indicating the lateral margin. There is a localizing wire in the\u000aspecimen, as well as an accompanying radiograph demonstrating the area\u000alocalized by the wire. On the superior side of the specimen towards the\u000aanterior portion there are multiple tan granules of foreign material, likely\u000aconsistent with gel foam that is injected by a surgeon to mark prior biopsy\u000asites. The specimen was inked by pathology according to the pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is largely\u000acomposed of fibrous tissue with no discrete masses. The specimen is sectioned\u000aserially from anterior to deep margin and entirely submitted. Note, the wire\u000alocalizes an area in the most anterior aspect of the specimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: anterior-most portion of the specimen containing the area\u000alocalized by the wire, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: remainder of the specimen, serially sectioned, REMOVED_DATE fags in\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aPart B is labeled "#2 - left breast wire loc biopsy", and consists of a breast\u000aexcision specimen, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is oriented by\u000athe surgeon, such that the short stitch indicates the superior margin, and the\u000along stitch indicates the lateral margin. The specimen is inked by pathology\u000aaccording to the pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. There is a wire in the specimen, as well as an accompanying\u000aradiograph. The wire localizes to a medial portion of the specimen. The\u000aspecimen is sectioned from medial to lateral. The specimen is composed of\u000afibroadipose tissue with no discrete nodules or masses. There is a white\u000aforeign material present in the posterior/lateral portion of the specimen,\u000alikely consistent with gel foam injected into a prior biopsy site. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted as follows:\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: medial-most section, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: next serial section, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: sections containing the area localized by wire, 1 frag in\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: additional sections of fibroadipose tissue, REMOVED_DATE frags in\u000aeach, ESS (NOTE: fragments in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID contain the previously noted foreign\u000amaterial.).\u000aESN/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/9/2005\u000a[report_end]
