VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIAN J PRIBAZ M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Cheryl Adackapara, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aGYNECOMASTIA with associated pseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aB. MEDIAN MARGIN OF LEFT BREAST MASS:\u000aVascular and adipose tissue with no significant pathologic change.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aC. INFERIOR MARGIN OF LEFT BREAST MASS:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, focal (see Note).\u000aGYNECOMASTIA with associated pseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aNote: The focus of ADH is seen only on the original slide (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and not on\u000adeeper levels. Dr. Susan Lester also reviewed REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and agrees with the diagnosis\u000aof ADH.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Male with painful L breast lump - excised.\u000aOperation: Excision left breast mass.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left breast mass, short/superior, long/lateral.\u000aB/2) median margin, left breast mass.\u000aC/3) inferior margin, left breast mass.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "Left breast mass, short superior, long lateral", consists of\u000aan irregular tan-yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose breast tissue (4.6 cm\u000amedial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to\u000aposterior) with a short suture designating as superior margin, and long suture\u000adesignating as lateral margin. The specimen is inked (superior red, inferior\u000ared, medial large, lateral yellow, anterior black and posterior blue. Please\u000anote the change of the anterior and posterior margins, which deviates from\u000astandard pathology protocol). The specimen is serially sectioned from medial\u000ato lateral. The cut surface is tan-yellow and homogenous with focal areas of\u000adense white fibrous tissue constituting approximately less than 10% of the\u000abreast parenchyma. No discrete lesions are grossly identified. The specimen\u000ais submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections medial to lateral, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "Left breast medial margin", consists of an unoriented\u000airregular tan-yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose breast tissue (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is inked, serially sectioned, and the cut surface is\u000atan-yellow and homogenous with no discrete lesions grossly identified. The\u000aspecimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, 2 frag each, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "Inferior margin left breast", consists of an unoriented\u000airregular tan-yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose breast tissue (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is inked, and the cut surface is tan-yellow and\u000ahomogenous with a focal area of dense white fibrous tissue constituting\u000aapproximately less than 10% of the breast parenchyma. The specimen is\u000asubmitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, 2 frag each, ESS.\u000aSEK/lp/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 23, 2008 at 03:17:34PM\u000a[report_end]
