VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 12:00, 11 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR ENHANCING\u000aAREA ON MRI:\u000aAdenosis with columnar cell change and mucin production.\u000aLEFT BREAST, 12:00, 11 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR AN\u000aENHANCING MASS BY MRI, LOBULATED MASS BY ULTRASOUND:\u000aSclerosing adenosis (at least REMOVED_DATE cm), associated with sclerotic stroma\u000aconsistent with a complex sclerosing lesion.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: #1. Enhancing area on right breast MRI at 12:00, ultrasound\u000ashows vague hypechoic area.\u000a#2. Enhancing area on left breast MRI at 12:00, ultrasound shows lobulated\u000ahypoechoic area.\u000aOperation: 11 G Ultrasound guided x 2.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Sclerosing adenosis.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast tissue in a blue cassette.\u000a#2. Left breast tissue in pink cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by WITKIEWICZ,AGNIESKA K.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in two parts, each labeled with the patient's name and\u000aunit number.\u000aPart one, received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast", in a blue cassette, and consists of multiple,\u000asoft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast", in a pink cassette, and consists of multiple, soft,\u000afragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro 2: Multi frags, ESS.\u000adf\u000aReports to: SMITH, DARRELL, NOLAN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
