VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DAVID I SOYBEL M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Paul A. VanderLaan, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aFibroadenoma with coarse calcifications (present in the deeper levels of\u000ablock REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aSkin is present.\u000aNote: The radiologic calcifications are present within the fibroadenoma.\u000aNo malignancy is seen after microscopic examination of the specimen, including\u000amargins.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aFibroadenoma with coarse calcifications (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aColumnar cell change.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aApocrine cyst.\u000aSkin is present.\u000aNote: No malignancy is seen after microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Not provided.\u000aOperation: Left wire localized breast excision; right wire localized breast\u000aexcision.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Microcalcifications right and left breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue ? mammo.\u000aB/2. Right breast tissue ? short superior, long lateral ? mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcifications in R and left. Dr. Meyer\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Left breast tissue", consists of two unoriented portions\u000aof fibrofatty tissues (measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThe specimen radiograph shows an area of chunky calcifications associated with\u000aa circumscribed tissue density. The smaller fragment displays a partially\u000ainserted needle localization wire, as displayed in the accompanying\u000aradiographs. The larger fibrofatty tissue displays a tan wrinkled skin ellipse\u000a(2.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm). Please note that due to the fragmented nature of the specimen,\u000athe exact location as to the calcifications cannot be determined. The\u000aspecimens are inked black and serially sectioned to reveal 99% yellow lobulated\u000aadipose tissue, and 1% white fibrous tissue, with no discrete masses or lesions\u000aidentified. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aThe tissue is radiographed and the radiologic calcifications are identified in\u000ablock REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Additional levels through the block are obtained.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Smaller unoriented portion of fibrofatty tissue, with inserted\u000aneedle localization wire, sequential cross sections, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Unoriented margin of larger fibrofatty tissue, with overlying\u000atan skin, radially.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, trisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, trisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, trisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Right breast tissue, short superior, long lateral",\u000aconsists of a portion of fibrofatty tissue (8.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a long\u000asuture designating lateral, and a short suture designating superior. There is\u000aan overlying tan wrinkled unremarkable skin ellipse along the anterior/medial\u000amargin (2.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen radiograph shows an area of chunky\u000acalcifications associated with a soft tissue density. There is an inserted\u000aneedle localization wire, as displayed on the accompanying radiograph, which\u000aenters along the skin along the anterior margin, and superficially exits along\u000athe lateral/inferior margin. The specimen is inked by the prosector, per\u000apathology protocol as anterior blue, posterior black, superior red, inferior\u000agreen, lateral yellow and medial orange. The specimen is serially sectioned to\u000areveal 98% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, and 2% white fibrous tissue, with\u000ano discrete masses or lesions identified. Please note that the fibrous tissue\u000a(1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), is concentrated within this area, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and\u000a7.0 cm from the medial margin. This area is consistent with the area of\u000acalcifications as seen on the accompanying radiograph. Representative\u000asections, to include every other cross section, and the entire fibrous area are\u000asubmitted. Please note that 85% of the specimen, to include the entire fibrous\u000aarea correlating to the area of calcifications on the accompanying radiograph\u000ais submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior/medial margin, radially, with the skin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, bisected, with the fibrous area in\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, bisected, with the fibrous area in\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, bisected, with the fibrous area in\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, radially, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCP/mgd/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/20/2008\u000a[report_end]
