the specimen. The specimen was inked\u000aby the pathologist per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral\u000a= yellow; medial = orange. The breast parenchyma is white/yellow/tan with no\u000adiscrete lesions identified. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely\u000asubmitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior margin, left breast from medial to lateral, mult frags,\u000aESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. anterior left breast", consists of a single fragment of\u000apink/yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior\u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral to medial x REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior. A short\u000ablack suture was placed by the surgeon to indicate the superior aspect of the\u000aspecimen and a long black suture was placed by the surgeon to indicate the\u000alateral aspect of the specimen. The specimen was inked by the pathologist per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior\u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aThere is a single firm white/tan nodule (0.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which appears to\u000aabut the posterior, lateral, and inferior margins. No other lesions are\u000agrossly identified. The specimen is approximately 70% adipose tissue and 30%\u000afibrous tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  anterior margin, left breast from superior to inferior, mult\u000afrags, ESS\u000adk\u000aReports to: LIN, AARON, C. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
