_DATE cm)\u000aperformed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing\u000athe patient's name.\u000aTen (10) slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 1" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 5"\u000aand "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 1" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 5", corresponding to A) right breast stereotactic core\u000aneedle biopsy for calcifications (2.5 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm) B) right breast\u000astereotactic core needle biopsy (2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aaccording to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aThirty-three (33) slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through\u000a"REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", corresponding to A) right breast needle localized\u000abiopsy for a mass (4.9 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 cm) B) right breast, deep margin, re-excision\u000afor a mass (6.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the\u000aaccompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a6/3/2005\u000a[report_end]
