VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP:\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia (see NOTE).\u000aFibroadenoma (0.6 cm), adjacent to the prior core needle biopsy site.\u000aIntraductal papilloma.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000aNOTE: No residual atypical hyperplasia is seen after complete microscopic\u000aexamination of the specimen, including margins. Case reviewed by\u000aDr. S. Lester.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast core biopsy with ADH bordering on DCIS.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast ADH vs DCIS\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast wire localization - mammo (short = superior,\u000along = lateral)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip in specimen. E.P. Frost,MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by REIMANN,JULIE DYLAN REGAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. right breast wire localization lumpectomy, short = superior, long =\u000alateral", and consists of a yellow/tan lumpectomy specimen (6.0 cm medial to\u000alateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior). A\u000awire protrudes from the lateral aspect of the specimen (marked by a long\u000asuture), and the specimen is accompanied by a specimen radiograph showing a\u000alocalization wire marking a clip. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior =\u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Serial sectioning\u000areveals a core biopsy site (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm). No discrete mass is\u000aidentified. The specimen is composed of approximately 40% fibrous tissue, the\u000arest is adipose tissue. A radiograph is taken by the pathologist and the clip\u000ais located. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 1: medial margin, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 2: medial and inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 3: medial and inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 4: medial and inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 5: medial, inferior and posterior margins, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 6: anterior and inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 7: superior, posterior and inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 8: superior, anterior margins, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 9: superior, posterior and inferior margins, 1 frag, (this\u000afragment contains the clip), ESS\u000aMicro 10: superior, posterior, and inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 11: inferior, posterior and superior margins, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 12: superior, anterior, and inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 13: posterior and inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 14: lateral and inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 15: lateral and inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS\u000aNOTE: (micros 5 through 10 contain core biopsy site)\u000ajdr\u000aReports to: GOLSHAN, MEHRA M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
