VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANNE GEORGIAN-SMITH M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Mariana A. Stoleru, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 6:00, STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA is present (see note).\u000aApocrine cysts, columnar cell change and microcysts with associated\u000acalcifications.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemistry for E-cadherin was performed. Although the foci\u000aapparent on H&E (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) are no longer present on the\u000aimmunostained level, an adjacent focus confirms absence of membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity. Slides also seen by Dr. Susan Lester, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 51 year old with amorphous calcs - right LIQ breast. Diff Dx: FCC -\u000aR/O DCIS.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: Calcifications on mammo.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: 6:00 o'clock.\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. Stereotactic.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast core biopsy in two blue cassettes - A/calcs and B/no calcs.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast 9:30", and consists of cores of fibroadipose tissue,\u000areceived in two blue cassettes, each with a blue lid, "A Ca++" (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) and "B" (2.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Right breast blue cassette, A cores, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Right breast blue cassette, B cores, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: 7965.\u000adb/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday\u000aFebruary 25, 2009 at 04:53:20PM\u000a[report_end]
