VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: David C. Park, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aApocrine metaplasia, cystic and columnar cell change.\u000aDuctal epithelial hyperplasia, and calcification in benign breast\u000aepithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, Breast Pathology, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 58 y/o female with h/o rt breast ADH; new left breast calcifications,\u000anot amenable to image-guided biopsy.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire-localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast abnormal mammogram, calcifications.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast wire-localized excisional biopsy; short suture - superior,\u000along suture - lateral --> mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Target calcifications, hook and wire are on the specimen\u000aradiograph. Called to Dr. Golshan. - Ayodale Odulate, MD.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "Left breast wire localized excisional biopsy" and consists of\u000aa left breast excision specimen (5.9 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to\u000aposterior, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior) with a short suture designating\u000asuperior, and a long suture lateral. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is\u000areceived with an accompanying radiograph demonstrating a localization wire\u000aentering the lateral aspect and multiple calcifications in the medial/inferior\u000aportion of the specimen. On cut section, specimen consists of approximately\u000a25% fibrous tissue and 75% lobulated adipose tissue. No discrete lesions or\u000amasses are identified. Representative sections, including the entirety of the\u000afibrous tissue, are submitted for histology.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular, 5 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central aspect of specimen, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicular, multi frags, ESS.\u000aDCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/20/2007\u000a[report_end]
