VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aRICHARDSON, ANDREA, L., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, 11 G STEREOTACTIC GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions with\u000aassociated ATYPIA and associated calcifications.\u000aNOTE: The atypia is best evaluated after excision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 50 year-old female with cluster of indeterminate calcifications\u000aleft upper outer quandrant.\u000aOperation: 11 G Stereotactic.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Rule out DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 11 g core samples left breast in pink cassettes.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by WITKIEWICZ,AGNIESKA K.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast", and consists of two (2) pink cassettes. One\u000acassette is labeled "A Ca++" and contains multiple, soft, fragmented, yellow\u000ato white tissue cores (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The other pink\u000acassette is labeled "B" and contains similar tissue fragments (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in aggregate).\u000aMicro 1: "A Ca++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000alm\u000aReports to: DURFEE, SARA, MANNARELLI M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
