VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1) SPECIMEN LABELED "MEDIAL LEFT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aMultiple foci of atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aExtensive columnar hyperplasia with atypia.\u000aCore biopsy site changes present.\u000aCalcifications in association with benign epithelium\u000aCysts.\u000a2) SPECIMEN LABELED "LATERAL LEFT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU in association with microcalcifications.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, multiple foci.\u000aExtensive columnar hyperplasia with atypia.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aCysts.\u000a3) SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT MEDIAL FINAL DEEP":\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia and florid hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar hyperplasia with atypia.\u000aNOTE: Case reviewed by Dr. A. Richardson, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Patient with history of ADH on core biopsy on outside. Core biopsy\u000areviewed at BWH.\u000aOperation: Wire localized lumpectomy REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: ADH REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1] medial left breast tissue (long/lateral, short/superior).\u000a#2] lateral left breast tissue (short/superior, long/lateral).\u000a#3] left medial final deep margin suture on new margin side.\u000aRadiology: #1 (medial)- clip and calcifications in specimen\u000a#2 (lateral)- clip and calcificaitons in specimen\u000aC. Denison, MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BROCK,JANE E.,M.B.,B.S.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, "#1 - left breast biopsy medial", consists of a breast lupectomy\u000aspecimen (5.3 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aanterior to posterior) with two sutures designating lateral and superior\u000amargins and a hook wire in place. A radiograph received with the specimen\u000ademonstrates a wire and a clip in the center with additional calcifications at\u000athe inferior and lateral edge of the specimen. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior =\u000ablue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aSectioning reveals a core biopsy sit (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an area of\u000asurrounding fat necrosis. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is grossly\u000aadipose tissue. The fibrous tissue surrounding the biopsy cavity extends to\u000a0.4 cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, 1 cm from the\u000alateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, the posterior margin, and is\u000a0.4 cm from the anterior margin. Ninety (90%) percent of all of the tissue and\u000aall of the fibrous tissue is submitted.\u000aMicro #1-3: Biopsy cavity in relation to medial, inferior, superior and\u000alateral margins, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #4+5: Fibrous tissue abutting posterior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #6+7: Fibrous tissue is relation to anterior margin, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aPart two, "#2 - left breast biopsy lateral", consists of breast lumpectomy\u000aspecimen (4.9 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aanterior to posterior), with two sutures designating short/superior,\u000along/lateral, and a hook wire in place. A radiograph received with the\u000aspecimen demonstrates a wire and a clip and calcifications. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black;\u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial =\u000aorange, and is serially sectioned to reveal a biopsy cavity (1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000awhich abuts the posterior margin is 1 cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to\u000asuperior, REMOVED_DATE cm to inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to lateral margin, and 2 cm to\u000amedial margin. The breast parenchyma is 90% adipose tissue. The remaining\u000afibrous tissue is firm, but without gross lesions. Ninety-eight (98%) percent\u000aof the specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro #8-11: Biopsy cavity including superior, anterior, posterior, and\u000ainferior margins, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #12: Posterior and superior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #13+14: Inferior margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #15: Medial margin, 2 fras, ESS.\u000aMicro #16: Lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart three, "#3 - left medial final deep, suture on new margin side", consists\u000aof a shave margin (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a single suture of a new margin.\u000aThe specimen is inked with the new margin in blue, and the remainder inked\u000ablack. Sectioning reveals the specimen to be firm fibrous tissue with focal\u000ahemorrhage. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro #17: Left medial final deep margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: GOLSHAN, MEHRA M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
