VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Patricia A. R. Brunker, M.D., D. Phil.\u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATION:\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aCalcifications in association with columnar cell change in cysts (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID;\u000alevels examined).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (present in only the original level of block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aApocrine metaplasia; columnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and\u000asecretions, epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester who concurs with this\u000ainterpretation.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: (L) breast abnormal mammogram, calcifications.\u000aOperation: (L) breast loc excisional bx.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Path pending.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA. Left breast wire localized excisional bx (to mammo) sutures: short - sup,\u000along - lateral\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aTarget calcifications and intact wire contained in specimen. S. Nielson\u000a5/17/06, 2:30 pm\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patients name, unit number,\u000aand "Left breast wire localized biopsy, short suture superior/long suture\u000alateral", and consists of an ovoid fragment of yellow/tan to tan/pink\u000afibroadipose tissue (2.9 M-L x REMOVED_DATE A-P x REMOVED_DATE S-I cm), which is oriented per\u000asurgeon with two sutures as indicated. The specimen was previously inked by\u000athe surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. There is one needle localization wire in place, which enters\u000athe inferior aspect of the specimen and exits the superoanterior aspect of the\u000aSpecimen. The specimen was previously radiographed and also a fat area of\u000acalcifications ????? by the ??????. The specimen is serially sectioned from\u000amedial to lateral to exhibit approximately 60% dense focally hemorrhagic\u000awhite/tan fibrous stroma and 40% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. No\u000adiscrete masses or lesions are identified. The needle localization wire\u000atraverses the dense fibrous stroma through the central specimen. The specimen\u000ais entirely sequentially submitted from medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: specimen sequentially submitted from medial to lateral with\u000aprobable calcifications in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aLMB/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/25/2006\u000a[report_end]
