VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM MASSACHUSETTS GENERAL HOSPITAL, BOSTON, MA:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 10:00, ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A SMALL\u000aSPICULATED MASS (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified\u000aBloom-Richardson grade II/III), measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size in this\u000alimited specimen.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aSpecial studies were performed at an outside institution with the\u000afollowing results (not reviewed):\u000aESTROGEN RECEPTOR - POSITIVE\u000aPROGESTERONE RECEPTOR - POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/NEU (IHC) - NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/NEU (FISH) - NOT AMPLIFIED\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION WITH ADDITIONAL MARGINS AND RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL\u000aLYMPH NODE BIOPSY (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified\u000aBloom-Richardson grade II/III), REMOVED_DATE cm by gross report (see note).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type (intermediate nuclear grade),\u000aassociated with necrosis and calcifications, is present in 4 of 10 slides\u000aas a minor component (EIC negative).\u000aThe invasive carcinoma is REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000alateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin and > REMOVED_DATE cm from superior\u000amargin.\u000aThe DCIS is < REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial and lateral margins.\u000aExcisions of final anterior, superior, lateral, medial, deep, and "final\u000aI" margins are negative for invasive and in situ carcinoma.\u000aOne sentinel node is negative for carcinoma examined by 1 H&E level. By\u000areport, keratin immunostains revealed rare (< 10) keratin positive cells\u000a(slides not sent for review).\u000aNOTE: The core needle biopsy site is in the center of the carcinoma and\u000athe gross size is likely an accurate post-biopsy size. However,\u000acorrelation with the radiologic size may be helpful to determine the best\u000asize for staging.\u000aThis carcinoma would be classified as AJCC (6th edition) REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb NO (sn) (i+)\u000aMX with reported single cells seen in a lymph node by\u000aimmunohistochemistry.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Consult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by YANG,TAO,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aReceived from Massachusetts General Hospital, Pathology Department, Boston, MA\u000aREMOVED_CASE_ID, are thirty-one (31) slides.\u000aOne (1) slide is labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "A", corresponding to a\u000aright breast, 10:00, core biopsy (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), according to\u000athe accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aThirty (30) slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "A" through "DD",\u000acorresponding to A-J) right breast lumpectomy (4.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) K-N) right\u000aaxillary sentinel lymph node excision (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) O-R) right breast,\u000afinal anterior, excision (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm, and 2 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate) S-U)\u000aright breast, final superior, excision (two fragments: REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and\u000a2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) V) right breast, final lateral, excision (2.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) W-X) right breast, final medial shaved margin, excision (2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aY-Z) right breast, final deep shaved margin, excision (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm) AA-DD)\u000aright breast, final I, excision (5 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aaccording to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aReports to: BURSTEIN, HAROLD, JOHN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000a[report_end]
