ially sectioned\u000ato reveal an 80% yellow lobulated fatty to 20% white fibrous tissue, in which\u000adefinitive abnormalities are not grossly appreciated. Representative sections\u000aare submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Left breast tissue, to include overlying skin, 2 frags in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Left breast, fibrous tissue, 12 frags, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "Left breast upper skin", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aaggregate of tan irregular soft tissue fragents, which are entirely submitted\u000ato research.\u000aPart three, labeled "Left breast lower skin", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aaggregate of tan irregular soft tissues, which are entirely submitted for\u000aresearch.\u000aPart four, labeled "Right breast tissue", consists of 1294 g, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm aggregate of fibrofatty breast tissue fragments, some of which are partially\u000asurfaced by a tan unremarkable skin. The specimen is sectioned to reveal a 95%\u000ayellow lobulated fatty to 5% dense white fibrous tissue, in which\u000arepresentative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Right breast tissue, to include overlying skin, 2 frags in each,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Right breaSt, fibrous tissue, FRAGS, RSS.\u000aPart five, labeled "Right breast upper skin", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aaggregate of tan irregular unremarkable skin fragments, which are entirely\u000asubmitted for research.\u000aPart six, labeled "Right breast lower skin", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aaggregate of tan/white irregular unremarkable skin fragments, which are\u000aentirely submitted for research.\u000alm\u000aReports to: HERGRUETER, CHARLES, A. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: TISSUE FOR RESEARCH ONLY (NO CHARGE)\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: TISSUE FOR 