VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kevin Golden, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA/1). LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (slides REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aOther findings: flat atypia, columnar cell change with calcifications,\u000asclerosing adenosis, usual ductal hyperplasia, apocrine cyst, core\u000abiopsy site.\u000aImmunohistochemical staining for e-cadherin is negative in the areas of\u000alobular carcinoma in situ.\u000aNo invasive carcinoma is identified upon complete histological\u000aexamination of the specimen. Levels examined.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: H/O atypia on core, L upper inner quadrant.\u000aOperation: L breast wide local excision with wire localization.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast atypia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast tissue with wire, to mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip and wire are seen within the specimen - Dr. Gombos.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Left breast tissue with wire", and consists of an ovoid breast\u000aexcision specimen (3.6 M-L x REMOVED_DATE A-P x REMOVED_DATE S-I cm). The specimen is inked by\u000athe surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. There is one needle localization wire, which enters the\u000aanteromedial aspect of the specimen with no clear exit point. The specimen was\u000apreviously radiographed, confirming the presence of a clip and an intact needle\u000alocalization wire within the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned from\u000amedial to lateral. In the medial aspect of the specimen, adjacent to the tip\u000aof the needle localization wire, there is a well delineated pink firm solid\u000amass (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) within which a small metal clip is identified. The\u000amass is REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainferior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. A REMOVED_DATE cm lateral to the\u000aaforementioned mass, in the lateral aspect of the specimen is a smooth-walled\u000amultiloculated cyst (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000alateral margin. The remainder of the specimen is composed of approximately 45%\u000adense white/pink fibrostroma and 55% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. The\u000aspecimen is entirely sequentially submitted from medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central specimen from medial to lateral with mass/clip/wire tip\u000asite in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin to include multiloculated cyst (also in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID),\u000amulti frags in each, ESS.\u000aLM/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/2/2007\u000a[report_end]
