VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION WITH WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (see NOTE).\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aCalcifications are present associated with columnar cell changes.\u000aNo invasive or in situ carcinoma present, including margins.\u000aNOTE: Case reviewed by Dr. S. Lester who concurs.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, POSTERIOR SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aBenign breast tissue with biopsy site changes.\u000aNo invasive or in situ carcinoma present, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: ADH of right breast.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized wide excisional biopsy\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Tissue from right breast (stitch marking short stitch\u000asuperior, long stitch lateral)\u000a#2) Posterior shave margin right margin (stitch marking short stitch superior,\u000along stitch lateral)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Ca++ are in specimen. Dr. D.N. Smith\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KATZ,SAMUEL G,M.D.,PH.D.,M.S.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. right breast tissue, stitch marking short = superior,\u000along = lateral", is accompanied by a radiograph showing a wire localizing\u000acalcifications within the specimen. This part is one fragment of soft\u000afibroadipose tissue (6.5 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, and\u000a1.8 cm anterior to posterior). The specimen comes previously inked by the\u000asurgeon and is oriented by the surgeon within the prosecting room as follows:\u000ared = superior, green = inferior, yellow = lateral, orange = medial, blue =\u000aposterior, and black = anterior. (per the surgeon, the locations of blue and\u000ablack inks were reveres from the standard protocol). The wire is removed and\u000athe specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a diffusely\u000aintermixed white fibrous tissue (20-30% of specimen) with yellow adipose\u000atissue. No discrete masses or lesions are present. There is one focus of\u000ahemorrhage (0.7 cm in greatest dimension), possibly corresponding to the prior\u000abiopsy site. One hundred per cent (100%) of the fibrous tissue is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue from medial to lateral, excluding medial\u000aand lateral tips, 1 frag each, ESS\u000aMicro 12 & 17: medial perpendicular tip, 3 frags/cass, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE  lateral perpendicular tip, 12 frags, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. posterior shave margin, right breast with stitch\u000amargins, short stitch = superior, long stitch = lateral", consists of one\u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue (3.4 cm medial to lateral, 2 cm superior to\u000ainferior and REMOVED_DATE cm posterior to anterior). The specimen comes with the\u000aposterior surface inked black by the surgeon and a long suture marking the\u000alateral side. The remaining sides are inked by the pathologist per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The short stitch\u000adesignating the superior surface arises at the junction between the superior\u000aand anterior surfaces. Per conversation with the surgeon in the prosecting\u000aroom, the only margin of interest is the posterior margin. The specimen was\u000aserially sectioned to reveal primarily fibroadipose tissue (<10% fibrous\u000atissue) with no lesions present. One hundred per cent (100%) of the fibrous\u000atissue is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posterior shave margin, 1 frag each, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral posterior shave margin, 7 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posterior shave margin from lateral to medial, 1 frag each, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial posterior shave margin, 4 frags each, ESS\u000asak\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
