aced per surgeon to designate the superior position and a long\u000astitch placed per surgeon to designate the lateral position. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe cut surface reveals an 80% fibrous parenchyma with a dense focus of fat\u000anecrosis consistent with prior excision site (located REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainferior margin). The specimen is entirely submitted for microscopic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin perpendicularly sectioned, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Section with prior excision site including medial, lateral, anterior\u000aand posterior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Successive sections, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 5 frags, perpendicularly sectioned, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Left medial shave margin, whipstitch new margin", consists\u000aof one yellow/tan fragment of fibroadipose tissue (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There\u000ais suture placed per surgeon to designate the new margin. The corresponding\u000asurface is inked black. The old margin is inked red. The sectioned surface is\u000apredominantly fibrous in composition. The specimen is entirely submitted for\u000amicroscopic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: New left medial shave margin, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aSWY/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 06, 2009 at 02:40:40PM\u000a[report_end]
