VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Stefan Kraft, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR\u000aARCHITECTURAL DISTORTION":\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, involving a radial sclerosing lesion (1.3 cm), with\u000acysts, apocrine metaplasia, sclerosing adenosis, columnar\u000ahyperplasia, florid ductal hyperplasia, and stromal calcifications.\u000aDouble immunostains (p63, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) were performed and support the above\u000adiagnosis.\u000aThere is no invasive carcinoma seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "INFERIOR BREAST, INFERIOR SHAVE MARGIN":\u000aBreast tissue with cysts, apocrine metaplasia, and epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe case was reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, Breast Pathology Service, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Area of architectural distortion, right breast.\u000aOperation: Loc/excision.\u000aOperative Findings: See op note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue, primary area of concern (mammo).\u000aB/2. Inferior shaved margin right breast tissue.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aArchitectural distortion is in specimen. E.P. Frost, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast tissue primary area of concern", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x\u000a3.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm excision of fibroadipose tissue, oriented by sutures designating\u000asuperior (short suture) and lateral (long suture) margins. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange\u000a(inked by surgeon). A localizing wire enters superolaterally and exits\u000ainferomedially. Specimen is received along with an accompanying radiograph\u000ashowing the localizing wire in place within an ill-defined area of\u000a"architectural distortion", which appears to involve the medial half of the\u000aspecimen. Sectioning demonstrates an ill-defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm area of\u000adiffusely cystic fibrous tissue, with a REMOVED_DATE cm focus of tan/yellow\u000acalcification. This ill-defined lesion extends to all margins, with exception\u000aof the lateral margin, which is greater than REMOVED_DATE cm from the area of interest.\u000aThere are no additional abnormalities. Specimen is sectioned and entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sequentially from medial to lateral, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aPlease note: Perpendicular medial margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, perpendicular lateral margin in\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, lesion in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (calcified area in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aPart B, "#2. Inferior shaved margin right breast tissue", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x\u000a2.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue with an undesignated suture on one\u000abroad surface. The opposing surface has been inked in green by the surgeon.\u000aThe sutured surface is inked blue by prosector and the specimen is sectioned\u000aand entirely submitted. Cut surfaces are grossly unremarkable, with a small\u000aamount of fibrous tissue along the blue-inked surface, but no masses, lesions\u000aor other abnormalities. Separately received in the specimen container is an\u000aunoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of hemorrhagic fibroadipose tissue,\u000aembedded in toto with the remainder of the specimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 5 frags total (hemorrhagic fragment in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), ESS.\u000adb/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/4/2007\u000a[report_end]
