sectioned from lateral to medial. In the central\u000aspecimen, there is a well-delineated pink/tan nodular lesion (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) which grossly extends to the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior/deep margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. A\u000asmall amount of clip is identified within the mass.\u000aThe remainder of the cut surface is composed of approximately 15% delicate\u000awhite/tan fibrous tissue and 85% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. No\u000aadditional discrete lesions are identified. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central specimen to include mass with superior, anterior, and\u000aposterior/deep margin sequentially submitted from lateral to medial, 1 frag in\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior and additional deep margin closest to mass, 1 frag in\u000aeach, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicular sections, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of the specimen, mult frags, ESS\u000aLMB/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/30/2008\u000a[report_end]
