VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Marianna B Ruzinova, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY":\u000aBenign breast tissue with biopsy changes and\u000acalcifications.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aB. SUPERIOR MARGIN, STITCH NEW MARGIN":\u000aBenign breast tissue with no significant pathologic change.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy (no atypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aidentified, specimen entirely submitted.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left ADH on core biopsy for Ca++.\u000aOperation: Left needle-localized breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: 2nd clip visualized and removed from superior margin.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/#1. Left breast excisional biopsy - to mammo.\u000aShort - superior, long - lateral.\u000aB/#2. Superior margin stitch on new margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: One clip and calcs seen. - Babagbemi\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname and unit number.\u000aThe specimen is accompanied by radiograph, labeled with patient's name and date\u000aof birth, demonstrating the specimen with the mass and clip and localizing\u000awire.\u000aPart A, sublabeled "1. Left breast excisional biopsy", consists of one fragment\u000aof fibroadipose tissue with the short suture, placed by the surgeon, to\u000aindicate superior aspect and long suture, placed by the surgeon, to indicate\u000alateral aspect, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with localizing wire entering the\u000alateral to medial aspect. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: Posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned to reveal white, multinodular mass, located REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial\u000amargin and measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, including soft and necrotic spots.\u000aThe specimen is radiographed to locate a clip, which is found in Slide 2 of the\u000aspecimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen sectioned from medial to lateral aspect with mass\u000ain REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID with clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, sublabeled "2. Superior margin, stitch on new margin", consists of one\u000a(1) fragment of fibroadipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with a stitch\u000aplaced to indicate the new margin. The new margin is inked black, and the old\u000amargin is inked blue, and the specimen is serially sectioned and entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: New margin, 6 frag, ESS.\u000aMRU/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Marianna B Ruzinova M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/17/2005\u000a[report_end]
