VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kremena V. Star, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED LUMPECTOMY FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia demonstrated by e-cadherin stain\u000a(block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aCalcifications in benign breast epithelium.\u000aFibroadenomatoid and cystic changes.\u000aMargins inked and evaluated.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. Amy Ly, Breast Pathology Service, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Microcalcs, Rt breast.\u000aOperation: Wire-directed excision.\u000aOperative Findings: See op note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Microcalcs, Rt breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Rt breast tissue with short stitch - superior, long - lateral (mammo)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "right breast tissue short stitch superior long stitch lateral", consists\u000aof an irregular fragment of fibroadipose tissue (6.0 cm S-I x REMOVED_DATE cm M-L x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm A-P) with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating\u000alateral per surgeon. Running from superior to inferior is a defect/? previous\u000asurgical incision (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm), coming REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior aspect. The\u000aspecimen is inked around this defect. There is a needle localization wire\u000aentering the superior aspect of the specimen, exiting through the inferior\u000aaspect of the specimen. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from superior to inferior to exhibit 95% yellow lobulated\u000aadipose tissue and 5% fibrous tissue. The fibrous tissue abuts the inferior\u000aaspect of the specimen and exhibits hemorrhage (consistent with needle\u000alocalization wire placement). No masses or lesions are grossly appreciated.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Body, sequentially submitted from superior to inferior, multi\u000afrags total, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular inferior margin to include area designated by\u000aneedle localization wire, 2 frags in each, ESS.\u000aJenC/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 21, 2009 at 05:28:10PM\u000a[report_end]
