VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Patricia A. R. Brunker, M.D., D. Phil.\u000aPathologist: Vania Nose, MD, PhD\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED ?LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED? EXCISION:\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia, sclerosing adenosis, intraductal\u000apapilloma, columnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts\u000aand secretions, core biopsy site, and apocrine metaplasia. See\u000aNOTE.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aNOTE: The previous biopsy (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) was reviewed in conjunction with\u000athis case. Similar histologic changes are not seen in the current specimen,\u000awhich has been entirely submitted for histologic evaluation. The clip site was\u000aidentified in multiple levels. Levels examined. This case was seen by Dr. D.\u000aDillon (Breast Pathology Service) who agrees.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 46 year old woman, S/P REMOVED_DATE  (BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) left breast stereotactic\u000acore biopsy for mammographic calcifications, revealing severely atypical ductal\u000ahyperplasia bordering on low-grade DCIS.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire-directed excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left abnormal mammogram, ADH.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1 - left wire localized biopsy (to mammo), short/superior, long/lateral,\u000awhip stitch at deep margin.\u000aRADIOGRAPHY REPORT: Wire and clip.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient?s name,\u000aunit number, and "#1 - left wire localized biopsy, short/superior,\u000along/lateral, whip stitch at deep margin (#34 REMOVED_DATE  left wire local whip at\u000adeep margin)", and consists of one fragment of white/yellow fibroadipose tissue\u000a(3.9 cm s-i, REMOVED_DATE cm m-l, and REMOVED_DATE cm a-p), consistent with a partial mastectomy\u000aspecimen. The specimen is received inked by the surgeon according to the\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThere are three sutures in the specimen placed by the surgeon, long designating\u000alateral, short in the superior, and a whip stitch at the black (deep and\u000aposterior) margin. There is a needle localization wire entering the specimen\u000ais the anterior aspect, with no exit site identified. The specimen is received\u000awith a radiograph, bearing the patient's name and medical record number, and\u000ademonstrating a soft tissue mass, approximate in the specimen, with a needle\u000alocalization wire, and a clip, which is encircled by the radiologist. No\u000adiscrete radiodense mass is identified. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000afrom superior to inferior, demonstrating firm, fibrous and focally cystic and\u000ahemorrhagic soft tissue, without a discretely identifiable mass. This firm\u000asoft tissue extends to all margins. The specimen is entirely, serially\u000asubmitted from superior to inferior, with the wire between the slices from\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: serially submitted from superior to inferior, with the wire\u000abetween the slices from REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, multiple frags,\u000aESS.\u000aPAB/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Patricia A. R. Brunker M.D., D. Phil., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
