VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Elizabeth Amy Morgan, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, UPPER INNER QUADRANT, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY:\u000aFocal atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aFocal atypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aApocrine metaplasia and apocrine cysts.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign breast epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aB. RIGHT BREAST, UPPER OUTER QUADRANT, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A\u000aMASS:\u000aFibroadenoma (1.2 cm).\u000aDuctal hyperplasia and apocrine cysts.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Not provided\u000aOperation: Rt breast wire biopsy x 2\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Rt breast mass, UOQ; Rt breast atypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Rt UIQ wire\u000aB/2. Rt UOQ wire with visible mass\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000a#1 Rt Upper Inner Quadrant Wire for ADH:\u000aWire and clip contained in specimen. Some ca++ contained in specimen.\u000a[signature illegible]\u000a#2 Rt UOQ Wire with Visible Mass - Short/superior, Long/lateral:\u000aWire and nodule in specimen.\u000aSR\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "RT upper inner quad wire for ADH", consists of a breast\u000awire-localization specimen (5.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an intact hook wire\u000a(entering at the superomedial aspect and exiting at the inferoposterior\u000aaspect). The specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange. The specimen is accompanied by\u000aa radiograph exhibiting an intact hook wire, clip, and focus of probable\u000acalcification. The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior.\u000aThere is a hemorrhagic probable biopsy site (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), containing a\u000atan/brown gelatinous substance and silver clip, which is REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000asuperior margin and grossly corresponds to the radiograph. The remaining\u000abreast tissue is composed of approximately 90% white/tan, dense, focally cystic\u000a(cyst measuring up to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension) fibrous stroma and 10%\u000ayellow lobulated adipose tissue. No other gross lesions are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue sequentially from superior to inferior, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy site/area of clip.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Probable calcifications (corresponding to accompanying\u000aradiograph).\u000aPart B, "RT UOQ wire with visible mass - short stitch sup, long lateral",\u000aconsists of a breast needle-localization wire specimen (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000awith an intact hook wire (entering at the superior aspect and exiting at the\u000amedial aspect) and two orienting sutures (short suture=superior; long\u000asuture=lateral). The specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange. The specimen is accompanied by\u000aa radiograph exhibiting an intact hook wire and a density consistent with a\u000amass. The tissue is serially sectioned from medial to lateral exhibiting a\u000awhite/tan, firm, encapsulated nodule (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that grossly extends\u000ato the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior\u000aand inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral and medial margins. The remaining\u000abreast tissue is composed approximately 75% tan/white dense stroma and 25%\u000ayellow lobulated adipose tissue. No additional gross lesions are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue sequentially from medial to lateral, multi frags,\u000aESS.\u000aNote: Nodule in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adl\u005cpab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/4/2008\u000a[report_end]
