VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: J. GREGORY KANE M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kristin S. Ricci, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Lynette M Sholl, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST MASS AT 3 O'CLOCK:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000aFibroadenomatous change.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aPrior biopsy site.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy in the specimen, including margins.\u000aB. LEFT BREAST MASS AT 12 O'CLOCK:\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aFibroadenomatous change.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aPrior biopsy site.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy in the specimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 45 year old REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID with enlarging fibroadenoma/fibrocystic change\u000ameasuring 36 x 13 x 36 mm, adjacent medial superior biopsy ADH focus. BWH\u000areview of slides showed epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: Left lumpectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Fibroadenoma, ADH.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast mass at 3 o'clock.\u000aB/2. Left breast mass at 12 o'clock.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000a1) Left Breast mass at 3 O'clock to mammo @ 1653\u000aCalled to OR HP, hookwire. Clip, density.\u000a2) Left Breast mass at 12 O'clock to mammo @ 1653\u000aCalled to OR HP 5:00 hookwire, clip, density.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "left breast mass at 3 o'clock", consists of an unoriented\u000apink/tan to tan/white dense white fibrous soft tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with\u000aa single needle localization wire in place. Received in the specimen container\u000ais an additional portion of needle localization wire. An accompanying specimen\u000aradiograph demonstrates two localizing wires entering the specimen and a\u000acentrally located surgical clip. The specimen is received with no identifying\u000amarkers and is inked black by the prosector. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned along the long axis of the specimen. The cut surface is pink/tan to\u000atan/white and homogeneous, consisting of dense white fibrous tissue. There is\u000aan irregular punctate cystic area (0.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), within which is a\u000asilver metallic surgical biopsy clip, adjacent to the needle localization wire.\u000aThe specimen is submitted in its entirety. The cyst comes within REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe nearest inked margin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, Block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID includes surgical clip.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "left breast at 12 o'clock", consists of three pink/tan to\u000atan/white unoriented dense white fibrous fragments of soft tissue with a scant\u000aamount of attached tan/yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue (3.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ain aggregate). An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates the tissue\u000aaggregate with a two associated localizing wires and a wire clip. Received\u000aseparately in the specimen container are two needle localization wire\u000afragments. Each unoriented fragment of soft tissue is inked black and is\u000aserially sectioned. The cut surface consists primarily of dense white fibrous\u000atissue, which constitutes approximately greater than 95% of the specimen. The\u000aremainder of the breast parenchyma is tan/yellow and homogeneous. Within the\u000alarger fibrous fragment of soft tissue is a clear tan/yellow serous filled\u000acystic structure (0.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), consistent with a previous biopsy\u000acavity, within which a silver metallic surgical biopsy clip is found. The\u000aspecimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Smaller fragment of soft tissue serially sectioned.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medium-sized fragment of soft tissue, serially sectioned, 3 frags\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Largest fragment of soft tissue serially sectioned, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include\u000aarea of cyst and clip, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000asek/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lynette M Sholl M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 03, 2009 at 02:05:12PM\u000a[report_end]
