VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Stefan Kraft, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-GUIDED EXCISION FOR A MASS AND A CLIP":\u000aAtypical Ductal Hyperplasia, single focus (<0.1cm, (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID),\u000aassociated with calcification.\u000aPeriductal fibrosis with a small focus of squamous metaplasia with\u000aatypia, consistent with reactive atypia (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID); the focus is present\u000aonly on the original slide and disappears on level sections.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aFocal fibrosis suggestive of a collapsed cyst (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aCalcifications associated with vessels.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 69 year old woman, S/P R breast LIQ core bx on REMOVED_DATE  revealing\u000aatypical papillary proliferation with associated calcifications best evaluated\u000aby excision.\u000aOperation: R breast WL bx.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right breast tissue - short/superior, long/lateral, whipstitch on deep\u000amargin.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aIntact wire, clip and density (prior biopsy location) are in the specimen. D/W\u000aDr. Rhei. P. Burns, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue, short superior, long lateral, whipstitch on deep\u000amargin", and consists of an ovoid yellow/tan breast excision specimen (5.6 A-P\u000ax REMOVED_DATE M-L x REMOVED_DATE S-I cm) oriented per surgeon as follows: Short equals\u000asuperior, long equals lateral, whipstitch equals deep margin. The specimen is\u000ainked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. There are two needle-localization wires in place, arbitrarily\u000adesignated as wire #1 and wire #2 per prosector. Wire #1 is more\u000asuperior/medial entering the anterior aspect of the specimen and exiting the\u000aposteromedial aspect of the specimen. Wire #2 is slightly more inferior,\u000aentering the anteroinferior aspect of the specimen and exiting the medial\u000ainferior aspect of the specimen. The specimen was previously radiographed,\u000aconfirming the presence of two intact wires, a clip, and a corresponding\u000adensity within the specimen (density/clip corresponding to wire designated as\u000awire #1 per prosector). The specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to\u000aposterior. In the posteroinferior aspect of the specimen, there is a poorly\u000adelineated dense tan/brown fibrous lesion (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) less than REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the posteroinferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial\u000amargin. The distal aspect of wire #1 traverses the aforementioned lesion, with\u000awire #2 traversing the parenchyma just posteromedial. A small metal clip is\u000aidentified within the fibrous lesion associated with wire #1. The remainder of\u000athe cut surface is composed of approximately 15% grossly unremarkable white/tan\u000afibrous stroma and 85% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue with no additional\u000adiscrete lesions identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep/posterior margin with fibrous lesion (in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), perpendicularly\u000asectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of fibrous lesion associated with wire #1 (clip site in\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) with inferior, deep/posterior, in medial margins, 3 frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin closest to fibrous lesion, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin closest to fibrous lesion, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Focally dense fibrous stroma, central aspect of the specimen (more\u000aanterior to lesion) with medial and inferior margins, traversed by wire #2, 3\u000afrags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of specimen, multi frags, ESS.\u000alm/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
