VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DAVID I SOYBEL M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Derek K Marsee, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Michelle S Hirsch, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST MASS":\u000aBreast tissue with focal atypical ductal hyperplasia, epithelial\u000ahyperplasia, and microcalcifications associated with benign\u000aepithelium.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Breast lump.\u000aOperation: Wire localized right breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Breast lump.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1 - right breast mass, suture marks long/lateral, short/superior (to mammo @\u000a1150).\u000aRADIOGRAPHY REPORT: Ca++ in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "right breast mass, long/lateral, short/superior", and consists of a breast\u000aexcision specimen (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a skin ellipse (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm), a\u000alocalization wire going through the skin ellipse, and two orienting sutures\u000a(long/lateral, short/superior). The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. An accompanying specimen\u000aradiograph demonstrates the localization wire adjacent to a tight cluster of\u000acalcifications. X-rays, performed in the Department of Pathology, revealed\u000acalcifications are localized to slice four, with possible calcifications in\u000aslices five and six. The specimen is entirely submitted for microscopic\u000aevaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: right breast mass (calcs in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aDM/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Derek K Marsee M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Review by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/1/2005\u000a[report_end]
