o exit the inferior/medial aspect. There is a\u000asingle fibrous/white firm mass at the medial aspect of the specimen (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm), which is located; REMOVED_DATE cm from superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom medial, greater than REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom posterior margins. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A specimen radiograph is\u000areceived with the specimen, which demonstrates the presence of a mass with a\u000awire transversing. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted\u000afor histology.\u000aNote: Although the radiologist interpretation states that there is a clip in\u000athe specimen, no clip is identified in the gross specimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, medial to lateral including mass in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aARL/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/12/2008\u000a[report_end]
