VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MARCELO MONTORZI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Rachel L Rucker-Schmidt, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER INNER, 1:30, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES\u000aFOR A MSS:\u000aFibroepithelial lesion with moderate hypercellularity, stromal overgrowth and\u000afocal stromal infiltration into adipose tissue, (See Note).\u000aMitoses number up to 3 per 10 high power fields.\u000aNOTE: Differential diagnosis includes low grade phyllodes tumor and cellular\u000afibroadenoma. Complete excision is recommended.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER INNER, 2:00, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES\u000aFOR A MASS:\u000aFibroepithelial lesion with modest hypercellularity, stromal overgrowth and\u000arare stromal mitoses (See Note).\u000aNOTE: Differential diagnosis includes low grade phyllodes tumor and cellular\u000afibroadenoma. Complete excision is recommended.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 42 y/o with h/o fibroadenomata with 2 masses in Right UIQ, each with\u000afeatures that makes masses minimally suspicious; bx x 2 (2:00 and 1:30).\u000aOperation: 14 G Ultrasound x 2.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: FS, R/O other.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast 1:30, REMOVED_DATE cores (small mass) --> in pink cassette.\u000aB/2) Right breast 2:00, 5 cores (larger mass) --> in blue cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart A, "Right breast 1:30", consists of a tan/pink cassette containing\u000amultiple tan/pink to tan/yellow fibrofatty cores of breast tissue (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.2 cm), which are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassettes of pink cassette, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "2 o'clock right breast", consists of a blue cassette, containing\u000amultiple tan/pink to tan/white fibrofatty cores of breast tissue (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.2 cm), which are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of blue cassette, multi frags, ESS.\u000aDRD/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/18/2007\u000a[report_end]
