VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Stacey A. Simons, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 1:30, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, with a micropapillary pattern, is present in two\u000ablocks (blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; levels examined) (see note). These areas are < REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the posterior margin.\u000aFibroadenoma (0.7 cm) associated with core needle biopsy site changes.\u000aNote: The areas of ADH approach a diagnosis of DCIS. If there is more breast\u000atissue at the posterior margin, re-excision may be helpful to determine if\u000athere are adjacent areas of DCIS.\u000aFeatures suggestive of a phyllodes tumor were seen in a prior core needle\u000abiopsy (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). These features are not seen in the excision and the mass\u000ais best classified as a fibroadenoma.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 2:00, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aFibroadenoma (0.7 cm) associated with core needle biopsy site changes.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia associated with columnar cell changes.\u000aNote: Features suggestive of a phyllodes tumor were seen in a prior core\u000aneedle biopsy (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). These features are not seen in the excision and the\u000amass is best classified as a fibroadenoma.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 42 year old female with right breast fibroepithelial lesion x 2, s/p\u000aimage guided core biopsy.\u000aOperation: None given.\u000aOperative Findings: Right breast fibroepithelial lesion x 2.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA. Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy 1:30 wire, short stitch\u000asuperior, long stitch lateral - mammo.\u000aB. Right breast wire localized excision biopsy 2:00 wire, short stitch\u000asuperior, long stitch lateral - mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Specimens #1 and 2: Wires and masses in both. OR called. Dr.\u000aSughra Raza\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. R breast, wire loc ex biopsy 1:30 wire", consists of an ovoid\u000afragment of yellow/tan to pink/tan fibroadipose tissue (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000awhich is oriented per surgeon with two sutures: short stitch superior, long\u000astitch lateral. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is one needle\u000alocalization wire in place, which enters the posteromedial aspect of the\u000aspecimen and exits the inferoposterior aspect of the specimen. The specimen\u000aradiograph shows a circumscribed mass associated with a clip and the\u000alocalization wire. The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial.\u000aIn the medial aspect of the specimen, there is a well-circumscribed white/tan\u000anodular lesion (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000aposterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin,\u000a0.9 cm of the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000alateral margin. The needle localization wire traverses the parenchyma adjacent\u000ato the nodular mass. The remainder of the cut surface is composed of\u000aapproximately 40% dense white/pink fibrous stroma and 60% yellow/tan lobulated\u000aadipose tissue with no additional discrete lesions identified. The specimen is\u000aentirely sequentially submitted from medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central specimen to include mass (in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags total, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. R breast wire loc excisional biopsy, 2 o'clock wire" consists of\u000aan ovoid fragment of yellow/tan to pink/tan fibroadipose tissue (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a2.6 cm), which is oriented per surgeon with two sutures: short suture equals\u000asuperior, long suture equals lateral. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen\u000aradiograph shows a circumscribed mass with a clip and the localization wire.\u000aThe wire enters the anteroinferior aspect of the specimen with no clear exit\u000apoint. The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to exhibit a\u000awell-circumscribed tan/white lobulated mass (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral\u000amargin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. The needle localization wire\u000atraverses the mass. A small metal clip is embedded within the mass as\u000aconsistent with the prior core biopsy procedure. The remainder of the cut\u000asurface is composed of approximately 40% dense white tan fibrous tissue and 60%\u000ayellow/tan adipose tissue with no additional discrete lesions identified. The\u000aentire specimen is examined microscopically.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin with mass, perpendicularly sectioned, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central specimen to include mass (clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag in each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of specimen, mult frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000almc/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a6/21/2007\u000a[report_end]
