ifications in the specimen. The specimen is\u000asectioned into eight slices, from inferior to superior, and it consists of\u000aapproximately 90% fibrous tissue and 10% adipose tissue. There is a collection\u000aof gel-foam beads (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) in slices five and six, which grossly\u000aabuts the anterior margin, and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice one, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice two, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice three, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice four, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice five with gel-beads, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice six with gel-beads, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice seven, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice eight, 8 frags, ESS.\u000aAF/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a6/13/2006\u000a[report_end]
