VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, mastectomy with regional lymph nodes\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Stefan Kraft, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Robert D Odze, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY":\u000aBreast tissue with calcifications in benign epithelium and\u000acolumnar cell changes.\u000aFive lymph nodes negative for tumor (0:5).\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY":\u000aBreast tissue with scar, granulation tissue reaction, foreign\u000abody giant cell reaction, and atypical lobular hyperplasia\u000awith pagetoid spread and atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aNo residual carcinoma is seen.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Bilateral simple mastectomy, right sentinel lymph node biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast, suture marking short/superior, long/lateral on axillary\u000atail.\u000aB/2. Left breast, suture marking short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast suture marking, short stitch superior, long stitch\u000alateral, and axillary tail", consists of an 845-gram mastectomy specimen (20.0\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). which is oriented for surgery with two stitches (short =\u000asuperior and long = lateral on axillary tail). There is an adherent hyperemic\u000atan/ovoid skin (14.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with the essential tan/wrinkled areola (3.0 x\u000a2.5 cm) in a slightly depressed tan/pink nipple (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE cm). No scars are\u000aidentified on the epithelial surface. There are two areas of blue/green\u000asentinel node dye discoloration (0.6 cm and REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension)\u000asurrounding the areola. The deep margin is inked black with a smooth fascial\u000aplane. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to exhibit\u000aapproximately 30% focally dense white/tan fibrous tissue and 70% yellow/tan\u000alobulated adipose tissue. No discrete masses or lesions are identified. There\u000aare multiple areas of blue/green dye discoloration that is consistent with\u000aprior sentinel node procedure.\u000aA small axillary tail (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is present at the lateral aspect of\u000athe specimen, containing seven pink/tan rubbery lymph node candidates(ranging\u000afrom REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension). The largest axillary lymph node\u000acandidate is discolored blue/green.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple/areola, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue, upper/outer quadrant to include 12 o'clock area, 3\u000afrags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue, upper/inner quadrant to include 12 o'clock area, 3\u000afrags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue, lower/outer quadrant, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue, lower/inner quadrant to include 5 o'clock area, 3\u000afrags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin, central breast, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Largest lymph node candidate, blue/green dye, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Three lymph node candidates, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Three lymph node candidates, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left breast, stitch marking, short stitch/superior, long\u000astitch/lateral", consists of a 640-gram simple mastectomy specimen (23.0 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm), which is oriented for surgery with two stitches as follows: short\u000astitch/superior and long stitch/lateral. There is an adherent tan/white\u000ahyperemic skin (15.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a central tan/wrinkled areola (3.7 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) and a pink/tan everted nipple (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a well-healed\u000acurvilinear scar (4.5 cm in length) along the superior/lateral areola. The\u000adeep margin (inked black) predominantly includes a fascial plane with a\u000afibrotic retracted area (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with associated strands of skeletal\u000amuscle. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral.\u000aCorresponding to the aforementioned retracted area in the deep margin there is\u000aa pink/tan fibrous area (grossly consistent with biopsy cavity, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) with associated areas of hemorrhage and gritty yellow/tan probable fat\u000anecrosis (ranging from REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension). The cavity is\u000asurrounded by dense/nodular pink/tan fibrous tissue, anteriorly.\u000aThe remainder of the specimen is composed of approximately 25% focally dense\u000atan/pink fibrous tissue and 75% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue with no\u000aadditional lesions identified.\u000aAn axillary tail is not present. The most lateral breast tissue is examined\u000afor intramammary lymph nodes, but none are grossly identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple/areola with scar, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower/outer quadrant fibrous area/cavity with deep margin,\u000asequentially submitted from lateral to medial, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower/outer quadrant, additional fibrous area/cavity with adjacent\u000aanterior dense fibrous tissue, 2 frags in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue, upper/outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue, upper/inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue, lower/outer quadrant away from fibrous area, 2\u000afrags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue, lower/inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000almb/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aADDENDUM:\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY":\u000aAdditional fibrotic areas were examined (Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aThey show benign breast tissue with foreign body giant cell reaction.\u000aAddendum #1 by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
