VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JEFFREY E KATZ M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Jane E Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, 3:00, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A\u000aCIRCUMSCRIBED/LOBULATED 1 CM MASS (A):\u000aFragments of a fibroadenoma.\u000aLEFT BREAST, 12:00, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A\u000aCIRCUMSCRIBED/LOBULATED REMOVED_DATE CM MASS (B):\u000aFibroadenomatoid changes (see note).\u000aNOTE: Radiologic/pathologic correlation is suggested to be certain the biopsy\u000ais representative of the radiologic area of interest.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, PERIAREOLAR, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A\u000aCIRCUMSCRIBED/LOBULATED PALPABLE REMOVED_DATE CM MASS (C):\u000aBreast tissue with apocrine cysts, columnar cell change, florid epithelial\u000ahyperplasia, focal pseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia and focal ATYPICAL\u000aLOBULAR HYPERPLASIA (see note).\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemistry for E-cadherin confirms absence of membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in atypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aSpecific histologic features of a mass-forming lesion are not seen.\u000aRadiologic/pathologic correlation is suggested.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 38 y/o female with two solid masses in the left breast. Previous\u000abenign biopsy of a fibroadenoma. Please rule out malignancy.\u000aA = 3:00 1 cm, B - 12:00 REMOVED_DATE cm. Site A is 3:00. Site B = 12:00.\u000aSubareolar palpable lump right breast. Probable FA.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: REMOVED_DATE cm (B), REMOVED_DATE cm (A) and Nonpalpable, circumscribed/lobulated mass.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: upper outer, 7 cm between masses.\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 14G Ultrasound\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 14G Ultrasound - Site A = 3:00 = Orange cassette; Site B = 12:00 = Yellow\u000acassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in three parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart A, "Left breast, orange cassette, 3 o'clock", consists of multiple\u000awhite-yellow irregular fibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000awhich are received in an orange cassette. The specimens are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "Left breast, yellow cassette, 12 o'clock", consists of multiple\u000awhite-yellow irregular fibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000awhich are received in a yellow cassette. The specimens are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "Right breast, brown cassette, 3 o'clock", consists of two white-yellow\u000airregular fibrofatty tissues (measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), which are received in a brown cassette. The specimen is submitted in\u000atoto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
