VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Priscilla S Chang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aCalcifications associated with LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU and columnar\u000ahyperplasia.\u000aFibroadenomatous change.\u000aDense interlobular fibrosis.\u000aNOTE: The entire specimen was submitted and reviewed microscopically.\u000aE-cadherin immunostain demonstrates loss of staining on the LCIS component.\u000aThese results support the above diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Abnormal mammogram, microcalcs.\u000aOperation: Right needle localized breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue - short stitch/superior, long/lateral - mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aCa++ in specimen. E. P. Frost, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue short stitch superior long lateral", and consists\u000aof an ovoid fragment of yellow/tan to tan/pink fibroadipose tissue (7.0 M-L x\u000a4.2 S-I x REMOVED_DATE A-P cm), which is oriented per surgeon with two sutures: Short\u000aequals superior, long equals lateral. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is one\u000aneedle localization wire in place, which enters the lateral aspect of the\u000aspecimen and exits the _____. The specimen was previously radiographed (per\u000aradiologist "calcifications in specimen"). The specimen is serially sectioned\u000afrom medial to lateral in to a total of fifteen slices (slice #1 equals medial,\u000aslice #15 equals lateral). The specimen is composed of approximately 30%\u000adense/lumpy/gritty white/tan fibrous stroma extending to all inked margins, and\u000aapproximately 70% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. The needle localization\u000awire traversed a focus of gritty fibrous stroma in slices #5 through #7\u000a(corresponding to the circled area of calcifications on the accompanying\u000aradiograph). No discrete masses are identified. The specimen is entirely\u000asequentially submitted as follows:\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #1, medial margin perpendicularly sectioned, multiple\u000afrags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slices #2 through #14 (area corresponding to circled\u000acalcifications on radiograph in blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID),\u000amultiple frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #15/lateral margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000almb/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/13/2006\u000a[report_end]
