VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: SARA M DURFEE M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Rachel E Factor, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER INNER, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, associated with mucin production and numerous\u000acalcifications.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aBiopsy site changes with foreign body giant cells.\u000aNote: ADH is best evaluated with excision.\u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aSITE #1:\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aColumnar cell change with mucin production.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aApocrine cysts with calcifications.\u000aSITE #2:\u000aMucinous cysts with calcifications.\u000aCalcifications in adipose tissue.\u000aCalcifications in a hyalinized duct.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 48-year-old with recent diagnosis of right DCIS with suspicious\u000abilateral calcifications.\u000aOperation: 11-G stereotactic.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Rule out DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a11-G cores, right and left breast calcifications.\u000aA/1. Right upper inner A - CA++, B - no CA++. Pink.\u000aB/2. Left upper outer - green, A - CA++, B - no CA++.\u000aC/3. Left upper outer - brown, A - CA++, B - no CA++.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in three parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name, unit number.\u000aPart A, "right breast - pink", and contains two pink cassettes. The first pink\u000acassette, "A CA++", contains multiple yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue cores (1.5\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The second pink cassette, "B", contains multiple\u000ahemorrhagic fibroadipose tissue cores (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "A CA++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "left breast site #1", and contains two green cassettes. The first\u000agreen cassette, "A CA++", contains multiple yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue\u000acores (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The second green cassette, "B",\u000acontains multiple focally hemorrhagic fibroadipose tissue cores (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.3 cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "A CA++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "left breast site #2 (brown)", and contains two brown cassettes. The\u000afirst brown cassette, "A CA++", contains multiple tan/yellow fibroadipose\u000atissue cores (1.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The second brown cassette,\u000a"B", contains multiple yellow/tan focally hemorrhagic fibroadipose tissue cores\u000a(2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "A CA++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adfi/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/20/2006\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aAccording to Dr. Durfee, the left breast biopsy from site #2 is from the upper\u000ainner breast.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
