VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Stacey A. Simons, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Xuefei Hong, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, "WIRE 3", WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY:\u000aFibroadenoma (0.7 cm).\u000aBenign breast tissue with columnar cell changes.\u000aB. RIGHT BREAST, "WIRE 1", WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY:\u000aFibroadenoma (1.2 cm).\u000aBenign breast tissue with columnar cell change.\u000aC. RIGHT BREAST, "WIRE 2", WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, only present on original slide).\u000aFibroadenoma (0.9 cm).\u000aBenign breast tissue with columnar cell change.\u000aLevels examined.\u000aSlides REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID also reviewed by Dr. Lester (Breast Pathology Service), who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Not provided.\u000aOperation: Wire localized "left" breast biopsy x 3 (see note below).\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aNOTE: PER OP report: 3 Right breast masses ("three needle localized right\u000abreast biopsies).\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Wire 3 short/superior, long/lateral.\u000aB/2. Wire 1 short/superior, long lateral.\u000aC/3. Wire 2 short/superior, long lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000a3 specimens, #s REMOVED_DATE marked with coins as follows - #1 = 1 coin, #2 = 2 coins,\u000a#3 = 3 coins. Each specimen contains an intact wire + mass lesion. Discussed\u000awith B. Shoji by E. Liter /R. Birdwell REMOVED_CASE_ID. NOTE: Radiographs are designated\u000a"R".\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Wire 3, short superior, long lateral", is an irregular fragment of\u000ayellow/tan to pink/tan fibroadipose tissue (3.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is\u000aoriented per surgeon with two sutures as indicated. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThere is one needle localization wire in place, which enters the anterolateral\u000aaspect of the specimen and exits the anteromedial aspect of the specimen. The\u000aspecimen was previously radiographed (per radiologist "each specimen contains\u000aan intact wire and mass lesion"). The specimen is serially sectioned from\u000alateral to medial to exhibit a central well-circumscribed pink/tan nodular mass\u000a(0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which grossly extends to the anterior and inferior\u000amargins, comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral margin. The\u000aneedle-localization wire traverses the parenchyma adjacent to the mass. The\u000aremainder of the cut surface is composed of approximately 90% dense white/tan\u000afibrous stroma and 10% yellow/tan adipose tissue. The specimen is sequentially\u000asubmitted in it's entirety from lateral to medial.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central specimen (mass in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 2 frags in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicularly sectioned, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Wire 1, short superior, long lateral", is an ovoid fragment of\u000ayellow/tan to pink/tan fibroadipose tissue (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is\u000aoriented per surgeon as indicated. The specimen is inked per prosector as\u000afollows: black equals anterior, blue equals posterior, red equals superior,\u000agreen equals inferior, orange equals medial and yellow equals lateral (please\u000anote, this deviates from the standard pathology protocol). There is one\u000aneedle-localization wire in place, entering the lateral aspect of the specimen\u000aand exiting the superomedial aspect of the specimen. The specimen was\u000apreviously radiographed (per radiologist "each specimen contains an intact wire\u000aand mass lesion"). The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to\u000ainferior to exhibit a cut surface composed of greater than 95% tan/pink focally\u000ahemorrhagic fibrous tissue extending to all six inked margins and less than 5%\u000ayellow/tan adipose tissue with no discrete masses identified. The wire\u000atraverses the aforementioned dense fibrous tissue. The specimen is entirely\u000asequentially submitted from superior to inferior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central specimen, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, perpendicularly sectioned, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Wire 2, short superior, long lateral", is an irregular fragment of\u000ayellow/tan to pink/tan fibroadipose tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is\u000aoriented per surgeon with two sutures as indicated. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThere is one needle-localization wire in place, which enters the posterolateral\u000aaspect of the specimen with no clear exit point. The specimen was previously\u000aradiographed (per radiologist "each specimen contains an intact wire and mass\u000alesion"). The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to exhibit\u000aa central, bulging, well-delineated tan/pink nodular mass (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000awhich comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral margin. The remainder of the cut\u000asurface is composed of approximately 90% dense focally hemorrhagic white/tan\u000afibrous stroma and 10% yellow/tan adipose tissue. The needle-localization wire\u000atraverses the aforementioned nodular mass. The specimen is entirely\u000asequentially submitted from medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central specimen to include mass (in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPlease note: On the form 86 received with these three specimens, the operation\u000asection was "wire-localized left breast biopsy x3." The three accompanying\u000aradiographs corresponding to each of the three specimens each exhibit "R"\u000aindicating that they are radiographs of right breast excision specimens. Per\u000aDr. Brent Shoji's op note, each of the three specimens is confirmed to be a\u000aright breast needle-localized excisional biopsy.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aLMB/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xuefei Hong M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
