VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: KATHARINE CARTER M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Stefan Kraft, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Edmund S Cibas, M.D.; Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE, WIRE-GUIDED EXCISION":\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present within a complex sclerosing\u000alesion (blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), with florid epithelial hyperplasia, sclerosing\u000aadenosis, stromal fibrosis, apocrine change, and associated\u000amicrocalcifications.\u000aMicrocalcifications are present in associated with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aDr. Andrea Richardson reviewed this case and concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of abnormal mammogram at HVMA. BWH reviewed of films\u000arecommended right wire loc of area of distortion right breast.\u000aOperation: Right mammographically directed breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram right breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue, mid outer right breast, short equals superior, long\u000aequals lateral (mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aMass and wire in specimen. Meyer.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue, mid outer right breast, short = superior, long =\u000alateral", and consists of a portion of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (5.9 x\u000a5.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with two orienting sutures ("short equals superior; long equals\u000alateral) and a needle localization wire in place (entering at the lateral\u000aaspect). The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial\u000ato lateral, exhibiting a white/tan, firm, ill-defined lesion (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), traverse by the needle localization wire, and coming to within REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe inferior and lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior and anterior margins,\u000a2.0 cm of the superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial margin. Adjacent to\u000athe lesion are multiple cylindrical hemorrhagic lesions, consistent with\u000aprevious biopsy site. The remaining breast tissue consists of approximately\u000a70% yellow lobulated adipose tissue and 30% tan/white dense fibrous stroma.\u000aThe specimen is accompanied by a radiograph, which confirms the presence of\u000a"mass and wire in specimen" (per radiology - Dr. Meyer).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lesion nearest lateral and inferior margins, multi frags, RSS.\u000aNote: The tissue at the lateral and inferior margins is focally disrupted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lesion nearest posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lesion nearest anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin nearest lesion, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin nearest lesion, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cylindrical hemorrhagic lesions adjacent to lesion, multi frags,\u000aRSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aDFI/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Edmund S Cibas M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
