VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Eric C Huang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA) SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION":\u000aColumnar cell proliferation with atypia.\u000aNo definitive calcifications identified.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy upon histologic examination of the entire\u000aspecimen including margins.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000aB) SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY CAVITY":\u000aBreast tissue with columnar cell changes and biopsy site changes.\u000aNo definitive calcifications identified.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy upon histologic examination of the entire\u000aspecimen including margins.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast DCIS versus ADH, on core needle biopsy.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire-localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast DCIS versus ADH.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast wire-localized excision, short stitch superior, long stitch\u000alateral.\u000aB/2. Right breast biopsy cavity - short stitch superior, long stitch lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSpecimen #1: Possible Ca++ in specimen. C. Denison, M.D.\u000aSpecimen #2: Clip and possible Ca++ are in specimen. C. Denison, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast wire-localized excision - short stitch superior, long\u000astitch lateral", and consists of one fragment of pink/tan fibroadipose tissue\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to\u000alateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior margin. There is a short\u000astitch designating as superior and long stitch designating as lateral, per\u000asurgeon. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is a wire localized for possible\u000acalcification (lateral margin), per mammography report, entering the lateral\u000amargin and exiting the medial/posterior margin. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from lateral to medial margin to reveal 95% fibrous tissue and 5%\u000aadipose tissue. A small focus of possible calcification measuring REMOVED_DATE cm is\u000aabutting the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior and superior margins, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the posterior margin, greater than REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior and medial\u000amargins. The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin with calcification, perpendicular, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior, lateral, anterior and posterior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior, anterior, posterior, and inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior, inferior, posterior, and medial margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior, posterior, and medial margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Right breast biopsy cavity - short stitch superior, long stitch\u000alateral", and consists of one fragment of pink/tan fibroadipose tissue\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior to inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to\u000alateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior to posterior margin. There is a\u000ashort stitch designating as superior and long stitch designating as lateral,\u000aper surgeon. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. Accompanying mammograph shows a clip in place.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial margin to reveal 98%\u000afibrous tissue and 2% adipose tissue. A possible biopsy cavity (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.3 cm) is abutting the anterior and inferior margins, REMOVED_DATE from the superior\u000aand posterior margins, and >1.0 from medial and lateral margins. The specimen\u000ais entirely submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral, superior, inferior, anterior and posterior margin, 2 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior, posterior, superior, and inferior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior, inferior, anterior, posterior and medial margin, 2 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aECH/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/6/2007\u000a[report_end]
