VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Qinghong Yang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Michael W Bennett, M.B., B.C.H.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, MASTECTOMY:\u000aAtypical ductal epithelial hyperplasia with scant microcalcifications.\u000aDuctal epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aFibroadenoma (0.22 cm).\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins\u000aRIGHT BREAST, MASTECTOMY:\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aFlorid ductal epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aFibroadenoma (1.2 cm).\u000aSkeletal muscle, negative for tumor.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right pleomorphic LCIS with 1 mm micro invasion.\u000aOperation: Bilateral mastectomy with insertion tissue expanders.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a#1. Left breast short stitch superior, long lateral, 140 gms.\u000a#2. Right breast short superior, long lateral 110 gms\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and medical record number.\u000aPart 1, labeled "#1. Left breast short stitch superior, long lateral", and\u000aconsists of a left simple mastectomy specimen (16.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a\u000awhite/tan skin ellipse (6.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a REMOVED_DATE cm nipple located at the\u000acenter of the skin ellipse with a REMOVED_DATE cm wrinkled areola around it. No biopsy\u000acavity is grossly identified. 80% of the breast tissue is composed of an\u000aill-defined tan/white/pink fibrotic area occupying the entire inner upper,\u000ainner lower, and the medial half of the upper outer and lower outer quadrants.\u000aThe fibrotic area abuts the black-inked deep resection margin. No surgical\u000ascar is grossly identified on the skin ellipse. The specimen is searched\u000acarefully but no lymph nodes identified. The gross specimen is reviewed by Dr.\u000aBennett.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple in relation to underlying fibrotic tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: The lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: The upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: The lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: The outer upper quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Right breast, short superior, long lateral", and consists of a\u000amastectomy specimen (14.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a tan/white skin ellipse (5.0 x\u000a3.5 cm) containing a REMOVED_DATE cm diameter nipple at the center and REMOVED_DATE cm wrinkled\u000aareola around the nipple. The deep resection margin is covered by fibrous\u000afascia with a shallow rent (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) at the center of the deep resection\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral resection margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial\u000aresection margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior resection margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainferior resection margin. A tan/pink well-circumscribed firm nodule (1.2 x\u000a0.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) is present at 1 o'clock and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the nipple. This\u000anodule is adjacent to a tan/white firm irregular-shaped fibrotic area (1.0 x\u000a1.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) laterally. Both the nodule and adjacent fibrotic area are less\u000athan REMOVED_DATE cm grossly from the deep resection margin (inked black). REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ainferior-laterally to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is a second, ill-defined tan/gray firm mass (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) that is REMOVED_DATE cm from the nipple. REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aclosest deep resection margin in the area the aforementioned rent on deep\u000aresection margin. The skin and underlying /neighboring breast tissue at 3\u000ao'clock (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) appears hemorrhagic/granular, consistent with old\u000asurgery/biopsy site. The rest of the specimen is composed about 60% fibrous\u000atissue and 40% adipose tissue. No lymph nodes are identified after carefully\u000asearching.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple in relation to the skin at 3 o'clock, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Rest of the hemorrhagic/granular skin and subcutaneous tissue at 3\u000ao'clock, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Well-circumscribed nodule at 1 o'clock (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) in relation to surround\u000afibrous tissue and black-inked deep resection margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and the fibrous tissue in between (the well-circumscribed\u000anodule side inked blue), 2 frags, 1 frag in each block, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 3 frags, 1 frag in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and 2 frags in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: The outer lower quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: The outer upper quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: The inner lower quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: The inner upper quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aqy/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on\u000a5/24/2007\u000a[report_end]
