er\u000aof calcifications. The sectioning demonstrates a large REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm band\u000aof tan/white fiber dense tissue occupying the majority (at least 80%) of the\u000aspecimen, particularly the medial half. There are no obvious masses, lesions\u000aor other abnormalities grossly. The entire specimen is submitted sequentially\u000afrom medial to lateral, with perpendicular medial margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and\u000aperpendicular lateral margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Area of interest per\u000aradiograph/localizing wire in approximately REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sequentially from medial to lateral, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000adb/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/30/2007\u000a[report_end]
