VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kevin Golden, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Vania Nose, MD, PhD\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aNo residual papilloma identified.\u000aNodular sclerosing adenosis, multiple foci.\u000aBiopsy site identified.\u000aNOTE:\u000aCase also reviewed on REMOVED_DATE  by Dr. S. Lester, Breast Pathology Service, who\u000aconcurs with the diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Hx core bx with severe ADH.\u000aOperation: L needle-loc bx.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnl left mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast tissue - to mammo, no F.S.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip on specimen radiograph, called to OR, Ayodale Odulate REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh and labeled with the patient's name and medical\u000arecord number along with the words "Left breast mass with wire". The specimen\u000ais received in a total of one part. The specimen consists of a wire localized\u000abreast excision specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE cm (S-I), REMOVED_DATE cm (A-P) and REMOVED_DATE cm (M-L).\u000aThere is a skin ellipse at the anterior/inferior aspect measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aIn addition, there is a small central core biopsy scar in the skin. There was\u000aa wire located that enters the sample in the skin. The specimen was pre-inked\u000apresumably as per pathology protocol. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The accompanying\u000aradiograph with the specimen demonstrates wire entering into the specimen along\u000awith a clip and a hyperdense region in the middle of the specimen. The\u000aspecimen was serially sectioned medial to lateral into nine slices and\u000arevealing a dense fibrous mass surrounded by adipose tissue along with changes\u000aconsistent with prior biopsy site. The mass measures approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. The specimen is located approximately REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe superior margin. The mass is located approximately REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral\u000amargin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. The mass is located primarily in\u000aslices #4, #5 and #6. The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic\u000asection.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicularly sliced lateral margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular sections of medial margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aThis case was reviewed with Dr. Jane E Brock, fellow in breast pathology.\u000aMDH/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
