VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Agoston Tony Agoston, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION":\u000aBreast tissue with core biopsy site.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aentire specimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 47 year old woman s/p right breast core bx's REMOVED_DATE  for ca++\u000arevealing ADH, ALH - excision recommended.\u000aOperation: Right breast wl bx.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: ADH.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) R breast (to mammo) wire localized excisional biopsy\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip and intact wire are seen within the specimen. Dr. Gombos\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, and labeled with the patient's name and medical\u000arecord number, and consists of one part.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy", consists of a\u000a13.7-gram wire-localized excision specimen (5.5 cm S-I, REMOVED_DATE cm M-L, REMOVED_DATE cm A-P)\u000athat is previously inked. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A wire enters the specimen\u000aanterior/inferiorly. The specimen is sectioned along the wire, and the clip is\u000afound, associated with white fibrous tissue that is present throughout the\u000aspecimen abutting all margins. There are no discrete masses or lesions\u000aidentified. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags per block, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entirely submitted specimen submitted medial to lateral, 1 frag\u000aper block, ESS. Note, the clip is associated with tissue in cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and\u000athe wire is between tissue submitted in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 2, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aTA/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aFriday REMOVED_MONTH 19, 2008 at 03:43:41PM\u000a[report_end]
