VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Stephanie Schulte, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Robert D Odze, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED LUMPECTOMY FOR A CLIP":\u000aBreast tissue with:\u000a- Atypical ductal hyperplasia (one focus, REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000a- Sclerosing adenosis and columnar cell changes\u000a- Calcifications associated with benign breast epithelium\u000a- Biopsy site changes\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 66 year old female with left breast ADH bordering on DCIS, S/P\u000aimage-guided core biopsy.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localized lumpectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left breast wire localized lumpectomy, short suture/superior, long\u000asuture/lateral (to mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aWire and clip in specimen. OR called. LBS.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and medical\u000arecord number and "#1. Left breast wire localized lumpectomy, short suture\u000asuperior, long suture lateral", and consists of a breast lumpectomy specimen\u000a(4.6 cm from medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000aanterior to posterior) with two orienting sutures (short equals superior, long\u000aequals lateral). A localization wire is in place entering the specimen at the\u000alateral aspect. The tip of the wire exits at the medial aspect. An\u000aaccompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates a localization wire in place\u000amarking a clip in the mid central portion of the specimen. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe specimen is cut along the wire to reveal a biopsy site (0.5 cm), located\u000a0.6 cm to the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm to medial, REMOVED_DATE cm to\u000alateral, REMOVED_DATE cm to anterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm to posterior. The breast parenchyma\u000aaround the biopsy site appears diffusely firm and fibrotic with areas of\u000afibrosis extending to the inferior, medial, superior, anterior, and posterior\u000amargins. There are small areas of hemorrhage within the fibrotic tissue,\u000aparticularly at the inferior margin. The specimen is to 60% composed of firm\u000awhite fibrous tissue and 40% yellow lobulated adipose tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, perpendicular, 4 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue from anterior to posterior (biopsy sites in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, perpendicular, 3 frags each, ESS.\u000aSTS/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
