VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Consult material\u000aProcedure Date:\u000aOrdering Provider: ERIC P WINER M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Ann K Folkins, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM NORTHEAST HOSPITALS, BEVERLY, MA:\u000aLEFT BREAST, CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR CALCIFICATIONS (S-REMOVED_CASE_ID-99; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aApocrine cysts and calcifications.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS (S-REMOVED_CASE_ID-99; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, well differentiated (modified Bloom-\u000aRichardson grade I/III), REMOVED_DATE cm, associated with calcifications.\u000aA single focus is suspicious for lymphovascular invasion.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type (intermediate nuclear grade)\u000ais present within the invasive carcinoma in the one slide reviewed. By\u000areport, DCIS was "scant to absent", consistent with an EIC negative\u000acarcinoma.\u000aInvasive carcinoma is < REMOVED_DATE cm from the margin.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed with the following results (not\u000areviewed):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu NEGATIVE\u000aNote: By report, a subsequent re-excision did not reveal residual\u000acarcinoma and ten lymph nodes were free of carcinoma (outside number S-\u000a1085-00; REMOVED_DATE ).\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION (S-8216-06; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA with ductal and lobular features, moderately\u000adifferentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson grade II/III), REMOVED_DATE cm, is present\u000ain an area of dense stroma (see note).\u000aA focus is suspicious for lymphovascular invasion.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type (intermediate nuclear grade), with\u000anecrosis and calcifications, is present.\u000aInvasive carcinoma is focally present at the margin.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed with the following results for\u000ainvasive cancer (not reviewed):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (FISH) NOT AMPLIFIED\u000aNote: The cancer has a different histologic appearance compared to the\u000aprior cancer in 1999. This suggests that this may be a new primary. It\u000awould be helpful to know the location of this cancer in the left breast, as\u000acompared to the prior cancer.\u000aThis cancer could be classified as AJCC (6th edition) REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc NX.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given\u000aClinical Diagnosis: IDLC\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aConsult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived from Northeast Hospitals, Pathology Department, 85 Herrick Street,\u000aBeverly, MA REMOVED_DATE  are twelve (12) glass slides.\u000aSix (6) slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "1A REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "1B REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "2A REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID"\u000athrough "2C REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and "3 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", corresponding to a left breast biopsies 1) (0.8 cm)\u000a2) (0.8 cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology\u000areport bearing the patient's name.\u000aThree (3) slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "A REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "A REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and "A\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", corresponding to a left breast wire guided excision (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aperformed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing\u000athe patient's name.\u000aThree (3) slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "A", "C" and "D",\u000acorresponding to a left breast excision (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed on\u000a6/21/06, according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's\u000aname.\u000aIncluded is a pathology report from the same institution numbered "S-1085-00"\u000aand dated REMOVED_DATE  referring to a left breast re-excision (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000abearing the patient's name.\u000aAlso included is a cytology report from the same hospital numbered "S-7447-06"\u000aand dated REMOVED_DATE  referring to a left breast, 2 o'clock, fine needle\u000aaspiration, bearing the patient's name (outside diagnosis: "suspicious for\u000amalignancy").\u000aIncluded also are two (2) lab reports from the same institution; one report is\u000anumbered "1210:REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and dated REMOVED_DATE  referring to immunohistochemistry\u000astudies performed on block "A" from the case listed above "S-1599S-99"; the\u000asecond report is numbered "0621:REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and dated REMOVED_DATE  referring to\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu by FISH analysis performed on block "B from the case listed above\u000a"S-8216-06" (NOT AMPLIFIED), bearing the patient's name.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/15/2008\u000a[report_end]
