VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kristin S. Ricci, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION":\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia with columnar cell change, with focal atypical\u000aductal hyperplasia, with associated calcifications.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aResection margins are free of atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aCalcifications in benign breast tissue.\u000aPrior biopsy site, with clip identified.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 46 year old premenopausal woman S/P REMOVED_DATE  R breast core bx revealing\u000aADH - excision recommended. Previous surgery: REMOVED_DATE  - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aOperation: R breast WL bx.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided/\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right breast tissue, short suture/superior, long/lateral, whipstitch on\u000achest wall margin (to mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aClip/Ca++/intact wire in specimen. Called to OR - Dr. Rhei by Dr. Ritner REMOVED_DATE \u000a@ 1 pm.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "#1. Right breast tissue, short suture/superior, long/lateral,\u000awhipstitch on chest wall margin", and consists of a wire-localized partial\u000amastectomy specimen (3.5 cm anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior,\u000a3.0 cm medial to lateral) with a short suture designating superior, a long\u000asuture designating lateral, and a whipstitch designating deep margins. The\u000aspecimen is inked in the by the surgeon for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. A radiograph demonstrates a localization wire entering the\u000aanterior aspect of the specimen and exiting the posterior aspect of the\u000aspecimen, designating a surgical clip at a prior biopsy site. Grossly the\u000asurgical clip is REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin,\u000agreater than REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial and lateral margins. A gross lesion at the\u000asite of the surgical clip is not seen. The tissue consists of 80% dense\u000afibrous tissue and 20% adipose tissue. The specimen is submitted entirely.\u000aGross photographs of the specimen are taken. The location of the tissue blocks\u000ais recorded on a specimen diagram.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial resection margin, radially sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections of breast from medial to lateral, surgical clip\u000ain REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral resection margin, radially sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aKRI/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
