fibroadipose breast tissue (23.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate) with overlying\u000atan/white wrinkled skin (21.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The cut surface is tan/yellow and\u000ahomogeneous with focal areas of dense white fibrous tissue constituting\u000aapproximately less than 10% of the breast parenchyma. No discrete lesions are\u000agrossly identified. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aAfter examination of the initial three blocks of tissue, the specimen is\u000are-examined grossly. No lesions are identified. Five additional blocks of\u000atissue are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin and breast tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aPart B, "right breast tissue", consists of 872 grams of tan/yellow lobulated\u000afibroadipose breast tissue (22.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with overlying tan/white\u000awrinkled skin (20.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The cut surface is tan/yellow and homogeneous\u000awith focal areas of dense white fibrous tissue constituting approximately less\u000athan 10% of the breast parenchyma. No discrete lesions are grossly identified.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin and breast tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aSEK/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/30/2008\u000a[report_end]
