VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Consult material\u000aProcedure Date:\u000aOrdering Provider: SUNITI N. NIMBKAR M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Mariana A. Stoleru, M.D.; Qinghong Yang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM SOUTH SHORE HOSPITAL, SOUTH WEYMOUTH, MA:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES X 2 (S-09-3298; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aRIGHT BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR CALCIFICATIONS (A):\u000aSEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, bordering on DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU,\u000asee NOTE\u000aNOTE: An atypical ductal proliferation with low nuclear grade and a\u000acribriforming pattern is present measuring REMOVED_DATE cm. This area is associated\u000awith calcifications and without necrosis. The lesional area is qualitatively\u000aconsistent with DCIS, but being low nuclear grade and < REMOVED_DATE cm in area it falls\u000ajust short quantitatively for a strict diagnosis of DCIS and is probably better\u000aclassified in this biopsy as ADH. ADH is best evaluated with excision. The\u000alesional cells are strongly ER positive and PR positive.\u000aRIGHT BREAST CORE BIOPSY (B):\u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA, see NOTE\u000aColumnar cell change with florid epithelial hyperplasia and apocrine\u000ametaplasia.\u000aFibroadenoma\u000aIntraductal papilloma\u000aScant microcalcifications associated with benign breast tissue\u000aNOTE: The targeted lesion of interest is not specified in the outside report\u000aand radiologic correlation is advised to ensure the biopsy is representative of\u000athe radiologic lesion.\u000aB. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A PREVIOUS BIOPSY SITE (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID;\u000a6/11/09):\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU. An E-cadherin stain performed highlights absent\u000amembranous staining in neoplastic cells.\u000a