VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE ANN RITNER M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Mariana A. Stoleru, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, 8 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A REMOVED_DATE CM\u000aAREA OF ARCHITECTURAL DISTORTION WITH CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aFragments of a radial sclerosing lesion.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar cell change with flat atypia.\u000aCalcifications are associated with cysts and sclerosing adenosis.\u000aNote: Flat atypia would be evaluated best with excision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: New architectural distortion in the left breast with a few amorphous\u000acalcifications. Differential diagnosis - radial scar, rule out cancer.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: REMOVED_DATE cm architectural distortion.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: upper outer\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 8 G Stereotactic Vacuum-assisted\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 8 G Stereotactic Vacuum-assisted - Orange cassettes.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in one part, labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number, and "left breast", and consists of two orange cassettes, one\u000alabeled "A. Ca++", and contains multiple cylindrical focally hemorrhagic\u000afibrofatty soft tissues (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The second orange\u000acassette labeled "B", and contains multiple cylindrical focally hemorrhagic\u000afibrofatty soft tissues (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The specimen is\u000asubmitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of orange cassette labeled "A. Ca++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of orange cassette labeled "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aJenC/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Monday\u000aMay 25, 2009 at 01:33:19PM\u000a[report_end]
