VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Lymph node biopsy (non-heme)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: J. GREGORY KANE M.D.\u000aCASE: BG-10-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Vinodh Pillai, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000a1/A. SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT AXILLARY NODAL TISSUE":\u000aNine (9) lymph nodes; negative for tumor.\u000a2/B. SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST (SHORT SUPERIOR; LONG LATERAL)":\u000aBreast parenchyma with extensive intraductal papillomatosis and focal\u000afat necrosis.\u000aScarring and fibrosis consistent with prior surgery.\u000aDuct ectasia with inspissation.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000a3/C. SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST SKIN":\u000aSkin and subcutaneus tissue with no significant pathologic change.\u000a4/D. SPECIMEN LABELED "SUBAREOLAR TISSUE":\u000aBenign breast parenchyma with focal duct ectasia and inspissation.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Past history of extensive papillomatosis of left breast, s/p breast\u000aresection, severe mastodynia.\u000aOperation: Right simple mastectomy\u000aOperative Findings: Same\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Papillomatosis right breast\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1/A. Right axillary nodal tissue\u000a2/B. Right breast (short superior; long lateral)\u000a3/C. Right breast skin\u000a4/D. Subareolar tissue\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimens are received in four parts, labeled with the patient's name and\u000amedical record number.\u000aPart A is labeled "#1. Right axillary nodal tissue", and consists of\u000afibroadipose tissue (4.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Approximately four lymph node\u000acandidates can be identified (up to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension). The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted for histological examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 lymph nodes each, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining fat, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B is labeled "#2. Right breast short superior, long lateral", and consists\u000aof a breast tissue oriented by short suture superiorly and long suture\u000alaterally. A posterior surface is identified, which is inked black. There is\u000ano attached skin. The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000asuperior to inferior and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior. There is an area of\u000adeficit (12.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) at the inferolateral margin anteriorly consistent\u000awith history of prior surgeries. The specimen is composed of less than 5%\u000afibrous stroma. No lesions are grossly identified. Representative sections\u000aare taken for histological examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous stroma, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aPart C is labeled "#3. Right breast skin", and consists of two tan/white skin\u000afragments with attached soft tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). No lesions or scars are identified. A representative section is\u000asubmitted from each piece.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Right breast skin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart D is labeled "#4. Subareolar tissue", and consists of fibroadipose tissue\u000a(2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The tissue contains fibrous stroma. This entire\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted for histological examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Subareolar tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BG-10-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aVIP/am\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday\u000aFebruary 10, 2010 at 04:26:35PM\u000a[report_end]
