VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Michael A. Seidman, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aBenign breast tissue with epithelial hyperplasia,\u000acolumnar cell change, and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aSkin and nipple with no significant pathologic change.\u000aB. RIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, focal.\u000aNo residual DCIS or Paget's disease.\u000aSkin with scar and prior excision site changes.\u000aBenign breast tissue with epithelial hyperplasia,\u000aexcision site changes, apocrine metaplasia, and\u000acalcifications.\u000aNipple is surgically absent.\u000aThe deep margin is negative for tumor.\u000aC. LEFT BREAST IMPLANT:\u000aGross examination only.\u000aD. RIGHT BREAST IMPLANT:\u000aGross examination only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 61 y/o postmenopausal woman with a family history of breast cancer in\u000aher sister (42), m. aunt (52) and p. grandmother (50's). Pt noted redness of\u000athe R nipple. Skin punch biopsy and subsequent excision revealed Paget's\u000aDisease and DCIS. REMOVED_DATE  MRI (-) REMOVED_DATE  mammogram (-).\u000aOperation: R simple mastectomy, L prophylactic simple mastectomy; bilateral\u000areconstruction (TE).\u000aPREVIOUS SURGERY: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aOperative Findings: None provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast; short stitch - superior.\u000aB/2) Right breast; short stitch - superior, long - lateral.\u000aC/3) Left breast implant for I.D.\u000aD/4) Right breast implant for I.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Left breast", consists of a REMOVED_DATE gram left simple\u000amastectomy specimen (26.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a white skin ellipse (9.5 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), which displays a tan areola (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and an everted nipple (1.5 x\u000a1.5 cm). There is a long suture designating lateral and a short suture\u000adesignating superior. The deep margin consists of a smooth fascial plane\u000awithout skeletal muscle present. Sectioning reveals 40% firm white fibrous\u000atissue and 60% adipose tissue with no discrete masses or lesions identified.\u000aThe most lateral tissue is palpated, however, no lymph nodes are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, multi frags, RSS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Right breast", consists of a REMOVED_DATE gram right simple\u000amastectomy specimen (27.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an irregular white skin (10.0 x\u000a5.5 cm). The skin displays a slightly pigmented tan area/? areola (6.0 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), which exhibits a central tan-pink well-healed linear scar (2.5 cm in\u000alength). There is no nipple present. The deep margin consists of a smooth\u000afascial plane without skeletal muscle present. Sectioning reveals 30%\u000atan-white firm fibrous tissue and 70% adipose tissue with no discrete masses\u000aidentified. The most lateral tissue is palpated, however, no lymph nodes are\u000aidentified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Linear scar entirely submitted to include superior skin margin in\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and inferior skin margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue underlying linear scar, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, multi frags, RSS.\u000aPart C, labeled "#3. Left breast implant for ID", consists of a deflated\u000atan-white discoid breast implant (12.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which displays the\u000ainscription 225. No sections are submitted. The specimen is for gross\u000aidentification only. Gross photographs are taken.\u000aPart D, labeled "#4. Right implant for ID", consists of an intact tan-white\u000adiscoid saline breast implant (10.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which displays the\u000ainscription 225. No sections are submitted. The specimen is for gross\u000aidentification only. Gross photographs are taken.\u000aLMC/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aMonday REMOVED_MONTH 26, 2009 at 09:04:49AM\u000a[report_end]
