VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: CHRISTINE M DENISON M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Revised Report **********\u000aResident: Mariana A. Stoleru, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, UPPER INNER, 8 G MRI GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A REMOVED_DATE CM\u000aAREA OF ENHANCEMENT:\u000aColumnar cell hyperplasia, see Note.\u000aNormal breast tissue with calcifications.\u000aNote: Radiologic correlation is advised to ensure the biopsy is representative\u000aof the radiologic lesion.\u000aB. LEFT BREAST, 12:00, 9 G MRI GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A REMOVED_DATE CM AREA OF\u000aENHANCEMENT:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia, focal (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). An E-Cadherin stain highlights\u000aabsent membranous staining in the small focus of ALH.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aColumnar cell change with calcifications.\u000aSclerosing adenosis with associated microcalcifications.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aNote. Radiologic correlation is advised to ensure the biopsy is representative\u000aof the radiologic lesion.\u000aC. LEFT BREAST, 9:00, SUBAREOLAR, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES\u000aFOR A CIRCUMSCRIBED/HYPOECHOIC REMOVED_DATE CM MASS:\u000aDiscrete nodule (0.7 cm) of breast tissue with dense stroma, likely\u000arepresenting lesion of interest.\u000aColumnar cell change.\u000a* This case has been amended to correct the tissue submitted in part B to a\u000aleft sided breast biopsy (site clarified by submitting radiologist Dr. Arpita\u000aSwami). The diagnosis otherwise remains unchanged.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 48 year old with multiple focal areas of enhancement on MRI. This\u000arepresents MRI-guided biopsy of R UIQ focal area, REMOVED_DATE mm size (site #1). This\u000arepresents MRI bx of 7 mm focal area of enhancement L mid upper breast (site\u000a#2). Solid 7 mm hypoechoic mass left subareolar breast at 9:00 region (site\u000a#3).\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: 8 mm, non-palpable, focal and non-mass forming on MRI (site #1).\u000a2. Left: 7 mm, non-palpable, focal and non-mass forming on MRI (site #2).\u000a3. Left: 7 mm, non-palpable and circumscribed/lobulated mass on ultrasound\u000a(site #3).\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: upper/inner (site #1).\u000a2. Left: 12:00 (site #2).\u000a3. Left: 9:00 region (site #3).\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 8G MRI and vacuum-assisted (site #1).\u000a2. 9G MRI and vacuum-assisted (site #2).\u000a3. 14G Ultrasound (site #3).\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast core biopsy in three cassettes with white bottoms/blue tops\u000ain formalin @ 9:40 am (site #1)\u000aB/2) Left breast core biopsy in three cassettes with white bottoms/green tops\u000a(site #2)\u000aC/3) Left breast core biopsy in 4 samples in a white cassette (site #3).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in three parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name, unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "blue top, white bottom right breast site 2 formalin 9:35\u000aa.m.", consists of multiple white-yellow fibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x\u000a2.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are received in three white cassettes with blue top. The\u000aspecimens are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with blue top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with blue top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with blue top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "green top, white bottom left breast site #1 formalin 9:45\u000aa.m.", consists of multiple white-yellow fibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x\u000a3.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are received in three white cassettes with green top. The\u000aspecimens are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with green top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with green top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with green top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "left breast white", consists of multiple yellow-white\u000afibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are received in a\u000awhite cassette. The specimens are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000acp/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 12, 2009\u000aat 04:33:53PM\u000aAmendment #1 by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aMonday REMOVED_MONTH 15, 2009 at 03:01:56PM\u000a[report_end]
