VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 07 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON: 07 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14:07 CLINICAL DATA: Left breast biopsy with needle localization. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: PSEUDOANGIOMATOUS STROMAL HYPERPLASIA. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (LEFT, "DEEP SUPERIOR"), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (LEFT, "DEEP INFERIOR"), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Diagnosis by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 10 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 12:24 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast biopsy" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fibrofatty breast tissue with one silk suture designating superior deep and two silk sutures designating inferior deep. The specimen is inked (anterior blue, posterior black, lateral yellow, and medial green), serially sectioned displaying a cut surface consistent with a serial sanguinous exudate, a tan-pink exudate, and blood. There is a minimal amount of uninvolved tan-yellow fibroadipose tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted sequentially from superior to inferior in cassettes A-L. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "deep superior left breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm focally cauterized irregular fibrofatty breast tissue which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassette M. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "inferior left breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm irregular, focally cauterized fibrofatty breast tissue which is serially sectioned displaying a REMOVED_DATE cm tan paste filled cyst. The remaining cut surface is tan-yellow fibrofatty breast tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted in cassette N. Gross Description by: JAMES BARRY Resident: RESIDENT-FREE SERVICE (FCK) =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Susan M. Briggs, M.D. PART A: BREAST(LEFT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: BREAST(LEFT,DEEP SUPERIOR),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C: BREAST(LEFT,DEEP INFERIOR),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY
