m from the medial margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin. The remaining uninvolved parenchyma consists of 70% tan-yellow lobulated adipose tissue and 30% dense white fibrous tissue. No discrete masses or lesions are appreciated. The specimen is entirely and sequentially submitted from posterior to anterior in cassettes A-L with the area denoted by the localizing wire and the ill-defined dense fibrotic area in cassettes D-J. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "left breast, final shaved margin superior" are REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm of irregular tan-pink yellow unoriented fibrofatty portions of tissue. The specimen is serially sectioned and no discrete masses or lesions are identified. The specimen is entirely submitted in M-R. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "left breast final shaved margin inferior" are REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm of irregular tan-pink to yellow unoriented portions of fibrofatty tissue. The specimen is serially sectioned no discrete masses or lesions are identified. The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes S-Y. Gross Description by: JENNIFER NASH Resident: RESIDENT-FREE SERVICE (SGR) =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: BREAST(LEFT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: BREAST(LEFT SUPERIOR),FINAL SHAVED MARGIN PART C: BREAST(LEFT INFERIOR),FINAL SHAVED MARGIN
