VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 02 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON: 02 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 10:28 CLINICAL DATA: Prophylactic bilateral mastectomy for strong family history of breast cancer. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (RIGHT), MASTECTOMY: ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA SCATTERED MICROSCOPIC FOCI. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. SCLEROSING ADENOSIS. UNREMARKABLE LYMPH NODE. BREAST (LEFT), MASTECTOMY: ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA RARE MICROSCOPIC FOCI. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. SCLEROSING ADENOSIS. SKIN (RIGHT CHEST WALL), EXCISION: FOCAL EPIDERMAL HYPERPLASIA. SKIN (LEFT CHEST WALL), EXCISION: NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED. Diagnosis by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 08 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 12:37 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm right breast mastectomy specimen. The specimen has an attached skin ellipse with nipple and areola measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm thick, with a long stitch marking the lateral margin and a short stitch marking the superior margin. There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm pigmented area adjacent to the nipple. The entire specimen except for the skin is covered with unremarkable tan-yellow fat. The anterior surface is inked blue and the posterior surface is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal that the majority of the specimen is tan-white, poorly defined, patchy firm fibrofatty tissue. Intermixed throughout this fibrofatty tissue there is tan-yellow unremarkable appearing fat. Representative sections of breast tissue to the posterior margin are submitted in cassettes A-J. One tan-purple lymph node that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm is identified and submitted in cassette K. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast", is a left breast mastectomy specimen that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a skin ellipse with areola and nipple that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a short stitch designating the superior aspect of the specimen and a long stitch designating the lateral aspect of the specimen. The areola and nipple are unremarkable. The remainder of the specimen appears as unremarkable tan-yellow adipose tissue. The anterior surface is inked blue and the posterior surface of the specimen is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal that the majority of the specimen is patchy tan-white fibrous appearing tissue with interspersed unremarkable tan-yellow adipose tissue. Representative sections of the breast tissue including the posterior margin are submitted in cassettes L-U. No lymph nodes were identified in the specimen. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right chest wall skin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm thick ellipse of skin. The deep and lateral margins are inked black, the tips are placed in cassette V, and a representative section is placed in cassette W. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left chest wall skin", is a ellipsoid piece of skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm thick. The lateral and deep margin are inked black and the ends are submitted in cassette X and representative sections from the main part of the specimen is submitted in Y. Resident: STEWART M. KNOEPP, MD., Ph.D. *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** GROSS DIAGNOSIS OF RIGHT AND LEFT PROPHYLACTIC MAMMOPLASTY: FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES, THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA. O.R. Resident: MINDY J. HULL, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: Andrew Eric Rosenberg, M.D. =======