VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 12 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON: 12 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13:57 CLINICAL DATA: Bilateral ductal carcinoma in-situ and strong family history of breast carcinoma. Left breast, 1994 lumpectomy and radiation in 1994. Right breast: carcinoma in two sites on breast biopsy 1995. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (RIGHT), MASTECTOMY: ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, MICROSCOPIC FOCI. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). FIBROTIC BIOPSY CAVITY. LYMPH NODES (RIGHT AXILLA), RESECTION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 8 OF 8 LYMPH NODES. BREAST (LEFT), MASTECTOMY: RADIATION CHANGES. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (LEFT, "ADDITIONAL LATERAL MARGIN), RESECTION: RADIATION CHANGES. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. UNREMARKABLE LYMPH NODE. LYMPH NODES (LEFT AXILLA) RESECTION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 4 OF 4 LYMPH NODES. Diagnosis by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 19 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15:06 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh labeled with the patient's name and unit number in four parts. Labeled "right breast" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm breast specimen, centered by a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm areola with a REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter nipple. The specimen is inked black with superior surface, designated by surgeon with short stitch, inked red over black and the lateral surface, designated by surgeon with long stitch, inked green over black. A linear REMOVED_DATE cm, well healed areolar scar is in the inferior quadrant. Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm firm, nodule, located deeply to the peri-areolar incision, which extends for an approximate length of REMOVED_DATE cm parallel to the areolar, with branching of white bands that reach to within REMOVED_DATE cm of closest inked resection margin. SECTION CODE: A-B: suspicious area, in relationship with closest inked resection margin C: suspicious area D-E: peri-areolar suspicious area F: suspicious area, in relationship with inked margin G-I: suspicious area and inked margin, additional section J: unremarkable breast parenchyma K-L: lymph nodes. Labeled "left axillary sampling" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of adipose tissue. A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of soft lymph nodes is submitted in cassette M. Labeled "additional left lateral margin" are two fragments of soft tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, respectively. Submitted entirely in cassette N through P. Labeled "left breast" is a 13 x REMOVED_DATE x 3 cm simple mastectomy specimen with a 5 x REMOVED_DATE cm areola centered by a REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter nipple. The specimen is inked black with the superior surface, designated by surgeon with a short stitch, inked red over black and the lateral surface, designated by surgeon with a long stitch, inked green over black. The specimen is sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma. Representative sections are submitted in cassettes Q through Y. Resident: EDI BROGI, MD, PhD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. Michael J Yaremchuk, M.D. Edi Brogi, M.D. PART A: RIGHT BREAST, MASTECTOMY PART B: LEFT BREAST, MASTECTOMY PART C: LEFT BREAST, LATERAL MARGIN PART D: LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
