VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 28 AUG 02 ACCESSIONED ON: 28 AUG 02 at 14:15 CLINICAL DATA: Breast mass. One stitch medial, and two stitches lateral. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT), NEEDLE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, GRADE 2, SOLID AND PAPILLARY, COALESCING AS A REMOVED_DATE CM GREATEST DIMENSION NODULE THAT IS LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM A LATERAL MARGIN. SEE NOTE. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES, HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS, WITH MODERATE DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA. NOTE: Although surrounded by prominent fibroplasia, no definite stromal invasion is identified; the finding of actin-immunopositive cells around the tumor cell nests confirms this impression. The tumor cells are positive for e-cadherin and negative for cytokeratin 903, consistent with the diagnosis of ductal carcinoma in situ. The tumor cells are negative for argyrophilic granules using a grimelius stain, but are focally immunopositive for chromogranin, indicating neuroendocrine differentiation. Diagnosis by: John H. Eichhorn, M.D. Signed On: 05 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 16:09 =============================================================================== *** IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum *** RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Left, block A): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Grace T. McKee,MD Signed On: 09 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 15:25 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast tissue", is a fragmented piece of breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate. One stitch designates the medial and two stitches the lateral part of the specimen. The two sutures are REMOVED_DATE cm apart. The specimen is inked black around the two stitches, and blue around the one stitch, and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE cm tan-brown, firm nodule with a dark rim that abutts the inked surfaces. The nodule and inked margin is submitted in A, B and C. Sectioning reveals a small area of calcification, REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter, which abutts the inked surfaces. The calcified region is entirely submitted as D. The radial section of the area with one stitch designating the medial surface is submitted as E. The radial section from the area with two designated stitches as lateral surface with relationship to inked surface is submitted in cassette F. Sections of the parenchyma away from the mass are submitted as G and H. Resident: ALIREZA SEPEHR, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Susan E Briggs, M.D. PART : BREAST(LEFT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY
