here is a large area, REMOVED_DATE cm in largest dimension, area of dense white fibrous tissue with scattered yellow discolored areas and microcysts. This abnormal tissue averages REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin. There is a REMOVED_DATE cm in largest dimension firm tan-white nodule, located in the medial aspect of the tissue, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior anterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin. A representative section of this nodule is in A. Representative sections of fibrous and cystic areas are in B-G. Representative sections of tissue beneath the scar are in H-J. Representative sections of skin papules are in K. There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of axillary tail attached to the specimen, with an axillary node designated by a long stitch. The axillary tail is dissected for lymph nodes, which are submitted in L-P. Cassette N contains sections of a single node. Further representative sections of the breast tissue are in Q-S. Designated "left breast lymph node, additional axillary tissue," is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of fatty tissue, containing several soft lymph nodes. The lymph nodes are fully submitted in T. Resident: KRISTINA M. BRAATEN, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: BREAST (LEFT), MASTECTOMY PART B: LYMPH NODES, LEFT AXILLA\u000a[report_end]
