r of the breast. H-N: Axillary nodes. Labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "highest node" and consists of a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of fatty tissue. Three tiny lymph nodes are dissected from the fatty tissue and submitted in cassette O. Resident: Navneet Narula, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Michael Ned Margolies, M.D. PART A: BREAST (RIGHT) PART B: RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
