VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 13 REMOVED_MONTH 99 ACCESSIONED ON: 13 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 11:38 CLINICAL DATA: Right nodule, strong family history. Right biopsy DCIS/ADH bilateral mastectomies, ? axillary dissection. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT), MASTECTOMY: FOCAL FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 3 OF 3 LYMPH NODES EXAMINED. BREAST (RIGHT), MASTECTOMY: SCLEROSING INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA, WITH FOCAL EPITHELIAL ATYPIA. THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 8 OF 8 LYMPH NODES EXAMINED. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES, FOCAL. BREAST ("RIGHT NODULE"), BIOPSY: FOCAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA AND COLLAGENOUS SPHERULOSIS. THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED. Diagnosis by: Jacqueline Haas, MD Signed On: 16 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 15:30 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast nodule" is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm piece of fibrous breast tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE cm tan firm nodule. The nodule is bisected and entirely frozen as FX #1, now in A. The additional tissue is submitted in cassette B. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast" is a 17 x 13 x 5 cm mastectomy specimen with an overlying ellipse of skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The nipple and areola are grossly unremarkable. The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal patchy white breast parenchyma consistent with fibrocystic changes. The specimen is examined in the frozen section lab and no tumor is identified grossly. The axillary portion of the specimen is removed and multiple small lymph nodes are removed. They are entirely submitted (see section code). A representative section of the nipple is submitted (see section code). Representative sections of the indurated white areas of the breast parenchyma are submitted (see section code). Section Code: C: Nipple D-F: Indurated areas G-H: Lymph nodes I-O: Indurated areas Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast" is a 16 x 10 x 5 cm mastectomy specimen. It is covered by an ellipse of skin which measures 13 x 5 cm. The nipple and areola are grossly unremarkable. A representative section of the nipple is submitted (see section code). Four surgical sutures are in place on the medial aspect of the areola, possibly designated a previous biopsy site. The specimen is inked black and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE cm firm, white nodule which is 1 cm from the deep margin, grossly suspicious for tumor. A representative section is frozen as FX #2, now in cassette P. The rest of the breast is similar to the changes describe in the left breast. Representative sections of the indurated areas are submitted (see section code). Additional sections from the firm area (frozen section) are submitted in cassette V. Further random sections are submitted(see section code). The axillary portion of the specimen is dissected and multiple lymph nodes are identified which are entirely submitted (see section code). Section Code: P: Frozen section #2 Q-U: Representative indurated areas V: Firm nodule W-X: Additional sections Y-Z: Lymph nodes ZZ: Nipple. Resident: JEROME T. O'CONNELL JR., MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1: BREAST (RIGHT, NODULE), EXCISION: FLORID INTRADUCTAL PROLIFERATION, FAVOR BENIGN; NO STROMAL INVASION IDENTIFIED. FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #2: BREAST (RIGHT): SCLEROSING PAPILLOMA, THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. GROSS DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (LEFT), MODIFIED RADICAL MASTATECTOMY: FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. NO INVASIVE TUMOR IS SEEN ON GROSS EXAMINATION. O.R. Resident: SAMANTHA J. PULLIAM, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: John H. Eichhorn, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: BREAST (RIGHT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B: BREAST (LEFT) and LYMPH NODE (AXILLA) PART C: BREAST ("RIGHT NODULE")\u000a[report_end]
