th the patient's name and unit number, are two parts. Labeled "Nipple duct, A" are two pink-tan, rubbery nodules of tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm; submitted entirely in cassette O. Labeled "Nipple duct, B" is a single fragment of fibroadipose tissue with duct and a long stitch designating distal and short designating superficial. Specimen is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The duct has length REMOVED_DATE cm and diameter REMOVED_DATE cm. The external surface is inked black and the superficial aspect is inked yellow on black and the distal margin of the nipple duct is submitted in cassette P. Representative sections of the duct are submitted in cassette Q, and representative sections of the breast material are submitted in cassette R through Y. Resident: Mark vanGorder, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1: (RIGHT BREAST MASS): FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. O.R. Resident: Douglas B. Flieder, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: Andrew Eric Rosenberg, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SURGICAL DAY CARE - ACC 3 REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: RIGHT BREAST MASS PART B: NIPPLE DUCT (LEFT) PART C: NIPPLE DUCT EXCISION\u000a[report_end]
