teriorly. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a large well-circumscribed tan-white to pink gelatinous firm tumor, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, with focal areas of hemorrhage, polypoid projections, and blood-filled cysts (0.2 to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension). The tumor comes to REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm of anterior margin. The skin and posterior skeletal muscle are grossly uninvolved by the tumor. Axillary lymph nodes are not identified along the edge of the specimen. The remaining breast parenchyma is largely fatty and grossly uninvolved by the tumor. A-B: Tumor to posterior margin with the closest approach in cassette A. C: The closest anterior margin (radial section). D: Tumor to skin surface. E: The closest posterior skeletal muscle (radial section). F-G: Representative sections of the cystic areas of the tumor. H-L: Representative sections of the polypoid areas of the tumor. M-N: Representative sections of the gelatinous areas of the tumor. O: A representative section of the hemorrhagic areas of the tumor. P-R: Representative sections of the solid areas of the tumor. S-T: Tumor to surrounding fatty tissue. U-V: Two additional representative sections of the largely fatty uninvolved breast parenchyma. W: The REMOVED_DATE cm skin papule, bisected. X: The REMOVED_DATE cm skin papule, bisected. Y: The REMOVED_DATE cm skin papule, bisected. Resident: TAI-YUAN LIN, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Kevin S. Hughes, M.D. PART : BREAST (RIGHT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY
