VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 09 REMOVED_MONTH 04 ACCESSIONED ON: 09 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 18:33 CLINICAL DATA: Right breast lumpectomy with sentinel node mapping. FNA showed ductal carcinoma. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA. SEE TABLE. DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU. SEE TABLE. TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS # 1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size: Two nodules: REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm; and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm (gross measurement). See note. Grade: 2 Lymphatic vessel invasion: Suspicious for lymphatic invasion in one focus. Blood vessel invasion: Not identified. Margin of invasive carcinoma: The distances to all margins measure REMOVED_DATE cm or greater. Location of ductal carcinoma in-situ: Within and beyond the region of the mass. Grade of ductal carcinoma in-situ: 1 Margin of ductal carcinoma in-situ: The distances to all margins measure REMOVED_DATE cm or greater. Stains for receptors: Requested. Note: The two nodules of tumor have an identical histological appearance, and there is a small amount of tumor in the intervening tissue, suggesting a bi-lobed configuration. LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLARY, PRIMARY SENTINEL, #182), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY (ONE NODE). SEE NOTE. NOTE: Keratin-positive tumor cells are not identified on three REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.3/Cam5.2 immunostained levels. LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLARY, SECONDARY SENTINEL, #77), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY (ONE NODE). SEE NOTE. NOTE: Keratin-positive tumor cells are not identified on three REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.3/Cam5.2 immunostained levels. LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLARY, TERTIARY SENTINEL, #71), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY (ONE NODE). SEE NOTE. NOTE: Keratin-positive tumor cells are not identified on three REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.3/Cam5.2 immunostained levels. DESIGNATED "QUARTARY NODE, #31", EXCISION: ADIPOSE TISSUE ONLY; THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. NOTE: Keratin-positive tumor cells are not identified on three REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.3/Cam5.2 immunostained levels. Diagnosis by: John H. Eichhorn, M.D. Signed On: 14 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 17:47 =============================================================================== *** IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum *** RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Left, block I): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells show moderate (2+) overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Atul Kumar Bhan, M.D. Signed On: 16 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 18:49 *** HER-2 Addendum *** RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION (FISH) FOR HER-2/NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast (Left, block I): HER-2/neu gene in tumor cells: REMOVED_DATE (Not Amplified). See note. Note: Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER-2 to chromosome 17 signals in 60 tumor cell nuclei. A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis. Added by: Atul Kumar Bhan, M.D. Signed On: 23 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 16:07 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "primary sentinel node #182", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-pink lymph node with minimal attached fat sectioning reveals a tan-pink cut surface and is entirely submitted as A. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "secondary sentinel node #77", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of tan-yellow fibroadipose tissue which is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm gray-pink lymph node. The lymph node is bisected to reveal a tan-pink cut surface and is entirely submitted as B. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "tertiary node #71", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm gray-pink lymph node with minimal attached tan-yellow adipose tissue. The specimen is bisected to reveal a tan-pink cut surface and is entirely submitted as C. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "quartary #31", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of tan-yellow fibroadipose tissue which is sectioned to reveal three gray-red nodules ranging from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension. The specimen is submitted in toto as D. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "left breast lump", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of tan-pink fibroadipose tissue with a short black stitch designating the anterior, a long black stitch the lateral, and a bowtie stitch the superior margins. Posterior margin is inked black, the anterior blue, the superior green, and the inferior yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal two stellate gray-white indurated nodules, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The former comes to REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior, and >5 cm of the medial and 4 cm of the lateral margin. The latter is REMOVED_DATE cm superior lateral to the first and comes to REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior, >5.0 cm of the medial, and > REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral margins. The remaining cut surface shows focally nodular dense gray-white fibrous tissue amidst predominantly tan-yellow unremarkable adipose tissue. Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral as follows: E: Representative dense, nodular, fibrous tissue to superior and posterior margins. F-G: Larger indurated nodule (nodule #1) closest posterior margin. H: Tissue between larger and smaller nodules, including posterior margin. I-J: Smaller indurated nodule to superior and anterior margins. K: Smaller indurated nodule to posterior margin. L: Representative radial sections of lateral margin. Gross Description by: STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident: JOSHUA B. KISH, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Kevin S. Hughes, M.D. PART A: LYMPH NODE(LEFT AXILLA, PRIMARY SENTINEL #182),EXC PART B: LYMPH NODE(LEFT AXILLA, SECONDARY SENTINEL #77),EX PART C: LYMPH NODE(LEFT, TERTIARY #71),EXCISION PART D: LYMPH NODE(LEFT, QUANTARY #31),EXCISION PART E: BREAST(LEFT),EXCISION
