lar"): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. See note. Note: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 07 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 07:02 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast biopsy, needle localization" are two fragments of breast parenchyma measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The larger of the fragment has a needle localization wire in place. The larger fragment is inked black and serially section to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm irregular white area of fibrous thickening with focal areas of calcification. The thickened area is entirely submitted in cassettes A-H with a remainder of the largest specimen entirely submitted in I-J. The smaller fragment is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm area of fibrous thickening at one edge of the specimen. The smaller fragment is entirely submitted in cassettes K-L. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast medial superior margin" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm unoriented fragment of fibrofatty tissue which is inked entirely in black and serially sectioned to reveal fibrofatty breast parenchyma. The entire specimen is submitted in M. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "left breast subareolar nodule" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x