ly of dense white fibrous tissue with focal, firm nodularity. A few small blue cysts are also identified within the parenchyma. Section code: A-B: Biopsy cavity in relation to closest suture deep margin; C: Biopsy cavity in relation to closest anterior margin; D: Biopsy cavity in relation to overlying skin; E-F: Parenchymal changes adjacent to biopsy site; G-H: Representative nodular fibrous tissue from remaining breast; No lymph nodes were identified from the mastectomy specimen. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "more left breast tissue" are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. One fragment is surfaced by an unremarkable REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan skin ellipse. Sectioning through the specimens reveals an unremarkable parenchyma with no discrete lesions. Representative sections are submitted in cassettes I-J. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "right breast tissue" are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and weighing 500 grams. The largest fragment measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. A few of the portions have overlying unremarkable portions of tan skin. Sectioning reveals moderate amounts of dense fibrous tissue. No discrete lesions are noted. Three lymph nodes are identified ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Representative sections of the fibrous parenchyma are submitted in cassettes K-O. Representative sections from each lymph node are submitted in cassette P. Additional sections of the breast tissue are submitted in Q-U. Gross Description by: JANINE L. DUDAC Resident: HOWARD CHANG, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Susan E Briggs, M.D. John Edmund Mayer Jr., 