se tissue with slight white fibrous tissue. Representative sections are submitted sequentially from lateral to medial as follows: D: Lateral most margin E: Full thickness F: Tumor to superior margin G: Tumor to posterior margin H-I: Tumor to anterior margin J: Tumor to posterior margin K: Tumor to inferior margin L: Posterior inferior margin M: Medial most margin Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "additional deep margin left breast" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue which is serially sectioned to reveal predominately dense white fibrous tissue with minimal yellow lobulated adipose tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted as N-S. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final shaved margin superior half of cavity" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of fibrofatty tissue which is serially sectioned to reveal a 50% yellow lobulated adipose tissue to 50% dense white fibrous tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted as T-X. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final shaved margin inferior half of cavity" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue which is serially sectioned to reveal predominately dense white fibrous tissue with minimal yellow lobulated adipose tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted as Y-DD. Gross Description by: BEN FARMER Resident: RESIDENT-FREE SERVICE (GTM) =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA SENTINEL LEVEL REMOVED_DATE #529) PART B: BREAST(LEFT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C: BREAST(LEFT),ADDITIONAL DEEP MARGIN PART D: BREAST(LEFT,SUPERIOR REMOVED_DATE OF CAVITY),EXCISION PART E: BREAST(LEFT,INFERIOR REMOVED_DATE OF CAVITY),EXCISION
