VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON: 05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08:55 CLINICAL DATA: {None Provided} =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (RIGHT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. BREAST (RIGHT, ADDITIONAL TISSUE): FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. LYMPH NODES (RIGHT AXILLA): UNREMARKABLE LYMPH NODES. BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. Diagnosis by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09:50 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with patient's name and unit number is a specimen in four parts. Labeled "left breast" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm simple mastectomy specimen. The nipple is attached eccentrically. A T-shaped skin attachment is REMOVED_DATE cm across and REMOVED_DATE cm down to where it attaches to the areolar. The parenchyma is markedly fibrotic and variably cystic throughout. There is no gross evidence of infiltrating carcinoma. A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm cavity is just deep to the nipple. Section code: A-E: representative sections of fibrocystic areas F: soft tissue cavity deep to nipple Labeled "right breast" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm simple mastectomy specimen with an eccentrically located nipple contiguous with the short arm of a T-shaped segment of attached skin, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a marking suture on one side of the specimen. The breast parenchyma is diffusely and irregularly fibrous and cystic throughout. The largest cyst noted is REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension. There is no gross evidence of an infiltrating carcinoma. Representative sections of the fibrocystic areas are in G-L and Y-EE. Labeled "right breast tissue" are four fragments of tissue, one with skin attached, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension; two pieces of grossly unremarkable adipose tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension; a skin ellipse, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, with minimal subcutaneous tissue attached. Two representative samples of the largest piece of breast tissue are in M and N. Single sections from each of the two smaller pieces of fibroadipose tissue are in O and P. Representative sections of the free skin segment are in Q. Labeled "right axillary lymph node, level I" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm piece of adipose tissue. The fatty tissue contains linear areas of tan, which could represent a lymph node. The specimen is submitted entirely in R-X. Resident: STUART HOUSER, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. James Warren May Jr., M.D. PART A: LEFT SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B: RIGHT SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART C: RIGHT BREAST, ADDITIONAL TISSUE PART D: RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
