VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 30 AUG 94 ACCESSIONED ON: 30 AUG 94 at 13:38 CLINICAL DATA: {None Provided} =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT), BIOPSY: -- PHYLLOIDES TUMOR, HIGH GRADE, WITH MULTIPLE AREAS OF STROMAL OVERGROWTH. (SEE NOTE): NOTE: Areas of stromal overgrowth are present in five of twelve slides. A study by Ward and Evans (1986) indicate that stromal overgrowth is a significant morphologic indicator of metastatic behavior. Tumor is present at inked surfaces. REF: Ward, RM, and Evans, HL. Cancer 1986; 58:2282-9. -- ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, FOCAL. BREAST (2ND LEFT BREAST MASS), BIOPSY: PHYLLOIDES TUMOR, HIGH GRADE, CONTAINING A SINGLE FOCUS OF SEVERAL ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. (SEE NOTE). NOTE: The focus of atypical intraductal hyperplasia (slide N) borders on a diagnosis of intraductal carcinoma. In the setting of a stromal neoplasm a more conservative diagnosis seems prudent. Dr. Frederick Koerner agrees with the interpretation. Diagnosis by: Dennis Sgroi, M.D. Signed On: 07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13:09 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: The specimen is received in two separately labeled containers. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "Left breast mass" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 cm red to tan, firm, irregular mass; the specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal homogeneous white cut surface. A representative section is frozen as frozen section #1, and kept frozen. Material is also sent for EM. Twelve additional sections are submitted in cassettes A through L, following photography of the specimen. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number only, it consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of fibroadipose tissue which is sectioned to reveal lobulated, well-demarcated, rubbery, pink nodule. This specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes M through P. Resident: JAMES J. TIESINGA, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1: (LEFT BREAST MASS, EXCISION): CELLULAR MIXED TUMOR ? PHYLLODES TUMOR. O.R. Resident: DARRYL E. PALMER-TOY, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: Robert Henry Young, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SURGICAL DAY CARE - ACC 3 REPORTS TO: Leslie Wayne Ottinger, M.D. PART A: BREAST MASS (LEFT) PART B: 2ND BREAST MASS (LEFT)\u000a[report_end]
