VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 03 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON: 03 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10:15 CLINICAL DATA: The patient has had a previous excison of a phylloides tumor, with a focus of intraductal carcinoma. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION: 1)RESIDUAL PHYLLOIDES TUMOR, HIGH GRADE. SEE NOTE. NOTE: In this specimen there is no stromal overgrowth or severely atypical intraductal hyperplasia as noted in the previous biopsy specimen (94-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). All of the resection margins are negative. No vascular invasion is identified. 2)HEALING BIOPSY SITE. Diagnosis by: Andrew Eric Rosenberg, M.D. Signed On: 06 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16:40 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh from the frozen section lab, labeled with the patient's name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm breast excision specimen partially covered by a narrow REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm skin ellipse with a central REMOVED_DATE cm well healed scar. A surgical stitch designates the medial margin of resection. The specimen is inked in black and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, well demarcated, tan, rubbery nodule that is REMOVED_DATE cm from the nearest superior resection margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the nearest deep resection margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the nearest inferior resection margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the skin ellipse. The nodule is surrounded inferiorly by focal hemorrhage. The remainder of the breast parenchyma demonstrates mature, yellow, lobulated, adipose tissue with intercolating fibrous septae. A prominent REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm firm fibrous area is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral resection, and abuts the inferior resection margin. The superior resection margin is re-inked in red, the inferior resection margin is re-inked in yellow, and the following sections are taken. The nodule is submitted entirely in cassette A through J; cassettes A and B represent the lateral aspect of the nodule (3.5 cm from the lateral resection margin), and cassettes I and J represents the medial aspect of the nodule (3.7 cm from the medial resection margin). Sections through the lateral inferior area of fibrosis are submitted in cassettes K through M. Sections through grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma taken REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial resection margin are submitted in cassette N and O. Skin and subcutaneous tissue overlying the closest (3.2 cm) portion of the nodule is submitted as cassette P. Breast tissue at the lateral resection margin is submitted as Q. Breast tissue at the medial resection margin is submitted as R. Resident: JAMES J. TIESINGA, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SURGICAL DAY CARE - ACC 3 REPORTS TO: Leslie Wayne Ottinger, M.D. PART : LEFT BREAST\u000a[report_end]
