VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 06 REMOVED_MONTH 04 ACCESSIONED ON: 06 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 11:21 CLINICAL DATA: History of grade 3 DCIS on core biopsy of the right breast. 1. Stitch short superior, long deep, first piece of tissue from needle loc was adjacent to "old cavity" (inferior). =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). HEALING BIOPSY SITE. SEE TABLE #1. SEE NOTE. NOTE: Stains for heavy chain myosin and p63 do not disclose invasive carcinoma. The neoplastic lobular cells do not stain for E-cadherin. Invasion of the stroma, blood vessels and lymphatic vessels is not seen. TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS #1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU Tumor size: Involving 3 of 5 blocks and spanning at least REMOVED_DATE cm. Grade: 3 Margin of ductal carcinoma in-situ: Ductal carcinoma extends to the anterior and lateral margins of the specimen and to REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin of the specimen. Stains for receptors: Not indicated See report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. BREAST (RIGHT, "SUPERIOR FINAL ASPECT", EXCISION: DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, IN 2 OF 6 BLOCKS AND EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MEDIAL MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. SEE NOTE. NOTE: Invasion of the stroma, blood vessels, and lymphatic vessels is not seen. BREAST (RIGHT "MEDIAL FINAL MARGIN"), EXCISION: SLIGHT ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. BREAST (RIGHT, "LATERAL FINAL MARGIN"), EXCISION: LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. FIBROADENOMA. BREAST (RIGHT, "INFERIOR FINAL MARGIN"), EXCISION: LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU). BREAST (RIGHT "ANTERIOR FINAL MARGIN"), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Diagnosis by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 09 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 16:13 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast needle loc" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of gray to tan-red fibroadipose tissue with a short black stitch designating the deep margin and a long black stitch the superior. A localization wire is in place. The deep (posterior) margin is inked black, the superficial (anterior) margin blue, the medial margin green, and lateral margin yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal dense focally nodular gray-white fibrous tissue. The most prominent nodule is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and focally abuts the medial margin along the superior half of the specimen. The specimen is entirely submitted from superior to inferior as A-E, with the area designated by the localization wire as D-E, and the most prominent nodule as B. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "superior aspect" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of fibrofatty soft tissue which has been oriented with a short stitch marking the superior and a long stitch marking the deep margins. There is also a drawing present on the requisition indicating the inferior surface as the "old cavity from case", inferior. The specimen is inked as follows: superior blue, medial green, lateral yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned from the anterior to posterior to reveal a tan-white and fibrotic cut surface surrounded by yellow adipose tissue. The previous cavity site is hemorrhagic and shaggy. The specimen is submitted in its entirety in a sequential fashion from anterior to posterior with F being the anterior margin and K being the posterior margin (deep). Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "medial margin" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm irregular tan-yellow fibrofatty soft tissue fragment which is inked black and submitted in its entirety in cassette L. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "lateral margin" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-yellow fibrofatty soft tissue fragment which is serially sectioned and submitted in its entirety in cassette M. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "inferior margin" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm irregular fragment of fibrofatty soft tissue. One surface is slightly hemorrhagic and shaggy and the nearest other surface is glistening. The glistening surface is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal tan-yellow lobulated cut surface. No tumor or masses are grossly identified. The specimen is submitted in its entirety in N-O. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "anterior margin" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of tan-yellow fibrofatty soft tissue fragments which are submitted in their entirety in cassettes P-Q. Gross Description by: RYAN W. SCHNIEDERJAN Resident: CHRISTOPHER M. WILLIAM, MD., Ph.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: BREAST(RIGHT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: BREAST(RIGHT SUPERIOR FINAL ASPECT),EXCISION PART C: BREAST(RIGHT MEDIAL FINAL MARGIN),EXCISION PART D: BREAST(RIGHT LATERAL FINAL MARGIN),EXCISION PART E: BREAST(RIGHT INFERIOR FINAL MARGIN),EXCISION PART F: BREAST (RIGHT ANTERIOR FINAL MARGIN),EXCISION
