necrosis and a central REMOVED_DATE cm cavity containing blood clot. The fat necrosis extends to REMOVED_DATE cm to the deep resection margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior resection margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin. There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm ill-defined area, underneath the superior surgical scar, with fat necrosis which extends to REMOVED_DATE cm to the deep resection margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior resection margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior resection marign. The remaining breast parenchyma is mostly fatty and contains focal fibrous areas. Section code: A-D: the inferior biopsy cavity E-H: superior biopsy cavity I,J: fibrous areas K-O: axillary lymph nodes Labeled "additional axillary tissue" are multiple fragments of adipose tissue, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate; submitted entirely in cassette P. The third specimen, labeled "left breast" weighs 875 grams in toto and consists of three parts. Labeled "left lateral breast" are four fragments of fibroadipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in toto. The largest fragment displays an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm piece of unremarkable skin. Sectioning of the breast parenchyma reveals unremarkable fibrofatty surfaces. Representative sections are submitted in cassettes Q, R,U and V. Labeled "left medial breast" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm piece of unremarkable fibrofatty tissue over-lined by a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm unremarkable piece of skin. Representative section is submitted in cassette S, W, and X . Labeled "left central breast" are two fragments of unremarkable fibroadipose tissue, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, respectively. Representative sections from each are submitted in cassette T, Y and Z. Resident: CHIN-LEE WU, MD, PhD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. Michael J Yaremchuk, M.D. PART A: BREAST (RIGHT), MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B: SOFT TISSUE (AXILLARY) PART C: BREAST (LEFT), REDUCTION\u000a[report_end]
