imen is entirely submitted laterally towards medially into cassettes A-J with the hemorrhagic region surrounding the surgical clip into cassettes G-J. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "additional tissue right breast inferior lateral" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of yellow and firm fibroadipose tissue which is serially sectioned to reveal scattered tan-white fibrous tissue and scattered small yellow foci. The specimen is entirely submitted into cassettes K-L. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "additional tissue right breast deep" is an oriented fragment of yellow fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The black stitch present denotes the deep margin. This surface is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned and does not reveal any grossly identified nodules. The specimen is entirely submitted into cassettes M-R. Resident: PAUL MICHAELS, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: BREAST(RIGHT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: BREAST(RIGHT INFERIOR LATERAL),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C: BREAST(RIGHT POSTERIOR),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY
