VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 24 AUG 00 ACCESSIONED ON: 24 AUG 00 at 11:31 CLINICAL DATA: Breast mass. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT), EXCISION: INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA. (SEE TABLE #1) TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS #1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size: REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE cm. Grade: 2 Lymphatic vessel invasion: present Blood vessel invasion: not identified Margin of invasive carcinoma: The distances to all margins measure REMOVED_DATE cm or greater. Location of ductal carcinoma in-situ: Beyond the region of the mass. Margin of ductal carcinoma in-situ: Ductal carcinoma in-situ extends to less than REMOVED_DATE cm. from the anterior margin of the specimen. Stains for receptors: Requested. DUCTAL CARCINOMA-IN-SITU. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. BREAST (FINAL MARGIN), EXCISION: LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA), LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE NEAREST MARGIN. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS. Diagnosis by: Grace T. McKee,MD Signed On: 28 AUG 00 at 15:40 Consulting Pathologist(s): Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. =============================================================================== *** BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum *** RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Left, block C): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells show moderate to strong overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Atul Kumar Bhan, M.D. Signed On: 31 AUG 00 at 14:31 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and no designation as to site, is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of breast with a long suture designating lateral margin, a short suture designating superior margin and a thick portion of a needle localization wire, inked as follows: anterior inked blue, posterior inked black, medial in red and lateral in yellow. Sections from superior to inferior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, ill-demarcated irregular shaped, tan-white firm mass with two foci of calcification measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter, which comes to the inked anterior margin and within REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest medial margin. Also identified is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm ill-demarcated, tan-white rubbery lesion which comes to the inked posterior margin. During sectioning, the incision is noted from the anterior margin to the specimen and held together by an additional suture. The specimen is submitted entirely and serially in cassettes A-H. (Firm mass in cassettes C-E, rubbery lesion in cassette H). Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "left breast final shaved margin" are five fragments of fibrofatty tissue measuring from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE x2.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm. Two of them are inked black and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm cyst which comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest inked margin. The specimen is submitted entirely and serially in cassettes I-O and P and remaining fragments are submitted in cassettes Q-R. Resident: Mari Mino, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-OUTPATIENT (OFF.P/CLINIC) REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, 