VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 18 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON: 18 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 10:36 CLINICAL DATA: Left breast cancer with lymphovascular invasion. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT), MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY: HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY; THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES, WITH MILD DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWO OF TWO INTRAPARENCHYMAL LYMPH NODES. SKIN AND SOFT TISSUE (LEFT BREAST, INFERIOR ADDITIONAL MARGIN), BIOPSY: NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLARY, SENTINEL #1), BIOPSY: METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA, SEVERAL FOCI (UP TO REMOVED_DATE CM) WITHIN A REMOVED_DATE CM DIAMETER NODE, WITHOUT EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION; THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED. LYMPH NODES (LEFT AXILLARY, SENTINEL #2), BIOPSY: METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA TO ONE OF TWO LYMPH NODES (0.2 CM FOCUS), WITHOUT EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION. LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLARY, ADDITIONAL), BIOPSY: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY (ONE LYMPH NODE). BREAST (RIGHT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES, HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS, WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND SMALL DUCT PAPILLOMAS. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. LYMPH NODES (RIGHT), REGIONAL DISSECTION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN SIX OF SIX LYMPH NODES. Diagnosis by: John H. Eichhorn, M.D. Signed On: 25 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 20:36 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "simple mastectomy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm right simple mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan skin ellipse and an intact nipple. A stitch marks REMOVED_DATE 'clock. Specimen is inked black and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm poorly circumscribed yellow tan firm area which is REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin and abuts the anterior skin ellipse. The firm area is more than REMOVED_DATE cm from all other resection margins. Multiple cysts ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter are identified within the firm area. Representative tissue is submitted. SECTION CODE: A: Posterior deep margin. B: Inferior resection margin. C: Firm area in relation to skin. D: Representative sections of nipple. E-L: Representative sections of the firm area (cystic in G-J). Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "modified radical mastectomy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen with a 25 x 11 cm tan skin ellipse and intact nipple. A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm scar with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm surface defect exposing an underlying cavity is present on the posterior resection margin. A stitch marks 12 o'clock. The specimen is inked black and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm biopsy cavity abutting the posterior margin. A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan firm ill defined area is present beneath this cavity, which is more than REMOVED_DATE cm from all inked margins. Representative tissue is submitted. SECTION CODE: M-N: Biopsy cavity in relation to the posterior resection margin. O-Q: Anterior wall of biopsy cavity. R-T: Representative sections of the mass. U: Representative sections of well circumscribed firm area at the superior margin, midline. V: Lymph node isolated from the lateral end of the specimen. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left inferior additional margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan skin ellipse, excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm. Also received in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of adipose tissue. The specimen is serially sectioned and unremarkable. Representative sections are submitted in W-FF. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left axillary sentinel node", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-red soft tissue fragment, containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm lymph node. The lymph node is bisected and entirely frozen as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and submitted in GG and HH. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left axilla sentinel node #2", are 2 lymph nodes, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in II. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left additional axillary content", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm adipose tissue. Dissection of the specimen reveals one lymph node measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm which is bisected and entirely submitted in JJ. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right axillary tail", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm adipose tissue, which is bisected to reveal multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Small lymph nodes are entirely submitted in cassette KK, two larger lymph nodes are bisected and entirely submitted in LL and MM. Resident: SONER ALTIOK, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS 1: LYMPH NODE, SENTINEL, LEFT AXILLARY: METASTATIC CARCINOMA. GROSS DIAGNOSIS 1: BREAST, RIGHT: NO OBVIOUS GROSS TUMOR. O.R. Resident: Mari Mino, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: Robert Henry Young, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: BREAST (LEFT), MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B: BREAST (LEFT, INFERIOR ADDITIONAL MARGIN) PART C: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLARY, SENTINEL #1) PART D: LYMPH NODES (LEFT AXILLARY, SENTINEL #2) PART E: LYMPH NODES (LEFT AXILLARY, ADDITIONAL) PART F: BREAST (RIGHT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART G: LYMPH NODES (RIGHT), REGIONAL DISSECTION
