VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 13 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON: 13 AUG 98 at 12:55 CLINICAL DATA: A. Short stitch superior, long stitch lateral, re-excision right breast. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (RIGHT), RE-EXCISION: HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (RIGHT "FINAL SHAVED MARGINS"), EXCISION: SEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, SINGLE FOCUS PRESENT AT THE RESECTION MARGIN. SEE NOTE. NOTE: The focus is distorted by cautery artifact. The atypia resembles that seen in ductal carcinoma in situ, and other pathologists may favour the latter interpretation. Diagnosis by: EDI BROGI, MD, PhD Signed On: 20 AUG 98 at 12:03 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "Right Breast Tissue, Short Stitch Superior, Long Stitch Lateral", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a short suture designating the superior margin, and a long suture designating the lateral margin. The lateral margin is surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm white skin ellipse. There is an irregular REMOVED_DATE cm sutured previous biopsy cavity on the inferior margin, coming within REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep margin. The entire specimen is inked black. The superior aspect is over-inked blue, the deep over-inked green. The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm biopsy cavity, which abuts the inferior margin (where the biopsy cavity is sutured closed). The biopsy site is focally hemorrhagic and is surrounded by firm, indurated, white parenchyma with diffuse, bright-yellow changes. The biopsy cavity is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest deep margin, as well as the medial margin. The irregular biopsy cavity is focally fragmented and at one point comes within REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest lateral margin. Extending from the biopsy site up to the skin margin, there are diffuse, bright-yellow changes in the pattern of a previous needle biopsy tract. These bright-yellow changes come within REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest anterior margin. The remaining parenchyma is predominantly fatty, with no additional masses. SECTION CODE: A : Radial sections of the sutured, fragmented biopsy cavity in relation to the inferior margin. B-C: The fragmented biopsy cavity in relation to the lateral margin. D : Two sections of the biopsy cavity in relation to the closest deep margin. E : Biopsy cavity in relation to the closest medial margin. F : Radial sections of the grossly uninvolved superior margin. G : A representative section of the anterior margin with adjacent lateral skin and underlying bright-yellow parenchymal changes. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "Part B, Right breast final shaved margins", are six fragments of irregular fibroadipose tissue, which are unoriented, aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Each is serially sectioned to reveal no discrete masses. The specimen is entirely submitted in Cassettes H-M. Gross Description by: JANINE L. DUDAC =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. Edi Brogi, M.D., PhD. PART A: BREAST (RIGHT), RE-EXCISION PART B: BREAST (RIGHT "FINAL SHAVED MARGINS"), EXCISION\u000a[report_end]
