c nipple are also present. It is inked black - anterior, blue - deep and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm poorly defined slightly firm area with a central REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter cavity. This area has a grey-white, heterogeneous cut-surface. It is REMOVED_DATE cm to the closest deep resection margin along a broad front. The other resection margins and the skin are not grossly involved. The remaining parenchyma is unremarkable. No lymph nodes are identified. Representative sections are submitted as follows: Sections of firm area are submitted in C-J with the deep resection margin included in C-F and cavity in I and J; K-anterior margin with the skin; L-superior margin; M-inferior margin; NandO-sections of unremarkable parenchyma. Resident: DI TIAN, MD, PhD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1: LYMPH NODE (LEFT SENTINEL- 1193, LEFT AXILLA): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #2: LYMPH NODE (LEFT SENTINEL -544): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. O.R. Resident: HONGMEI LI, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: Eugene Jerome Mark, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. Michael J Yaremchuk, M.D. PART A: BREAST (LEFT), MASTECTOMY PART B: LYMPH NODE (LEFT SENTINEL - 1193), EXCISION PART C: LYMPH NODE (LEFT SENTINEL - 544), EXCISION\u000a[report_end]
