d as follows: medial-black, lateral-blue, anterior-red, posterior-yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal two nodules. The first nodule measures 1 x 1 x 1 cm and is white, firm and abuts one needle localization wire and is located <0.1 cm from the medial resection margin. The second nodule is also white and firm and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and abuts the second needle localization wire (designating the clip) and is located <0.1 cm from the medial resection margin. Multiple soft white fibrous areas are also encountered measuring up to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension throughout the breast parenchyma. No gross calcifications are identified. Representative sections are submitted from superior to inferior in cassettes A-M with the previously described nodules in B and M. Additional representative sections from the inferior half are submitted in AA-BB. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "final shave margin-superior" is a 6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue which is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes N-P. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "final shaved margin-inferior" is a 4 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue which is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes Q-R. Resident: CHRISTINE GARCIA, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: BREAST (LEFT SUPERIOR), FINAL SHAVED MARGIN PART C: BREAST (LEFT INFERIOR), FINAL SHAVED MARGIN
