y the thick portion of the needle wire is submitted in cassettes B-D. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "anterior right breast", are two irregular portions of breast tissue which measure in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The tissue is not oriented. Both fragments are inked blue and serially sectioned to reveal an approximately 95% fibrous and 10% adipose tissue. The fibrous tissue is ill-defined, white-gray and soft. No discrete lesions are noted. The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes G-I. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "inferior right breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of unoriented, predominately fibrous breast tissue. The specimen is inked black, serially sectioned and submitted entirely as cassettes J-K. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "anterior lateral right breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm portion of unoriented breast tissue. The tissue is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal a white-gray homogeneous soft fibrous tissue. The specimen is submitted entirely as cassettes L-M. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast, deep margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of unoriented breast tissue. The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal homogeneous white-gray fibrous tissue. In the approximate center of the specimen there is a REMOVED_DATE cm metal clip, located REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest inked resection margin. The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes N-R, the breast tissue surrounding the clip is submitted in cassette R. Resident: JULIA TURBINER, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: BREAST(RIGHT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: BREAST(RIGHT