VREMOVED_CASE_ID HAMWEY,ANGELA 46/F <REG REF REMOVED_DATE > (REMOVED_CASE_ID) WIC AUGUST,ALLISON M.D.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------Specimen: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID SOUT Received: REMOVED_DATE -1600 Spec Type: - Clinical diagnosis & history: Suspicious clustered microcalcifications of upper outer quadrant of right breast and solid nodules of upper inner quadrant near nipple; #1, ductal carcinoma in situ vs fibrocystic changes; #2, solid nodule, ? fibroadenoma Edited by: REMOVED_DATE  - 0659 PAT.MURJ Gross description: The specimen is received in formalin in two containers. Specimen A labeled "guided breast biopsies, right breast, lateral #1, 10 o'clock" and consists of a 1 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm. aggregate of tan-white, firm, glistening needle biopsies admixed with blood clot measuring REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm. in diameter. 1 agg. all. Specimen B labeled "guided breast biopsies, right breast, 12:30" and consists of four firm, yellowish-white, glistening needle biopsies measuring REMOVED_DATE cm. in length x REMOVED_DATE cm. in diameter to REMOVED_DATE cm. in length x REMOVED_DATE cm. in diameter. 4X all. Dictated by: LV Edited by: REMOVED_DATE  - 0815 PAT.MURJ DIAGNOSIS: A. Right breast, 10 o'clock, needle core biopsy: Atypical ductal hyperplasia (see note). No microcalcifications identified; multiple level sections were obtained. B. Right breast, 12:30, needle core biopsy: DIAGNOSIS: (Continued) Fibroadenoma. Edited by: REMOVED_DATE  - 1038 PAT.MURJ DESCRIPTIVE COMMENT: NOTE: Specimen A (needle core biopsy at 10 o'clock) was sent to Dr. Frederick Koerner at Massachusetts General Hospital. He concurs with the diagnosis. His note and recommendation for excision reads as follows: "The sections of this core biopsy specimen show a background of slight fibrocystic changes. Atypical epithelial cells occupy a small duct and associated lobules. Those in the duct have columnar shapes and they possess slightly enlarged nuclei and eosinophilic apical cytoplasm. I would classify these cells as atypical columnar cells and the proliferation as an especially mild form of atypical ductal hyperplasia. The cells in the nearby acini display more pronounced atypia. They look large and they contain large nuclei, pale, homogeneous chromatin, small nucleoli, and abundant, eosinophilic cytoplasm. The cells pile up slightly and, thereby, fill and slightly distend the glands. I regard these cells, too, as atypical ductal cells and the focus as atypical ductal hyperplasia. It could represent a small portion of a ductal carcinoma in situ. A few other acini distant from this region contain atypical epithelial cells that look a bit different. They appear slightly smaller, the nuclei look smaller and darker and the nucleoli seem less evident, moreover, the cytoplasm has a grey-blue color. I cannot confidently identify the nature of these cells, but I suspect that they may represent small regions of lobular neoplasia (atypical lobular hyperplasia). In light of the presence of these atypical epithelial proliferations and the absence of calcifications, I would suggest that the patient and her physicians seriously consider an excision of this region of the right breast." Final Diagnosis by: Nicole A. Mihok, M.D. Edited by: REMOVED_DATE  - 1044 PAT.MURJ Notes: REMOVED_DATE  7 slides ret'd from NEMC /jam (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) REMOVED_DATE  NEMC report rec'd /djd REMOVED_DATE  Per Dr. Homa Safaii, NEMC Path, sent 7 (A's) to her /dg REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_DATE  7 slides ret'd from MGH /djd CR REMOVED_DATE  Path report faxed from MGH /jam REMOVED_DATE  Report (letter) faxed from MGH /jam REMOVED_DATE  7 slides (all A) to Dr. Frederick Koerner, MGH Pathology for opinion per NAM/djd CO Edited by: REMOVED_DATE  - 1615 PAT.DORD REMOVED_DATE  - 0644 PAT.MURJ REMOVED_DATE  - 0742 PAT.MURJ Notes: (Continued) REMOVED_DATE  - 1034 PAT.DORD REMOVED_DATE  - 1005 PAT.GILD REMOVED_DATE  - 0805 PAT.DORD REMOVED_DATE  - 1104 PAT.MURJCODES: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - Right breast, N-Needle REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - Right breast, N-Plural REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - Right breast, N-Atypical hyperp REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - Right breast, N-Fibroadenoma, N BREANBX - -BREANBX Edited by: REMOVED_DATE  - 0659 PAT.MURJ REMOVED_DATE  - 1038 PAT.MURJCOPIES TO: AUGUST,ALLISON M.D. COMMONWEALTH OB/GYN, P.C. WELLESLEY, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID (781)237-0080 RUBENS,JAMI R. M.D. RADIOLOGY DEPARTMENT NEWTON, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID (617)243-6600MARKERS: Breast Disease Related, Consult Case Out, Consult Out 2, Consult Case Return, Consult Return 2 Edited by: REMOVED_DATE  - 0659 PAT.MURJ REMOVED_DATE  - 1615 PAT.DORD REMOVED_DATE  - 1034 PAT.DORD REMOVED_DATE  - 1005 PAT.GILD REMOVED_DATE  - 1105 PAT.MURJPROCEDURES: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (12/21/06-1044 PAT.MURJ) Edited by: REMOVED_DATE  - 0659 PAT.MURJ REMOVED_DATE  - 1044 PAT.MURJTISSUES: A. Breast, needle biopsy - right, 10 o'clock B. Breast, needle biopsy - right, 12:30 Edited by: REMOVED_DATE  - 0659 PAT.MURJFinal: FEEN,DENNIS J. M.D. * REMOVED_DATE  <12/21/06-1051> by MD.FEED MIHOK,NICOLE MD***** * REMOVED_DATE  <12/21/06-1055> by MD.MIHN --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
