VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Right axillary sentinel lymph nodes, excision:\u000aTwo lymph nodes with no diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aNo metastatic tumor identified after section leveling and pankeratin\u000aimmunohistochemical staining.\u000aB. Right breast, excision and remainder of biopsy cavity:\u000aPrevious biopsy site and cavity with chronic inflammation and foreign\u000abody giant cell reaction.\u000aSkin with scar.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia, (single focus).\u000aFocal ductal hyperplasia.\u000aNOTE: The previous surgical pathology report is reviewed (Mass General\u000aHospital REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). No residual invasive ductal carcinoma or\u000aductal carcinoma in situ is seen in the specimen. E cadherin stain is\u000anegative in the atypical lobular hyperplasia consistent with the\u000adiagnosis.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Michael J. Ross, M.D.\u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE CONSULTATION:\u000aOPERATING ROOM CONSULTATION (TISSUE EXAMINATION):\u000aSentinel lymph nodes: Two lymph nodes with no gross tumor seen.\u000aMJR\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aRight breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - right axillary\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - right\u000aGross description:\u000aSpecimen A labeled "right axillary sentinel node" consists of two nodular\u000afragments of yellow adipose bearing lymph nodes. One is REMOVED_DATE x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm. and\u000athe other, REMOVED_DATE x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimens have been previously transversely\u000asectioned and reveal a cut surface consisting of a brownish cortex and a\u000ayellowish medulla. There is no gross evidence of tumor. 2 agg.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "right breast re-excision" consists of two fragments of\u000atissue. One fragment contains green sutures for orientation purposes. The\u000aoverall dimensions are 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 cm. The anterior surface is concave. The\u000asuperior surface is marked with a short green suture; the lateral surface with\u000aa long green suture. The deep surface is marked with black ink. The superior\u000asurface is marked with blue ink. The superior portion of the specimen is\u000asubmitted in its entirety proceeding from medial to lateral margin designated\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The remainder of the specimen is also submitted from medial to lateral\u000adesignated REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The second portion of the specimen also consists of an oval\u000afragment of firm, yellowish-grey fibroadipose and fibrocollagenous tissue.\u000aThere are no orienting suture markings. The outer margins are inked. The cut\u000asurface reveals a hemorrhagic, irregular cavity-like area 2 x 1 cm. The entire\u000aspecimen is embedded designated REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 21X.\u000aDictated by: DJF____(signature on file)____NICOLE MIHOK, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____MICHAEL J. ROSS, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
