el lymph nodes).\u000aCOMMENT: The sentinel lymph nodes, specimens A and D, is examined at multiple\u000alevels with H&E stains and immunohistochemical stains for keratin.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aLeft breast needle localized excision; Massachusetts General Hospital\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE \u000aAJCC pTNM Classification (6th Ed.): pTis pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(sn)(i-) pMX\u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information\u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Nicole A. Mihok, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - right, 88 count\u000aB.Lymph node, biopsy - right\u000aC.Breast, simple mastectomy - right\u000aD.Sentinel lymph node - left, 208 count\u000aE.Specimen designated as - supernumerary nipple\u000aF.Breast, simple mastectomy - left\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in six containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "right sentinel lymph node, 88 count" is received in\u000aformalin and consists of a single REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. lymph node. The lymph\u000anode is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in one cassette. 1 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "right non sentinel lymph node" is received in formalin and\u000aconsists of a single lymph node that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen\u000ais trisected and entirely submitted in one cassette. 3X all.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "right breast" is received fresh from the Operating Room and\u000aconsists of a 557 gram simple mastectomy with a stitch said to designate the\u000aaxillary tail. The breast measures up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. On the surface\u000aof the breast is an ellipse of skin containing unremarkable skin and a nipple\u000awith areola. The skin with nipple and areola is up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. and the\u000anipple is up to REMOVED_DATE cm. in greatest height. The skin is unremarkable. The\u000aareola shows a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. slightly reddish nodule on the surface. The\u000abreast is inked as follows: upper outer quadrant, blue; lower outer quadrant,\u000agreen; upper inner quadrant, red; lower inner quadrant, yellow; deep margin,\u000ablack. The specimen is serially sectioned and no abnormalities are identified.\u000aThe breast parenchyma is yellowish-white and without lesions. Representative\u000asections are submitted.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - skin and the small nodule described\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - nipple with areola\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - underneath nipple\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - upper outer quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - lower outer quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - upper inner quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - lower inner quadrant\u000aSpecimen D labeled "left sentinel lymph node 208" is received in formalin and\u000aconsists of a single lymph node with attached adipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm. The node is trisected and submitted entirely in cassette D. 3X\u000aall.\u000aSpecimen E labeled "left supernumerary nipple" is received in formalin and\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of skin excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm. The\u000asurface of the skin shows slightly wrinkled beige skin. The specimen is\u000abisected and submitted entirely in cassette E. 2X all.\u000aSpecimen F labeled "left breast" is received fresh from the Operating Room and\u000aconsists of a 582 gram simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch designating the\u000aaxillary tail. The breast measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x up to REMOVED_DATE cm. On the\u000asurface, there is an ellipse of skin with a scar and a nipple and areola in\u000aplace. The ellipse of skin is up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The nipple is up to REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. in height. The nipple and areola are unremarkable. The skin shows a well\u000ahealed scar that is REMOVED_DATE cm. and is towards the lateral end of the skin ellipse.\u000aThe breast is inked as follows: upper outer quadrant, green; lower outer\u000aquadrant, blue; upper inner quadrant, red; lower inner quadrant, yellow; deep\u000amargin, black. The specimen is serially sectioned and the cut surface shows a\u000ahealing biopsy cavity with adjacent area of scarring. The biopsy cavity is REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. in greatest dimension and the area of scarring around it is up to REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aSlightly inferior to the area of prior biopsy change is a slightly gritty,\u000ayellow focus that is REMOVED_DATE cm. in greatest dimension. The cavity, scar and\u000ayellowish area are all widely clear of the surgical margin. They are located\u000aslightly lateral, underneath the nipple and at the 3 o'clock area of the\u000ajunction of the upper outer quadrant and lower outer quadrants. The remainder\u000aof the breast shows an area consistent with an intraductal papilloma in the\u000aupper inner quadrant. The specimen is sectioned and submitted as follows. 15\u000aagg.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - nipple, areola and skin with scar\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - random sections from upper outer quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - random sections from lower outer quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - random sections from upper inner quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - random sections from lower inner quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - sections of entire biopsy cavity and area of fibrosis\u000aaround the area of biopsy cavity (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID contains the\u000aslightly gritty, yellowish area)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - deep margin closest to the prior biopsy site\u000aTotal fixation time is 28 hours.\u000aDictated by: NAM____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____NICOLE MIHOK, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
